\s1 Elkanah and His Wives
\r (\ref Psalm 113:1–9|PSA 113:1-9\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Now there was|וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb a|אֶחָ֜ד\rb* \rb man|אִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb named|וּשְׁמ֡וֹ\rb* \rb Elkanah|אֶ֠לְקָנָה\rb* \rb who was from|מִן־\rb*\rb |הָרָמָתַ֛יִם\rb* \rb Ramathaim-zophim|צוֹפִ֖ים\rb*\f + \fr 1:1 \ft Or \fqa from Ramathaim, a Zuphite\ft ; see LXX and \ref 1 Chronicles 6:26|1CH 6:26\ref* and 35.\f* \rb in the hill country|מֵהַ֣ר\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרָ֑יִם\rb*. \rb He was the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jeroham|יְרֹחָ֧ם\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Elihu|אֱלִיה֛וּא\rb*,\f + \fr 1:1 \fqa Elihu \ft is also called \fqa Eliab \ft and \fqa Eliel\ft ; see \ref 1 Chronicles 6:27|1CH 6:27\ref* and 34.\f* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Tohu|תֹּ֥חוּ\rb*, \rb the son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Zuph|צ֖וּף\rb*, \rb an Ephraimite|אֶפְרָתִֽי׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb He had|וְלוֹ֙\rb* \rb two|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb wives|נָשִׁ֔ים\rb*, \rb one|אַחַת֙\rb* \rb named|שֵׁ֤ם\rb* \rb Hannah|חַנָּ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb and the other|הַשֵּׁנִ֖ית\rb* \rb Peninnah|פְּנִנָּ֑ה\rb*. \rb And Peninnah|לִפְנִנָּה֙\rb* \rb had|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb children|יְלָדִ֔ים\rb*, \rb but Hannah|וּלְחַנָּ֖ה\rb* \rb had none|אֵ֥ין\rb*\rb |יְלָדִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Year after year|מִיָּמִ֣ים׀\rb*\rb |יָמִ֔ימָה\rb* \rb Elkanah|הַה֤וּא\rb*\rb |הָאִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb would go up|וְעָלָה֩\rb* \rb from his city|מֵֽעִירוֹ֙\rb* \rb to worship|לְהִֽשְׁתַּחֲוֺ֧ת\rb* \rb and sacrifice|וְלִזְבֹּ֛חַ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb at Shiloh|בְּשִׁלֹ֑ה\rb*, \rb where|וְשָׁ֞ם\rb* \rb Eli’s|עֵלִ֗י\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb sons|בְנֵֽי־\rb*, \rb Hophni|חָפְנִי֙\rb* \rb and Phinehas|וּפִ֣נְחָ֔ס\rb*, \rb were priests|כֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb And whenever the day|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb for Elkanah|אֶלְקָנָ֑ה\rb* \rb to present his sacrifice|וַיִּזְבַּ֖ח\rb*, \rb he would give|וְנָתַ֞ן\rb* \rb portions|מָנֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb to his wife|אִשְׁתּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb Peninnah|לִפְנִנָּ֣ה\rb* \rb and to all|וּֽלְכָל־\rb* \rb her sons|בָּנֶ֛יהָ\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבְנוֹתֶ֖יהָ\rb*. \v 5 \rb But to Hannah|וּלְחַנָּ֕ה\rb* \rb he would give|יִתֵּ֛ן\rb* \rb a|אַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb double|אַפָּ֑יִם\rb* \rb portion|מָנָ֥ה\rb*,\f + \fr 1:5 \ft Or \fqa a choice portion\f* \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb he loved|אָהֵ֔ב\rb* \rb her|חַנָּה֙\rb* \rb even though the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb had closed|סָגַ֥ר\rb* \rb her womb|רַחְמָֽהּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb had closed|סָגַ֥ר\rb*\rb |בְּעַ֥ד\rb* \rb Hannah’s womb|רַחְמָֽהּ׃\rb*, \rb her rival|צָֽרָתָהּ֙\rb*\rb |גַּם־\rb*\rb |בַּעֲב֖וּר\rb* \rb would provoke her|הַרְּעִמָ֑הּ\rb* \rb viciously|כַּ֔עַס\rb* \rb to taunt her|וְכִֽעֲסַ֤תָּה\rb*. \v 7 \rb And this went on|וְכֵ֨ן\rb*\rb |יַעֲשֶׂ֜ה\rb* \rb year|שָׁנָ֣ה\rb* \rb after year|בְשָׁנָ֗ה\rb*. \rb Whenever|מִדֵּ֤י\rb* \rb Hannah went up|עֲלֹתָהּ֙\rb* \rb to the house|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |כֵּ֖ן\rb*, \rb her rival taunted her|תַּכְעִסֶ֑נָּה\rb* \rb until she wept|וַתִּבְכֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb and would not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb eat|תֹאכַֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 “\rb Hannah|חַנָּה֙\rb*, \rb why|לָ֣מֶה\rb* \rb are you crying|תִבְכִּ֗י\rb*?” \rb her husband|אִישָׁ֗הּ\rb* \rb Elkanah|אֶלְקָנָ֣ה\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*. “\rb Why|וְלָ֙מֶה֙\rb* \rb won’t you|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb eat|תֹֽאכְלִ֔י\rb*? \rb Why|וְלָ֖מֶה\rb* \rb is your heart|לְבָבֵ֑ךְ\rb* \rb so grieved|יֵרַ֣ע\rb*? \rb Am I|אָֽנֹכִי֙\rb* \rb not|הֲל֤וֹא\rb* \rb better|ט֣וֹב\rb* \rb to you|לָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb than ten|מֵעֲשָׂרָ֖ה\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִֽים׃\rb*?”
\s1 Hannah Prays for a Son
\p \v 9 \rb So after|אַחֲרֵ֛י\rb* \rb they had finished eating|אָכְלָ֥ה\rb* \rb and drinking|שָׁתֹ֑ה\rb* \rb in Shiloh|בְשִׁלֹ֖ה\rb*, \rb Hannah|חַנָּ֔ה\rb* \rb stood up|וַתָּ֣קָם\rb*\rb |וְאַחֲרֵ֣י\rb*. \rb Now Eli|וְעֵלִ֣י\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֗ן\rb* \rb was sitting|יֹשֵׁב֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb a chair|הַכִּסֵּ֔א\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb the doorpost|מְזוּזַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the temple|הֵיכַ֥ל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb |וְהִ֖יא\rb* \rb In her bitter distress|מָ֣רַת\rb*\rb |נָ֑פֶשׁ\rb*, \rb Hannah prayed|וַתִּתְפַּלֵּ֥ל\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb and wept with many tears|וּבָכֹ֥ה\rb*\rb |תִבְכֶּֽה׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb And she made|וַתִּדֹּ֨ר\rb* \rb a vow|נֶ֜דֶר\rb*, \rb saying|וַתֹּאמַ֗ר\rb*, “\rb O LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֜וֹת\rb*, \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb only You will look|רָאֹ֥ה\rb*\rb |תִרְאֶ֣ה׀\rb* \rb upon the affliction|בָּעֳנִ֣י\rb* \rb of Your maidservant|אֲמָתֶ֗ךָ\rb* \rb and remember me|וּזְכַרְתַּ֙נִי֙\rb*, \rb not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb forgetting Your maidservant|תִשְׁכַּ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb but giving|וְנָתַתָּ֥ה\rb*\rb |לַאֲמָתְךָ֖\rb* \rb her|אֲמָתֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb a son|זֶ֣רַע\rb*\rb |אֲנָשִׁ֑ים\rb*, \rb then I will dedicate him|וּנְתַתִּ֤יו\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of his life|חַיָּ֔יו\rb*, \rb and no|לֹא־\rb* \rb razor|וּמוֹרָ֖ה\rb* \rb shall ever touch|יַעֲלֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb his head|רֹאשֽׁוֹ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 12 \rb |וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb As|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb Hannah kept on|הִרְבְּתָ֔ה\rb* \rb praying|לְהִתְפַּלֵּ֖ל\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb Eli|וְעֵלִ֖י\rb* \rb watched|שֹׁמֵ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb her mouth|פִּֽיהָ׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb Hannah|וְחַנָּ֗ה\rb*\rb |הִ֚יא\rb* \rb was praying|מְדַבֶּ֣רֶת\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb her heart|לִבָּ֔הּ\rb*, \rb and though|רַ֚ק\rb* \rb her lips|שְׂפָתֶ֣יהָ\rb* \rb were moving|נָּע֔וֹת\rb*, \rb her voice|וְקוֹלָ֖הּ\rb* \rb could not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb be heard|יִשָּׁמֵ֑עַ\rb*.
\p \rb So Eli|עֵלִ֖י\rb* \rb thought|וַיַּחְשְׁבֶ֥הָ\rb* \rb she was drunk|לְשִׁכֹּרָֽה׃\rb* \v 14 \rb and said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to her|אֵלֶ֙יהָ֙\rb*\rb |עֵלִ֔י\rb*, “\rb How|עַד־\rb* \rb long|מָתַ֖י\rb* \rb will you be drunk|תִּשְׁתַּכָּרִ֑ין\rb*? \rb Put away|הָסִ֥ירִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your wine|יֵינֵ֖ךְ\rb*\rb |מֵעָלָֽיִךְ׃\rb*!”
\p \v 15 “\rb No|לֹ֣א\rb*, \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֔י\rb*,” \rb Hannah|חַנָּ֤ה\rb*\rb |וַתֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb replied|וַתַּ֨עַן\rb*. “\rb I|אָנֹ֔כִי\rb* \rb am a woman|אִשָּׁ֤ה\rb* \rb troubled|קְשַׁת־\rb* \rb in spirit|ר֙וּחַ֙\rb*. \rb I have not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb had|שָׁתִ֑יתִי\rb* \rb any wine|וְיַ֥יִן\rb* \rb or strong drink|וְשֵׁכָ֖ר\rb*, \rb but I have poured out|וָאֶשְׁפֹּ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my soul|נַפְשִׁ֖י\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb take|תִּתֵּן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb your servant|אֲמָ֣תְךָ֔\rb* \rb for a wicked|בְּלִיָּ֑עַל\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb woman|בַּת־\rb*, \rb for all this time|עַד־\rb*\rb |הֵֽנָּה׃\rb* \rb I have been praying|דִּבַּ֥רְתִּי\rb* \rb out of the depth|מֵרֹ֥ב\rb* \rb of my anguish|שִׂיחִ֛י\rb* \rb and grief|וְכַעְסִ֖י\rb*.”
\p \v 17 “\rb Go|לְכִ֣י\rb* \rb in peace|לְשָׁל֑וֹם\rb*,” \rb Eli|עֵלִ֛י\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb replied|וַיַּ֧עַן\rb*, “\rb and may the God|וֵאלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb grant|יִתֵּן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the petition|שֵׁ֣לָתֵ֔ךְ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you have asked|שָׁאַ֖לְתְּ\rb* \rb of Him|מֵעִמּֽוֹ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 18 “\rb May your maidservant|שִׁפְחָתְךָ֛\rb* \rb find|תִּמְצָ֧א\rb* \rb favor|חֵ֖ן\rb* \rb with you|בְּעֵינֶ֑יךָ\rb*,” \rb said Hannah|וַתֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*. \rb Then she|הָאִשָּׁ֤ה\rb* \rb went|וַתֵּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb on her way|לְדַרְכָּהּ֙\rb*, \rb and she began to eat|וַתֹּאכַ֔ל\rb*, \rb and her face|וּפָנֶ֥יהָ\rb* \rb was no|לֹא־\rb* \rb longer|עֽוֹד׃\rb* \rb downcast|הָיוּ־\rb*.
\s1 The Birth of Samuel
\p \v 19 \rb The next morning|בַבֹּ֗קֶר\rb* \rb they got up early|וַיַּשְׁכִּ֣מוּ\rb* \rb to bow in worship|וַיִּֽשְׁתַּחֲווּ֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and then they returned|וַיָּשֻׁ֛בוּ\rb*\rb |וַיָּבֹ֥אוּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb home|בֵּיתָ֖ם\rb* \rb to Ramah|הָרָמָ֑תָה\rb*.
\p \rb And Elkanah|אֶלְקָנָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had relations with|וַיֵּ֤דַע\rb* \rb his wife|אִשְׁתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb Hannah|חַנָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb and the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb remembered her|וַיִּֽזְכְּרֶ֖הָ\rb*. \v 20 \rb So|וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb in the course|לִתְקֻפ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of time|הַיָּמִ֔ים\rb*, \rb Hannah|חַנָּ֖ה\rb* \rb conceived|וַתַּ֥הַר\rb* \rb and gave birth to|וַתֵּ֣לֶד\rb* \rb a son|בֵּ֑ן\rb*. \rb She named|וַתִּקְרָ֤א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|שְׁמוֹ֙\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֔ל\rb*,\f + \fr 1:20 \fqa Samuel \ft sounds like the Hebrew for \fqa heard of God\ft .\f*\rb saying, “Because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I have asked for him|שְׁאִלְתִּֽיו׃\rb* \rb from the LORD|מֵיְהוָ֖ה\rb*.”
\p \v 21 \rb Then Elkanah|אֶלְקָנָ֖ה\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his house|בֵּית֑וֹ\rb* \rb went up|וַיַּ֛עַל\rb*\rb |הָאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb to make|לִזְבֹּ֧חַ\rb* \rb the annual|הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb sacrifice|זֶ֥בַח\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb and to fulfill|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb his vow|נִדְרֽוֹ׃\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \v 22 \rb but Hannah|וְחַנָּ֖ה\rb* \rb did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb go|עָלָ֑תָה\rb*.\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* “\rb After|עַ֣ד\rb* \rb the boy|הַנַּ֙עַר֙\rb* \rb is weaned|יִגָּמֵ֤ל\rb*,” \rb she said|אָמְרָ֣ה\rb* \rb to her husband|לְאִישָׁ֗הּ\rb*, “\rb I will take him|וַהֲבִאֹתִ֗יו\rb* \rb to appear|וְנִרְאָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb before|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and to stay|וְיָ֥שַׁב\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb permanently|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָֽם׃\rb*.”\f + \fr 1:22 \ft MT; DSS include \fqa I will offer him as a Nazirite for all time.\f*
\p \v 23 “\rb Do|עֲשִׂ֧י\rb* \rb what you think|בְּעֵינַ֗יִךְ\rb* \rb is best|הַטּ֣וֹב\rb*,” \rb her husband|אִישָׁ֜הּ\rb* \rb Elkanah|אֶלְקָנָ֨ה\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb and stay|שְׁבִי֙\rb* \rb here until|עַד־\rb* \rb you have weaned him|גָּמְלֵ֣ךְ\rb*.\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb Only|אַ֛ךְ\rb* \rb may the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb confirm|יָקֵ֥ם\rb* \rb His word|דְּבָר֑וֹ\rb*.”\f + \fr 1:23 \ft MT; DSS, LXX, and Syriac \fqa your word\f*
\p \rb So Hannah|הָֽאִשָּׁה֙\rb* \rb stayed|וַתֵּ֤שֶׁב\rb* \rb and nursed|וַתֵּ֣ינֶק\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb her son|בְּנָ֔הּ\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb she had weaned|גָּמְלָ֖הּ\rb* \rb him|אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb Once|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb she had weaned him|גְּמָלַ֗תּוּ\rb*, \rb Hannah took the boy|וַתַּעֲלֵ֨הוּ\rb* \rb with her|עִמָּ֜הּ\rb*, \rb along with a three-year-old|שְׁלֹשָׁה֙\rb* \rb bull|בְּפָרִ֤ים\rb*,\f + \fr 1:24 \ft DSS, LXX, and Syriac; MT \fqa three bulls\f* \rb an ephah|וְאֵיפָ֨ה\rb*\rb |אַחַ֥ת\rb* \rb of flour|קֶ֙מַח֙\rb*,\f + \fr 1:24 \fqa An ephah \ft is approximately 20 dry quarts or 22 liters (probably about 25.5 pounds or 11.6 kilograms of flour).\f* \rb and a skin|וְנֵ֣בֶל\rb* \rb of wine|יַ֔יִן\rb*. \rb Though the boy|וְהַנַּ֖עַר\rb* \rb was still young|נָֽעַר׃\rb*, \rb she brought him|וַתְּבִאֵ֥הוּ\rb* \rb to the house|בֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb at Shiloh|שִׁל֑וֹ\rb*. \v 25 \rb And when they had slaughtered|וַֽיִּשְׁחֲט֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the bull|הַפָּ֑ר\rb*, \rb they brought|וַיָּבִ֥יאוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the boy|הַנַּ֖עַר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Eli|עֵלִֽי׃\rb*.
\p \v 26 “\rb Please|בִּ֣י\rb*, \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֔י\rb*,” \rb said Hannah|וַתֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb as surely as you|נַפְשְׁךָ֖\rb* \rb live|חֵ֥י\rb*, \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֑י\rb*, \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the woman|הָאִשָּׁ֗ה\rb* \rb who stood|הַנִּצֶּ֤בֶת\rb* \rb here|בָּזֶ֔ה\rb* \rb beside|עִמְּכָה֙\rb* \rb you praying|לְהִתְפַּלֵּ֖ל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 27 \rb I prayed|הִתְפַּלָּ֑לְתִּי\rb* \rb for|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb boy|הַנַּ֥עַר\rb*, \rb and since the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb has granted|וַיִּתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb me|לִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |שְׁאֵ֣לָתִ֔י\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I asked|שָׁאַ֖לְתִּי\rb* \rb of Him|מֵעִמּֽוֹ׃\rb*, \v 28 \rb I|אָנֹכִ֗י\rb* \rb now|וְגַ֣ם\rb* \rb dedicate the boy|הִשְׁאִלְתִּ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb*. \rb For as|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִים֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb long as he lives|הָיָ֔ה\rb*, \rb he|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb is dedicated|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb*.”
\p \rb So they worshiped|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֥חוּ\rb*\f + \fr 1:28 \ft One DSS manuscript; MT \fqa he worshiped\f* \rb the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃פ\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb*.
\c 2
\s1 Hannah’s Prayer of Thanksgiving
\r (\ref Luke 1:46–56|LUK 1:46-56\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb At that time Hannah|חַנָּה֙\rb*\rb |וַתֹּאמַ֔ר\rb* \rb prayed|וַתִּתְפַּלֵּ֤ל\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb My heart|לִבִּי֙\rb* \rb rejoices|עָלַ֤ץ\rb* \rb in the LORD|בַּֽיהוָ֔ה\rb*;
\q2 \rb my horn|קַרְנִ֖י\rb*\f + \fr 2:1 \ft Or \fqa strength\ft ; also in verse 10\f* \rb is exalted|רָ֥מָה\rb* \rb in the LORD|בַּֽיהוָ֑ה\rb*.
\q1 \rb My mouth|פִּי֙\rb* \rb speaks boldly|רָ֤חַב\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb my enemies|א֣וֹיְבַ֔י\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I rejoice|שָׂמַ֖חְתִּי\rb* \rb in Your salvation|בִּישׁוּעָתֶֽךָ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 2 \rb There is no one|אֵין־\rb* \rb holy|קָד֥וֹשׁ\rb* \rb like the LORD|כַּיהוָ֖ה\rb*.
\q2 \rb Indeed|כִּ֣י\rb*, \rb there is no one|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb besides You|בִּלְתֶּ֑ךָ\rb*!
\q2 \rb And there is no|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb Rock|צ֖וּר\rb* \rb like our God|כֵּאלֹהֵֽינוּ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb boast|תַּרְבּ֤וּ\rb*\rb |תְדַבְּרוּ֙\rb* \rb so proudly|גְּבֹהָ֣ה\rb*\rb |גְבֹהָ֔ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb or let arrogance|עָתָ֖ק\rb* \rb come|יֵצֵ֥א\rb* \rb from your mouth|מִפִּיכֶ֑ם\rb*,
\q1 \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb is a God|אֵ֤ל\rb* \rb who knows|דֵּעוֹת֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb and by Him|וְלֹא\rb* \rb actions|עֲלִלֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb are weighed|נִתְכְּנ֖וּ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb The bows|קֶ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb of the mighty|גִּבֹּרִ֖ים\rb* \rb are broken|חַתִּ֑ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb but the feeble|וְנִכְשָׁלִ֖ים\rb* \rb are equipped|אָ֥זְרוּ\rb* \rb with strength|חָֽיִל׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb The well-fed|שְׂבֵעִ֤ים\rb* \rb hire themselves out|נִשְׂכָּ֔רוּ\rb* \rb for food|בַּלֶּ֙חֶם֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb but the starving|וּרְעֵבִ֖ים\rb* \rb hunger no more|חָדֵ֑לּוּ\rb*.\rb |עַד־\rb*
\q1 \rb The barren woman|עֲקָרָה֙\rb* \rb gives birth to|יָלְדָ֣ה\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעָ֔ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb but she who has many|וְרַבַּ֥ת\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb pines away|אֻמְלָֽלָה׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 6 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb brings death|מֵמִ֣ית\rb* \rb and gives life|וּמְחַיֶּ֑ה\rb*;
\q2 \rb He brings|מוֹרִ֥יד\rb* \rb down to Sheol|שְׁא֖וֹל\rb* \rb and raises up|וַיָּֽעַל׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb sends poverty|מוֹרִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb and wealth|וּמַעֲשִׁ֑יר\rb*;
\q2 \rb He humbles|מַשְׁפִּ֖יל\rb* \rb and|אַף־\rb* \rb He exalts|מְרוֹמֵֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb He raises|מֵקִ֨ים\rb* \rb the poor|דָּ֗ל\rb* \rb from the dust|מֵעָפָ֜ר\rb*
\q2 \rb and lifts|יָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb the needy|אֶבְי֔וֹן\rb* \rb from the ash heap|מֵֽאַשְׁפֹּת֙\rb*.
\q1 \rb He seats them|לְהוֹשִׁיב֙\rb* \rb among|עִם־\rb* \rb princes|נְדִיבִ֔ים\rb*
\q2 \rb and bestows on them|יַנְחִלֵ֑ם\rb* \rb a throne|וְכִסֵּ֥א\rb* \rb of honor|כָב֖וֹד\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the foundations|מְצֻ֣קֵי\rb* \rb of the earth|אֶ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb are the LORD’s|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb and upon them|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb He has set|וַיָּ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb the world|תֵּבֵֽל׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb He guards|יִשְׁמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb the steps|רַגְלֵ֤י\rb* \rb of His faithful ones|חֲסִידוֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb but the wicked|וּרְשָׁעִ֖ים\rb* \rb perish|יִדָּ֑מּוּ\rb* \rb in darkness|בַּחֹ֣שֶׁךְ\rb*;
\q2 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb by his own strength|בְכֹ֖חַ\rb* \rb shall no|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb man|אִֽישׁ׃\rb* \rb prevail|יִגְבַּר־\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 10 \rb Those who oppose|מְרִיבוֹ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֞ה\rb* \rb will be shattered|יֵחַ֣תּוּ\rb*.
\q2 \rb He will thunder|יַרְעֵ֔ם\rb* \rb from heaven|בַּשָּׁמַ֣יִם\rb* \rb against them|עָלוֹ\rb*.
\q1 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb will judge|יָדִ֣ין\rb* \rb the ends|אַפְסֵי־\rb* \rb of the earth|אָ֑רֶץ\rb*
\q2 \rb and will give|וְיִתֶּן־\rb* \rb power|עֹ֣ז\rb* \rb to His king|לְמַלְכּ֔וֹ\rb*.
\q2 \rb He will exalt|וְיָרֵ֖ם\rb* \rb the horn|קֶ֥רֶן\rb* \rb of His anointed|מְשִׁיחֽוֹ׃פ\rb*.”
\p \v 11 \rb Then Elkanah|אֶלְקָנָ֛ה\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֧לֶךְ\rb* \rb home|בֵּית֑וֹ\rb* \rb to Ramah|הָרָמָ֖תָה\rb*,\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb but the boy|וְהַנַּ֗עַר\rb*\rb |הָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb began ministering|מְשָׁרֵת֙\rb* \rb to|אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb before|פְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb Eli|עֵלִ֥י\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵֽן׃\rb*.
\s1 Eli’s Wicked Sons
\p \v 12 \rb Now the sons|וּבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Eli|עֵלִ֖י\rb* \rb were wicked|בְלִיָּ֑עַל\rb* \rb men|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*; \rb they had no|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb regard|יָדְע֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb for the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 13 \rb or for the custom|וּמִשְׁפַּ֥ט\rb* \rb of the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb*.
\p \rb When any|כָּל־\rb* \rb man|אִ֞ישׁ\rb* \rb offered|זֹבֵ֣חַ\rb* \rb a sacrifice|זֶ֗בַח\rb*, \rb the servant|נַ֤עַר\rb* \rb of the priest|הַכֹּהֵן֙\rb* \rb would come|וּבָ֨א\rb* \rb with a three-pronged|שְׁלֹ֥שׁ־\rb*\rb |הַשִּׁנַּ֖יִם\rb*\rb |בְּיָדֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb meat fork|וְהַמַּזְלֵ֛ג\rb* \rb while the meat|הַבָּשָׂ֔ר\rb* \rb was boiling|כְּבַשֵּׁ֣ל\rb* \v 14 \rb and plunge it|וְהִכָּ֨ה\rb* \rb into the pan|בַכִּיּ֜וֹר\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb kettle|בַדּ֗וּד\rb* \rb or|א֤וֹ\rb* \rb cauldron|בַקַּלַּ֙חַת֙\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb cooking pot|בַפָּר֔וּר\rb*. \rb And the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb would claim|יִקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb for himself|בּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb whatever|כֹּ֚ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the meat fork|הַמַּזְלֵ֔ג\rb* \rb brought up|יַעֲלֶ֣ה\rb*. \rb This is how|כָּ֚כָה\rb* \rb they treated|יַעֲשׂ֣וּ\rb* \rb all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb who came|הַבָּאִ֥ים\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb to Shiloh|בְּשִׁלֹֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Even|גַּם֮\rb* \rb before|בְּטֶרֶם֮\rb* \rb the fat|הַחֵלֶב֒\rb* \rb was burned|יַקְטִר֣וּן\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the servant|נַ֣עַר\rb* \rb of the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֗ן\rb* \rb would come|וּבָ֣א׀\rb* \rb and say|וְאָמַר֙\rb* \rb to the man|לָאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb who was sacrificing|הַזֹּבֵ֔חַ\rb*, “\rb Give|תְּנָ֣ה\rb* \rb the priest|לַכֹּהֵ֑ן\rb* \rb some meat|בָשָׂ֔ר\rb* \rb to roast|לִצְל֖וֹת\rb*, \rb because he will not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb accept|יִקַּ֧ח\rb* \rb boiled|מְבֻשָּׁ֖ל\rb* \rb meat|בָּשָׂ֥ר\rb* \rb from|מִמְּךָ֛\rb* \rb you|כִּ֥י\rb*, \rb but only|אִם־\rb* \rb raw|חָֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 16 \rb And if any man|הָאִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֜יו\rb*, “\rb The fat|הַחֵ֔לֶב\rb* \rb must be burned|קַטֵּ֨ר\rb*\rb |יַקְטִיר֤וּן\rb* \rb first|כַּיּוֹם֙\rb*; \rb then you may take|וְקַ֨ח־\rb*\rb |לְךָ֔\rb* \rb whatever|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you|נַפְשֶׁ֑ךָ\rb* \rb want|תְּאַוֶּ֖ה\rb*,” \rb the servant would reply|וְאָמַ֥ר׀\rb*, “\rb No|לֹ֖א\rb*,\rb |כִּ֚י\rb* \rb you must give it to me|תִתֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb right now|עַתָּ֣ה\rb*. \rb If you refuse|וְאִם־\rb*, \rb I will take it|לָקַ֥חְתִּי\rb* \rb by force|בְחָזְקָֽה׃\rb*!”
\p \v 17 \rb Thus the sin|חַטַּ֧את\rb* \rb of these young men|הַנְּעָרִ֛ים\rb* \rb was|וַתְּהִ֨י\rb* \rb severe|גְּדוֹלָ֥ה\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֖ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in the sight|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb they|הָֽאֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb*\f + \fr 2:17 \ft DSS and LXX; MT \fqa men\f* \rb were treating the LORD’s|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb offering|מִנְחַ֥ת\rb* \rb with contempt|נִֽאֲצוּ֙\rb*.\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb Now Samuel|וּשְׁמוּאֵ֕ל\rb* \rb was ministering|מְשָׁרֵ֖ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb before|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* — \rb a boy|נַ֕עַר\rb* \rb wearing|חָג֖וּר\rb* \rb a linen|בָּֽד׃\rb* \rb ephod|אֵפ֥וֹד\rb*. \v 19 \rb Each year|מִיָּמִ֣ים׀\rb*\rb |יָמִ֑ימָה\rb* \rb his mother|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb would make|תַּעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb him|לּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb a little|קָטֹן֙\rb* \rb robe|וּמְעִ֤יל\rb* \rb and bring it|וְהַעַלְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb to him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb when she went|בַּֽעֲלוֹתָהּ֙\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb her husband|אִישָׁ֔הּ\rb* \rb to offer|לִזְבֹּ֖חַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the annual|הַיָּמִֽים׃\rb* \rb sacrifice|זֶ֥בַח\rb*. \v 20 \rb And Eli|עֵלִ֜י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb would bless|וּבֵרַ֨ךְ\rb* \rb Elkanah|אֶלְקָנָ֣ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his wife|אִשְׁתּ֗וֹ\rb*, \rb saying|וְאָמַר֙\rb*, “\rb May the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb give|יָשֵׂם֩\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֥\rb* \rb children|זֶ֙רַע֙\rb* \rb by|מִן־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb woman|הָאִשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb in place of|תַּ֚חַת\rb* \rb the one|הַשְּׁאֵלָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb she dedicated to|שָׁאַ֖ל\rb* \rb the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb*.\f + \fr 2:20 \ft DSS; MT \fqa in place of the one requested from the LORD\f*” \rb Then they would go|וְהָלְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb home|לִמְקֹמֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb So|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb attended to|פָקַ֤ד\rb* \rb Hannah|חַנָּ֔ה\rb*, \rb and she conceived|וַתַּ֛הַר\rb* \rb and gave birth to|וַתֵּ֥לֶד\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹשָֽׁה־\rb* \rb sons|בָנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and two|וּשְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb daughters|בָנ֑וֹת\rb*.
\p \rb Meanwhile, the boy|הַנַּ֥עַר\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb grew up|וַיִּגְדַּ֛ל\rb* \rb in the presence of|עִם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb Now Eli|וְעֵלִ֖י\rb* \rb was very|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb old|זָקֵ֣ן\rb*, \rb and he heard|וְשָׁמַ֗ע\rb*\rb |אֵת֩\rb* \rb about everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb his sons|בָּנָיו֙\rb* \rb were doing|יַעֲשׂ֤וּן\rb* \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and|וְאֵ֤ת\rb* \rb how|אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb they were sleeping|יִשְׁכְּבוּן֙\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb the women|הַנָּשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb who served|הַצֹּ֣בְא֔וֹת\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb to the Tent|אֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵֽד׃\rb*.
\p \v 23 “\rb Why|לָ֥מָּה\rb* \rb are you doing|תַעֲשׂ֖וּן\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb things|כַּדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb*?” \rb Eli said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to his sons|לָהֶ֔ם\rb*. “\rb I|אָנֹכִ֤י\rb* \rb hear|שֹׁמֵ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb about|אֶת־\rb* \rb your wicked|רָעִ֔ים\rb* \rb deeds|דִּבְרֵיכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb from|מֵאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|אֵֽלֶּה׃\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֥ם\rb*. \v 24 \rb No|אַ֖ל\rb*, \rb my sons|בָּנָ֑י\rb*;\rb |כִּ֠י\rb* \rb it is not|לֽוֹא־\rb* \rb a good|טוֹבָ֤ה\rb* \rb report|הַשְּׁמֻעָה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֣י\rb* \rb hear|שֹׁמֵ֔עַ\rb* \rb circulating among|מַעֲבִרִ֖ים\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb people|עַם־\rb*. \v 25 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb sins|יֶחֱטָ֨א\rb* \rb against another man|לְאִישׁ֙\rb*, \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*\f + \fr 2:25 \ft Or \fqa the judges\f* \rb can intercede for him|וּפִֽלְל֣וֹ\rb*; \rb but if|וְאִ֤ם\rb* \rb a man|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb sins|יֶֽחֱטָא־\rb* \rb against the LORD|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb*, \rb who|מִ֖י\rb* \rb can intercede|יִתְפַּלֶּל־\rb* \rb for him|ל֑וֹ\rb*?”
\p \rb But they would not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb listen|יִשְׁמְעוּ֙\rb*\rb |לְק֣וֹל\rb* \rb to their father|אֲבִיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb since|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb intended|חָפֵ֥ץ\rb* \rb to put them to death|לַהֲמִיתָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb And the boy|וְהַנַּ֣עַר\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb continued to grow|הֹלֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb in stature|וְגָדֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and in favor|וָט֑וֹב\rb*\rb |גַּ֚ם\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְגַ֖ם\rb* \rb and with|עִם־\rb* \rb man|אֲנָשִֽׁים׃ס\rb*.
\s1 A Prophecy against the House of Eli
\p \v 27 \rb Then a man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Eli|עֵלִ֑י\rb* \rb and told|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb him|אֵלָ֗יו\rb*, “\rb This is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*: ‘\rb Did I not clearly reveal Myself|הֲנִגְלֹ֤ה\rb*\rb |נִגְלֵ֙יתִי֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your father’s|אָבִ֔יךָ\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb when they were|בִּֽהְיוֹתָ֥ם\rb* \rb in Egypt|בְּמִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb under Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹֽה׃\rb* \rb house|לְבֵ֥ית\rb*? \v 28 \rb And out of all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb I selected|וּבָחֹ֣ר\rb* \rb your father|אֹ֠תוֹ\rb* \rb to be My|לִי֙\rb* \rb priest|לְכֹהֵ֔ן\rb*, \rb to offer sacrifices|לַעֲל֣וֹת\rb* \rb on|עַֽל־\rb* \rb My altar|מִזְבְּחִ֗י\rb*, \rb to burn|לְהַקְטִ֥יר\rb* \rb incense|קְטֹ֛רֶת\rb*, \rb and to wear|לָשֵׂ֥את\rb* \rb an ephod|אֵפ֖וֹד\rb* \rb in My presence|לְפָנָ֑י\rb*. \rb I also gave|וָֽאֶתְּנָה֙\rb* \rb to the house|לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of your father|אָבִ֔יךָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the food offerings|אִשֵּׁ֖י\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb Why then|לָ֣מָּה\rb* \rb do you kick at|תִבְעֲט֗וּ\rb*\f + \fr 2:29 \ft Or \fqa scorn\f* \rb My sacrifice|בְּזִבְחִי֙\rb* \rb and offering|וּבְמִנְחָתִ֔י\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have prescribed|צִוִּ֖יתִי\rb* \rb for My dwelling place|מָע֑וֹן\rb*? \rb You have honored|וַתְּכַבֵּ֤ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your sons|בָּנֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb more than Me|מִמֶּ֔נִּי\rb* \rb by fattening yourselves|לְהַבְרִֽיאֲכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb with the best|מֵרֵאשִׁ֛ית\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the offerings|מִנְחַ֥ת\rb* \rb of My people|לְעַמִּֽי׃\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*.’
\p \v 30 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֗ן\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֮\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֒\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb*:
\b 
\q1 ‘\rb I did indeed|אָמ֣וֹר\rb* \rb say|אָמַ֔רְתִּי\rb* \rb that your house|בֵּֽיתְךָ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and the house|וּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of your father|אָבִ֔יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb would walk|יִתְהַלְּכ֥וּ\rb* \rb before Me|לְפָנַ֖י\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb forever|עוֹלָ֑ם\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \rb But now|וְעַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb*:
\q2 \rb Far be it|חָלִ֣ילָה\rb* \rb from Me|לִּ֔י\rb*!
\q1 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I will honor|אֲכַבֵּ֖ד\rb* \rb those who honor Me|מְכַבְּדַ֥י\rb*,
\q2 \rb but those who despise Me|וּבֹזַ֥י\rb* \rb will be disdained|יֵקָֽלּוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 31 \rb Behold|הִנֵּה֙\rb*, \rb the days|יָמִ֣ים\rb* \rb are coming|בָּאִ֔ים\rb* \rb when I will cut off|וְגָֽדַעְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your strength|זְרֹ֣עֲךָ֔\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the strength|זְרֹ֖עַ\rb* \rb of your father’s|אָבִ֑יךָ\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֣ית\rb*, \rb so that no one in it|בְּבֵיתֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb will reach|מִֽהְי֥וֹת\rb* \rb old age|זָקֵ֖ן\rb*. \v 32 \rb You will see|וְהִבַּטְתָּ֙\rb* \rb distress|צַ֣ר\rb* \rb in My dwelling place|מָע֔וֹן\rb*. \rb Despite all|בְּכֹ֥ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb is good|יֵיטִ֖יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb no one|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb in your house|בְּבֵיתְךָ֖\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb will ever again|הַיָּמִֽים׃\rb* \rb reach|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb old age|זָקֵ֛ן\rb*. \v 33 \rb And every one|וְאִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb of you|לְךָ֙\rb* \rb that I do not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb cut off|אַכְרִ֤ית\rb* \rb from|מֵעִ֣ם\rb* \rb My altar|מִזְבְּחִ֔י\rb*, \rb I will cause your eyes|עֵינֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb to fail|לְכַלּ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and your heart|נַפְשֶׁ֑ךָ\rb* \rb to grieve|וְלַאֲדִ֣יב\rb*.\f + \fr 2:33 \ft Hebrew; LXX \fqa his eyes will fail and his heart will grieve\f* \rb All|וְכָל־\rb* \rb your descendants|מַרְבִּ֥ית\rb*\f + \fr 2:33 \ft Or \fqa increase \f*\rb |בֵּיתְךָ֖\rb* \rb will die by the sword|יָמ֥וּתוּ\rb* \rb of men|אֲנָשִֽׁים׃\rb*.\f + \fr 2:33 \ft DSS and LXX; MT \fqa will die as mortals \ft or \fqa will die in the prime of life\f*
\p \v 34 \rb And this|וְזֶה־\rb* \rb sign|הָא֗וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb shall come|יָבֹא֙\rb* \rb to you|לְּךָ֣\rb* \rb concerning|אֶל־\rb* \rb your two|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb sons|בָנֶ֔יךָ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Hophni|חָפְנִ֖י\rb* \rb and Phinehas|וּפִֽינְחָ֑ס\rb*: \rb They will both|שְׁנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb die|יָמ֥וּתוּ\rb* \rb on the same|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb day|בְּי֥וֹם\rb*.
\p \v 35 \rb Then I will raise up|וַהֲקִימֹתִ֥י\rb* \rb for Myself|לִי֙\rb* \rb a faithful|נֶאֱמָ֔ן\rb* \rb priest|כֹּהֵ֣ן\rb*. \rb He will do|יַעֲשֶׂ֑ה\rb* \rb whatever|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb is in My heart|בִּלְבָבִ֥י\rb* \rb and mind|וּבְנַפְשִׁ֖י\rb*. \rb And I will build|וּבָנִ֤יתִי\rb* \rb for him|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb an enduring|נֶאֱמָ֔ן\rb* \rb house|בַּ֣יִת\rb*, \rb and he will walk|וְהִתְהַלֵּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb My anointed one|מְשִׁיחִ֖י\rb* \rb for all time|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 36 \rb And|וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb everyone|כָּל־\rb* \rb left|הַנּוֹתָר֙\rb* \rb in your house|בְּבֵ֣יתְךָ֔\rb* \rb will come|יָבוֹא֙\rb* \rb and bow down|לְהִשְׁתַּחֲוֺ֣ת\rb* \rb to him|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb for a piece|לַאֲג֥וֹרַת\rb* \rb of silver|כֶּ֖סֶף\rb* \rb or a morsel|וְכִכַּר־\rb* \rb of bread|לָ֑חֶם\rb*, \rb pleading|וְאָמַ֗ר\rb*, “\rb Please|נָ֛א\rb* \rb appoint me|סְפָחֵ֥נִי\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb some|אַחַ֥ת\rb* \rb priestly office|הַכְּהֻנּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb so that I can eat|לֶאֱכֹ֥ל\rb* \rb a piece|פַּת־\rb* \rb of bread|לָֽחֶם׃ס\rb*.”’”
\c 3
\s1 The LORD Calls Samuel
\p \v 1 \rb And the boy|וְהַנַּ֧עַר\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb ministered|מְשָׁרֵ֥ת\rb* \rb to|אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Eli|עֵלִ֑י\rb*.
\p \rb Now in those|הָהֵ֔ם\rb* \rb days|בַּיָּמִ֣ים\rb* \rb the word|וּדְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb rare|יָקָר֙\rb*, \rb and visions|חָז֖וֹן\rb* \rb were|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb scarce|נִפְרָֽץ׃ס\rb*. \v 2 \rb And|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb at that time|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*\rb |הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb Eli|וְעֵלִ֖י\rb*, \rb whose eyesight|וְעֵינוֹ\rb*\rb |הֵחֵ֣לּוּ\rb* \rb had grown so dim|כֵה֔וֹת\rb* \rb that he could|יוּכַ֖ל\rb* \rb not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb see|לִרְאֽוֹת׃\rb*, \rb was lying|שֹׁכֵ֣ב\rb* \rb in his room|בִּמְקֹמ֑וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Before|טֶ֣רֶם\rb* \rb the lamp|וְנֵ֤ר\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb had gone out|יִכְבֶּ֔ה\rb*, \rb Samuel|וּשְׁמוּאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb was lying down|שֹׁכֵ֑ב\rb* \rb in the temple|בְּהֵיכַ֣ל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִֽים׃פ\rb* \rb was located|שָׁ֖ם\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb called|וַיִּקְרָ֧א\rb* \rb to Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb and he answered|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Here I am|הִנֵּֽנִי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb He ran|וַיָּ֣רָץ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Eli|עֵלִ֗י\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Here I am|הִנְנִי֙\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you have called|קָרָ֣אתָ\rb* \rb me|לִּ֔י\rb*.”
\p “\rb I did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb call|קָרָ֖אתִי\rb*,” \rb Eli replied|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*. “\rb Go back|שׁ֣וּב\rb* \rb and lie down|שְׁכָ֑ב\rb*.”
\p \rb So he went|וַיֵּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb and lay down|וַיִּשְׁכָּֽב׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Once again|וַיֹּ֣סֶף\rb*\rb |עוֹד֮\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb called|קְרֹ֣א\rb*, “\rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵל֒\rb*!”
\p \rb So Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵל֙\rb* \rb got up|וַיָּ֤קָם\rb*, \rb went|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Eli|עֵלִ֔י\rb*, \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Here I am|הִנְנִ֔י\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you have called|קָרָ֖אתָ\rb* \rb me|לִ֑י\rb*.”
\p “\rb My son|בְנִ֖י\rb*, \rb I did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb call|קָרָ֥אתִי\rb*,” \rb Eli replied|וַיֹּ֛אמֶר\rb*. “\rb Go back|שׁ֥וּב\rb* \rb and lie down|שְׁכָֽב׃\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb Now Samuel|וּשְׁמוּאֵ֕ל\rb* \rb did not yet|טֶ֖רֶם\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֣ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb because the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb had not yet|וְטֶ֛רֶם\rb* \rb been revealed|יִגָּלֶ֥ה\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֖יו\rb*. \v 8 \rb Once again|וַיֹּ֨סֶף\rb*, \rb for the third time|בַּשְּׁלִשִׁית֒\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb called|קְרֹא־\rb* \rb to Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵל֮\rb*. \rb He got up|וַיָּ֙קָם֙\rb*, \rb went|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Eli|עֵלִ֔י\rb*, \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Here I am|הִנְנִ֔י\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you have called|קָרָ֖אתָ\rb* \rb me|לִ֑י\rb*.”
\p \rb Then Eli|עֵלִ֔י\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb realized|וַיָּ֣בֶן\rb* \rb that it was the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb who was calling|קֹרֵ֥א\rb* \rb the boy|לַנָּֽעַר׃\rb*. \v 9 “\rb Go|לֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb and lie down|שְׁכָב֒\rb*,” \rb he|עֵלִ֣י\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to Samuel|לִשְׁמוּאֵל֮\rb*, “\rb and|וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb He calls you|יִקְרָ֣א\rb*,\rb |אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb say|וְאָֽמַרְתָּ֙\rb*, ‘\rb Speak|דַּבֵּ֣ר\rb*, \rb LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb Your servant|עַבְדֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb is listening|שֹׁמֵ֖עַ\rb*.’”
\p \rb So Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb and lay down|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֖ב\rb* \rb in his place|בִּמְקוֹמֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֤א\rb* \rb and stood there|וַיִּתְיַצַּ֔ב\rb*, \rb calling|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb* \rb as before|כְפַֽעַם־\rb*\rb |בְּפַ֖עַם\rb*, “\rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֣ל׀\rb*! \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֑ל\rb*!”
\p \rb And Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵל֙\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Speak|דַּבֵּ֔ר\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb Your servant|עַבְדֶּֽךָ׃פ\rb* \rb is listening|שֹׁמֵ֖עַ\rb*.”
\p \v 11 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֔ל\rb*,\rb |הִנֵּ֧ה\rb* “\rb I|אָנֹכִ֛י\rb* \rb am about to do|עֹשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb something|דָבָ֖ר\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb at which|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb*\rb |שְׁתֵּ֥י\rb* \rb the ears|אָזְנָֽיו׃\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who hear it|שֹׁ֣מְע֔וֹ\rb* \rb will tingle|תְּצִלֶּ֖ינָה\rb*. \v 12 \rb On that|הַהוּא֙\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֤וֹם\rb* \rb I will carry out|אָקִ֣ים\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb Eli|עֵלִ֔י\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have spoken|דִּבַּ֖רְתִּי\rb* \rb about|אֶל־\rb* \rb his house|בֵּית֑וֹ\rb*, \rb from beginning|הָחֵ֖ל\rb* \rb to end|וְכַלֵּֽה׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb I told|וְהִגַּ֣דְתִּי\rb* \rb him|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֛י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb would judge|שֹׁפֵ֥ט\rb* \rb his house|בֵּית֖וֹ\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb forever|עוֹלָ֑ם\rb* \rb for the iniquity|בַּעֲוֺ֣ן\rb* \rb of which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he knows|יָדַ֗ע\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb his sons|בָּנָ֔יו\rb* \rb blasphemed God|מְקַֽלְלִ֤ים\rb*\rb |לָהֶם֙\rb*\f + \fr 3:13 \ft LXX; Hebrew \fqa made themselves contemptible\f* \rb and he did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb restrain|כִהָ֖ה\rb* \rb them|בָּֽם׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb Therefore|וְלָכֵ֥ן\rb* \rb I have sworn|נִשְׁבַּ֖עְתִּי\rb* \rb to the house|לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of Eli|עֵלִ֑י\rb*, ‘\rb The iniquity|עֲוֺ֧ן\rb* \rb of Eli’s|עֵלִ֛י\rb* \rb house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb shall never|אִֽם־\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָֽם׃\rb* \rb be atoned for|יִתְכַּפֵּ֞ר\rb* \rb by sacrifice|בְּזֶ֥בַח\rb* \rb or offering|וּבְמִנְחָ֖ה\rb*.’”
\s1 Samuel Shares the Vision
\p \v 15 \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵל֙\rb* \rb lay down|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֤ב\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the morning|הַבֹּ֔קֶר\rb*; \rb then he opened|וַיִּפְתַּ֖ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the doors|דַּלְת֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb He|וּשְׁמוּאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb was afraid|יָרֵ֔א\rb* \rb to tell|מֵהַגִּ֥יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Eli|עֵלִֽי׃\rb* \rb the vision|הַמַּרְאָ֖ה\rb*,\rb |אֶל־\rb* \v 16 \rb but Eli|עֵלִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb called|וַיִּקְרָ֤א\rb* \rb to him|שְׁמוּאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֣ל\rb*, \rb my son|בְּנִ֑י\rb*.”
\p “\rb Here I am|הִנֵּֽנִי׃\rb*,” \rb answered Samuel|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*.
\p \v 17 “\rb What|מָ֤ה\rb* \rb was the message|הַדָּבָר֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He gave you|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb*?”\rb |אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb Eli asked|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*. “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb*\rb |נָ֥א\rb* \rb hide|תְכַחֵ֖ד\rb* \rb it from me|מִמֶּ֑נִּי\rb*. \rb May God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb punish|כֹּ֣ה\rb*\rb |יַעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb you|לְּךָ֤\rb*, \rb and ever so|וְכֹ֣ה\rb* \rb severely|יוֹסִ֔יף\rb*, \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you hide|תְּכַחֵ֤ד\rb* \rb from me|מִמֶּ֙נִּי֙\rb* \rb anything|דָּבָ֔ר\rb*\rb |מִכָּל־\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb He said|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 18 \rb So Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb told|וַיַּגֶּד־\rb* \rb him|ל֤וֹ\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַדְּבָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb and did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb hide|כִחֵ֖ד\rb* \rb a thing from him|מִמֶּ֑נּוּ\rb*.
\p “\rb He|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb is the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb*,” \rb replied Eli|וַיֹּאמַ֕ר\rb*. “\rb Let Him do|יַעֲשֶֽׂה׃פ\rb* \rb what is good|הַטּ֥וֹב\rb* \rb in His eyes|בְּעֵינָ֖ו\rb*.”
\p \v 19 \rb And Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb grew|וַיִּגְדַּ֖ל\rb*, \rb and the LORD|וַֽיהוָה֙\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and He let none|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb of|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb Samuel’s words|דְּבָרָ֖יו\rb* \rb fall|הִפִּ֥יל\rb* \rb to the ground|אָֽרְצָה׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb So all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb from Dan|מִדָּ֖ן\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb*\rb |בְּאֵ֣ר\rb* \rb Beersheba|שָׁ֑בַע\rb* \rb knew|וַיֵּ֙דַע֙\rb* \rb that|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb was confirmed|נֶאֱמָ֣ן\rb* \rb as a prophet|לְנָבִ֖יא\rb* \rb of the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb continued|וַיֹּ֥סֶף\rb* \rb to appear|לְהֵרָאֹ֣ה\rb* \rb at Shiloh|בְשִׁלֹ֑ה\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb there|בְּשִׁל֖וֹ\rb* \rb He|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb revealed Himself|נִגְלָ֨ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb by His|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb* \rb word|בִּדְבַ֥ר\rb*.
\c 4
\s1 The Philistines Capture the Ark
\p \v 1 \rb Thus the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*.
\p \rb Now the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵל֩\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּצֵ֣א\rb* \rb to meet|לִקְרַ֨את\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֜ים\rb* \rb in battle|לַמִּלְחָמָ֗ה\rb* \rb and camped|וַֽיַּחֲנוּ֙\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb*\rb |הָאֶ֣בֶן\rb* \rb Ebenezer|הָעֵ֔זֶר\rb*, \rb while the Philistines|וּפְלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb camped|חָנ֥וּ\rb* \rb at Aphek|בַאֲפֵֽק׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb The Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֜ים\rb* \rb arrayed themselves|וַיַּעַרְכ֨וּ\rb* \rb against|לִקְרַ֣את\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*, \rb and as the battle|הַמִּלְחָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb spread|וַתִּטֹּשׁ֙\rb*, \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb was defeated|וַיִּנָּ֥גֶף\rb* \rb by|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb*, \rb who struck down|וַיַּכּ֤וּ\rb* \rb about four|כְּאַרְבַּ֥עַת\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִ֖ים\rb* \rb men|אִֽישׁ׃\rb* \rb on the battlefield|בַמַּֽעֲרָכָה֙\rb*\rb |בַּשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb When the troops|הָעָם֮\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶה֒\rb*, \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּֽאמְרוּ֙\rb*, “\rb Why|לָ֣מָּה\rb* \rb has the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb brought defeat on us|נְגָפָ֧נוּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֖וֹם\rb*? \rb Let us bring|נִקְחָ֧ה\rb*\rb |אֵלֵ֣ינוּ\rb* \rb the ark|אֲרוֹן֙\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb from Shiloh|מִשִּׁלֹ֗ה\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb so that it may go|וְיָבֹ֣א\rb*\f + \fr 4:3 \ft Or \fqa He may go\f* \rb with us|בְקִרְבֵּ֔נוּ\rb* \rb to save us|וְיֹשִׁעֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb from the hand|מִכַּ֥ף\rb* \rb of our enemies|אֹיְבֵֽינוּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb So the people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb men to Shiloh|שִׁלֹ֔ה\rb*, \rb and they brought|וַיִּשְׂא֣וּ\rb* \rb back|מִשָּׁ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֧וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb*, \rb who sits enthroned|יֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb between the cherubim|הַכְּרֻבִ֑ים\rb*. \rb And the two|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb sons|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Eli|עֵלִ֗י\rb*, \rb Hophni|חָפְנִ֖י\rb* \rb and Phinehas|וּפִֽינְחָֽס׃\rb*, \rb were there|וְשָׁ֞ם\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲרוֹן֙\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִ֣ית\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb When|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֤וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb entered|כְּב֨וֹא\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֔ה\rb*, \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb raised|גְדוֹלָ֑ה\rb* \rb such a great|תְּרוּעָ֣ה\rb* \rb shout|וַיָּרִ֥עוּ\rb* \rb that the ground|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb shook|וַתֵּהֹ֖ם\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb On hearing|וַיִּשְׁמְע֤וּ\rb* \rb the noise|ק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of the shout|הַתְּרוּעָ֔ה\rb*, \rb the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּים֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb*, “\rb What is|מֶ֠ה\rb*\rb |ק֣וֹל\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb loud|הַגְּדוֹלָ֛ה\rb* \rb shouting|הַתְּרוּעָ֧ה\rb* \rb in the camp|בְּמַחֲנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of the Hebrews|הָעִבְרִ֑ים\rb*?”
\p \rb And when they realized|וַיֵּ֣דְע֔וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb had entered|בָּ֖א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶֽה׃\rb*, \v 7 \rb the Philistines|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb were afraid|וַיִּֽרְאוּ֙\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י\rb*. “\rb The gods|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb have entered|בָּ֥א\rb*\f + \fr 4:7 \ft Or \fqa A god has entered\f*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb their camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֑ה\rb*!”\rb |וַיֹּאמְרוּ֙\rb* \rb they said|אָמְר֔וּ\rb*. “\rb Woe|א֣וֹי\rb* \rb to us|לָ֔נוּ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb nothing|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb like this|כָּזֹ֖את\rb* \rb has happened|הָיְתָ֛ה\rb* \rb before|אֶתְמ֥וֹל\rb*\rb |שִׁלְשֹֽׁם׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb Woe|א֣וֹי\rb* \rb to us|לָ֔נוּ\rb*! \rb Who|מִ֣י\rb* \rb will deliver us|יַצִּילֵ֔נוּ\rb* \rb from the hand|מִיַּ֛ד\rb* \rb of these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb mighty|הָאַדִּירִ֖ים\rb* \rb gods|הָאֱלֹהִ֥ים\rb*? \rb These|אֵ֧לֶּה\rb*\rb |הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb are the gods|הָאֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb who struck|הַמַּכִּ֧ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֛יִם\rb* \rb with all kinds|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb of plagues|מַכָּ֖ה\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּֽר׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb Take courage|הִֽתְחַזְּק֞וּ\rb* \rb and be|וִֽהְי֤וּ\rb* \rb men|לַֽאֲנָשִׁים֙\rb*, \rb O Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb*! \rb Otherwise|פֶּ֚ן\rb*, \rb you will serve|תַּעַבְד֣וּ\rb* \rb the Hebrews|לָעִבְרִ֔ים\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb they served|עָבְד֖וּ\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb Now be|וִהְיִיתֶ֥ם\rb* \rb men|לַאֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb and fight|וְנִלְחַמְתֶּֽם׃\rb*!”
\p \v 10 \rb So the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֗ים\rb* \rb fought|וַיִּלָּחֲמ֣וּ\rb*, \rb and Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb was defeated|וַיִּנָּ֤גֶף\rb*, \rb and each man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb fled|וַיָּנֻ֙סוּ֙\rb* \rb to his tent|לְאֹהָלָ֔יו\rb*. \rb The slaughter|הַמַּכָּ֖ה\rb* \rb was|וַתְּהִ֥י\rb* \rb very|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb great|גְּדוֹלָ֣ה\rb* — \rb thirty|שְׁלֹשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb thousand|אֶ֖לֶף\rb* \rb foot soldiers|רַגְלִֽי׃\rb* \rb of Israel|מִיִּשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb fell|וַיִּפֹּל֙\rb*. \v 11 \rb The ark|וַאֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb was captured|נִלְקָ֑ח\rb*, \rb and Eli’s|עֵלִי֙\rb* \rb two|וּשְׁנֵ֤י\rb* \rb sons|בְנֵֽי־\rb*, \rb Hophni|חָפְנִ֖י\rb* \rb and Phinehas|וּפִֽינְחָֽס׃\rb*, \rb died|מֵ֔תוּ\rb*.
\s1 The Death of Eli
\p \v 12 \rb That same|הַה֑וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb a Benjamite|בִּנְיָמִן֙\rb*\rb |אִישׁ־\rb* \rb ran|וַיָּ֤רָץ\rb* \rb from the battle line|מֵהַמַּ֣עֲרָכָ֔ה\rb* \rb all the way|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb to Shiloh|שִׁלֹ֖ה\rb*, \rb with his clothes|וּמַדָּ֣יו\rb* \rb torn|קְרֻעִ֔ים\rb* \rb and dirt|וַאֲדָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his head|רֹאשֽׁוֹ׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb When he arrived|וַיָּב֗וֹא\rb*, \rb there|וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb was Eli|עֵ֠לִי\rb*, \rb sitting|יֹשֵׁ֨ב\rb* \rb on|עַֽל־\rb* \rb his chair|הַכִּסֵּ֜א\rb* \rb beside|יַךְ\rb* \rb the road|דֶּ֙רֶךְ֙\rb* \rb and watching|מְצַפֶּ֔ה\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb his heart|לִבּוֹ֙\rb*\rb |הָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb trembled|חָרֵ֔ד\rb* \rb for|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*.
\p \rb When the man|וְהָאִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb entered|בָּ֚א\rb* \rb the city|בָּעִ֔יר\rb* \rb to give a report|לְהַגִּ֣יד\rb*, \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb city|הָעִֽיר׃\rb* \rb cried out|וַתִּזְעַ֖ק\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb Eli|עֵלִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֤ע\rb* \rb the outcry|ק֣וֹל\rb*\rb |הַצְּעָקָ֔ה\rb* \rb and asked|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Why|מֶ֛ה\rb*\rb |ק֥וֹל\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb commotion|הֶהָמ֖וֹן\rb*?”
\p \rb So the man|וְהָאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb hurried over|מִהַ֔ר\rb*\rb |וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb* \rb and reported|וַיַּגֵּ֥ד\rb* \rb to Eli|לְעֵלִֽי׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb Now Eli|וְעֵלִ֕י\rb* \rb was ninety-eight|תִּשְׁעִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁמֹנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and his gaze|וְעֵינָ֣יו\rb* \rb was fixed|קָ֔מָה\rb* \rb because he could not|וְלֹ֥א\rb*\rb |יָכ֖וֹל\rb* \rb see|לִרְאֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 “\rb I|אָֽנֹכִי֙\rb* \rb have just come|הַבָּ֣א\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the battle|הַמַּעֲרָכָ֔ה\rb*,” \rb the man|הָאִ֜ישׁ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Eli|עֵלִ֗י\rb*. “\rb I|וַאֲנִ֕י\rb* \rb fled|נַ֣סְתִּי\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb there today|הַמַּעֲרָכָ֖ה\rb*\rb |הַיּ֑וֹם\rb*.”
\p “\rb What|מֶֽה־\rb* \rb happened|הָיָ֥ה\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb*, \rb my son|בְּנִֽי׃\rb*?” \rb Eli asked|וַיֹּ֛אמֶר\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb The messenger|הַֽמְבַשֵּׂ֜ר\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּ֨עַן\rb*, “\rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb has fled|נָ֤ס\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb and|וְגַ֛ם\rb* \rb there has been|הָיְתָ֣ה\rb* \rb a great|גְדוֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb slaughter|מַגֵּפָ֥ה\rb* \rb among the people|בָעָ֑ם\rb*.\rb |וְגַם־\rb* \rb Your two|שְׁנֵ֨י\rb* \rb sons|בָנֶ֜יךָ\rb*, \rb Hophni|חָפְנִי֙\rb* \rb and Phinehas|וּפִ֣ינְחָ֔ס\rb*, \rb are both dead|מֵ֗תוּ\rb*, \rb and the ark|וַאֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb has been captured|נִלְקָֽחָה׃פ\rb*.”
\p \v 18 \rb As soon as|וַיְהִ֞י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb was mentioned|כְּהַזְכִּיר֣וֹ׀\rb*, \rb Eli fell|וַיִּפֹּ֣ל\rb* \rb backward|אֲחֹ֨רַנִּ֜ית\rb*\rb |בְּעַ֣ד׀\rb* \rb from|מֵֽעַל־\rb* \rb his chair|הַ֠כִּסֵּא\rb* \rb by|יַ֣ד\rb* \rb the city gate|הַשַּׁ֗עַר\rb*, \rb and being|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |הָאִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb old|זָקֵ֥ן\rb* \rb and heavy|וְכָבֵ֑ד\rb*, \rb he broke|וַתִּשָּׁבֵ֤ר\rb* \rb his neck|מַפְרַקְתּוֹ֙\rb* \rb and died|וַיָּמֹ֔ת\rb*. \rb And Eli|וְה֛וּא\rb* \rb had judged|שָׁפַ֥ט\rb*\f + \fr 4:18 \ft Or \fqa governed \ft or \fqa led\f*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb forty|אַרְבָּעִ֥ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb Now Eli’s daughter-in-law|וְכַלָּת֣וֹ\rb*, \rb the wife|אֵֽשֶׁת־\rb* \rb of Phinehas|פִּינְחָס֮\rb*, \rb was pregnant|הָרָ֣ה\rb* \rb and about to give birth|לָלַת֒\rb*. \rb When she heard|וַתִּשְׁמַ֣ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the news|הַשְּׁמֻעָ֔ה\rb* \rb of|אֶל־\rb* \rb the capture|הִלָּקַח֙\rb* \rb of God’s|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb and the deaths|וּמֵ֥ת\rb* \rb of her father-in-law|חָמִ֖יהָ\rb* \rb and her husband|וְאִישָׁ֑הּ\rb*, \rb she collapsed|וַתִּכְרַ֣ע\rb* \rb and gave birth|וַתֵּ֔לֶד\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb her labor pains|צִרֶֽיהָ׃\rb* \rb overtook|נֶהֶפְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb her|עָלֶ֖יהָ\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb As|וּכְעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb she was dying|מוּתָ֗הּ\rb*, \rb the women attending|הַנִּצָּב֣וֹת\rb* \rb to her|עָלֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb said|וַתְּדַבֵּ֙רְנָה֙\rb*, “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּֽירְאִ֖י\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you have given birth to|יָלָ֑דְתְּ\rb* \rb a son|בֵ֣ן\rb*!”
\p \rb But she did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb respond|עָנְתָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְלֹא־\rb* \rb or pay any heed|שָׁ֥תָה\rb*\rb |לִבָּֽהּ׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb And she named|וַתִּקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb the boy|לַנַּ֗עַר\rb*\rb |אִֽי־\rb* \rb Ichabod|כָבוֹד֙\rb*,\f + \fr 4:21 \fqa Ichabod \ft means \fqa no glory\ft .\f* \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb The glory|כָב֖וֹד\rb* \rb has departed|גָּלָ֥ה\rb*\f + \fr 4:21 \ft Or \fqa gone into exile\ft ; also in verse 22\f* \rb from Israel|מִיִּשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*,” \rb because|אֶל־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb had been captured|הִלָּקַח֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb her father-in-law|חָמִ֖יהָ\rb* \rb and her husband had been killed|וְאִישָֽׁהּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 “\rb The glory|כָב֖וֹד\rb* \rb has departed|גָּלָ֥ה\rb* \rb from Israel|מִיִּשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*,” \rb she said|וַתֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃פ\rb* \rb has been captured|נִלְקַ֖ח\rb*.”
\c 5
\s1 The Ark Afflicts the Philistines
\p \v 1 \rb After the Philistines|וּפְלִשְׁתִּים֙\rb* \rb had captured|לָֽקְח֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*, \rb they took it|וַיְבִאֻ֛הוּ\rb* \rb from|מֵאֶ֥בֶן\rb* \rb Ebenezer|הָעֵ֖זֶר\rb* \rb to Ashdod|אַשְׁדּֽוֹדָה׃\rb*, \v 2 \rb |וַיִּקְח֤וּ\rb*\rb |פְלִשְׁתִּים֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |אֲר֣וֹן\rb*\rb |הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb carried it into|וַיָּבִ֥יאוּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb the temple|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Dagon|דָּג֑וֹן\rb*, \rb and set|וַיַּצִּ֥יגוּ\rb* \rb it|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb beside|אֵ֥צֶל\rb* \rb his statue|דָּגֽוֹן׃\rb*.\f + \fr 5:2 \ft Literally \fqa set it beside Dagon\f*
\p \v 3 \rb When the people of Ashdod|אַשְׁדּוֹדִים֙\rb* \rb got up early|וַיַּשְׁכִּ֤מוּ\rb* \rb the next morning|מִֽמָּחֳרָ֔ת\rb*, \rb there|וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb was Dagon|דָג֗וֹן\rb*, \rb fallen|נֹפֵ֤ל\rb* \rb on his face|לְפָנָיו֙\rb*\rb |אַ֔רְצָה\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb So they took|וַיִּקְחוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Dagon|דָּג֔וֹן\rb* \rb and returned|וַיָּשִׁ֥בוּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb to his place|לִמְקוֹמֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb But when they got up early|וַיַּשְׁכִּ֣מוּ\rb* \rb the next|מִֽמָּחֳרָת֒\rb* \rb morning|בַבֹּקֶר֮\rb*, \rb there|וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb was Dagon|דָג֗וֹן\rb*, \rb fallen|נֹפֵ֤ל\rb* \rb on his face|לְפָנָיו֙\rb*\rb |אַ֔רְצָה\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb with his head|וְרֹ֨אשׁ\rb*\rb |דָּג֜וֹן\rb*\rb |וּשְׁתֵּ֣י׀\rb* \rb and|כַּפּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb his hands|יָדָ֗יו\rb* \rb broken off|כְּרֻתוֹת֙\rb* \rb and lying on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the threshold|הַמִּפְתָּ֔ן\rb*. \rb Only|רַ֥ק\rb* \rb the torso|דָּג֖וֹן\rb* \rb remained|נִשְׁאַ֥ר\rb*\rb |עָלָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb That is why|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֡ן\rb*, \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃ס\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*, \rb the priests|כֹהֲנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Dagon|דָג֜וֹן\rb* \rb and all|וְכָֽל־\rb* \rb who enter|הַבָּאִ֧ים\rb* \rb the temple|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of Dagon|דָּג֛וֹן\rb* \rb in Ashdod|בְּאַשְׁדּ֑וֹד\rb* \rb do not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb step|יִדְרְכוּ֩\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the threshold|מִפְתַּ֥ן\rb*\rb |דָּג֖וֹן\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Now the hand|יַד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb was heavy|וַתִּכְבַּ֧ד\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the people of Ashdod|הָאַשְׁדּוֹדִ֖ים\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb its vicinity|גְּבוּלֶֽיהָ׃\rb*, \rb ravaging them|וַיְשִׁמֵּ֑ם\rb* \rb and afflicting|וַיַּ֤ךְ\rb* \rb them|אֹתָם֙\rb* \rb with tumors|בָּעֳפָלִים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |אַשְׁדּ֖וֹד\rb*.\f + \fr 5:6 \ft Hebrew; LXX and Vulgate include \fqa And rats appeared in their land, and death and destruction were throughout the city.\f* \v 7 \rb And when the men|אַנְשֵֽׁי־\rb* \rb of Ashdod|אַשְׁדּ֖וֹד\rb* \rb saw|וַיִּרְא֥וּ\rb* \rb what was happening|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |כֵ֑ן\rb*, \rb they said|וְאָמְר֗וּ\rb*, “\rb The ark|אֲר֨וֹן\rb* \rb of the God|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb must not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb stay|יֵשֵׁ֞ב\rb* \rb here with us|עִמָּ֔נוּ\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb His hand|יָדוֹ֙\rb* \rb is heavy|קָשְׁתָ֤ה\rb* \rb upon us|עָלֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb and upon|וְעַ֖ל\rb* \rb our god|אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ׃\rb* \rb Dagon|דָּג֥וֹן\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb |וַיִּשְׁלְח֡וּ\rb* \rb So they called together|וַיַּאַסְפוּ֩\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb the rulers|סַרְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֜ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and asked|וַיֹּֽאמְרוּ֙\rb*, “\rb What|מַֽה־\rb* \rb shall we do|נַּעֲשֶׂ֗ה\rb* \rb with the ark|לַֽאֲרוֹן֙\rb* \rb of the God of|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*?”
\p “\rb It|אֲר֖וֹן\rb*\rb |אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb must be moved|יִסֹּ֔ב\rb* \rb to Gath|גַּ֣ת\rb*,” \rb they replied|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb*. \rb So they carried away|וַיַּסֵּ֕בּוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֖וֹן\rb* \rb of the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb But after|אַחֲרֵ֣י׀\rb* \rb they had moved|הֵסַ֣בּוּ\rb* \rb the ark to Gath|אֹת֗וֹ\rb*,\rb |וַתְּהִ֨י\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָ֤ה׀\rb* \rb hand|יַד־\rb* \rb was also|וַיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb against that city|בָּעִיר֙\rb*, \rb throwing it into great confusion|מְהוּמָה֙\rb*\rb |גְּדוֹלָ֣ה\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb and afflicting|וַיַּךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the men|אַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb*, \rb both young|מִקָּטֹ֖ן\rb* \rb and|וְעַד־\rb* \rb old|גָּד֑וֹל\rb*, \rb with an outbreak|וַיִּשָּׂתְר֥וּ\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb of tumors|עֳפָלִים׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb So they sent|וַֽיְשַׁלְּח֛וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb to Ekron|עֶקְר֑וֹן\rb*,\rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb but as it|אֲר֤וֹן\rb*\rb |הָאֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb arrived|כְּב֨וֹא\rb*\rb |עֶקְר֔וֹן\rb*, \rb the Ekronites|הָֽעֶקְרֹנִ֜ים\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb cried out|וַיִּזְעֲק֨וּ\rb*, “\rb They have brought|הֵסַ֤בּוּ\rb* \rb us|אֵלַי֙\rb* \rb the ark|אֲרוֹן֙\rb* \rb of the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in order to kill us|לַהֲמִיתֵ֖נִי\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb our people|עַמִּֽי׃\rb*!”
\p \v 11 \rb |וַיִּשְׁלְח֨וּ\rb* \rb Then the Ekronites called together|וַיַּאַסְפ֜וּ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the rulers|סַרְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּֽאמְרוּ֙\rb*, “\rb Send away|שַׁלְּח֞וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֨וֹן\rb* \rb of the God|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*. \rb It must return|וְיָשֹׁ֣ב\rb* \rb to its place|לִמְקֹמ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb so that it will not|וְלֹֽא־\rb*\f + \fr 5:11 \ft Or \fqa He will not\f* \rb kill|יָמִ֥ית\rb* \rb us|אֹתִ֖י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and our people|עַמִּ֑י\rb*!”
\p \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a deadly|מָ֙וֶת֙\rb* \rb confusion|מְהֽוּמַת־\rb* \rb had pervaded|הָיְתָ֤ה\rb*\rb |בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb*; \rb the hand|יַ֥ד\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb was very|מְאֹ֛ד\rb* \rb heavy|כָּבְדָ֥ה\rb* \rb upon it|שָֽׁם׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb Those|וְהָֽאֲנָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb die|מֵ֔תוּ\rb* \rb were afflicted|הֻכּ֖וּ\rb* \rb with tumors|בָּעֳפָלִים\rb*, \rb and the outcry|שַֽׁוְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb went up|וַתַּ֛עַל\rb* \rb to heaven|הַשָּׁמָֽיִם׃\rb*.
\c 6
\s1 The Ark Returned to Israel
\p \v 1 \rb When the ark|אֲרוֹן־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb had been|וַיְהִ֧י\rb* \rb in the land|בִּשְׂדֵ֥ה\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעָ֥ה\rb* \rb months|חֳדָשִֽׁים׃\rb*, \v 2 \rb the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֗ים\rb* \rb summoned|וַיִּקְרְא֣וּ\rb* \rb the priests|לַכֹּהֲנִ֤ים\rb* \rb and diviners|וְלַקֹּֽסְמִים֙\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb What|מַֽה־\rb* \rb shall we do|נַּעֲשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb with the ark|לַאֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*? \rb Tell us|הוֹדִעֻ֕נוּ\rb* \rb how|בַּמֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb to send it back|נְשַׁלְּחֶ֥נּוּ\rb* \rb to its place|לִמְקוֹמֽוֹ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 3 \rb They replied|וַיֹּאמְר֗וּ\rb*, “\rb If|אִֽם־\rb* \rb you return|מְשַׁלְּחִ֞ים\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֨וֹן\rb* \rb of the God|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb send it away|תְּשַׁלְּח֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb empty|רֵיקָ֔ם\rb*, \rb but|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb by all means return it|הָשֵׁ֥ב\rb*\rb |תָּשִׁ֛יבוּ\rb* \rb to Him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb with a guilt offering|אָשָׁ֑ם\rb*. \rb Then|אָ֤ז\rb* \rb you will be healed|תֵּרָֽפְאוּ֙\rb*, \rb and you will understand|וְנוֹדַ֣ע\rb* \rb why|לָ֛מָּה\rb* \rb His hand|יָד֖וֹ\rb* \rb has not|לֹא־\rb* \rb been lifted|תָס֥וּר\rb* \rb from|מִכֶּֽם׃\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֔ם\rb*.”
\p \v 4 “\rb What|מָ֣ה\rb* \rb guilt offering|הָאָשָׁם֮\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb should we send back|נָשִׁ֣יב\rb* \rb to Him|לוֹ֒\rb*?” \rb asked the Philistines|וַיֹּאמְר֗וּ\rb*.
\p “\rb Five|חֲמִשָּׁה֙\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֔ב\rb* \rb tumors|עָפְלֵי\rb* \rb and five|וַחֲמִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֑ב\rb* \rb rats|עַכְבְּרֵ֣י\rb*,” \rb they said|וַיֹּאמְר֗וּ\rb*, “\rb according to the number|מִסְפַּר֙\rb* \rb of rulers|סַרְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb since|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the same|אַחַ֛ת\rb* \rb plague has struck|מַגֵּפָ֥ה\rb* \rb both you|לְכֻלָּ֖ם\rb* \rb and your rulers|וּלְסַרְנֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb Make|וַעֲשִׂיתֶם֩\rb* \rb images|צַלְמֵ֨י\rb* \rb of your tumors|עָפְלֵיכֶם\rb*\rb |וְצַלְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb and of the rats|עַכְבְּרֵיכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb that are ravaging|הַמַּשְׁחִיתִם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*. \rb Give|וּנְתַתֶּ֛ם\rb* \rb glory|כָּב֑וֹד\rb* \rb to the God|לֵאלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb and perhaps|אוּלַ֗י\rb* \rb He will lift|יָקֵ֤ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb His hand|יָדוֹ֙\rb* \rb from you|מֵֽעֲלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and|וּמֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb your gods|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and|וּמֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb your land|אַרְצְכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Why|וְלָ֤מָּה\rb* \rb harden|תְכַבְּדוּ֙\rb*\f + \fr 6:6 \ft Or \fqa make heavy\ft ; similarly again in this verse\f*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your hearts|לְבַבְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֥יִם\rb* \rb and Pharaoh|וּפַרְעֹ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb hardened|כִּבְּד֛וּ\rb* \rb theirs|לִבָּ֑ם\rb*? \rb When|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He afflicted|הִתְעַלֵּ֣ל\rb* \rb them|בָּהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb did they not|הֲלוֹא֙\rb* \rb send the people out|וַֽיְשַׁלְּח֖וּם\rb* \rb so they could go on their way|וַיֵּלֵֽכוּ׃\rb*?
\p \v 7 \rb Now, therefore|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb*,\rb |קְח֨וּ\rb* \rb prepare|וַעֲשׂ֜וּ\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֔ת\rb* \rb new|חֲדָשָׁה֙\rb* \rb cart|עֲגָלָ֤ה\rb* \rb with two|וּשְׁתֵּ֤י\rb* \rb milk|עָל֔וֹת\rb* \rb cows|פָרוֹת֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb have never|לֹא־\rb* \rb been yoked|עָלָ֥ה\rb*\rb |עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |עֹ֑ל\rb*. \rb Hitch|וַאֲסַרְתֶּ֤ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the cows|הַפָּרוֹת֙\rb* \rb to the cart|בָּעֲגָלָ֔ה\rb*, \rb but take their calves|בְּנֵיהֶ֛ם\rb*\rb |מֵאַחֲרֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb away|וַהֲשֵׁיבֹתֶ֧ם\rb* \rb and pen them up|הַבָּֽיְתָה׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb Take|וּלְקַחְתֶּ֞ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb set|וּנְתַתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb it|אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the cart|הָ֣עֲגָלָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and|וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb in a chest|בָאַרְגַּ֖ז\rb* \rb beside it|מִצִּדּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb put|תָּשִׂ֥ימוּ\rb* \rb the gold|הַזָּהָ֗ב\rb* \rb objects|כְּלֵ֣י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you are sending back|הֲשֵׁבֹתֶ֥ם\rb* \rb to Him|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb as a guilt offering|אָשָׁ֔ם\rb*.
\p \rb Then send|וְשִׁלַּחְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb the ark|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb on its way|וְהָלָֽךְ׃\rb*, \v 9 \rb but keep watching it|וּרְאִיתֶ֗ם\rb*. \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb it goes up|יַֽעֲלֶה֙\rb* \rb the road|דֶּ֨רֶךְ\rb* \rb to its homeland|גְּבוּל֤וֹ\rb*,\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb toward Beth-shemesh|שֶׁ֔מֶשׁ\rb*, \rb it is the LORD|ה֚וּא\rb* \rb who has brought|עָ֣שָׂה\rb* \rb on us|לָ֔נוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb great|הַגְּדוֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb disaster|הָרָעָ֥ה\rb*. \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb it does not|לֹ֗א\rb*, \rb then we will know|וְיָדַ֙עְנוּ֙\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb it was not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb His hand|יָדוֹ֙\rb* \rb that punished|נָ֣גְעָה\rb* \rb us|בָּ֔נוּ\rb* \rb and that it|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb happened|הָ֥יָה\rb*\rb |לָֽנוּ׃\rb* \rb by chance|מִקְרֶ֥ה\rb*.”
\p \v 10 \rb So the men|הָאֲנָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb did|וַיַּעֲשׂ֤וּ\rb* \rb as instructed|כֵּ֔ן\rb*. \rb They took|וַיִּקְח֗וּ\rb* \rb two|שְׁתֵּ֤י\rb* \rb milk|עָל֔וֹת\rb* \rb cows|פָרוֹת֙\rb*, \rb hitched them|וַיַּאַסְר֖וּם\rb* \rb to the cart|בָּעֲגָלָ֑ה\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and penned up|כָּל֥וּ\rb*\rb |בַבָּֽיִת׃\rb* \rb their calves|בְּנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*. \v 11 \rb Then they put|וַיָּשִׂ֛מוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the cart|הָעֲגָלָ֑ה\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb along with the chest|הָאַרְגַּ֗ז\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb containing the gold|הַזָּהָ֔ב\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb rats|עַכְבְּרֵ֣י\rb* \rb and the images|צַלְמֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the tumors|טְחֹרֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb And the cows|הַפָּר֜וֹת\rb* \rb headed straight|וַיִשַּׁ֨רְנָה\rb* \rb up the road|בַּדֶּ֗רֶךְ\rb* \rb toward|עַל־\rb*\rb |דֶּ֙רֶךְ֙\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb Beth-shemesh|שֶׁ֔מֶשׁ\rb*, \rb staying on that one|אַחַ֗ת\rb* \rb highway|בִּמְסִלָּ֣ה\rb* \rb and lowing|וְגָע֔וֹ\rb* \rb as they went|הָלְכ֤וּ\rb*\rb |הָלֹךְ֙\rb*, \rb never|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb straying|סָ֖רוּ\rb* \rb to the right|יָמִ֣ין\rb* \rb or to the left|וּשְׂמֹ֑אול\rb*. \rb The rulers|וְסַרְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּים֙\rb* \rb followed|הֹלְכִ֣ים\rb* \rb behind them|אַחֲרֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the border|גְּב֖וּל\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Beth-shemesh|שָֽׁמֶשׁ׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb |וּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb Now the people of Beth-shemesh|שֶׁ֔מֶשׁ\rb* \rb were harvesting|קֹצְרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |קְצִיר־\rb* \rb wheat|חִטִּ֖ים\rb* \rb in the valley|בָּעֵ֑מֶק\rb*, \rb and when they looked up|וַיִּשְׂא֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |עֵינֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb and saw|וַיִּרְאוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|הָ֣אָר֔וֹן\rb*, \rb they were overjoyed|וַֽיִּשְׂמְח֖וּ\rb* \rb at the sight|לִרְאֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb The cart|וְהָעֲגָלָ֡ה\rb* \rb came|בָּ֠אָה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the field|שְׂדֵ֨ה\rb* \rb of Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֤עַ\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of Beth-shemesh|הַשִּׁמְשִׁי֙\rb* \rb and stopped|וַתַּעֲמֹ֣ד\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְשָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb near a large|גְּדוֹלָ֑ה\rb* \rb rock|אֶ֣בֶן\rb*. \rb The people chopped up|וַֽיְבַקְּעוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |עֲצֵ֣י\rb* \rb the cart|הָעֲגָלָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and offered|הֶעֱל֥וּ\rb* \rb the cows|הַ֨פָּר֔וֹת\rb* \rb as a burnt offering|עֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃ס\rb*. \v 15 \rb And the Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּ֞ם\rb* \rb took down|הוֹרִ֣ידוּ׀\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the chest|הָאַרְגַּ֤ז\rb* \rb containing|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |אִתּוֹ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |בּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb the gold|זָהָ֔ב\rb* \rb objects|כְלֵֽי־\rb*, \rb and they placed them|וַיָּשִׂ֖מוּ\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the large|הַגְּדוֹלָ֑ה\rb* \rb rock|הָאֶ֣בֶן\rb*. \rb That|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb the men|וְאַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb*\rb |בֵֽית־\rb* \rb of Beth-shemesh|שֶׁ֗מֶשׁ\rb* \rb offered|הֶעֱל֨וּ\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹל֜וֹת\rb* \rb and made|וַֽיִּזְבְּח֧וּ\rb* \rb sacrifices|זְבָחִ֛ים\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb And when the five|וַחֲמִשָּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb rulers|סַרְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb saw this|רָא֑וּ\rb*, \rb they returned|וַיָּשֻׁ֥בוּ\rb* \rb to Ekron|עֶקְר֖וֹן\rb* \rb that same|הַהֽוּא׃ס\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb |וְאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb As a guilt offering|אָשָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֛ים\rb* \rb had sent back|הֵשִׁ֧יבוּ\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֜ד\rb* \rb gold|הַזָּהָ֔ב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb tumor for each city|טְחֹרֵ֣י\rb*: \rb Ashdod|לְאַשְׁדּ֨וֹד\rb*, \rb Gaza|לְעַזָּ֤ה\rb*,\rb |אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb Ashkelon|לְאַשְׁקְל֣וֹן\rb*,\rb |אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb Gath|לְגַ֥ת\rb*,\rb |אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb and Ekron|לְעֶקְר֥וֹן\rb*.\rb |אֶחָֽד׃ס\rb* \v 18 \rb The number of gold|הַזָּהָ֗ב\rb* \rb rats|וְעַכְבְּרֵ֣י\rb* \rb also corresponded to the number|מִסְפַּ֞ר\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb of Philistine|פְלִשְׁתִּים֙\rb* \rb cities|עָרֵ֤י\rb* \rb belonging to the five|לַחֲמֵ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb rulers|הַסְּרָנִ֔ים\rb* — \rb the fortified|מִבְצָ֔ר\rb* \rb cities|מֵעִ֣יר\rb* \rb and|וְעַ֖ד\rb* \rb their outlying|הַפְּרָזִ֑י\rb*\rb |וְעַ֣ד׀\rb* \rb villages|כֹּ֣פֶר\rb*. \rb And the large|הַגְּדוֹלָ֗ה\rb* \rb rock|אָבֵ֣ל\rb*\f + \fr 6:18 \ft Or \fqa great meadow\ft ; Hebrew \fqa Abel-haggedolah\f* \rb on|עָלֶ֙יהָ֙\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb they placed|הִנִּ֤יחוּ\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb stands to|עַ֚ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb in the field|בִּשְׂדֵ֥ה\rb* \rb of Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of Beth-shemesh|הַשִּׁמְשִֽׁי׃\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb But God struck down|וַיַּ֞ךְ\rb*\rb |בְּאַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb some of the people|בֵֽית־\rb* \rb of Beth-shemesh|שֶׁ֗מֶשׁ\rb* \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb they looked|רָאוּ֙\rb* \rb inside the ark|בַּאֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*. \rb He struck down|וַיַּ֤ךְ\rb*\rb |בָּעָם֙\rb* \rb seventy|שִׁבְעִ֣ים\rb* \rb men|אִ֔ישׁ\rb*\rb |חֲמִשִּׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶ֖לֶף\rb*\rb |אִ֑ישׁ\rb*,\f + \fr 6:19 \ft A few late Hebrew manuscripts and Josephus; most Hebrew manuscripts \fqa 70 men and 50,000 men\ft ; LXX \fqa 70 men and 50,000 men of the people\ft ; Syriac and Arabic \fqa 70 men and 5,000 men\ft ; alternately, possibly \fqa 70 men and 50 oxen\f* \rb and the people mourned|וַיִּֽתְאַבְּל֣וּ\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |בָּעָ֖ם\rb* \rb had struck|הִכָּ֧ה\rb* \rb them|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb with a great|גְדוֹלָֽה\rb* \rb slaughter|מַכָּ֥ה\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb The men|אַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb*\rb |בֵֽית־\rb* \rb of Beth-shemesh|שֶׁ֔מֶשׁ\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּֽאמְרוּ֙\rb*, “\rb Who|מִ֚י\rb* \rb can|יוּכַ֣ל\rb* \rb stand|לַעֲמֹ֔ד\rb* \rb in the presence|לִפְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb*, \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb holy|הַקָּד֖וֹשׁ\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb*? \rb To|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb whom|מִ֖י\rb* \rb should the ark go up|יַעֲלֶ֥ה\rb* \rb from here|מֵעָלֵֽינוּ׃ס\rb*?”
