\c 7
\s1 Samuel Subdues the Philistines
\p \v 1 \rb Then the men|אַנְשֵׁ֣י׀\rb*\rb |קִרְיַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Kiriath-jearim|יְעָרִ֗ים\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֜אוּ\rb* \rb for the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and took|וַֽיַּעֲלוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |וַיָּבִ֣אוּ\rb* \rb it|אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb Abinadab’s|אֲבִינָדָ֖ב\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb on the hill|בַּגִּבְעָ֑ה\rb*. \rb And|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb they consecrated|קִדְּשׁ֔וּ\rb* \rb his son|בְּנוֹ֙\rb* \rb Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֤ר\rb* \rb to guard|לִשְׁמֹ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb And from that day|מִיּ֞וֹם\rb* \rb a long|וַיִּרְבּוּ֙\rb* \rb time|הַיָּמִ֔ים\rb* \rb passed|וַיְהִ֗י\rb*, \rb twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb in all|וַיִּֽהְי֖וּ\rb*, \rb as the ark|הָֽאָרוֹן֙\rb* \rb remained|שֶׁ֤בֶת\rb*\rb |בְּקִרְיַ֣ת\rb* \rb at Kiriath-jearim|יְעָרִ֔ים\rb*. \rb And all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb mournfully|וַיִּנָּה֛וּ\rb* \rb sought|אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Then Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֮\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹר֒\rb*, “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb are returning|שָׁבִים֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb your hearts|לְבַבְכֶ֗ם\rb*, \rb then put away|הָסִ֜ירוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the foreign|הַנֵּכָ֛ר\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהֵ֧י\rb* \rb and Ashtoreths|וְהָעַשְׁתָּר֑וֹת\rb* \rb among you|מִתּוֹכְכֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb prepare|וְהָכִ֨ינוּ\rb* \rb your hearts|לְבַבְכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb for|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb and serve Him|וְעִבְדֻ֣הוּ\rb* \rb only|לְבַדּ֔וֹ\rb*. \rb And He will deliver|וְיַצֵּ֥ל\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb from the hand|מִיַּ֥ד\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּֽים׃\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb So the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb put away|וַיָּסִ֙ירוּ֙\rb* \rb the Baals|הַבְּעָלִ֖ים\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Ashtoreths|הָעַשְׁתָּרֹ֑ת\rb* \rb and served|וַיַּעַבְד֥וּ\rb* \rb only|לְבַדּֽוֹ׃פ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Then Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Gather|קִבְצ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb to Mizpah|הַמִּצְפָּ֑תָה\rb*, \rb and I will pray|וְאֶתְפַּלֵּ֥ל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb on your behalf|בַּעַדְכֶ֖ם\rb*.”
\p \v 6 \rb When they had gathered|וַיִּקָּבְצ֣וּ\rb* \rb at Mizpah|הַ֠מִּצְפָּתָה\rb*, \rb they drew|וַיִּֽשְׁאֲבוּ־\rb* \rb water|מַ֜יִם\rb* \rb and poured it out|וַֽיִּשְׁפְּכ֣וּ׀\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*. \rb On that|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb they fasted|וַיָּצ֙וּמוּ֙\rb*, \rb and there|שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb they confessed|וַיֹּ֣אמְרוּ\rb*, “\rb We have sinned|חָטָ֖אנוּ\rb* \rb against the LORD|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb*.” \rb And Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb judged|וַיִּשְׁפֹּ֧ט\rb*\f + \fr 7:6 \ft Or \fqa governed \ft or \fqa led\ft ; similarly in verses 15, 16, and 17\f* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb at Mizpah|בַּמִּצְפָּֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb When the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֗ים\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמְע֣וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb had gathered|הִתְקַבְּצ֤וּ\rb* \rb at Mizpah|הַמִּצְפָּ֔תָה\rb*, \rb their|פְלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb rulers|סַרְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb marched up|וַיַּעֲל֥וּ\rb* \rb toward|אֶל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb And when the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb learned of this|וַֽיִּשְׁמְעוּ֙\rb*, \rb they feared|וַיִּֽרְא֖וּ\rb*\rb |מִפְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּֽים׃\rb* \v 8 \rb and|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמְר֤וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֔ל\rb*, “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb stop|תַּחֲרֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb crying out|מִזְּעֹ֖ק\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb for us|מִמֶּ֔נּוּ\rb*, \rb that He may save us|וְיֹשִׁעֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb from the hand|מִיַּ֥ד\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּֽים׃\rb*.”
\p \v 9 \rb Then Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb a|אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb suckling|חָלָב֙\rb* \rb lamb|טְלֵ֤ה\rb* \rb and offered it|וַיַּעֲלֶה\rb* \rb as a whole|כָּלִ֖יל\rb* \rb burnt offering|עוֹלָ֛ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb He|שְׁמוּאֵ֤ל\rb* \rb cried out|וַיִּזְעַ֨ק\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb on behalf of|בְּעַ֣ד\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb and the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb answered him|וַֽיַּעֲנֵ֖הוּ\rb*. \v 10 \rb As the Philistines|וּפְלִשְׁתִּ֣ים\rb* \rb drew near|נִגְּשׁ֔וּ\rb* \rb to fight|לַמִּלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb against Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵל֙\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb offering up|מַעֲלֶ֣ה\rb* \rb the burnt offering|הָעוֹלָ֔ה\rb*. \rb But that|הַה֤וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֨וֹם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb thundered|וַיַּרְעֵ֣ם\rb* \rb loudly|בְּקוֹל־\rb*\rb |גָּ֠דוֹל\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּים֙\rb* \rb and threw them into such confusion|וַיְהֻמֵּ֔ם\rb* \rb that they fled|וַיִּנָּגְפ֖וּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb Then the men|אַנְשֵׁ֤י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb charged out|וַיֵּ֨צְא֜וּ\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb Mizpah|הַמִּצְפָּ֔ה\rb* \rb and pursued|וַֽיִּרְדְּפ֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb*, \rb striking them down|וַיַּכּ֕וּם\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb all the way to|מִתַּ֖חַת\rb*\rb |לְבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb an area below Beth-car|כָּֽר׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb Afterward, Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֜ל\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb a|אַחַ֗ת\rb* \rb stone|אֶ֣בֶן\rb* \rb and set it up|וַיָּ֤שֶׂם\rb* \rb between|בֵּֽין־\rb* \rb Mizpah|הַמִּצְפָּה֙\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb and Shen|הַשֵּׁ֔ן\rb*.\f + \fr 7:12 \ft Hebrew; LXX and Syriac \fqa Jeshanah\f* \rb He named|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |שְׁמָ֖הּ\rb*\rb |אֶ֣בֶן\rb* \rb it Ebenezer|הָעָ֑זֶר\rb*,\f + \fr 7:12 \fqa Ebenezer \ft means \fqa stone of help\ft .\f* \rb saying|וַיֹּאמַ֕ר\rb*, “\rb Thus|הֵ֖נָּה\rb* \rb far|עַד־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb has helped us|עֲזָרָ֥נוּ\rb*.”
\p \v 13 \rb So the Philistines|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb were subdued|וַיִּכָּֽנְעוּ֙\rb*, \rb and they stopped|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb invading|לָב֖וֹא\rb* \rb the territory|בִּגְב֣וּל\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*\rb |יָסְפ֣וּ\rb*\rb |ע֔וֹד\rb*. \rb And the hand|יַד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb was|וַתְּהִ֤י\rb* \rb against the Philistines|בַּפְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb The cities|הֶעָרִ֡ים\rb* \rb from Ekron|מֵעֶקְר֣וֹן\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb Gath|גַּ֔ת\rb*,\rb |וְאֶ֨ת־\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּים֩\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb had taken|לָֽקְחוּ־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֤ל׀\rb*, \rb were restored|וַתָּשֹׁ֣בְנָה\rb* \rb to Israel|לְיִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*, \rb who|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb also delivered|הִצִּ֥יל\rb* \rb the surrounding territory|גְּבוּלָ֔ן\rb* \rb from the hand|מִיַּ֣ד\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb*. \rb And there was|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb peace|שָׁל֔וֹם\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb and the Amorites|הָאֱמֹרִֽי׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb So Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb judged|וַיִּשְׁפֹּ֤ט\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֥י\rb* \rb of his life|חַיָּֽיו׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb Every year|שָׁנָה֙\rb*\rb |בְּשָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb he would go|וְהָלַ֗ךְ\rb* \rb on a circuit|וְסָבַב֙\rb* \rb from|מִדֵּ֤י\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb Bethel|אֵ֔ל\rb* \rb to Gilgal|וְהַגִּלְגָּ֖ל\rb* \rb to Mizpah|וְהַמִּצְפָּ֑ה\rb*, \rb judging|וְשָׁפַט֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb in|אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb* \rb places|הַמְּקוֹמ֖וֹת\rb*. \v 17 \rb Then he would return|וּתְשֻׁבָת֤וֹ\rb* \rb to Ramah|הָרָמָ֙תָה֙\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb his home|בֵּית֔וֹ\rb* \rb was there|שָׁ֣ם\rb*, \rb and there|וְשָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb he judged|שָׁפָ֣ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and built|וַיִּֽבֶן־\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָֽה׃פ\rb*\rb |שָׁ֥ם\rb*.
\c 8
\s1 Israel Demands a King
\r (\ref Deuteronomy 17:14–20|DEU 17:14-20\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb |וַיְהִ֕י\rb* \rb When|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb grew old|זָקֵ֖ן\rb*, \rb he appointed|וַיָּ֧שֶׂם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his sons|בָּנָ֛יו\rb* \rb as judges|שֹׁפְטִ֖ים\rb*\f + \fr 8:1 \ft Or \fqa governors \ft or \fqa leaders\ft ; similarly in verses 2, 5, 6, and 20\f* \rb over Israel|לְיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb The name|שֶׁם־\rb* \rb of his firstborn|הַבְּכוֹר֙\rb* \rb son|בְּנ֤וֹ\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb Joel|יוֹאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb and the name|וְשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb of his second|מִשְׁנֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb was Abijah|אֲבִיָּ֑ה\rb*. \rb They were judges|שֹׁפְטִ֖ים\rb*\rb |בִּבְאֵ֥ר\rb* \rb in Beersheba|שָֽׁבַע׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb But his sons|בָנָיו֙\rb* \rb did not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb walk|הָלְכ֤וּ\rb* \rb in his ways|בְּדַרְכּוֹ\rb*; \rb they turned aside|וַיִּטּ֖וּ\rb* \rb toward|אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb dishonest gain|הַבָּ֑צַע\rb*, \rb accepting|וַיִּ֨קְחוּ־\rb* \rb bribes|שֹׁ֔חַד\rb* \rb and perverting|וַיַּטּ֖וּ\rb* \rb justice|מִשְׁפָּֽט׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb So all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb gathered together|וַיִּֽתְקַבְּצ֔וּ\rb* \rb and came|וַיָּבֹ֥אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb at Ramah|הָרָמָֽתָה׃\rb*. \v 5 “\rb Look|הִנֵּה֙\rb*,” \rb they said|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֗יו\rb*, “\rb you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb are old|זָקַ֔נְתָּ\rb*, \rb and your sons|וּבָנֶ֕יךָ\rb* \rb do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb walk|הָלְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb in your ways|בִּדְרָכֶ֑יךָ\rb*. \rb Now|עַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb appoint|שִֽׂימָה־\rb*\rb |לָּ֥נוּ\rb* \rb a king|מֶ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb to judge us|לְשָׁפְטֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb like all|כְּכָל־\rb* \rb the other nations|הַגּוֹיִֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 6 \rb But when|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they said|אָמְר֔וּ\rb*, “\rb Give|תְּנָה־\rb* \rb us|לָּ֥נוּ\rb* \rb a king|מֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb to judge us|לְשָׁפְטֵ֑נוּ\rb*,” \rb their demand|הַדָּבָר֙\rb* \rb was displeasing|וַיֵּ֤רַע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֔ל\rb*; \rb so he|שְׁמוּאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb prayed|וַיִּתְפַּלֵּ֥ל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֔ל\rb*, “\rb Listen|שְׁמַע֙\rb* \rb to the voice|בְּק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb in all|לְכֹ֥ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they say|יֹאמְר֖וּ\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֑יךָ\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb it is not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb you|אֹֽתְךָ֙\rb* \rb they have rejected|מָאָ֔סוּ\rb*, \rb but|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they have rejected|מָאֲס֖וּ\rb* \rb Me|אֹתִ֥י\rb* \rb as their king|מִמְּלֹ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |עֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb Just as|כְּכָֽל־\rb*\rb |הַמַּעֲשִׂ֣ים\rb* \rb they have done|עָשׂ֗וּ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb from the day|מִיּוֹם֩\rb* \rb I brought them up|הַעֲלֹתִ֨י\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֤ם\rb* \rb out of Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb until|וְעַד־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*, \rb forsaking Me|וַיַּ֣עַזְבֻ֔נִי\rb* \rb and serving|וַיַּעַבְד֖וּ\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֑ים\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb*,\rb |גַּם־\rb* \rb so|כֵּ֛ן\rb* \rb they|הֵ֥מָּה\rb* \rb are doing|עֹשִׂ֖ים\rb* \rb to you|לָֽךְ׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb listen to|שְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb their voice|בְּקוֹלָ֑ם\rb*; \rb but|אַ֗ךְ\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you must solemnly warn|הָעֵ֤ד\rb*\rb |תָּעִיד֙\rb* \rb them|בָּהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and show|וְהִגַּדְתָּ֣\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb the manner|מִשְׁפַּ֣ט\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb will reign|יִמְלֹ֖ךְ\rb* \rb over them|עֲלֵיהֶֽם׃ס\rb*.”
\s1 Samuel’s Warning
\p \v 10 \rb So Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb spoke|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֕ם\rb* \rb who were asking him for|הַשֹּׁאֲלִ֥ים\rb*\rb |מֵאִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb a king|מֶֽלֶךְ׃ס\rb*. \v 11 \rb He said|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb This|זֶ֗ה\rb* \rb will be|יִֽהְיֶה֙\rb* \rb the manner|מִשְׁפַּ֣ט\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb will reign|יִמְלֹ֖ךְ\rb* \rb over you|עֲלֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*:\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb He will take|יִקָּ֗ח\rb* \rb your sons|בְּנֵיכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb and appoint them|וְשָׂ֥ם\rb* \rb to serve|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb his own chariots|בְּמֶרְכַּבְתּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb and horses|וּבְפָרָשָׁ֔יו\rb*, \rb and to run|וְרָצ֖וּ\rb* \rb in front of|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb his chariots|מֶרְכַּבְתּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb He will appoint|וְלָשׂ֣וּם\rb* \rb some for himself|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb as commanders|שָׂרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of thousands|אֲלָפִ֖ים\rb* \rb and of|וְשָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb fifties|חֲמִשִּׁ֑ים\rb*, \rb and others to plow|וְלַחֲרֹ֤שׁ\rb* \rb his ground|חֲרִישׁוֹ֙\rb*, \rb to reap|וְלִקְצֹ֣ר\rb* \rb his harvest|קְצִיר֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and to make|וְלַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb his weapons|כְּלֵֽי־\rb* \rb of war|מִלְחַמְתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb and equipment|וּכְלֵ֥י\rb* \rb for his chariots|רִכְבּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb And|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb he will take|יִקָּ֑ח\rb* \rb your daughters|בְּנוֹתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to be perfumers|לְרַקָּח֥וֹת\rb*, \rb cooks|וּלְטַבָּח֖וֹת\rb*, \rb and bakers|וּלְאֹפֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb He will take|יִקָּ֑ח\rb* \rb the best|הַטּוֹבִ֖ים\rb* \rb of your fields|שְׂ֠דֽוֹתֵיכֶם\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb vineyards|כַּרְמֵיכֶ֧ם\rb* \rb and olive groves|וְזֵיתֵיכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb and give them|וְנָתַ֖ן\rb* \rb to his servants|לַעֲבָדָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb He will take a tenth|יַעְשֹׂ֑ר\rb* \rb of your grain|וְזַרְעֵיכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb and grape harvest|וְכַרְמֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and give it|וְנָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb to his officials|לְסָרִיסָ֖יו\rb* \rb and servants|וְלַעֲבָדָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb And|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb he will take|יִקָּ֑ח\rb* \rb your menservants|עַבְדֵיכֶם֩\rb* \rb and|וְֽאֶת־\rb* \rb maidservants|שִׁפְח֨וֹתֵיכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb your best|הַטּוֹבִ֛ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb cattle|בַּחוּרֵיכֶ֧ם\rb*\f + \fr 8:16 \ft LXX; Hebrew \fqa your best young men\f* \rb and donkeys|חֲמוֹרֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and put them|וְעָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb to his own use|לִמְלַאכְתּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb He will take a tenth|יַעְשֹׂ֑ר\rb* \rb of your flocks|צֹאנְכֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb and you yourselves|וְאַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb will become|תִּֽהְיוּ־\rb* \rb his|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb slaves|לַעֲבָדִֽים׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb When that|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb day comes|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*, \rb you will beg|וּזְעַקְתֶּם֙\rb* \rb for relief from|מִלִּפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכְּכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you have chosen|בְּחַרְתֶּ֖ם\rb*\rb |לָכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb but the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb will not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb answer you|יַעֲנֶ֧ה\rb* \rb on that|הַהֽוּא׃\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb*.”
\s1 God Grants the Request
\p \v 19 \rb Nevertheless , the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb refused|וַיְמָאֲנ֣וּ\rb* \rb to listen|לִשְׁמֹ֖עַ\rb*\rb |בְּק֣וֹל\rb* \rb to Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֑ל\rb*. “\rb No|לֹּ֔א\rb*!”\rb |כִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb they said|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*. “\rb We must have|יִֽהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb a king|מֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb over us|עָלֵֽינוּ׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb Then we will|אֲנַ֖חְנוּ\rb* \rb be|וְהָיִ֥ינוּ\rb*\rb |גַם־\rb* \rb like all|כְּכָל־\rb* \rb the other nations|הַגּוֹיִ֑ם\rb*, \rb with a king|מַלְכֵּ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb to judge us|וּשְׁפָטָ֤נוּ\rb*, \rb to go out|וְיָצָ֣א\rb* \rb before us|לְפָנֵ֔ינוּ\rb*, \rb and to fight|וְנִלְחַ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb our battles|מִלְחֲמֹתֵֽנוּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 21 \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb listened|וַיִּשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb to all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb and repeated them|וַֽיְדַבְּרֵ֖ם\rb* \rb in the hearing|בְּאָזְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 22 “\rb Listen|שְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb to their voice|בְּקוֹלָ֔ם\rb*,” \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵל֙\rb*. “\rb Appoint|וְהִמְלַכְתָּ֥\rb* \rb a king|מֶ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb for them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb*.”
\p \rb Then Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵל֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb the men|אַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, “\rb Everyone|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb must go back|לְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb to his city|לְעִירֽוֹ׃פ\rb*.”
\c 9
\s1 Saul Chosen as King
\p \v 1 \rb Now there was|וַֽיְהִי־\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb a Benjamite|מִבִּן־\rb*, \rb a powerful man|גִּבּ֖וֹר\rb*\rb |חָֽיִל׃\rb*\rb |יָמִין\rb*, \rb whose name|וּ֠שְׁמוֹ\rb* \rb was Kish|קִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Abiel|אֲבִיאֵ֞ל\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zeror|צְר֧וֹר\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Becorath|בְּכוֹרַ֛ת\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Aphiah|אֲפִ֖יחַ\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of Benjamin|יְמִינִ֑י\rb*. \v 2 \rb And|וְלוֹ־\rb* \rb he had|הָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb a son|בֵ֜ן\rb* \rb named|וּשְׁמ֤וֹ\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb*, \rb choice|בָּח֣וּר\rb* \rb and handsome|וָט֔וֹב\rb*, \rb without equal|וְאֵ֥ין\rb*\rb |אִ֛ישׁ\rb*\rb |ט֣וֹב\rb* \rb among|מִמֶּ֑נּוּ\rb* \rb the Israelites|מִבְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* — \rb a head|מִשִּׁכְמ֣וֹ\rb*\rb |וָמַ֔עְלָה\rb* \rb taller|גָּבֹ֖הַּ\rb* \rb than any|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb One day the donkeys|הָאֲתֹנ֔וֹת\rb* \rb of Saul’s|שָׁא֑וּל\rb* \rb father|אֲבִ֣י\rb* \rb Kish|לְקִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb wandered off|וַתֹּאבַ֙דְנָה֙\rb*, \rb and Kish|קִ֜ישׁ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his son|בְּנ֗וֹ\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֣וּל\rb*, “\rb Take|קַח־\rb*\rb |נָ֤א\rb* \rb one|אַחַ֣ד\rb* \rb of the servants|מֵֽהַנְּעָרִ֔ים\rb*\rb |וְק֣וּם\rb*\rb |אִתְּךָ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and go|לֵ֔ךְ\rb* \rb look for|בַּקֵּ֖שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the donkeys|הָאֲתֹנֹֽת׃\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb So Saul passed|וַיַּעֲבֹ֧ר\rb* \rb through the hill country|בְּהַר־\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֛יִם\rb* \rb and then through the land|בְּאֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of Shalishah|שָׁלִ֖שָׁה\rb*, \rb but they did not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb find the donkeys|מָצָ֑אוּ\rb*. \rb He and the servant went|וַיַּעֲבֹ֥ר\rb* \rb through the region|בְאֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of Shaalim|שַׁעֲלִים֙\rb*, \rb but they were not there|וָאַ֔יִן\rb*.\rb |וַיַּעֲבֹ֥ר\rb* \rb Then they went|וַיַּעַבְר֤וּ\rb* \rb through the land|בְּאֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of Benjamin|יְמִינִ֖י\rb*, \rb and still they did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb find them|מָצָֽאוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb When they|הֵ֗מָּה\rb* \rb reached|בָּ֚אוּ\rb* \rb the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Zuph|צ֔וּף\rb*, \rb Saul|וְשָׁא֥וּל\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֛ר\rb* \rb to his servant|לְנַעֲר֥וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |עִמּ֖וֹ\rb*, “\rb Come|לְכָ֣ה\rb*, \rb let us go back|וְנָשׁ֑וּבָה\rb*, \rb or|פֶּן־\rb* \rb my father|אָבִ֛י\rb* \rb will stop worrying|יֶחְדַּ֥ל\rb* \rb about|מִן־\rb* \rb the donkeys|הָאֲתֹנ֖וֹת\rb* \rb and start worrying|וְדָ֥אַג\rb* \rb about us|לָֽנוּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 6 “\rb Look|הִנֵּה־\rb*,”\rb |נָ֤א\rb* \rb said the servant|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb in this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb city|בָּעִ֣יר\rb* \rb there is a man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb who|וְהָאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb is highly respected|נִכְבָּ֔ד\rb*; \rb everything|כֹּ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he says|יְדַבֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb surely comes to pass|בּ֣וֹא\rb*\rb |יָב֑וֹא\rb*. \rb Let us go|נֵ֣לֲכָה\rb* \rb there|שָּׁ֔ם\rb* \rb now|עַתָּה֙\rb*. \rb Perhaps|אוּלַי֙\rb* \rb he will tell|יַגִּ֣יד\rb* \rb us|לָ֔נוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb way|דַּרְכֵּ֖נוּ\rb* \rb to go|הָלַ֥כְנוּ\rb*\rb |עָלֶֽיהָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 7 “\rb If|וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb we do go|נֵלֵךְ֮\rb*,” \rb Saul|שָׁא֜וּל\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |לְנַעֲר֗וֹ\rb*, “\rb what|וּמַה־\rb* \rb can we give|נָּבִ֣יא\rb* \rb the man|לָאִישׁ֒\rb*? \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the bread|הַלֶּ֙חֶם֙\rb* \rb in our packs|מִכֵּלֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb is gone|אָזַ֣ל\rb*, \rb and there is no|אֵין־\rb* \rb gift|וּתְשׁוּרָ֥ה\rb* \rb to take|לְהָבִ֖יא\rb* \rb to the man|לְאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*. \rb What|מָ֖ה\rb* \rb do we have|אִתָּֽנוּ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 8 \rb The servant|הַנַּ֙עַר֙\rb* \rb answered|לַעֲנ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb again|וַיֹּ֤סֶף\rb*. “\rb Look|הִנֵּה֙\rb*,” \rb he said|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I have here|נִמְצָ֣א\rb* \rb in my hand|בְיָדִ֔י\rb* \rb a quarter|רֶ֖בַע\rb* \rb shekel|שֶׁ֣קֶל\rb* \rb of silver|כָּ֑סֶף\rb*.\f + \fr 9:8 \fqa A quarter shekel \ft is approximately 0.1 ounces or 2.85 grams of silver.\f* \rb I will give|וְנָֽתַתִּי֙\rb* \rb it to the man|לְאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*, \rb and he will tell|וְהִגִּ֥יד\rb* \rb us|לָ֖נוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb our way|דַּרְכֵּֽנוּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 9 (\rb Formerly|לְפָנִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*,\rb |כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb a man|הָאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb on his way|בְּלֶכְתּוֹ֙\rb* \rb to inquire|לִדְר֣וֹשׁ\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb would say|אָמַ֤ר\rb*, “\rb Come|לְכ֥וּ\rb*, \rb let us go|וְנֵלְכָ֖ה\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the seer|הָרֹאֶ֑ה\rb*.” \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the prophet|לַנָּבִיא֙\rb* \rb of today|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb was formerly|לְפָנִ֖ים\rb* \rb called|יִקָּרֵ֥א\rb* \rb the seer|הָרֹאֶֽה׃\rb*.)
\p \v 10 “\rb Good|ט֥וֹב\rb*,”\rb |דְּבָרְךָ֖\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֧וּל\rb* \rb to his servant|לְנַעֲר֛וֹ\rb*. “\rb Come|לְכָ֣ה׀\rb*, \rb let us go|נֵלֵ֑כָה\rb*.” \rb So they set out|וַיֵּֽלְכוּ֙\rb* \rb for|אֶל־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb where|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb the man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of God was|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb And as they|הֵ֗מָּה\rb* \rb were climbing|עֹלִים֙\rb* \rb the hill|בְּמַעֲלֵ֣ה\rb* \rb to the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb*, \rb they|וְהֵ֙מָּה֙\rb* \rb met|מָצְא֣וּ\rb* \rb some young women|נְעָר֔וֹת\rb* \rb coming out|יֹצְא֖וֹת\rb* \rb to draw|לִשְׁאֹ֣ב\rb* \rb water|מָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and asked|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*, “\rb Is|הֲיֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb the seer here|הָרֹאֶֽה׃\rb*\rb |בָּזֶ֖ה\rb*?”
\p \v 12 “\rb Yes|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb*, \rb he is|יֵּ֖שׁ\rb* \rb ahead of you|לְפָנֶ֑יךָ\rb*,” \rb they answered|וַתַּעֲנֶ֧ינָה\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֛ם\rb*\rb |וַתֹּאמַ֥רְנָה\rb*. “\rb Hurry|מַהֵ֣ר׀\rb* \rb now|עַתָּ֗ה\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb today|הַיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb he has come|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb to the city|לָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the people have|לָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb a sacrifice|זֶ֧בַח\rb* \rb on the high place|בַּבָּמָֽה׃\rb*\rb |הַיּ֛וֹם\rb*. \v 13 \rb As soon as you enter|כְּבֹאֲכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֣יר\rb*,\rb |כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb you will find|תִּמְצְא֣וּן\rb* \rb him|אֹת֡וֹ\rb* \rb before|בְּטֶרֶם֩\rb* \rb he goes up|יַעֲלֶ֨ה\rb* \rb to the high place|הַבָּמָ֜תָה\rb* \rb to eat|לֶאֱכֹ֗ל\rb*.\rb |כִּ֠י\rb* \rb The people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb eat|יֹאכַ֤ל\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb he comes|בֹּא֔וֹ\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he|הוּא֙\rb* \rb must bless|יְבָרֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb the sacrifice|הַזֶּ֔בַח\rb*; \rb after that|אַחֲרֵי־\rb*,\rb |כֵ֖ן\rb* \rb the guests|הַקְּרֻאִ֑ים\rb*\rb |וְעַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb will eat|יֹאכְל֣וּ\rb*. \rb Go up|עֲל֔וּ\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |אֹת֥וֹ\rb* \rb at once|כְהַיּ֖וֹם\rb*; \rb you will find|תִּמְצְא֥וּן\rb* \rb him|אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb So Saul and his servant went up|וַֽיַּעֲל֖וּ\rb* \rb toward the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb*, \rb and as they|הֵ֗מָּה\rb* \rb were entering|בָּאִים֙\rb*\rb |בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb it|הָעִ֔יר\rb*, \rb there was|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵל֙\rb* \rb coming|יֹצֵ֣א\rb* \rb toward them|לִקְרָאתָ֔ם\rb* \rb on his way up|לַעֲל֖וֹת\rb* \rb to the high place|הַבָּמָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Now on the day|י֣וֹם\rb*\rb |אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Saul’s|שָׁא֖וּל\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb arrival|בֽוֹא־\rb*, \rb the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb had revealed|גָּלָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |אֹ֣זֶן\rb* \rb to Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֑ל\rb*, \v 16 “\rb At this time|כָּעֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb tomorrow|מָחָ֡ר\rb* \rb I will send|אֶשְׁלַח֩\rb* \rb you|אֵלֶ֨יךָ\rb* \rb a man|אִ֜ישׁ\rb* \rb from the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Benjamin|בִּנְיָמִ֗ן\rb*, \rb and you are to anoint him|וּמְשַׁחְתּ֤וֹ\rb* \rb ruler|לְנָגִיד֙\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֣י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*; \rb he will save|וְהוֹשִׁ֥יעַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb them|עַמִּ֖י\rb* \rb from the hand|מִיַּ֣ד\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb I have looked upon|רָאִ֙יתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֔י\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb their cry|צַעֲקָת֖וֹ\rb* \rb has come|בָּ֥אָה\rb* \rb to Me|אֵלָֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 17 \rb When Samuel|וּשְׁמוּאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb saw|רָאָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֑וּל\rb*, \rb the LORD|וַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb told him|עָנָ֔הוּ\rb*, “\rb Here|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb is the man|הָאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb of whom|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I spoke|אָמַ֣רְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb*; \rb he|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb shall rule|יַעְצֹ֥ר\rb* \rb over My people|בְּעַמִּֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 18 \rb Saul|שָׁא֛וּל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb approached|וַיִּגַּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb in|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the gateway|הַשָּׁ֑עַר\rb* \rb and asked|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb Would you please|נָּ֣א\rb* \rb tell|הַגִּֽידָה־\rb* \rb me|לִ֔י\rb* \rb where|אֵי־\rb*\rb |זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb the seer’s|הָרֹאֶֽה׃\rb* \rb house is|בֵּ֥ית\rb*?”
\p \v 19 “\rb I|אָנֹכִ֣י\rb* \rb am the seer|הָרֹאֶ֔ה\rb*,” \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֜ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |שָׁא֗וּל\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb replied|וַיַּ֨עַן\rb*. “\rb Go up|עֲלֵ֤ה\rb* \rb before me|לְפָנַי֙\rb* \rb to the high place|הַבָּמָ֔ה\rb*, \rb for you shall eat|וַאֲכַלְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb with me|עִמִּ֖י\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֑וֹם\rb*. \rb And when I send you off|וְשִׁלַּחְתִּ֣יךָ\rb* \rb in the morning|בַבֹּ֔קֶר\rb*, \rb I will tell|אַגִּ֥יד\rb* \rb you|לָֽךְ׃\rb* \rb all|וְכֹ֛ל\rb* \rb that is|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb in your heart|בִּֽלְבָבְךָ֖\rb*. \v 20 \rb As for the donkeys|וְלָאֲתֹנ֞וֹת\rb* \rb you lost|הָאֹבְד֣וֹת\rb*\rb |לְךָ֗\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|הַיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb ago|הַיָּמִ֔ים\rb*, \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb worry|תָּ֧שֶׂם\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb*\rb |לִבְּךָ֛\rb* \rb about them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they have been found|נִמְצָ֑אוּ\rb*. \rb And upon whom is|וּלְמִי֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the desire|חֶמְדַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb if not|הֲל֣וֹא\rb* \rb upon you|לְךָ֔\rb* \rb and all|וּלְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb your father’s|אָבִֽיךָ׃ס\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֥ית\rb*?”
\p \v 21 \rb Saul|שָׁא֜וּל\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb replied|וַיַּ֨עַן\rb*, “\rb Am I|אָ֙נֹכִי֙\rb* \rb not|הֲל֨וֹא\rb*\rb |בֶן־\rb* \rb a Benjamite|יְמִינִ֤י\rb* \rb from the smallest|מִקַּטַנֵּי֙\rb* \rb tribe|שִׁבְטֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb and is not my clan|וּמִשְׁפַּחְתִּי֙\rb* \rb the least|הַצְּעִרָ֔ה\rb* \rb of all|מִכָּֽל־\rb* \rb the clans|מִשְׁפְּח֖וֹת\rb* \rb of Benjamin|בִנְיָמִ֑ן\rb*\rb |שִׁבְטֵ֣י\rb*? \rb So why|וְלָ֙מָּה֙\rb* \rb would you say|דִּבַּ֣רְתָּ\rb* \rb such a thing|כַּדָּבָ֖ר\rb*\rb |הַזֶּֽה׃ס\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֔י\rb*?”
\p \v 22 \rb Then Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֤ח\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֣וּל\rb* \rb and|וְאֶֽת־\rb* \rb his servant|נַעֲר֔וֹ\rb*, \rb brought them|וַיְבִיאֵ֖ם\rb* \rb into the hall|לִשְׁכָּ֑תָה\rb*, \rb and seated|וַיִּתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֤ם\rb* \rb in the place|מָקוֹם֙\rb* \rb of honor|בְּרֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb among those who were invited|הַקְּרוּאִ֔ים\rb*\rb |וְהֵ֖מָּה\rb* — \rb about thirty|כִּשְׁלֹשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb in all|אִֽישׁ׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb And Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵל֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to the cook|לַטַּבָּ֔ח\rb*, “\rb Bring|תְּנָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the portion|הַמָּנָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I gave|נָתַ֖תִּי\rb* \rb you|לָ֑ךְ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb and told|אָמַ֣רְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb you to set|שִׂ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb aside|עִמָּֽךְ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 24 \rb So the cook|הַ֠טַּבָּח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb picked up|וַיָּ֣רֶם\rb* \rb the leg|הַשּׁ֨וֹק\rb* \rb and what was attached to it|וְהֶעָלֶ֜יהָ\rb* \rb and set it|וַיָּ֣שֶׂם׀\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֗וּל\rb*. \rb Then Samuel said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb Here is|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb what was kept back|הַנִּשְׁאָר֙\rb*. \rb It was set apart|שִׂים־\rb* \rb for you|לְפָנֶ֣יךָ\rb*. \rb Eat|אֱכֹ֔ל\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֧י\rb* \rb it has been kept|שָֽׁמוּר־\rb* \rb for you|לְךָ֥\rb* \rb for this occasion|לַמּוֹעֵ֛ד\rb*, \rb from the time I said|לֵאמֹ֖ר\rb*, ‘\rb I have invited|קָרָ֑אתִי\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֣ם׀\rb*.’” \rb So Saul|שָׁא֛וּל\rb* \rb dined|וַיֹּ֧אכַל\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb that|הַהֽוּא׃\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb And after they had come down|וַיֵּרְד֥וּ\rb* \rb from the high place|מֵהַבָּמָ֖ה\rb* \rb into the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb*, \rb Samuel spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the roof of his house|הַגָּֽג׃\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb They got up early in the morning|וַיַּשְׁכִּ֗מוּ\rb*,\rb |וַיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb and just before|כַּעֲל֤וֹת\rb* \rb dawn|הַשַּׁ֙חַר֙\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֤ל\rb* \rb called|וַיִּקְרָ֨א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb* \rb on the roof|הַגָּג\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* “\rb Get ready|ק֖וּמָה\rb*, \rb and I will send you on your way|וַאֲשַׁלְּחֶ֑ךָּ\rb*!” \rb So Saul|שָׁא֗וּל\rb* \rb got ready|וַיָּ֣קָם\rb*, \rb and both|שְׁנֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb he|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb and Samuel|וּשְׁמוּאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּצְא֧וּ\rb* \rb outside together|הַחֽוּצָה׃\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb As they|הֵ֗מָּה\rb* \rb were going down|יֽוֹרְדִים֙\rb* \rb to the edge|בִּקְצֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb*, \rb Samuel|וּשְׁמוּאֵ֞ל\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֗וּל\rb*, “\rb Tell|אֱמֹ֥ר\rb* \rb the servant|לַנַּ֛עַר\rb* \rb to go on|וְיַעֲבֹ֥ר\rb* \rb ahead of us|לְפָנֵ֖ינוּ\rb*, \rb but you|וְאַתָּה֙\rb* \rb stay|עֲמֹ֣ד\rb* \rb for a while|כַּיּ֔וֹם\rb*, \rb and I will reveal to you|וְאַשְׁמִיעֲךָ֖\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַ֥ר\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִֽים׃פ\rb*.” \rb So the servant went on|וַֽיַּעֲבֹ֑ר\rb*.
\c 10
\s1 Samuel Anoints Saul
\p \v 1 \rb Then Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֜ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb a flask|פַּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb of oil|הַשֶּׁ֛מֶן\rb*, \rb poured it|וַיִּצֹ֥ק\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb Saul’s head|רֹאשׁ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb kissed him|וַיִּשָּׁקֵ֑הוּ\rb*, \rb and said|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Has not|הֲל֗וֹא\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb anointed you|מְשָׁחֲךָ֧\rb* \rb ruler|לְנָגִֽיד׃\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb His inheritance|נַחֲלָת֖וֹ\rb*?\f + \fr 10:1 \ft Hebrew; LXX \fqa “Has not the LORD anointed you ruler over Israel? And you will rule over the LORD’s people and save them from their enemies around them. This will be the sign to you that the LORD has appointed you to be leader over His inheritance.\f* \v 2 \rb When you leave|בְּלֶכְתְּךָ֤\rb* \rb me|מֵעִמָּדִ֔י\rb* \rb today|הַיּוֹם֙\rb*, \rb you will find|וּמָצָאתָ֩\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵ֨י\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֜ים\rb* \rb at|עִם־\rb* \rb Rachel’s|רָחֵ֛ל\rb* \rb tomb|קְבֻרַ֥ת\rb* \rb in Zelzah|בְּצֶלְצַ֑ח\rb* \rb on the border|בִּגְב֥וּל\rb* \rb of Benjamin|בִּנְיָמִ֖ן\rb*. \rb They will say|וְאָמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֗יךָ\rb*, ‘\rb The donkeys|הָאֲתֹנוֹת֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you seek|הָלַ֣כְתָּ\rb*\rb |לְבַקֵּ֔שׁ\rb* \rb have been found|נִמְצְא֤וּ\rb*, \rb and now|וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb your father|אָבִ֙יךָ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has stopped|נָטַ֤שׁ\rb* \rb worrying about|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb the donkeys|הָאֲתֹנ֔וֹת\rb* \rb and started worrying|וְדָאַ֤ג\rb* \rb about you|לָכֶם֙\rb*, \rb asking|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb What|מָ֥ה\rb* \rb should I do|אֶעֱשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb about my son|לִבְנִֽי׃\rb*?”’
\p \v 3 \rb Then you will go|וְחָלַפְתָּ֨\rb* \rb on|וָהָ֗לְאָה\rb* \rb from there|מִשָּׁ֜ם\rb* \rb until you come|וּבָ֙אתָ֙\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the Oak|אֵל֣וֹן\rb*\f + \fr 10:3 \ft Or \fqa Terebinth \ft or \fqa Great Tree\f* \rb of Tabor|תָּב֔וֹר\rb*. \rb Three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb going up|עֹלִ֥ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb at Bethel|אֵ֑ל\rb* \rb will meet you|וּמְצָא֤וּךָ\rb* \rb there|שָּׁם֙\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָ֞ד\rb* \rb carrying|נֹשֵׂ֣א׀\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb* \rb young goats|גְדָיִ֗ים\rb*, \rb another|וְאֶחָד֙\rb* \rb carrying|נֹשֵׂ֗א\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֙שֶׁת֙\rb* \rb loaves|כִּכְּר֣וֹת\rb* \rb of bread|לֶ֔חֶם\rb*, \rb and another|וְאֶחָ֥ד\rb* \rb carrying|נֹשֵׂ֖א\rb* \rb a skin|נֵֽבֶל־\rb* \rb of wine|יָֽיִן׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb They will greet you|וְשָׁאֲל֥וּ\rb*\rb |לְךָ֖\rb*\rb |לְשָׁל֑וֹם\rb* \rb and give|וְנָתְנ֤וּ\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֙\rb* \rb two|שְׁתֵּי־\rb* \rb loaves of bread|לֶ֔חֶם\rb*, \rb which you will accept|וְלָקַחְתָּ֖\rb* \rb from their hands|מִיָּדָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb After|אַ֣חַר\rb* \rb that|כֵּ֗ן\rb* \rb you will come|תָּבוֹא֙\rb* \rb to Gibeah|גִּבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*,\f + \fr 10:5 \ft Hebrew \fqa Gibeath-Elohim\ft , meaning \fqa the hill of God\f* \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb* \rb have an outpost|נְצִבֵ֣י\rb*.\rb |וִיהִי֩\rb* \rb As you approach|כְבֹאֲךָ֨\rb*\rb |שָׁ֜ם\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֗יר\rb*, \rb you will meet|וּפָגַעְתָּ֞\rb* \rb a group|חֶ֤בֶל\rb* \rb of prophets|נְבִיאִים֙\rb* \rb coming down|יֹרְדִ֣ים\rb* \rb from the high place|מֵֽהַבָּמָ֔ה\rb*, \rb preceded|וְלִפְנֵיהֶ֞ם\rb* \rb by harps|נֵ֤בֶל\rb*, \rb tambourines|וְתֹף֙\rb*, \rb flutes|וְחָלִ֣יל\rb*, \rb and lyres|וְכִנּ֔וֹר\rb*, \rb and they|וְהֵ֖מָּה\rb* \rb will be prophesying|מִֽתְנַבְּאִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Then the Spirit|ר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb will rush|וְצָלְחָ֤ה\rb* \rb upon you|עָלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*, \rb and you will prophesy|וְהִתְנַבִּ֖יתָ\rb* \rb with them|עִמָּ֑ם\rb*; \rb and you will be transformed|וְנֶהְפַּכְתָּ֖\rb* \rb into a different|אַחֵֽר׃\rb* \rb person|לְאִ֥ישׁ\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb |וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb When|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb signs|הָאֹת֥וֹת\rb* \rb have come|תְבֹאֶינָה\rb*, \rb do|עֲשֵׂ֤ה\rb* \rb as the occasion|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb demands|תִּמְצָ֣א\rb*,\rb |יָדֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb God is|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּֽךְ׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb And you shall go|וְיָרַדְתָּ֣\rb* \rb before me|לְפָנַי֮\rb* \rb to Gilgal|הַגִּלְגָּל֒\rb*, \rb and surely|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb I|אָֽנֹכִי֙\rb* \rb will come|יֹרֵ֣ד\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb to offer|לְהַעֲל֣וֹת\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹל֔וֹת\rb* \rb and to sacrifice|לִזְבֹּ֖חַ\rb* \rb peace offerings|שְׁלָמִ֑ים\rb*\rb |זִבְחֵ֣י\rb*. \rb Wait|תּוֹחֵל֙\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעַ֨ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֤ים\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb I come|בּוֹאִ֣י\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and show|וְהוֹדַעְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֔\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you are to do|תַּעֲשֶֽׂה׃\rb*.”
\s1 Samuel’s Signs Fulfilled
\p \v 9 \rb |וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb As Saul turned|כְּהַפְנֹת֤וֹ\rb*\rb |שִׁכְמוֹ֙\rb* \rb to leave|לָלֶ֙כֶת֙\rb*\rb |מֵעִ֣ם\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb changed|וַיַּהֲפָךְ־\rb* \rb Saul’s|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb heart|לֵ֣ב\rb*,\rb |אַחֵ֑ר\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the signs|הָאֹת֥וֹת\rb*\rb |הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb came to pass|וַיָּבֹ֛אוּ\rb* \rb that|הַהֽוּא׃ס\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb*. \v 10 \rb When Saul and his servant arrived|וַיָּבֹ֤אוּ\rb*\rb |שָׁם֙\rb* \rb at Gibeah|הַגִּבְעָ֔תָה\rb*,\f + \fr 10:10 \fqa Gibeah \ft means \fqa the hill\ft .\f*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb a group|חֶֽבֶל־\rb* \rb of prophets|נְבִאִ֖ים\rb* \rb met him|לִקְרָאת֑וֹ\rb*. \rb Then the Spirit|ר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb rushed|וַתִּצְלַ֤ח\rb* \rb upon him|עָלָיו֙\rb*, \rb and he prophesied|וַיִּתְנַבֵּ֖א\rb* \rb along with them|בְּתוֹכָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb When|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb all those|כָּל־\rb* \rb who had formerly|מֵאִתְּמ֣וֹל\rb* \rb known Saul|יֽוֹדְעוֹ֙\rb*\rb |שִׁלְשׁ֔וֹם\rb* \rb saw him|וַיִּרְא֕וּ\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb prophesying|נִבָּ֑א\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the prophets|נְבִאִ֖ים\rb*, \rb they asked|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |הָעָ֜ם\rb* \rb one|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb another|רֵעֵ֗הוּ\rb*, “\rb What|מַה־\rb*\rb |זֶּה֙\rb* \rb has happened|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb to the son|לְבֶן־\rb* \rb of Kish|קִ֔ישׁ\rb*? \rb Is Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb also|הֲגַ֥ם\rb* \rb among the prophets|בַּנְּבִיאִֽים׃\rb*?”
\p \v 12 \rb Then a man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb who lived there|מִשָּׁ֛ם\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb replied|וַיַּ֨עַן\rb*, “\rb And who|וּמִ֣י\rb* \rb is their father|אֲבִיהֶ֑ם\rb*?” \rb So|עַל־\rb* \rb the saying|כֵּן֙\rb* \rb became|הָיְתָ֣ה\rb* \rb a proverb|לְמָשָׁ֔ל\rb*: “\rb Is Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb also|הֲגַ֥ם\rb* \rb among the prophets|בַּנְּבִאִֽים׃\rb*?”
\p \v 13 \rb And when Saul had finished|וַיְכַל֙\rb* \rb prophesying|מֵֽהִתְנַבּ֔וֹת\rb*, \rb he went up|וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb* \rb to the high place|הַבָּמָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb Now Saul’s|שָׁא֥וּל\rb* \rb uncle|דּ֨וֹד\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb him|אֵלָ֛יו\rb* \rb and|וְאֶֽל־\rb* \rb his servant|נַעֲר֖וֹ\rb*, “\rb Where|אָ֣ן\rb* \rb did you go|הֲלַכְתֶּ֑ם\rb*?”
\p “\rb To look for|לְבַקֵּשׁ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the donkeys|הָ֣אֲתֹנ֔וֹת\rb*,” \rb Saul replied|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*. “\rb When we saw|וַנִּרְאֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |כִי־\rb* \rb they were not to be found|אַ֔יִן\rb*, \rb we went|וַנָּב֖וֹא\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵֽל׃\rb*.”
\p \v 15 “\rb Tell|הַגִּֽידָה־\rb*\rb |נָּ֣א\rb* \rb me|לִ֔י\rb*,” \rb Saul’s|שָׁא֑וּל\rb* \rb uncle|דּ֣וֹד\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb what|מָֽה־\rb* \rb did Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb say to you|אָמַ֥ר\rb*?”
\p \v 16 \rb And Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |דּוֹד֔וֹ\rb*, “\rb He assured|הַגֵּ֤ד\rb*\rb |הִגִּיד֙\rb* \rb us|לָ֔נוּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the donkeys|הָאֲתֹנ֑וֹת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb had been found|נִמְצְא֖וּ\rb*.” \rb But Saul did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb tell|הִגִּ֣יד\rb* \rb his uncle|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵֽל׃פ\rb* \rb had said|אָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb about|דְּבַ֤ר\rb* \rb the kingship|הַמְּלוּכָה֙\rb*.
\s1 Saul Proclaimed King
\p \v 17 \rb After this, Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb summoned|וַיַּצְעֵ֤ק\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb at Mizpah|הַמִּצְפָּֽה׃\rb* \v 18 \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר׀\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל פ\rb*, “\rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb says|אָמַ֤ר\rb*: ‘\rb I|אָנֹכִ֛י\rb* \rb brought|הֶעֱלֵ֥יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb up out of Egypt|מִמִּצְרָ֑יִם\rb*, \rb and I rescued|וָאַצִּ֤יל\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb from the hands|מִיַּ֣ד\rb* \rb of the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*\rb |וּמִיַּד֙\rb* \rb and of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the kingdoms|הַמַּמְלָכ֔וֹת\rb* \rb that oppressed you|הַלֹּחֲצִ֖ים\rb*.’\rb |אֶתְכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb But today|הַיּ֜וֹם\rb* \rb you|וְאַתֶּ֨ם\rb* \rb have rejected|מְאַסְתֶּ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֗ם\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |ה֣וּא\rb* \rb saves|מוֹשִׁ֣יעַ\rb* \rb you|לָכֶם֮\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb your troubles|רָעוֹתֵיכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb and afflictions|וְצָרֹֽתֵיכֶם֒\rb*, \rb and you have said|וַתֹּ֣אמְרוּ\rb* \rb to Him|ל֔וֹ\rb*, ‘\rb No|כִּי־\rb*, \rb set|תָּשִׂ֣ים\rb* \rb a king|מֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb over us|עָלֵ֑ינוּ\rb*.’ \rb Now therefore|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb present yourselves|הִֽתְיַצְּבוּ֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb by your tribes|לְשִׁבְטֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and clans|וּלְאַלְפֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 20 \rb Thus Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb had all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb come forward|וַיַּקְרֵ֣ב\rb*, \rb and the tribe|שֵׁ֥בֶט\rb* \rb of Benjamin|בִּנְיָמִֽן׃\rb* \rb was selected|וַיִּלָּכֵ֖ד\rb*. \v 21 \rb Then he had the tribe|שֵׁ֤בֶט\rb* \rb of Benjamin|בִּנְיָמִן֙\rb* \rb come forward|וַיַּקְרֵ֞ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb by its clans|לְמִשְׁפַּחְתּוֹ\rb*, \rb and the clan|מִשְׁפַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb of Matri|הַמַּטְרִ֑י\rb* \rb was selected|וַתִּלָּכֵ֖ד\rb*.\f + \fr 10:21 \ft LXX includes \fqa And he brought the family of the Matrites near, man by man.\f* \rb Finally, Saul|שָׁא֣וּל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Kish|קִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb was selected|וַיִּלָּכֵד֙\rb*. \rb But when they looked for him|וַיְבַקְשֻׁ֖הוּ\rb*, \rb they could not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb find him|נִמְצָֽא׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb So again|עוֹד֙\rb* \rb they inquired|וַיִּשְׁאֲלוּ־\rb* \rb of the LORD|בַּֽיהוָ֔ה\rb*, “\rb Has the man|אִ֑ישׁס\rb* \rb come|הֲבָ֥א\rb* \rb here|הֲלֹ֣ם\rb* \rb yet|ע֖וֹד\rb*?”
\p \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Behold|הִנֵּה־\rb*, \rb he has hidden|נֶחְבָּ֖א\rb* \rb himself|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb among|אֶל־\rb* \rb the baggage|הַכֵּלִֽים׃\rb*.”
\p \v 23 \rb So they ran|וַיָּרֻ֙צוּ֙\rb* \rb and brought Saul|וַיִּקָּחֻ֣הוּ\rb*\rb |מִשָּׁ֔ם\rb*, \rb and when he stood|וַיִּתְיַצֵּ֖ב\rb* \rb among|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb*, \rb he was a head|מִשִּׁכְמ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |וָמָֽעְלָה׃\rb* \rb taller|וַיִּגְבַּהּ֙\rb* \rb than any|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb of the others|הָעָ֔ם\rb*. \v 24 \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֜ל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֗ם\rb*, “\rb Do you see|הַרְּאִיתֶם֙\rb* \rb the one|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |כִּ֛י\rb* \rb has chosen|בָּֽחַר־\rb*? \rb There is no one|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb like him|כָּמֹ֖הוּ\rb* \rb among all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb*.”
\p \rb And all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֛ם\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמְר֖וּ\rb* \rb shouted|וַיָּרִ֧עוּ\rb*, “\rb Long live|יְחִ֥י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃פ\rb*!”
\p \v 25 \rb Then Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֜ל\rb* \rb explained|וַיְדַבֵּ֨ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb the rights|מִשְׁפַּ֣ט\rb* \rb of kingship|הַמְּלֻכָ֔ה\rb*. \rb He wrote them|וַיִּכְתֹּ֣ב\rb* \rb on a scroll|בַּסֵּ֔פֶר\rb* \rb and laid it up|וַיַּנַּ֖ח\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb And Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sent all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb away|וַיְשַׁלַּ֧ח\rb*, \rb each|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb to his own home|לְבֵיתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb also|וְגַ֨ם־\rb* \rb went|הָלַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb to his home|לְבֵית֖וֹ\rb* \rb in Gibeah|גִּבְעָ֑תָה\rb*, \rb and the men of valor|הַחַ֕יִל\rb* \rb whose|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb hearts|בְּלִבָּֽם׃\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb had touched|נָגַ֥ע\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּלְכ֣וּ\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֔וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb But some worthless|בְלִיַּ֣עַל\rb* \rb men|וּבְנֵ֧י\rb* \rb said|אָמְר֗וּ\rb*, “\rb How|מַה־\rb* \rb can this man|זֶ֔ה\rb* \rb save us|יֹּשִׁעֵ֙נוּ֙\rb*?” \rb So they despised him|וַיִּבְזֻ֕הוּ\rb* \rb and brought|הֵבִ֥יאוּ\rb* \rb him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb no|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb gifts|מִנְחָ֑ה\rb*; \rb but Saul remained|וַיְהִ֖י\rb* \rb silent about it|כְּמַחֲרִֽישׁ׃פ\rb*.\f + \fr 10:27 \ft MT and LXX; one DSS manuscript includes \fqa Nahash, king of the Ammonites, had viciously oppressed the people of Gad and Reuben, gouging out the right eye of each Israelite dwelling there. He would not allow anyone to rescue them, and there was no Israelite east of the Jordan whose right eye had not been gouged out. But 7,000 men had escaped from the Ammonites and settled in Jabesh-gilead.\f*
\c 11
\s1 Saul Defeats the Ammonites
\p \v 1 \rb Then Nahash|נָחָשׁ֙\rb*\f + \fr 11:1 \ft DSS and LXX \fqa About a month later Nahash\f* \rb the Ammonite|הָֽעַמּוֹנִ֔י\rb* \rb came up|וַיַּ֗עַל\rb* \rb and laid siege|וַיִּ֖חַן\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb Jabesh-gilead|יָבֵ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |גִּלְעָ֑ד\rb*. \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb the men|אַנְשֵׁ֤י\rb* \rb of Jabesh|יָבֵישׁ֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמְר֜וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb him|נָחָ֔שׁ\rb*, “\rb Make|כְּרָת־\rb* \rb a treaty|בְרִ֖ית\rb*\f + \fr 11:1 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa berit \ft are translated in most passages as \fqa covenant\ft .\f* \rb with us|לָ֥נוּ\rb*, \rb and we will serve you|וְנַעַבְדֶֽךָּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 2 \rb But Nahash|נָחָשׁ֙\rb* \rb the Ammonite|הָעַמּוֹנִ֔י\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*,\rb |אֲלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* “\rb I will make a treaty|אֶכְרֹ֣ת\rb* \rb with you|לָכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb on one condition|בְּזֹאת֙\rb*, \rb that I may put out|בִּנְק֥וֹר\rb*\rb |לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb everyone’s|כָּל־\rb* \rb right|יָמִ֑ין\rb* \rb eye|עֵ֣ין\rb* \rb and bring|וְשַׂמְתִּ֥יהָ\rb* \rb reproach|חֶרְפָּ֖ה\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.”
\p \v 3 “\rb Hold off|הֶ֤רֶף\rb* \rb for|לָ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֔ים\rb*,” \rb replied|וַיֹּאמְר֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֜יו\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Jabesh|יָבֵ֗ישׁ\rb*, “\rb and let us send|וְנִשְׁלְחָה֙\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִ֔ים\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb*\rb |גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb If|וְאִם־\rb* \rb there is no one|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb to save|מוֹשִׁ֛יעַ\rb* \rb us|אֹתָ֖נוּ\rb*, \rb we will surrender|וְיָצָ֥אנוּ\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb When the messengers|הַמַּלְאָכִים֙\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֤אוּ\rb* \rb to Gibeah|גִּבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb and relayed|וַיְדַבְּר֥וּ\rb* \rb these words|הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb in the hearing|בְּאָזְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb*, \rb they all|כָל־\rb*\rb |הָעָ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb wept|וַיִּבְכּֽוּ׃\rb* \rb aloud|וַיִּשְׂא֧וּ\rb*\rb |קוֹלָ֖ם\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Just then|וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֗וּל\rb* \rb was returning|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb*, \rb behind|אַחֲרֵ֤י\rb* \rb his oxen|הַבָּקָר֙\rb*. “\rb What troubles|מַה־\rb* \rb the people|לָּעָ֖ם\rb*?” \rb asked|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb*. “\rb Why|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb are they weeping|יִבְכּ֑וּ\rb*?” \rb And they relayed|וַיְסַ֨פְּרוּ־\rb* \rb to him|ל֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the words of|דִּבְרֵ֖י\rb* \rb the men|אַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb from Jabesh|יָבֵֽישׁ׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb When Saul heard|בְּשָׁמְעוֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb*, \rb the Spirit|רֽוּחַ־\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb rushed|וַתִּצְלַ֤ח\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb him|שָׁא֔וּל\rb*, \rb and he burned with great anger|אַפּ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |וַיִּ֥חַר\rb*\rb |מְאֹֽד׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb He took|וַיִּקַּח֩\rb* \rb a pair|צֶ֨מֶד\rb* \rb of oxen|בָּקָ֜ר\rb*, \rb cut them into pieces|וַֽיְנַתְּחֵ֗הוּ\rb*, \rb and sent them|וַיְשַׁלַּ֞ח\rb* \rb by|בְּיַ֣ד\rb* \rb messengers|הַמַּלְאָכִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the land|גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֮\rb*, \rb proclaiming|לֵאמֹר֒\rb*, “\rb This is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb will be done|יֵעָשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb to the oxen|לִבְקָר֑וֹ\rb* \rb of anyone who|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb does not|אֵינֶ֨נּוּ\rb* \rb march|יֹצֵ֜א\rb* \rb behind|אַחֲרֵ֤י\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb*\rb |וְאַחַ֣ר\rb* \rb and Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֔ל\rb*.”
\p \rb Then the terror|פַּֽחַד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb fell|וַיִּפֹּ֤ל\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb*, \rb and they came out together|וַיֵּצְא֖וּ\rb* \rb as one|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb man|כְּאִ֥ישׁ\rb*. \v 8 \rb And when Saul numbered them|וַֽיִּפְקְדֵ֖ם\rb* \rb at Bezek|בְּבָ֑זֶק\rb*, \rb there were|וַיִּהְי֤וּ\rb* \rb 300,000|שְׁלֹ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֣וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶ֔לֶף\rb* \rb Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb and 30,000|שְׁלֹשִׁ֥ים\rb*\f + \fr 11:8 \ft DSS and LXX \fqa 70,000\f*\rb |אָֽלֶף׃\rb* \rb men|וְאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb*. \v 9 \rb So they said|וַיֹּאמְר֞וּ\rb* \rb to the messengers|לַמַּלְאָכִ֣ים\rb* \rb who had come|הַבָּאִ֗ים\rb*, “\rb Tell|תֹֽאמְרוּן֙\rb*\rb |כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the men|לְאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb of Jabesh-gilead|יָבֵ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |גִּלְעָ֔ד\rb*: ‘\rb Deliverance|תְּשׁוּעָ֖ה\rb* \rb will be|תִּהְיֶֽה־\rb* \rb yours|לָכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb tomorrow|מָחָ֛ר\rb* \rb by the time the sun|הַשָּׁ֑מֶשׁ\rb*\rb |וַיָּבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb is hot|בְּחֹם\rb*.’”
\p \rb And when the messengers|הַמַּלְאָכִ֗ים\rb* \rb relayed this|וַיַּגִּ֛ידוּ\rb* \rb to the men|לְאַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of Jabesh|יָבֵ֖ישׁ\rb*, \rb they rejoiced|וַיִּשְׂמָֽחוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Then the men|אַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of Jabesh|יָבֵ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb said to Nahash|וַֽיֹּאמְרוּ֙\rb*, “\rb Tomorrow|מָחָ֖ר\rb* \rb we will come out|נֵצֵ֣א\rb*,\rb |אֲלֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and you can do|וַעֲשִׂיתֶ֣ם\rb* \rb with us|לָּ֔נוּ\rb* \rb whatever|כְּכָל־\rb* \rb seems good|הַטּ֖וֹב\rb* \rb to you|בְּעֵינֵיכֶֽם׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 11 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb The next day|מִֽמָּחֳרָ֗ת\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֣וּל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb organized|וַיָּ֨שֶׂם\rb* \rb the troops|הָעָם֮\rb* \rb into three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb* \rb divisions|רָאשִׁים֒\rb*, \rb and during the morning|הַבֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb watch|בְּאַשְׁמֹ֣רֶת\rb* \rb they invaded|וַיָּבֹ֤אוּ\rb*\rb |בְתוֹךְ־\rb* \rb the camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶה֙\rb* \rb of the Ammonites|עַמּ֖וֹן\rb* \rb and slaughtered them|וַיַּכּ֥וּ\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the hottest part|חֹ֣ם\rb* \rb of the day|הַיּ֑וֹם\rb*. \rb And|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb the survivors|הַנִּשְׁאָרִים֙\rb* \rb were so scattered|וַיָּפֻ֔צוּ\rb* \rb that no|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb two|שְׁנַ֥יִם\rb* \rb of them|בָ֖ם\rb* \rb were left|נִשְׁאֲרוּ־\rb* \rb together|יָֽחַד׃\rb*.
\s1 Saul Confirmed as King
\p \v 12 \rb Then the people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֔ל\rb*, “\rb Who|מִ֣י\rb* \rb said|הָאֹמֵ֔ר\rb* \rb that Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb should not reign|יִמְלֹ֣ךְ\rb* \rb over us|עָלֵ֑ינוּ\rb*? \rb Bring|תְּנ֥וּ\rb* \rb those men here|הָאֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb so we can kill them|וּנְמִיתֵֽם׃\rb*!”
\p \v 13 \rb But Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb ordered|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb No|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb one|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb shall be put to death|יוּמַ֥ת\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֛וֹם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb has worked|עָשָֽׂה־\rb* \rb salvation|תְּשׁוּעָ֖ה\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb Then Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵל֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb*, “\rb Come|לְכ֖וּ\rb*, \rb let us go|וְנֵלְכָ֣ה\rb* \rb to Gilgal|הַגִּלְגָּ֑ל\rb* \rb and renew|וּנְחַדֵּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb the kingship|הַמְּלוּכָֽה׃\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb*.”
\p \v 15 \rb So all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֜ם\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּלְכ֨וּ\rb* \rb to Gilgal|הַגִּלְגָּ֗ל\rb* \rb and|שָׁ֨ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb confirmed Saul|שָׁא֜וּל\rb* \rb as king|וַיַּמְלִכוּ֩\rb* \rb in the presence of|לִפְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |בַּגִּלְגָּ֔ל\rb*. \rb There|שָׁ֛ם\rb* \rb they sacrificed|וַיִּזְבְּחוּ־\rb* \rb peace offerings|שְׁלָמִ֖ים\rb*\rb |זְבָחִ֥ים\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and Saul|שָׁא֛וּל\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |אַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb rejoiced|וַיִּשְׂמַ֨ח\rb*\rb |שָׁ֥ם\rb* \rb greatly|עַד־\rb*\rb |מְאֹֽד׃פ\rb*.
\c 12
\s1 Samuel’s Farewell Address
\p \v 1 \rb Then Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵל֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*,\rb |הִנֵּה֙\rb* “\rb I have listened|שָׁמַ֣עְתִּי\rb* \rb to your voice|בְקֹֽלְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb in all|לְכֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb that you have said|אֲמַרְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb to me|לִ֑י\rb*, \rb and I have set|וָאַמְלִ֥יךְ\rb* \rb over you|עֲלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb a king|מֶֽלֶךְ׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֞ה\rb* \rb here is|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ׀\rb* \rb walking|מִתְהַלֵּ֣ךְ\rb* \rb before you|לִפְנֵיכֶ֗ם\rb*, \rb and I|וַאֲנִי֙\rb* \rb am old|זָקַ֣נְתִּי\rb* \rb and gray|וָשַׂ֔בְתִּי\rb*, \rb and my sons|וּבָנַ֖י\rb* \rb are here|הִנָּ֣ם\rb* \rb with you|אִתְּכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb I|וַאֲנִי֙\rb* \rb have walked|הִתְהַלַּ֣כְתִּי\rb* \rb before you|לִפְנֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb from my youth|מִנְּעֻרַ֖י\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Here I am|הִנְנִ֣י\rb*. \rb Bear witness|עֲנ֣וּ\rb* \rb against me|בִי֩\rb* \rb before|נֶ֨גֶד\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb and before|וְנֶ֣גֶד\rb* \rb His anointed|מְשִׁיח֗וֹ\rb*:\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Whose|מִ֨י\rb* \rb ox|שׁוֹר֩׀\rb* \rb or donkey|וַחֲמ֧וֹר\rb* \rb have I taken|לָקַ֜חְתִּי\rb*? \rb Whom|מִ֣י\rb*\rb |לָקַ֗חְתִּי\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb have I cheated|עָשַׁ֙קְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |מִ֣י\rb* \rb or oppressed|רַצּ֔וֹתִי\rb*? \rb From whose|מִ֤י\rb* \rb hand|וּמִיַּד־\rb*\rb |מִי֙\rb* \rb have I accepted|לָקַ֣חְתִּי\rb* \rb a bribe|כֹ֔פֶר\rb* \rb and closed|וְאַעְלִ֥ים\rb* \rb my eyes|עֵינַ֖י\rb*\rb |בּ֑וֹ\rb*? \rb Tell me, and I will restore it|וְאָשִׁ֖יב\rb*\f + \fr 12:3 \ft Hebrew \fqa And I will restore it\ft ; LXX \fqa Testify against me, and I will restore it\f* \rb to you|לָכֶֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 4 “\rb You have not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb cheated us|עֲשַׁקְתָּ֖נוּ\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb oppressed us|רַצּוֹתָ֑נוּ\rb*,” \rb they replied|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb*, “\rb nor|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb have you taken|לָקַ֥חְתָּ\rb* \rb anything|מְאֽוּמָה׃\rb* \rb from the hand|מִיַּד־\rb* \rb of man|אִ֖ישׁ\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb Samuel said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵיהֶ֜ם\rb*, “\rb The LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb is a witness|עֵ֧ד\rb* \rb against you|בָּכֶ֗ם\rb*, \rb and His anointed|מְשִׁיחוֹ֙\rb* \rb is a witness|וְעֵ֤ד\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*,\rb |הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you have not|לֹ֧א\rb* \rb found|מְצָאתֶ֛ם\rb* \rb anything|מְא֑וּמָה\rb* \rb in my hand|בְּיָדִ֖י\rb*.”
\p “\rb He is a witness|עֵֽד׃פ\rb*,” \rb they replied|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Then Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb*, “\rb The LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb is the One who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb*\f + \fr 12:6 \ft Hebrew; LXX \fqa The LORD is the witness who\f* \rb appointed|עָשָׂה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽת־\rb* \rb and Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֔ן\rb*, \rb and who|וַאֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb brought|הֶעֱלָ֛ה\rb* \rb your fathers up|אֲבֹתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb present yourselves|הִֽתְיַצְּב֛וּ\rb*, \rb so that I may confront|וְאִשָּׁפְטָ֥ה\rb* \rb you|אִתְּכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb with all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the righteous acts|צִדְק֣וֹת\rb* \rb He|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb has done|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb for you|אִתְּכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb your fathers|אֲבוֹתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb When|כַּֽאֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb went|בָּ֥א\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*,\f + \fr 12:8 \ft Hebrew; LXX includes \fqa and the Egyptians oppressed them\f* \rb your fathers|אֲבֽוֹתֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb cried out|וַיִּזְעֲק֤וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and He|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sent them|וַיִּשְׁלַ֨ח\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽת־\rb* \rb and Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֗ן\rb*, \rb who brought|וַיּוֹצִ֤יאוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your fathers|אֲבֹֽתֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb out of Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and settled them|וַיֹּשִׁב֖וּם\rb* \rb in this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb place|בַּמָּק֥וֹם\rb*. \v 9 \rb But they forgot|וַֽיִּשְׁכְּח֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb their God|אֱלֹהֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb and He sold|וַיִּמְכֹּ֣ר\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֡ם\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַ֣ד\rb* \rb of Sisera|סִֽיסְרָא֩\rb* \rb the commander|שַׂר־\rb* \rb of the army|צְבָ֨א\rb* \rb of Hazor|חָצ֜וֹר\rb*,\f + \fr 12:9 \ft LXX \fqa the army of Jabin king of Hazor\f* \rb and into the hands|וּבְיַד־\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֗ים\rb*\rb |וּבְיַד֙\rb* \rb and the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Moab|מוֹאָ֔ב\rb*, \rb who fought|וַיִּֽלָּחֲמ֖וּ\rb* \rb against them|בָּֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Then they cried out|וַיִּזְעֲק֤וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּאמֶר\rb*, ‘\rb We have sinned|חָטָ֔אנוּ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb we have forsaken|עָזַ֙בְנוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and served|וַנַּעֲבֹ֥ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Baals|הַבְּעָלִ֖ים\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Ashtoreths|הָעַשְׁתָּר֑וֹת\rb*. \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb deliver us|הַצִּילֵ֛נוּ\rb* \rb from the hands|מִיַּ֥ד\rb* \rb of our enemies|אֹיְבֵ֖ינוּ\rb*, \rb that we may serve You|וְנַעַבְדֶֽךָּ׃\rb*.’
\p \v 11 \rb So the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb Jerubbaal|יְרֻבַּ֣עַל\rb*,\f + \fr 12:11 \fqa Jerubbaal \ft is another name for \fqa Gideon \ft and probably means \fqa let Baal contend\ft ; see \ref Judges 6:32|JDG 6:32\ref*.\f*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Barak|בְּדָ֔ן\rb*,\f + \fr 12:11 \ft LXX and Syriac; Hebrew \fqa Bedan\f*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Jephthah|יִפְתָּ֖ח\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֑ל\rb*,\f + \fr 12:11 \ft LXX and Syriac \fqa Samson\f* \rb and He delivered|וַיַּצֵּ֨ל\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb from the hands|מִיַּ֤ד\rb* \rb of your enemies|אֹֽיְבֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb on every side|מִסָּבִ֔יב\rb*, \rb and you dwelt|וַתֵּשְׁב֖וּ\rb* \rb securely|בֶּֽטַח׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb But when you saw|וַתִּרְא֗וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Nahash|נָחָ֞שׁ\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of the Ammonites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |עַמּוֹן֮\rb* \rb was moving|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb against you|עֲלֵיכֶם֒\rb*, \rb you said|וַתֹּ֣אמְרוּ\rb* \rb to me|לִ֔י\rb*, ‘\rb No|לֹ֕א\rb*,\rb |כִּי־\rb* \rb we must have a king|מֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb to rule|יִמְלֹ֣ךְ\rb* \rb over us|עָלֵ֑ינוּ\rb*’— \rb even though the LORD|וַיהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb was your king|מַלְכְּכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb here is|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb you have chosen|בְּחַרְתֶּ֖ם\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the one|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you requested|שְׁאֶלְתֶּ֑ם\rb*. \rb Behold|וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb has placed|נָתַ֧ן\rb* \rb a king|מֶֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb over you|עֲלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you fear|תִּֽירְא֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb and serve|וַעֲבַדְתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb Him|אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb and obey|וּשְׁמַעְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb His voice|בְּקֹל֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and if you do not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb rebel|תַמְר֖וּ\rb* \rb against|אֶת־\rb* \rb the command|פִּ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and if|וִהְיִתֶ֣ם\rb* \rb both|גַּם־\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb and|וְגַם־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb rules|מָלַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb over you|עֲלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb follow|אַחַ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God, then all will be well|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.\f + \fr 12:14 \fqa then all will be well \ft is implied; Literally \fqa If you fear the LORD and serve Him and obey His voice, and if you do not rebel against the command of the LORD, (then) both you and the king who reigns over you will follow the LORD your God.\f* \v 15 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you disobey|לֹ֤א\rb*\rb |תִשְׁמְעוּ֙\rb*\rb |בְּק֣וֹל\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and rebel|וּמְרִיתֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb against His|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb command|פִּ֣י\rb*, \rb then the hand|יַד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb will be|וְהָיְתָ֧ה\rb* \rb against you|בָּכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb as it was against your fathers|וּבַאֲבֹתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.\f + \fr 12:15 \ft Hebrew; LXX \fqa against your king\f*
\p \v 16 \rb Now|עַתָּה֙\rb*, \rb therefore|גַּם־\rb*, \rb present yourselves|הִתְיַצְּב֣וּ\rb* \rb and see|וּרְא֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb great|הַגָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb thing|הַדָּבָ֥ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb will do|עֹשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb before your eyes|לְעֵינֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb Is it not|הֲל֤וֹא\rb* \rb the wheat|חִטִּים֙\rb* \rb harvest|קְצִיר־\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb*? \rb I will call|אֶקְרָא֙\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb to send|וְיִתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb thunder|קֹל֖וֹת\rb* \rb and rain|וּמָטָ֑ר\rb*, \rb so that you will know|וּדְע֣וּ\rb* \rb and see|וּרְא֗וּ\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb what a great|רַבָּה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb evil|רָעַתְכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb you have committed|עֲשִׂיתֶם֙\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb by asking|לִשְׁא֥וֹל\rb* \rb for|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb a king|מֶֽלֶךְ׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 18 \rb So Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵל֙\rb* \rb called|וַיִּקְרָ֤א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and on that|הַה֑וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּתֵּ֧ן\rb* \rb thunder|קֹלֹ֥ת\rb* \rb and rain|וּמָטָ֖ר\rb*.
\p \rb As a result, all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֥ם\rb* \rb greatly|מְאֹ֛ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb feared|וַיִּירָ֨א\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb They|כָל־\rb*\rb |הָעָ֜ם\rb* \rb pleaded|וַיֹּאמְר֨וּ\rb* \rb with|אֶל־\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֗ל\rb*, “\rb Pray|הִתְפַּלֵּ֧ל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb for|בְּעַד־\rb* \rb your servants|עֲבָדֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb so that we will not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb die|נָמ֑וּת\rb*! \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb we have added|יָסַ֤פְנוּ\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb our sins|חַטֹּאתֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb the evil|רָעָ֔ה\rb* \rb of asking|לִשְׁאֹ֥ל\rb* \rb for|לָ֖נוּ\rb* \rb a king|מֶֽלֶךְ׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 20 “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּירָ֔אוּ\rb*,” \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֤ל\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |הָעָם֙\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*. “\rb Even though you|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb have committed|עֲשִׂיתֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb*\rb |אַ֗ךְ\rb* \rb evil|הָרָעָ֖ה\rb*, \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb turn aside|תָּס֙וּרוּ֙\rb* \rb from following|מֵאַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb but serve|וַעֲבַדְתֶּ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb your heart|לְבַבְכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb Do not|וְלֹ֖א\rb* \rb turn aside|תָּס֑וּרוּ\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb worthless|הַתֹּ֗הוּ\rb* \rb things that|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb cannot|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb profit you|יוֹעִ֛ילוּ\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb or deliver you|יַצִּ֖ילוּ\rb*, \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb they are|הֵֽמָּה׃\rb* \rb empty|תֹ֥הוּ\rb*. \v 22 \rb Indeed|כִּ֠י\rb*, \rb for the sake|בַּעֲב֖וּר\rb* \rb of His great|הַגָּד֑וֹל\rb* \rb name|שְׁמ֣וֹ\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb abandon|יִטֹּ֤שׁ\rb* \rb His people|עַמּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb He|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb was pleased|הוֹאִ֣יל\rb* \rb to make|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb His|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb own|לְעָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb As for|גַּ֣ם\rb* \rb me|אָנֹכִ֗י\rb*, \rb far be it from me|חָלִ֤ילָה\rb* \rb that I|לִּי֙\rb* \rb should sin|מֵחֲטֹ֣א\rb* \rb against the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb by ceasing|מֵחֲדֹ֖ל\rb* \rb to pray|לְהִתְפַּלֵּ֣ל\rb* \rb for you|בַּעַדְכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb And I will continue to teach|וְהוֹרֵיתִ֣י\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb the good|הַטּוֹבָ֖ה\rb* \rb and right|וְהַיְשָׁרָֽה׃\rb* \rb way|בְּדֶ֥רֶךְ\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb Above all|אַ֣ךְ׀\rb*, \rb fear|יְר֣אוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb and serve|וַעֲבַדְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb Him|אֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb faithfully|בֶּאֱמֶ֖ת\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb your heart|לְבַבְכֶ֑ם\rb*;\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb consider|רְא֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb great things He has done|הִגְדִּ֖ל\rb* \rb for you|עִמָּכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you persist in doing evil|הָרֵ֖עַ\rb*\rb |תָּרֵ֑עוּ\rb*, \rb both|גַּם־\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb and|גַּֽם־\rb* \rb your king|מַלְכְּכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb will be swept away|תִּסָּפֽוּ׃פ\rb*.”
\c 13
\s1 War with the Philistines
\p \v 1 \rb Saul|שָׁא֣וּל\rb* \rb was thirty|בֶּן־\rb* \rb years old|שָׁנָ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 13:1 \ft A few late LXX manuscripts; MT \fqa Saul was a son of a year\f* \rb when he became king|בְּמָלְכ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb forty-two|וּשְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֔ים\rb*.\f + \fr 13:1 \ft Or \fqa over Israel forty years\ft (see \ref Acts 13:21|ACT 13:21\ref*); MT \fqa over Israel two years\f* \v 2 \rb He|שָׁא֜וּל\rb* \rb chose|וַיִּבְחַר־\rb* \rb for himself|ל֨וֹ\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb thousand men|אֲלָפִים֮\rb* \rb of Israel|מִיִּשְׂרָאֵל֒\rb*: \rb Two thousand|אַלְפַּ֗יִם\rb* \rb were|וַיִּהְי֨וּ\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֜וּל\rb* \rb at Michmash|בְּמִכְמָשׂ֙\rb* \rb and in the hill country|וּבְהַ֣ר\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of Bethel|אֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb and a thousand|וְאֶ֗לֶף\rb* \rb were|הָיוּ֙\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb Jonathan|י֣וֹנָתָ֔ן\rb* \rb in Gibeah|בְּגִבְעַ֖ת\rb* \rb of Benjamin|בִּנְיָמִ֑ין\rb*. \rb And the rest|וְיֶ֣תֶר\rb* \rb of the troops|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb he sent away|שִׁלַּ֖ח\rb*, \rb each|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb to his own home|לְאֹהָלָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Then Jonathan|יוֹנָתָ֗ן\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb attacked|וַיַּ֣ךְ\rb* \rb the Philistine|פְּלִשְׁתִּים֙\rb* \rb outpost|נְצִ֤יב\rb* \rb at Geba|בְּגֶ֔בַע\rb*, \rb and the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb* \rb heard about it|וַֽיִּשְׁמְע֖וּ\rb*. \rb So Saul|וְשָׁאוּל֩\rb* \rb blew|תָּקַ֨ע\rb* \rb the ram’s horn|בַּשּׁוֹפָ֤ר\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb Let the Hebrews|הָעִבְרִֽים׃\rb* \rb hear|יִשְׁמְע֖וּ\rb*!”
\p \v 4 \rb And all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֞ל\rb* \rb heard|שָׁמְע֣וּ\rb* \rb the news|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb*: “\rb Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has attacked|הִכָּ֤ה\rb* \rb an outpost|נְצִ֣יב\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb and now|וְגַם־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb has become a stench|נִבְאַשׁ\rb* \rb to the Philistines|בַּפְּלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb*!” \rb Then the people|הָעָ֛ם\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb were summoned|וַיִּצָּעֲק֥וּ\rb* \rb to join Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb at Gilgal|הַגִּלְגָּֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Now the Philistines|וּפְלִשְׁתִּ֞ים\rb* \rb assembled|נֶאֶסְפ֣וּ׀\rb* \rb to fight|לְהִלָּחֵ֣ם\rb* \rb against|עִם־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb with three|שְׁלֹשִׁ֨ים\rb* \rb thousand|אֶ֤לֶף\rb*\f + \fr 13:5 \ft Some LXX manuscripts and Syriac; Hebrew \fqa thirty thousand\f* \rb chariots|רֶ֙כֶב֙\rb*, \rb six|וְשֵׁ֤שֶׁת\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִים֙\rb* \rb horsemen|פָּרָשִׁ֔ים\rb*, \rb and troops|וְעָ֕ם\rb* \rb as numerous|לָרֹ֑ב\rb* \rb as the sand|כַּח֛וֹל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the seashore|שְׂפַֽת־\rb*\rb |הַיָּ֖ם\rb*. \rb They went up|וַֽיַּעֲלוּ֙\rb* \rb and camped|וַיַּחֲנ֣וּ\rb* \rb at Michmash|בְמִכְמָ֔שׂ\rb*, \rb east|קִדְמַ֖ת\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Beth-aven|אָֽוֶן׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Seeing|רָאוּ֙\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they were|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb in danger|צַר־\rb* \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb their troops|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb were hard-pressed|נִגַּ֖שׂ\rb*, \rb the men|וְאִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֤ל\rb*\rb |הָעָ֗ם\rb* \rb hid|וַיִּֽתְחַבְּא֣וּ\rb* \rb in caves|בַּמְּעָר֤וֹת\rb* \rb and thickets|וּבַֽחֲוָחִים֙\rb*, \rb among the rocks|וּבַסְּלָעִ֔ים\rb*, \rb and in cellars|וּבַצְּרִחִ֖ים\rb* \rb and cisterns|וּבַבֹּרֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb Some Hebrews|וְעִבְרִ֗ים\rb* \rb even crossed|עָֽבְרוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb into the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Gad|גָּ֖ד\rb* \rb and Gilead|וְגִלְעָ֑ד\rb*. \rb Saul, however|וְשָׁאוּל֙\rb*, \rb remained|עוֹדֶ֣נּוּ\rb* \rb at Gilgal|בַגִּלְגָּ֔ל\rb*, \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his troops|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb were quaking in fear|חָרְד֥וּ\rb*\rb |אַחֲרָֽיו׃\rb*.
\s1 Saul’s Unlawful Sacrifice
\p \v 8 \rb And Saul waited|וַיִּיחֶל\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֗ים\rb* \rb for the time appointed|לַמּוֹעֵד֙\rb* \rb by|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb but Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb did not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb come|בָ֥א\rb* \rb to Gilgal|הַגִּלְגָּ֑ל\rb*, \rb and the troops|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb began to desert|וַיָּ֥פֶץ\rb* \rb Saul|מֵעָלָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb So he|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Bring me|הַגִּ֣שׁוּ\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb the burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb and the peace offerings|וְהַשְּׁלָמִ֑ים\rb*.” \rb And he offered up|וַיַּ֖עַל\rb* \rb the burnt offering|הָעֹלָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb Just as he finished|כְּכַלֹּתוֹ֙\rb* \rb offering|לְהַעֲל֣וֹת\rb* \rb the burnt offering|הָעֹלָ֔ה\rb*,\rb |וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb arrived|בָּ֑א\rb*, \rb and Saul|שָׁא֛וּל\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּצֵ֥א\rb*\rb |לִקְרָאת֖וֹ\rb* \rb to greet him|לְבָרֲכֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 “\rb What|מֶ֣ה\rb* \rb have you done|עָשִׂ֑יתָ\rb*?” \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*.
\p \rb And Saul|שָׁא֡וּל\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I saw|רָאִיתִי֩\rb* \rb that|כִֽי־\rb* \rb the troops|הָעָ֜ם\rb* \rb were deserting|נָפַ֨ץ\rb* \rb me|מֵעָלַ֗י\rb*, \rb and that you|וְאַתָּה֙\rb* \rb did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb come|בָ֙אתָ֙\rb* \rb at the appointed|לְמוֹעֵ֣ד\rb* \rb time|הַיָּמִ֔ים\rb* \rb and the Philistines|וּפְלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb were gathering|נֶאֱסָפִ֥ים\rb* \rb at Michmash|מִכְמָֽשׂ׃\rb*, \v 12 \rb I thought|וָאֹמַ֗ר\rb*, ‘\rb Now|עַ֠תָּה\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֤ים\rb* \rb will descend|יֵרְד֨וּ\rb* \rb upon me|אֵלַי֙\rb* \rb at Gilgal|הַגִּלְגָּ֔ל\rb*, \rb and I have not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb sought|חִלִּ֑יתִי\rb* \rb the favor|וּפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*.’ \rb So I felt compelled|וָֽאֶתְאַפַּ֔ק\rb* \rb to offer|וָאַעֲלֶ֖ה\rb* \rb the burnt offering|הָעֹלָֽה׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 13 “\rb You have acted foolishly|נִסְכָּ֑לְתָּ\rb*,” \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb declared|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |שָׁא֖וּל\rb*. “\rb You have not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb kept|שָׁמַ֗רְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the command|מִצְוַ֞ת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb gave you|צִוָּ֔ךְ\rb*;\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb if you had|עַתָּ֗ה\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb would have established|הֵכִ֨ין\rb* \rb your kingdom|מַֽמְלַכְתְּךָ֛\rb* \rb over|אֶל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb for|עַד־\rb* \rb all time|עוֹלָֽם׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb But now|וְעַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb your kingdom|מַמְלַכְתְּךָ֣\rb* \rb will not|לֹא־\rb* \rb endure|תָק֑וּם\rb*; \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb has sought|בִּקֵּשׁ֩\rb* \rb a man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb after His own heart|כִּלְבָב֗וֹ\rb* \rb and appointed him|וַיְצַוֵּ֨הוּ\rb*\rb |יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb ruler|לְנָגִיד֙\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb His people|עַמּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb you have not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb kept|שָׁמַ֔רְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb the command|צִוְּךָ֖\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.”
\p \v 15 \rb Then Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb set out|וַיָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb Gilgal|הַגִּלְגָּ֖ל\rb* \rb and went|וַיַּ֛עַל\rb* \rb up to Gibeah|גִּבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb in Benjamin|בִּנְיָמִ֑ן\rb*.\f + \fr 13:15 \ft LXX \fqa Then Samuel set out, and the rest of the people went up after Saul to meet the army; they went up from Gilgal to Gibeah of Benjamin.\f* \rb And Saul|שָׁא֗וּל\rb* \rb numbered|וַיִּפְקֹ֣ד\rb* \rb the troops|הָעָם֙\rb*\rb |הַנִּמְצְאִ֣ים\rb* \rb who were with him|עִמּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb about six|כְּשֵׁ֥שׁ\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֖וֹת\rb* \rb men|אִֽישׁ׃\rb*.
\s1 Israel without Weapons
\p \v 16 \rb Now Saul|וְשָׁא֞וּל\rb* \rb and Jonathan|וְיוֹנָתָ֣ן\rb* \rb his son|בְּנ֗וֹ\rb* \rb and the troops|וְהָעָם֙\rb*\rb |הַנִּמְצָ֣א\rb* \rb with them|עִמָּ֔ם\rb* \rb were staying|יֹשְׁבִ֖ים\rb* \rb in Geba|בְּגֶ֣בַע\rb* \rb of Benjamin|בִּנְיָמִ֑ן\rb*, \rb while the Philistines|וּפְלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb camped|חָנ֥וּ\rb* \rb at Michmash|בְמִכְמָֽשׂ׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb And raiders|הַמַּשְׁחִ֛ית\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּצֵ֧א\rb* \rb of the Philistine|פְלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb camp|מִמַּחֲנֵ֥ה\rb* \rb in three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb* \rb divisions|רָאשִׁ֑ים\rb*. \rb One|אֶחָ֥ד\rb*\rb |הָרֹ֨אשׁ\rb* \rb headed|יִפְנֶ֛ה\rb* \rb toward|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ophrah|עָפְרָ֖ה\rb*\rb |דֶּ֥רֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb in the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Shual|שׁוּעָֽל׃\rb*, \v 18 \rb another|אֶחָד֙\rb*\rb |וְהָרֹ֤אשׁ\rb*\rb |יִפְנֶ֔ה\rb* \rb toward Beth-horon|חֹר֑וֹן\rb*\rb |דֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb*,\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb and the third|וְהָרֹ֨אשׁ\rb*\rb |אֶחָ֤ד\rb*\rb |יִפְנֶה֙\rb* \rb down the border|הַגְּב֔וּל\rb* \rb road|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb overlooking|הַנִּשְׁקָ֛ף\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the Valley|גֵּ֥י\rb* \rb of Zeboim|הַצְּבֹעִ֖ים\rb* \rb facing the wilderness|הַמִּדְבָּֽרָה׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb And no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb blacksmith|וְחָרָשׁ֙\rb* \rb could be found|יִמָּצֵ֔א\rb* \rb in all|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb had said|אָמַר\rb*, “\rb The Hebrews|הָעִבְרִ֔ים\rb* \rb must not be allowed|פֶּ֚ן\rb* \rb to make|יַעֲשׂ֣וּ\rb* \rb swords|חֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb spears|חֲנִֽית׃\rb*.” \v 20 \rb Instead, all|כָל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb would go down|וַיֵּרְד֥וּ\rb* \rb to the Philistines|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb* \rb to sharpen|לִ֠לְטוֹשׁ\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their plowshares|מַחֲרַשְׁתּ֤וֹ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb mattocks|אֵתוֹ֙\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb axes|קַרְדֻּמּ֔וֹ\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and sickles|מַחֲרֵשָׁתֽוֹ׃\rb*.\f + \fr 13:20 \ft LXX; Hebrew \fqa and plowshares\ft ; (so plowshare appears twice in the Hebrew).\f* \v 21 \rb The charge|הַפְּצִ֣ירָה\rb* \rb was|וְֽהָיְתָ֞ה\rb* \rb a pim|פִ֗ים\rb*\f + \fr 13:21 \fqa A pim \ft possibly refers to a polished stone weighing approximately 0.25 ounces or 7 grams found in excavations. This is equivalent to about two-thirds of a shekel and likely refers to the price charged by the Philistines for the services listed.\f* \rb for sharpening a plowshare|לַמַּֽחֲרֵשֹׁת֙\rb* \rb or mattock|וְלָ֣אֵתִ֔ים\rb*, \rb a third of a shekel|וְלִשְׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb* \rb for sharpening a pitchfork|קִלְּשׁ֖וֹן\rb* \rb or an axe|וּלְהַקַּרְדֻּמִּ֑ים\rb*, \rb and a third of a shekel for repointing|וּלְהַצִּ֖יב\rb* \rb an oxgoad|הַדָּרְבָֽן׃\rb*.\f + \fr 13:21 \ft Hebrew does not include the currency unit \fqa of a shekel \ft charged for sharpening a pitchfork, an axe, or an oxgoad; alternatively, possibly \fqa a third of a pim \ft for each.\f*
\p \v 22 \rb So|וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb on the day|בְּי֣וֹם\rb* \rb of battle|מִלְחֶ֔מֶת\rb* \rb not|וְלֹ֨א\rb* \rb a sword|חֶ֤רֶב\rb* \rb or spear|וַחֲנִית֙\rb* \rb could be found|נִמְצָ֜א\rb* \rb in the hands|בְּיַ֣ד\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb of the troops|הָעָ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Jonathan|יוֹנָתָ֑ן\rb*;\rb |וַתִּמָּצֵ֣א\rb* \rb only Saul|לְשָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb and his son|בְּנֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb Jonathan had weapons|וּלְיוֹנָתָ֖ן\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb And a garrison|מַצַּ֣ב\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֶֽל־\rb* \rb had gone out|וַיֵּצֵא֙\rb* \rb to the pass|מַעֲבַ֖ר\rb* \rb at Michmash|מִכְמָֽשׂ׃ס\rb*.
\c 14
\s1 Jonathan’s Victory over the Philistines
\p \v 1 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb One day|הַיּ֗וֹם\rb* \rb Jonathan|יוֹנָתָ֤ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the young man|הַנַּ֙עַר֙\rb* \rb bearing|נֹשֵׂ֣א\rb* \rb his armor|כֵלָ֔יו\rb*, “\rb Come|לְכָ֗ה\rb*, \rb let us cross over|וְנַעְבְּרָה֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Philistine|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb outpost|מַצַּ֣ב\rb* \rb on the other side|מֵעֵ֣בֶר\rb*\rb |הַלָּ֑ז\rb*.” \rb But Jonathan did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb tell|הִגִּֽיד׃\rb* \rb his father|וּלְאָבִ֖יו\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb Meanwhile, Saul|וְשָׁא֗וּל\rb* \rb was staying|יוֹשֵׁב֙\rb* \rb under|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb the pomegranate tree|הָרִמּ֖וֹן\rb*\f + \fr 14:2 \ft Or \fqa around the rock of Rimmon \ft or \fqa in the pomegranate cave\ft ; see \ref Judges 20:45|JDG 20:45\ref*, Judges 20:47, and Judges 21:13.\f*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in Migron|בְּמִגְר֑וֹן\rb* \rb on the outskirts|בִּקְצֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of Gibeah|הַגִּבְעָ֔ה\rb*. \rb And the troops|וְהָעָם֙\rb* \rb who were|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb numbered about six|כְּשֵׁ֥שׁ\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֖וֹת\rb* \rb men|אִֽישׁ׃\rb*, \v 3 \rb including Ahijah|וַאֲחִיָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb who was wearing|נֹשֵׂ֣א\rb* \rb an ephod|אֵפ֑וֹד\rb*. \rb He was the son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Ichabod’s|אִיכָב֣וֹד׀\rb* \rb brother|אֲחִ֡י\rb* \rb Ahitub|אֲחִט֡וּב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Phinehas|פִּינְחָ֨ס\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Eli|עֵלִ֜י\rb* \rb the priest|כֹּהֵ֧ן׀\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb in Shiloh|בְּשִׁל֖וֹ\rb*. \rb But the troops|וְהָעָם֙\rb* \rb did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֔ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb Jonathan|יוֹנָתָֽן׃\rb* \rb had left|הָלַ֖ךְ\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Now there were cliffs|שֵׁן־\rb*\rb |הַסֶּ֤לַע\rb* \rb on both sides|מֵהָעֵ֙בֶר֙\rb*\rb |מִזֶּ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְשֵׁן־\rb*\rb |הַסֶּ֥לַע\rb*\rb |מֵהָעֵ֖בֶר\rb*\rb |מִזֶּ֑ה\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb of the pass|הַֽמַּעְבְּר֗וֹת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Jonathan|יֽוֹנָתָן֙\rb* \rb intended|בִּקֵּ֤שׁ\rb* \rb to cross|לַֽעֲבֹר֙\rb* \rb to reach|עַל־\rb* \rb the Philistine|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb outpost|מַצַּ֣ב\rb*. \rb One|הָֽאֶחָד֙\rb* \rb was named|וְשֵׁ֤ם\rb* \rb Bozez|בּוֹצֵ֔ץ\rb*\rb |וְשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb and the other|הָאֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb Seneh|סֶֽנֶּה׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb One|הָאֶחָ֛ד\rb* \rb cliff|הַשֵּׁ֧ן\rb* \rb stood|מָצ֥וּק\rb* \rb to the north|מִצָּפ֖וֹן\rb* \rb toward|מ֣וּל\rb* \rb Michmash|מִכְמָ֑שׂ\rb*, \rb and the other|וְהָאֶחָ֥ד\rb* \rb to the south|מִנֶּ֖גֶב\rb* \rb toward|מ֥וּל\rb* \rb Geba|גָּֽבַע׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֜ן\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the young man|הַנַּ֣עַר׀\rb* \rb bearing|נֹשֵׂ֣א\rb* \rb his armor|כֵלָ֗יו\rb*, “\rb Come|לְכָה֙\rb*, \rb let us cross over|וְנַעְבְּרָ֗ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the outpost|מַצַּב֙\rb* \rb of these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb uncircumcised men|הָעֲרֵלִ֣ים\rb*. \rb Perhaps|אוּלַ֛י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb will work|יַעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb on our|לָ֑נוּ\rb* \rb behalf|כִּ֣י\rb*. \rb Nothing|אֵ֤ין\rb* \rb can hinder|מַעְצ֔וֹר\rb* \rb the LORD|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb* \rb from saving|לְהוֹשִׁ֥יעַ\rb*, \rb whether by many|בְּרַ֖ב\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb by few|בִמְעָֽט׃\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb His armor-bearer|נֹשֵׂ֣א\rb*\rb |כֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Do|עֲשֵׂ֖ה\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that is|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in your heart|בִּלְבָבֶ֑ךָ\rb*. \rb Go ahead|נְטֵ֣ה\rb*; \rb I am|הִנְנִ֥י\rb* \rb with you|עִמְּךָ֖\rb* \rb heart and soul|כִּלְבָבֶֽךָ׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 8 “\rb Very well|הִנֵּ֛ה\rb*,” \rb said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb Jonathan|יְה֣וֹנָתָ֔ן\rb*, “\rb we will|אֲנַ֥חְנוּ\rb* \rb cross over|עֹבְרִ֖ים\rb* \rb toward|אֶל־\rb* \rb these men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb and show ourselves|וְנִגְלִ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb If|אִם־\rb*\rb |כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb they say|יֹֽאמְרוּ֙\rb*, ‘\rb Wait|דֹּ֕מּוּ\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb we come|הַגִּיעֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb to you|אֲלֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*,’ \rb then we will stay|וְעָמַ֣דְנוּ\rb* \rb where we are|תַחְתֵּ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb and will not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb go up|נַעֲלֶ֖ה\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb*\rb |כֹּ֨ה\rb* \rb they say|יֹאמְר֜וּ\rb*, ‘\rb Come on up|עֲל֤וּ\rb*,’\rb |עָלֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb then we will go up|וְעָלִ֔ינוּ\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb this|וְזֶה־\rb*\rb |לָּ֖נוּ\rb* \rb will be our sign|הָאֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb that the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has delivered them|נְתָנָ֥ם\rb* \rb into our hands|בְּיָדֵ֑נוּ\rb*.”
\p \v 11 \rb So the two of them|שְׁנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb showed themselves|וַיִּגָּל֣וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the outpost|מַצַּ֖ב\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb*, \rb who|פְלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb exclaimed|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*, “\rb Look|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb*, \rb the Hebrews|עִבְרִים֙\rb* \rb are coming out|יֹֽצְאִ֔ים\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the holes|הַחֹרִ֖ים\rb* \rb in which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb they were hiding|הִתְחַבְּאוּ־\rb*!”\rb |שָֽׁם׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb So the men|אַנְשֵׁ֨י\rb* \rb of the outpost|הַמַּצָּבָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb called out|וַיַּעֲנוּ֩\rb* \rb to Jonathan|יוֹנָתָ֣ן׀\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his armor-bearer|נֹשֵׂ֣א\rb*\rb |כֵלָ֗יו\rb*\rb |וַיֹּֽאמְרוּ֙\rb*, “\rb Come on up|עֲל֣וּ\rb*,\rb |אֵלֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb and we will teach|וְנוֹדִ֥יעָה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb you a lesson|דָּבָ֑ר פ\rb*!”
\p “\rb Follow|עֲלֵ֣ה\rb* \rb me|אַחֲרַ֔י\rb*,” \rb Jonathan|יוֹנָתָ֜ן\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb his armor-bearer|נֹשֵׂ֤א\rb*\rb |כֵלָיו֙\rb*, “\rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has delivered them|נְתָנָ֥ם\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַ֥ד\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.”
\p \v 13 \rb So Jonathan|יוֹנָתָ֗ן\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb climbed up|וַיַּ֣עַל\rb* \rb on his hands|יָדָיו֙\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and feet|רַגְלָ֔יו\rb*, \rb with his armor-bearer|וְנֹשֵׂ֥א\rb*\rb |כֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb behind him|אַחֲרָ֑יו\rb*. \rb And the Philistines fell|וַֽיִּפְּלוּ֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Jonathan|יוֹנָתָ֔ן\rb*, \rb and his armor-bearer|וְנֹשֵׂ֥א\rb*\rb |כֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb followed|אַחֲרָֽיו׃\rb* \rb and finished them off|מְמוֹתֵ֥ת\rb*. \v 14 \rb |וַתְּהִ֞י\rb* \rb In that first|הָרִאשֹׁנָ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb assault|הַמַּכָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb Jonathan|יוֹנָתָ֛ן\rb* \rb and his armor-bearer|וְנֹשֵׂ֥א\rb*\rb |כֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb struck down|הִכָּ֧ה\rb* \rb about twenty|כְּעֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb* \rb men|אִ֑ישׁ\rb* \rb in about half|כְּבַחֲצִ֥י\rb* \rb an acre|מַעֲנָ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 14:14 \ft Hebrew \fqa half a yoke\ft . A \fqa yoke \ft was the amount of land plowed by a pair of yoked oxen in one day.\f*\rb |צֶ֥מֶד\rb* \rb of land|שָׂדֶֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Then panic|חֲרָדָ֨ה\rb* \rb struck the Philistines|וַתְּהִי֩\rb* \rb in the camp|בַמַּחֲנֶ֤ה\rb*, \rb in the field|בַשָּׂדֶה֙\rb*, \rb and among all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb*. \rb Even those in the outposts|הַמַּצָּב֙\rb* \rb and raiding parties|וְהַמַּשְׁחִ֔ית\rb* \rb trembled|חָרְד֖וּ\rb*. \rb Indeed|גַּם־\rb*,\rb |הֵ֑מָּה\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb quaked|וַתִּרְגַּ֣ז\rb*, \rb and panic|לְחֶרְדַּ֥ת\rb* \rb spread|וַתְּהִ֖י\rb* \rb from God|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*.\f + \fr 14:15 \ft Or \fqa and a terrible panic spread\f*
\p \v 16 \rb Now when Saul’s|לְשָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb watchmen|הַצֹּפִים֙\rb* \rb at Gibeah|בְּגִבְעַ֖ת\rb* \rb in Benjamin|בִּנְיָמִ֑ן\rb* \rb looked|וַיִּרְא֤וּ\rb* \rb and saw|וְהִנֵּ֧ה\rb* \rb the troops|הֶהָמ֛וֹן\rb* \rb melting away|נָמ֖וֹג\rb* \rb and scattering|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb in every direction|וַהֲלֹֽם׃פ\rb*,\f + \fr 14:16 \ft Or \fqa melting away and going here and there\f* \v 17 \rb Saul|שָׁא֗וּל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to the troops|לָעָם֙\rb* \rb who were|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֔וֹ\rb*, “\rb Call the roll|פִּקְדוּ־\rb*\rb |נָ֣א\rb* \rb and see|וּרְא֔וּ\rb* \rb who|מִ֖י\rb* \rb has left|הָלַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb us|מֵעִמָּ֑נוּ\rb*.”
\p \rb And when they had called the roll|וַֽיִּפְקְד֔וּ\rb*, \rb they saw|וְהִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb that Jonathan|יוֹנָתָ֖ן\rb* \rb and his armor-bearer|וְנֹשֵׂ֥א\rb*\rb |כֵלָֽיו׃\rb* \rb were not there|אֵ֥ין\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb Then Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to Ahijah|לַֽאֲחִיָּ֔ה\rb*, “\rb Bring|הַגִּ֖ישָׁה\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*.” (\rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb at that|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb time|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb it|אֲר֧וֹן\rb*\rb |הָאֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֞ה\rb* \rb with the Israelites|וּבְנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.)\f + \fr 14:18 \ft Hebrew; LXX \fqa “Bring the ephod.” For at that time he wore the ephod before the Israelites.\f* \v 19 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb While|עַ֣ד\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb* \rb was talking|דִּבֶּ֤ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb*, \rb the commotion|וְהֶהָמ֗וֹן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb in the Philistine|פְלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb camp|בְּמַחֲנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb continued to|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb*\rb |הָל֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb increase|וָרָ֑ב פ\rb*. \rb So Saul|שָׁא֛וּל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb*, “\rb Withdraw|אֱסֹ֥ף\rb* \rb your hand|יָדֶֽךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 20 \rb Then Saul|שָׁא֗וּל\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his troops|הָעָם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |אִתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb assembled|וַיִּזָּעֵ֣ק\rb* \rb and marched|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the battle|הַמִּלְחָמָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and they found the Philistines|וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb in total|מְאֹֽד׃\rb*\rb |גְּדוֹלָ֥ה\rb* \rb confusion|מְהוּמָ֖ה\rb*, \rb with each man|אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb wielding|הָיְתָ֜ה\rb* \rb the sword|חֶ֤רֶב\rb* \rb against his neighbor|בְּרֵעֵ֔הוּ\rb*. \v 21 \rb |הָי֤וּ\rb* \rb And the Hebrews|וְהָעִבְרִ֗ים\rb* \rb who had|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb previously|כְּאֶתְמ֣וֹל\rb*\rb |שִׁלְשׁ֔וֹם\rb* \rb gone up|עָל֥וּ\rb* \rb into the surrounding camps|בַּֽמַּחֲנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb to join the Philistines|לַפְּלִשְׁתִּים֙\rb* \rb now|וְגַם־\rb*\rb |הֵ֗מָּה\rb* \rb went over to|סָבִ֑יב\rb*\rb |לִֽהְיוֹת֙\rb*\rb |עִם־\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb were with|עִם־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb and Jonathan|וְיוֹנָתָֽן׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb When all|וְכֹל֩\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb*\rb |אִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb who had been hiding|הַמִּֽתְחַבְּאִ֤ים\rb* \rb in the hill country|בְּהַר־\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb heard|שָֽׁמְע֔וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb* \rb were fleeing|נָ֖סוּ\rb*, \rb they|הֵ֛מָּה\rb* \rb also|גַם־\rb* \rb joined the battle|בַּמִּלְחָמָֽה׃\rb* \rb in close pursuit|וַֽיַּדְבְּק֥וּ\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb So the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb saved|וַיּ֧וֹשַׁע\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb that|הַה֖וּא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb*, \rb and the battle|וְהַ֨מִּלְחָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb moved on|עָבְרָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb beyond Beth-aven|אָֽוֶן׃\rb*.
\s1 Jonathan Eats the Honey
\p \v 24 \rb Now the men|וְאִֽישׁ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb were in distress|נִגַּ֖שׂ\rb* \rb that|הַה֑וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*, \rb for Saul|שָׁא֨וּל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had placed the troops|הָעָ֜ם\rb* \rb under an oath|וַיֹּאֶל֩\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb*, “\rb Cursed is|אָר֣וּר\rb* \rb the man|הָ֠אִישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb eats|יֹ֨אכַל\rb* \rb any food|לֶ֜חֶם\rb* \rb before|עַד־\rb* \rb evening|הָעֶ֗רֶב\rb*, \rb before I have taken vengeance|וְנִקַּמְתִּי֙\rb* \rb on my enemies|מֵאֹ֣יְבַ֔י\rb*.” \rb So none|וְלֹֽא\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb of the troops|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb tasted|טָעַ֥ם\rb* \rb any food|לָֽחֶם׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb Then all the troops|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb entered|בָּ֣אוּ\rb* \rb the forest|בַיָּ֑עַר\rb*, \rb and there was|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb honey|דְבַ֖שׁ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the ground|פְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַשָּׂדֶֽה׃\rb*. \v 26 \rb And when they|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb entered|וַיָּבֹ֤א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the forest|הַיַּ֔עַר\rb* \rb and saw|וְהִנֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb the flowing|הֵ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb honey|דְּבָ֑שׁ\rb*, \rb not one of them|וְאֵין־\rb* \rb put|מַשִּׂ֤יג\rb* \rb his hand|יָדוֹ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his mouth|פִּ֔יו\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they|הָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb feared|יָרֵ֥א\rb* \rb the oath|הַשְּׁבֻעָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb Jonathan, however|וְיוֹנָתָ֣ן\rb*, \rb had not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb heard that|שָׁמַ֗ע\rb* \rb his father|אָבִיו֮\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had bound the people|הָעָם֒\rb* \rb with the oath|בְּהַשְׁבִּ֣יעַ\rb*. \rb So he reached out|וַיִּשְׁלַ֗ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the end|קְצֵ֤ה\rb* \rb of the staff|הַמַּטֶּה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in his hand|בְּיָד֔וֹ\rb*, \rb dipped|וַיִּטְבֹּ֥ל\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb it into the honeycomb|בְּיַעְרַ֣ת\rb*\rb |הַדְּבָ֑שׁ\rb*, \rb and put|וַיָּ֤שֶׁב\rb* \rb his hand|יָדוֹ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his mouth|פִּ֔יו\rb*, \rb and his eyes|עֵינָֽיו׃\rb* \rb brightened|וַתָּרֹאנָה\rb*.\f + \fr 14:27 \ft Or \fqa his strength was renewed\ft ; similarly in verse 29\f* \v 28 \rb Then|וַיַּעַן֩\rb* \rb one|אִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb of the soldiers|מֵֽהָעָ֜ם\rb* \rb told him|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Your father|אָבִ֤יךָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb bound the troops|הָעָם֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb with a solemn oath|הַשְׁבֵּעַ֩\rb*, \rb saying|הִשְׁבִּ֨יעַ\rb*, ‘\rb Cursed is|אָר֥וּר\rb* \rb the man|הָאִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb eats|יֹ֥אכַל\rb* \rb food|לֶ֖חֶם\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֑וֹם\rb*.’ \rb That is why the people|הָעָֽם׃\rb* \rb are faint|וַיָּ֖עַף\rb*.”
\p \v 29 “\rb My father|אָבִ֖י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has brought trouble|עָכַ֥ר\rb* \rb to the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*,” \rb Jonathan|יֽוֹנָתָ֔ן\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*. “\rb Just look|רְאוּ־\rb*\rb |נָא֙\rb* \rb at how|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb my eyes|עֵינַ֔י\rb* \rb have brightened|אֹ֣רוּ\rb* \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I tasted|טָעַ֔מְתִּי\rb* \rb a little|מְעַ֖ט\rb* \rb of this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb honey|דְּבַ֥שׁ\rb*. \v 30 \rb How much better it would have been|אַ֗ף\rb*\rb |כִּ֡י\rb* \rb if|לוּא֩\rb* \rb the troops|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb had eaten freely|אָכֹ֨ל\rb*\rb |אָכַ֤ל\rb* \rb today|הַיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb from the plunder|מִשְּׁלַ֥ל\rb* \rb they took|מָצָ֑א\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb from their enemies|אֹיְבָ֖יו\rb*!\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Would not|עַתָּ֛ה\rb*\rb |לֹֽא־\rb* \rb the slaughter|מַכָּ֖ה\rb* \rb of the Philistines|בַּפְּלִשְׁתִּֽים׃\rb* \rb have been much greater|רָבְתָ֥ה\rb*?”
\p \v 31 \rb That|הַהוּא֙\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֤וֹם\rb*, \rb after the Israelites had struck down|וַיַּכּ֞וּ\rb* \rb the Philistines|בַּפְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb from Michmash|מִמִּכְמָ֖שׂ\rb* \rb to Aijalon|אַיָּלֹ֑נָה\rb*, \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb were very|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb faint|וַיָּ֥עַף\rb*. \v 32 \rb So they rushed greedily|וַיַּעַשׂ\rb*\rb |הָעָם֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the plunder|שָׁלָל\rb*, \rb taking|וַיִּקְח֨וּ\rb* \rb sheep|צֹ֧אן\rb*, \rb cattle|וּבָקָ֛ר\rb*, \rb and calves|וּבְנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |בָקָ֖ר\rb*. \rb They slaughtered them|וַיִּשְׁחֲטוּ־\rb* \rb on the ground|אָ֑רְצָה\rb* \rb and ate|וַיֹּ֥אכַל\rb*\rb |הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb meat with|עַל־\rb* \rb the blood still in it|הַדָּֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 33 \rb Then someone reported|וַיַּגִּ֤ידוּ\rb* \rb to Saul|לְשָׁאוּל֙\rb*: “\rb Look|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb*, \rb the troops|הָעָ֛ם\rb* \rb are sinning|חֹטִ֥אים\rb* \rb against the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb by eating|לֶאֱכֹ֣ל\rb* \rb meat with|עַל־\rb* \rb the blood still in it|הַדָּ֑ם\rb*.”
\p “\rb You have broken faith|בְּגַדְתֶּ֔ם\rb*,” \rb said Saul|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*. “\rb Roll|גֹּֽלּוּ־\rb* \rb a large|גְּדוֹלָֽה׃\rb* \rb stone|אֶ֥בֶן\rb* \rb over here|אֵלַ֥י\rb* \rb at once|הַיּ֖וֹם\rb*.” \v 34 \rb Then he|שָׁא֣וּל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Go|פֻּ֣צוּ\rb* \rb among the troops|בָעָ֡ם\rb* \rb and tell|וַאֲמַרְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֡ם\rb*, ‘\rb Each man|אִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb must bring|הַגִּ֣ישׁוּ\rb* \rb me|אֵלַי֩\rb* \rb his ox|שׁוֹר֜וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb or his sheep|שְׂיֵ֗הוּ\rb*, \rb slaughter them|וּשְׁחַטְתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb in this place|בָּזֶה֙\rb*, \rb and then eat|וַאֲכַלְתֶּ֔ם\rb*. \rb Do not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb sin|תֶחֶטְא֥וּ\rb* \rb against the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb by eating|לֶאֱכֹ֣ל\rb* \rb meat with|אֶל־\rb* \rb the blood still in it|הַדָּ֑ם\rb*.’”
\p \rb So that night|הַלַּ֖יְלָה\rb* \rb everyone|כָל־\rb*\rb |הָעָ֜ם\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb brought|וַיַּגִּ֨שׁוּ\rb* \rb his ox|שׁוֹר֧וֹ\rb*\rb |בְיָד֛וֹ\rb* \rb and slaughtered|וַיִּשְׁחֲטוּ־\rb* \rb it there|שָֽׁם׃\rb*. \v 35 \rb Then Saul|שָׁא֛וּל\rb* \rb built|וַיִּ֧בֶן\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb*;\rb |אֹת֣וֹ\rb* \rb it was the first|הֵחֵ֔ל\rb* \rb time he had built|לִבְנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 36 \rb And Saul|שָׁא֡וּל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Let us go down|נֵרְדָ֣ה\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵי֩\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֨ים׀\rb* \rb by night|לַ֜יְלָה\rb* \rb and plunder|וְֽנָבֹ֥זָה\rb* \rb them|בָהֶ֣ם׀\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb dawn|א֣וֹר\rb*\rb |הַבֹּ֗קֶר\rb*, \rb leaving|נַשְׁאֵ֤ר\rb* \rb no|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb man alive|אִ֔ישׁ\rb*!”
\p “\rb Do|עֲשֵׂ֑הס\rb* \rb what|כָּל־\rb* \rb seems good|הַטּ֥וֹב\rb* \rb to you|בְּעֵינֶ֖יךָ\rb*,” \rb the troops replied|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb*.
\p \rb But the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb We must consult|נִקְרְבָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb* \rb here|הֲלֹ֖ם\rb*.”
\s1 The People Save Jonathan
\p \v 37 \rb So Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb* \rb inquired|וַיִּשְׁאַ֤ל\rb* \rb of God|בֵּֽאלֹהִ֔ים\rb*, “\rb Shall I go down|הַֽאֵרֵד֙\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb*? \rb Will You give them|הֲתִתְּנֵ֖ם\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַ֣ד\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*?”
\p \rb But God did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb answer him|עָנָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb that|הַהֽוּא׃\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb*.
\p \v 38 \rb Therefore Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Come|גֹּ֣שֽׁוּ\rb* \rb here|הֲלֹ֔ם\rb*, \rb all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb you leaders|פִּנּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the troops|הָעָ֑ם\rb*, \rb and let us investigate|וּדְע֣וּ\rb*\rb |וּרְא֔וּ\rb* \rb how|בַּמָּ֗ה\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb sin|הַחַטָּ֥את\rb* \rb has occurred|הָֽיְתָ֛ה\rb* \rb today|הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb*. \v 39 \rb As surely as|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb who saves|הַמּוֹשִׁ֙יעַ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb lives|חַי־\rb*, \rb even|כִּ֧י\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb it is|יֶשְׁנ֛וֹ\rb* \rb my son|בְּנִ֖י\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb Jonathan|בְּיוֹנָתָ֥ן\rb*, \rb he must die|מ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |יָמ֑וּת\rb*!”
\p \rb But not one|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb of the troops|הָעָֽם׃\rb* \rb said|עֹנֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb a word|מִכָּל־\rb*.
\p \v 40 \rb Then Saul said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*, “\rb You|אַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb stand|תִּֽהְיוּ֙\rb* \rb on one|אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb side|לְעֵ֣בֶר\rb*, \rb and I|וַֽאֲנִי֙\rb* \rb and my son|בְּנִ֔י\rb* \rb Jonathan|וְיוֹנָתָ֣ן\rb* \rb will stand|נִהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb on the other|אֶחָ֑ד\rb* \rb side|לְעֵ֣בֶר\rb*.”
\p “\rb Do|עֲשֵֽׂה׃ס\rb* \rb what seems good|הַטּ֥וֹב\rb* \rb to you|בְּעֵינֶ֖יךָ\rb*,” \rb the troops|הָעָם֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּאמְר֤וּ\rb*.
\p \v 41 \rb So Saul|שָׁא֗וּל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*, “\rb Why have You not answered Your servant this day? If the fault is with me or my son Jonathan, respond with Urim, but if the fault is with the men of Israel, respond|הָ֣בָה\rb* \rb with Thummim|תָמִ֑ים\rb*.”\f + \fr 14:41 \ft LXX and Vulgate; MT contains only the short quotation, \fqa “Give a perfect (lot).”\f* \rb And Jonathan|יוֹנָתָ֛ן\rb* \rb and Saul|וְשָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb were selected|וַיִּלָּכֵ֧ד\rb*, \rb but the people|וְהָעָ֥ם\rb* \rb were cleared of the charge|יָצָֽאוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 42 \rb Then Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Cast the lot|הַפִּ֕ילוּ\rb* \rb between me|בֵּינִ֕י\rb* \rb and|וּבֵ֖ין\rb* \rb my son|בְּנִ֑י\rb* \rb Jonathan|יוֹנָתָ֣ן\rb*.” \rb And Jonathan|יוֹנָתָֽן׃\rb* \rb was selected|וַיִּלָּכֵ֖ד\rb*.
\p \v 43 “\rb Tell|הַגִּ֥ידָה\rb* \rb me|לִּ֖י\rb* \rb what|מֶ֣ה\rb* \rb you have done|עָשִׂ֑יתָה\rb*,” \rb Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb* \rb commanded|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb him|י֣וֹנָתָ֔ן\rb*.
\p \rb So Jonathan|יוֹנָתָ֗ן\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb told|וַיַּגֶּד־\rb* \rb him|ל֣וֹ\rb*, “\rb I only tasted|טָעֹ֨ם\rb*\rb |טָעַ֜מְתִּי\rb* \rb a little|מְעַ֥ט\rb* \rb honey|דְּבַ֖שׁ\rb* \rb with the end|בִּקְצֵ֨ה\rb* \rb of the staff|הַמַּטֶּ֧ה\rb* \rb that was|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in my hand|בְּיָדִ֛י\rb*. \rb And now|הִנְנִ֥י\rb* \rb I must die|אָמֽוּת׃\rb*?”
\p \v 44 \rb And Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb declared|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb May God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*\rb |כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb punish me|יַעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb*, \rb and ever so|וְכֹ֣ה\rb* \rb severely|יוֹסִ֑ף\rb*, \rb if you, Jonathan|יוֹנָתָֽן׃\rb*, \rb do not|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb surely die|מ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |תָּמ֖וּת\rb*!”
\p \v 45 \rb But the people|הָעָ֜ם\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֗וּל\rb*, “\rb Must Jonathan|הֲֽיוֹנָתָ֤ן׀\rb* \rb die|יָמוּת֙\rb* — \rb he who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb accomplished|עָ֠שָׂה\rb* \rb such|הַזֹּאת֮\rb* \rb a great|הַגְּדוֹלָ֣ה\rb* \rb deliverance|הַיְשׁוּעָ֨ה\rb* \rb for Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵל֒\rb*? \rb Never|חָלִ֗ילָה\rb*! \rb As surely as the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb lives|חַי־\rb*, \rb not|אִם־\rb* \rb a hair|מִשַּׂעֲרַ֤ת\rb* \rb of his head|רֹאשׁוֹ֙\rb* \rb will fall|יִפֹּ֞ל\rb* \rb to the ground|אַ֔רְצָה\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb God’s help|אֱלֹהִ֥ים\rb* \rb he has accomplished this|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֑ה\rb*.”
\p \rb So the people|הָעָ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb rescued|וַיִּפְדּ֥וּ\rb* \rb Jonathan|יוֹנָתָ֖ן\rb*, \rb and he did not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb die|מֵֽת׃ס\rb*. \v 46 \rb Then Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb gave up|וַיַּ֣עַל\rb* \rb his pursuit|מֵאַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb*, \rb and the Philistines|וּפְלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb returned|הָלְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb to their own land|לִמְקוֹמָֽם׃\rb*.
\s1 Saul’s Victories
\p \v 47 \rb After Saul|וְשָׁא֛וּל\rb* \rb had assumed|לָכַ֥ד\rb* \rb the kingship|הַמְּלוּכָ֖ה\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb he fought|וַיִּלָּ֣חֶם\rb* \rb against all|בְּֽכָל־\rb* \rb his enemies|אֹיְבָ֡יו\rb* \rb on every side|סָבִ֣יב׀\rb* — \rb the Moabites|בְּמוֹאָ֣ב׀\rb*, \rb the Ammonites|וּבִבְנֵי־\rb*\rb |עַמּ֨וֹן\rb*, \rb the Edomites|וּבֶאֱד֜וֹם\rb*, \rb the kings|וּבְמַלְכֵ֤י\rb*\f + \fr 14:47 \ft MT; DSS and LXX \fqa king\f* \rb of Zobah|צוֹבָה֙\rb*, \rb and the Philistines|וּבַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb*. \rb Wherever|וּבְכֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he turned|יִפְנֶ֖ה\rb*, \rb he routed them|יַרְשִֽׁיעַ׃\rb*.\f + \fr 14:47 \ft Or \fqa he inflicted punishment on them \ft from Hebrew; LXX \fqa he was victorious\f* \v 48 \rb He fought|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb valiantly|חַ֔יִל\rb* \rb and defeated|וַיַּ֖ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Amalekites|עֲמָלֵ֑ק\rb*, \rb delivering|וַיַּצֵּ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb from the hands|מִיַּ֥ד\rb* \rb of its plunderers|שֹׁסֵֽהוּ׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 49 \rb Now the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb were|וַיִּֽהְיוּ֙\rb* \rb Jonathan|יוֹנָתָ֥ן\rb*, \rb Ishvi|וְיִשְׁוִ֖י\rb*,\rb |וּמַלְכִּי־\rb* \rb and Malchishua|שׁ֑וּעַ\rb*.\rb |וְשֵׁם֙\rb* \rb His two|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb daughters|בְנֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb were named|שֵׁ֤ם\rb* \rb Merab|מֵרַ֔ב\rb* (\rb his firstborn|הַבְּכִירָה֙\rb*)\rb |וְשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb and Michal|מִיכַֽל׃\rb* (\rb his younger daughter|הַקְּטַנָּ֖ה\rb*). \v 50 \rb His|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb wife’s|אֵ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁם֙\rb* \rb was Ahinoam|אֲחִינֹ֖עַם\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Ahimaaz|אֲחִימָ֑עַץ\rb*. \rb The name|וְשֵׁ֤ם\rb* \rb of the commander|שַׂר־\rb* \rb of his army|צְבָאוֹ֙\rb* \rb was Abner|אֲבִינֵ֔ר\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Saul’s|שָׁאֽוּל׃\rb* \rb uncle|דּ֥וֹד\rb* \rb Ner|נֵ֖ר\rb*. \v 51 \rb Saul’s|שָׁא֛וּל\rb* \rb father|אֲבִֽי־\rb* \rb Kish|וְקִ֧ישׁ\rb* \rb and Abner’s|אַבְנֵ֖ר\rb* \rb father|אֲבִֽי־\rb* \rb Ner|וְנֵ֥ר\rb* \rb were sons|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Abiel|אֲבִיאֵֽל׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 52 \rb And the war|הַמִּלְחָמָה֙\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb was|וַתְּהִ֤י\rb* \rb fierce|חֲזָקָ֣ה\rb* \rb for all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֑וּל\rb*. \rb So whenever he|שָׁא֜וּל\rb* \rb noticed|וְרָאָ֨ה\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb strong|גִּבּוֹר֙\rb*\rb |וְכָל־\rb* \rb or brave|חַ֔יִל\rb*\rb |אֵלָֽיו׃ס\rb* \rb man|בֶּן־\rb*, \rb Saul would enlist him|וַיַּאַסְפֵ֖הוּ\rb*.
\c 15
\s1 Saul’s Disobedience
\p \v 1 \rb Then Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵל֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb*, “\rb The LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb sent|שָׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb me|אֹתִ֨י\rb* \rb to anoint you|לִמְשָׁחֳךָ֣\rb* \rb king|לְמֶ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb His people|עַמּ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb Now therefore|וְעַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb listen|שְׁמַ֔ע\rb*\rb |לְק֖וֹל\rb* \rb to the words|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*. \v 2 \rb This is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: ‘\rb I witnessed|פָּקַ֕דְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the Amalekites|עֲמָלֵ֖ק\rb* \rb did|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb to the Israelites|לְיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb when|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they opposed|שָׂ֥ם\rb* \rb them|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb on their way|בַּדֶּ֔רֶךְ\rb* \rb up|בַּעֲלֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb from Egypt|מִמִּצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb Now|עַתָּה֩\rb* \rb go|לֵ֨ךְ\rb* \rb and attack|וְהִכִּֽיתָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Amalekites|עֲמָלֵ֗ק\rb* \rb and devote to destruction|וְהַֽחֲרַמְתֶּם֙\rb*\f + \fr 15:3 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering; also in verses 8, 9, 15, 18, 20, and 21.\f*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb belongs to them|ל֔וֹ\rb*. \rb Do not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb spare|תַחְמֹ֖ל\rb* \rb them|עָלָ֑יו\rb*, \rb but put to death|וְהֵמַתָּ֞ה\rb* \rb men|מֵאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb and|עַד־\rb* \rb women|אִשָּׁ֗ה\rb*, \rb children|מֵֽעֹלֵל֙\rb* \rb and|וְעַד־\rb* \rb infants|יוֹנֵ֔ק\rb*, \rb oxen|מִשּׁ֣וֹר\rb* \rb and|וְעַד־\rb* \rb sheep|שֶׂ֔ה\rb*, \rb camels|מִגָּמָ֖ל\rb* \rb and|וְעַד־\rb* \rb donkeys|חֲמֽוֹר׃ס\rb*.’”
\p \v 4 \rb So Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb summoned|וַיְשַׁמַּ֤ע\rb* \rb the troops|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb and numbered them|וַֽיִּפְקְדֵם֙\rb* \rb at Telaim|בַּטְּלָאִ֔ים\rb* — \rb 200,000|מָאתַ֥יִם\rb*\rb |אֶ֖לֶף\rb* \rb foot soldiers|רַגְלִ֑י\rb* \rb and 10,000|וַעֲשֶׂ֥רֶת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb men|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the city|עִ֣יר\rb* \rb of Amalek|עֲמָלֵ֑ק\rb* \rb and lay in wait|וַיָּ֖רֶב\rb* \rb in the valley|בַּנָּֽחַל׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb And he|שָׁא֣וּל\rb* \rb warned|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶֽל־\rb* \rb the Kenites|הַקֵּינִ֡י\rb*, “\rb Since you|וְאַתָּ֞ה\rb* \rb showed|עָשִׂ֤יתָה\rb* \rb kindness|חֶ֙סֶד֙\rb* \rb to|עִם־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb when they came up|בַּעֲלוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb out of Egypt|מִמִּצְרָ֑יִם\rb*, \rb go on|לְכוּ֩\rb*\rb |סֻּ֨רוּ\rb* \rb and get away|רְד֜וּ\rb* \rb from|מִתּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the Amalekites|עֲמָלֵקִ֗י\rb*. \rb Otherwise|פֶּן־\rb* \rb I will sweep you away|אֹֽסִפְךָ֙\rb* \rb with them|עִמּ֔וֹ\rb*.”
\p \rb So the Kenites|קֵינִ֖י\rb* \rb moved away|וַיָּ֥סַר\rb* \rb from|מִתּ֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb the Amalekites|עֲמָלֵֽק׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb Then Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb struck down|וַיַּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb the Amalekites|עֲמָלֵ֑ק\rb* \rb all the way|בּוֹאֲךָ֣\rb* \rb from Havilah|מֵֽחֲוִילָה֙\rb* \rb to Shur|שׁ֔וּר\rb*, \rb which is|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb east|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb He captured|וַיִּתְפֹּ֛שׂ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Agag|אֲגַ֥ג\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Amalek|עֲמָלֵ֖ק\rb* \rb alive|חָ֑י\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb but devoted|הֶחֱרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the others to destruction|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb with the sword|חָֽרֶב׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb Saul|שָׁא֨וּל\rb* \rb and his troops|וְהָעָ֜ם\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb spared|וַיַּחְמֹל֩\rb* \rb Agag|אֲגָ֗ג\rb*, \rb along with|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the best|מֵיטַ֣ב\rb* \rb of the sheep|הַצֹּאן֩\rb* \rb and cattle|וְהַבָּקָ֨ר\rb*, \rb the fat calves|וְהַמִּשְׁנִ֤ים\rb*\f + \fr 15:9 \ft Or \fqa the grown bulls\f* \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb lambs|הַכָּרִים֙\rb*, \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the best|הַטּ֔וֹב\rb* \rb of everything else|כָּל־\rb*.\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb They were unwilling|אָב֖וּ\rb* \rb to devote them to destruction|הַחֲרִימָ֑ם\rb*, \rb but they devoted to destruction|הֶחֱרִֽימוּ׃פ\rb* \rb all|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |הַמְּלָאכָ֛ה\rb* \rb that was despised|נְמִבְזָ֥ה\rb* \rb and worthless|וְנָמֵ֖ס\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֥הּ\rb*.
\s1 Samuel Denounces Saul
\p \v 10 \rb Then the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb came|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 11 “\rb I regret|נִחַ֗מְתִּי\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I have made Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb* \rb king|הִמְלַ֤כְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |לְמֶ֔לֶךְ\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he has turned away|שָׁב֙\rb* \rb from following Me|מֵאַֽחֲרַ֔י\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb has not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb carried out|הֵקִ֑ים\rb* \rb My instructions|דְּבָרַ֖י\rb*.”
\p \rb And Samuel|לִשְׁמוּאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb was distressed|וַיִּ֙חַר֙\rb* \rb and cried out|וַיִּזְעַ֥ק\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that night|הַלָּֽיְלָה׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb Early in the morning|בַּבֹּ֑קֶר\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb got up|וַיַּשְׁכֵּ֧ם\rb* \rb to confront|לִקְרַ֥את\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb*, \rb but he was told|וַיֻּגַּ֨ד\rb*\rb |לִשְׁמוּאֵ֜ל\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* “\rb Saul|שָׁא֤וּל\rb* \rb has gone|בָּֽא־\rb* \rb to Carmel|הַכַּרְמֶ֙לָה֙\rb*, \rb and behold|וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb*, \rb he has set up|מַצִּ֥יב\rb* \rb a monument|יָ֔ד\rb* \rb for himself|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb and has turned|וַיִּסֹּב֙\rb*\rb |וַֽיַּעֲבֹ֔ר\rb* \rb and gone down|וַיֵּ֖רֶד\rb* \rb to Gilgal|הַגִּלְגָּֽל׃\rb*.”
\p \v 13 \rb When Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb reached|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb him|שָׁא֑וּל\rb*, \rb Saul|שָׁא֗וּל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|ל֣וֹ\rb*, “\rb May the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb bless|בָּר֤וּךְ\rb* \rb you|אַתָּה֙\rb*. \rb I have carried out|הֲקִימֹ֖תִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb instructions|דְּבַ֥ר\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb But Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Then what|וּמֶ֛ה\rb* \rb is this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb*\rb |בְּאָזְנָ֑י\rb* \rb bleating|קֽוֹל־\rb* \rb of sheep|הַצֹּ֥אן\rb* \rb and lowing|וְק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of cattle|הַבָּקָ֔ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb hear|שֹׁמֵֽעַ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 15 \rb Saul|שָׁא֜וּל\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*, “\rb The troops|הָעָם֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb brought them|הֱבִיא֗וּם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb from the Amalekites|מֵעֲמָלֵקִ֣י\rb*; \rb they spared|חָמַ֤ל\rb* \rb the best|מֵיטַ֤ב\rb* \rb sheep|הַצֹּאן֙\rb* \rb and cattle|וְהַבָּקָ֔ר\rb* \rb to|לְמַ֥עַן\rb* \rb sacrifice|זְבֹ֖חַ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb*, \rb but|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the rest|הַיּוֹתֵ֖ר\rb* \rb we devoted to destruction|הֶחֱרַֽמְנוּ׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 16 “\rb Stop|הֶ֚רֶף\rb*!” \rb exclaimed|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵל֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |שָׁא֔וּל\rb*. “\rb Let me tell|וְאַגִּ֣ידָה\rb* \rb you|לְּךָ֔\rb*\rb |אֵת֩\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb said|דִּבֶּ֧ר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֖י\rb* \rb last night|הַלָּ֑יְלָה\rb*.”
\p “\rb Tell me|דַּבֵּֽר׃ס\rb*,” \rb Saul replied|וַיֹּאמְרוּ\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb And Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Although|אִם־\rb* \rb you were once|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb small|קָטֹ֤ן\rb* \rb in your own eyes|בְּעֵינֶ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb have you|אָ֑תָּה\rb* \rb not|הֲל֗וֹא\rb* \rb become the head|רֹ֛אשׁ\rb* \rb of the tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*? \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb anointed|וַיִּמְשָׁחֲךָ֧\rb* \rb you king|לְמֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 18 \rb and sent|וַיִּשְׁלָחֲךָ֥\rb*\rb |יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb you on a mission|בְּדָ֑רֶךְ\rb*, \rb saying|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, ‘\rb Go|לֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb and devote to destruction|וְהַחֲרַמְתָּ֞ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sinful|הַֽחַטָּאִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Amalekites|עֲמָלֵ֔ק\rb*. \rb Fight|וְנִלְחַמְתָּ֣\rb* \rb against them|ב֔וֹ\rb* \rb until|עַ֥ד\rb* \rb you have wiped them out|כַּלּוֹתָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֹתָֽם׃\rb*.’ \v 19 \rb So why|וְלָ֥מָּה\rb* \rb did you not|לֹא־\rb* \rb obey|שָׁמַ֖עְתָּ\rb*\rb |בְּק֣וֹל\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*? \rb Why did you rush|וַתַּ֙עַט֙\rb* \rb upon|אֶל־\rb* \rb the plunder|הַשָּׁלָ֔ל\rb* \rb and do|וַתַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*?”
\p \v 20 “\rb But I did obey|שָׁמַ֙עְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |בְּק֣וֹל\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*,” \rb Saul|שָׁא֜וּל\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |שְׁמוּאֵ֗ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*. “\rb I went|וָאֵלֵ֕ךְ\rb* \rb on the mission|בַּדֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb gave me|שְׁלָחַ֣נִי\rb*. \rb I brought back|וָאָבִ֗יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Agag|אֲגַג֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Amalek|עֲמָלֵ֔ק\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and devoted|הֶחֱרַֽמְתִּי׃\rb* \rb the Amalekites to destruction|עֲמָלֵ֖ק\rb*. \v 21 \rb The troops|הָעָ֧ם\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb sheep|צֹ֥אן\rb* \rb and cattle|וּבָקָ֖ר\rb* \rb from the plunder|מֵהַשָּׁלָ֛ל\rb*, \rb the best of|רֵאשִׁ֣ית\rb* \rb the things devoted to destruction|הַחֵ֑רֶם\rb*, \rb in order to sacrifice them|לִזְבֹּ֛חַ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb at Gilgal|בַּגִּלְגָּֽל׃\rb*.”
\p \v 22 \rb But Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb declared|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb Does the LORD|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb* \rb delight|הַחֵ֤פֶץ\rb* \rb in burnt offerings|בְּעֹל֣וֹת\rb* \rb and sacrifices|וּזְבָחִ֔ים\rb*
\q2 \rb as much as in obedience|כִּשְׁמֹ֖עַ\rb* \rb to His voice|בְּק֣וֹל\rb*\rb |יְהוָ֑ה\rb*?
\q1 \rb Behold|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb*, \rb obedience|שְׁמֹ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb is better|ט֔וֹב\rb* \rb than sacrifice|מִזֶּ֣בַח\rb*,
\q2 \rb and attentiveness|לְהַקְשִׁ֖יב\rb* \rb is better than the fat|מֵחֵ֥לֶב\rb* \rb of rams|אֵילִֽים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 23 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb rebellion|מֶ֔רִי\rb* \rb is like the sin|חַטַּאת־\rb* \rb of divination|קֶ֙סֶם֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb and arrogance|הַפְצַ֑ר\rb* \rb is like the wickedness|וְאָ֥וֶן\rb* \rb of idolatry|וּתְרָפִ֖ים\rb*.
\q1 \rb Because|יַ֗עַן\rb* \rb you have rejected|מָאַ֙סְתָּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb He has rejected you|וַיִּמְאָסְךָ֖\rb* \rb as king|מִמֶּֽלֶךְ׃ס\rb*.”
\s1 Saul’s Confession
\p \v 24 \rb Then Saul|שָׁא֤וּל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵל֙\rb*, “\rb I have sinned|חָטָ֔אתִי\rb*;\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I have transgressed|עָבַ֥רְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb commandment|פִּֽי־\rb* \rb and your instructions|דְּבָרֶ֑יךָ\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb I feared|יָרֵ֙אתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb and obeyed|וָאֶשְׁמַ֖ע\rb* \rb their voice|בְּקוֹלָֽם׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb Now therefore|וְעַתָּ֕ה\rb*, \rb please|נָ֖א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb forgive|שָׂ֥א\rb* \rb my sin|חַטָּאתִ֑י\rb* \rb and return|וְשׁ֣וּב\rb* \rb with me|עִמִּ֔י\rb* \rb so I can worship|וְאֶֽשְׁתַּחֲוֶ֖ה\rb* \rb the LORD|לַֽיהוָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 26 “\rb I will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb return|אָשׁ֖וּב\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּ֑ךְ\rb*,” \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵל֙\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |שָׁא֔וּל\rb*. “\rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb you have rejected|מָאַ֙סְתָּה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and He|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb has rejected you|וַיִּמְאָסְךָ֣\rb* \rb as|מִהְי֥וֹת\rb* \rb king|מֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 27 \rb As Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb turned|וַיִּסֹּ֥ב\rb* \rb to go|לָלֶ֑כֶת\rb*, \rb Saul grabbed|וַיַּחֲזֵ֥ק\rb* \rb the hem|בִּכְנַף־\rb* \rb of his robe|מְעִיל֖וֹ\rb*, \rb and it tore|וַיִּקָּרַֽע׃\rb*. \v 28 \rb So Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָיו֙\rb*, “\rb The LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb has torn|קָרַ֨ע\rb* \rb the kingdom|מַמְלְכ֧וּת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb from you|מֵעָלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֑וֹם\rb* \rb and has given|וּנְתָנָ֕הּ\rb* \rb it to your neighbor|לְרֵעֲךָ֖\rb* \rb who is better|הַטּ֥וֹב\rb* \rb than you|מִמֶּֽךָּ׃\rb*. \v 29 \rb Moreover|וְגַם֙\rb*, \rb the Glory|נֵ֣צַח\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb does not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb lie|יְשַׁקֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb or change His mind|יִנָּחֵ֑ם\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb He|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb is not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb a man|אָדָ֛ם\rb*, \rb that He should change His mind|לְהִנָּחֵֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 30 “\rb I have sinned|חָטָ֔אתִי\rb*,” \rb Saul replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*. “\rb Please|נָ֛א\rb* \rb honor me|כַּבְּדֵ֥נִי\rb* \rb now|עַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb before|נֶ֥גֶד\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of my people|עַמִּ֖י\rb* \rb and before|וְנֶ֣גֶד\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb Come back|וְשׁ֣וּב\rb* \rb with me|עִמִּ֔י\rb*, \rb so that I may worship|וְהִֽשְׁתַּחֲוֵ֖יתִי\rb* \rb the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 31 \rb So Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb went back|וַיָּ֥שָׁב\rb* \rb with|אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֑וּל\rb*, \rb and Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb worshiped|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֥חוּ\rb* \rb the LORD|לַֽיהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 32 \rb Then Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Bring|הַגִּ֤ישׁוּ\rb* \rb me|אֵלַי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Agag|אֲגַג֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of the Amalekites|עֲמָלֵ֔ק\rb*.”
\p \rb Agag|אֲגַ֖ג\rb* \rb came|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb cheerfully|מַעֲדַנֹּ֑ת\rb*,\f + \fr 15:32 \ft Or \fqa cautiously \ft or \fqa in chains\ft ; see DSS and LXX.\f* \rb for he|אֲגָ֔ג\rb* \rb thought|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Surely|אָכֵ֖ן\rb* \rb the bitterness|מַר־\rb* \rb of death|הַמָּֽוֶת׃ס\rb* \rb is past|סָ֥ר\rb*.”\f + \fr 15:32 \ft Or \fqa “Surely this is the bitterness of death.” \ft See DSS and LXX.\f*
\p \v 33 \rb But Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb declared|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb As|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb your sword|חַרְבֶּ֔ךָ\rb* \rb has made women|נָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb childless|שִׁכְּלָ֤ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb so|כֵּן־\rb* \rb your mother|אִמֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb will be childless|תִּשְׁכַּ֥ל\rb* \rb among women|מִנָּשִׁ֖ים\rb*.”
\p \rb And Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֧ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb hacked Agag|אֲגָ֛ג\rb* \rb to pieces|וַיְשַׁסֵּ֨ף\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb at Gilgal|בַּגִּלְגָּֽל׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 34 \rb Then Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb to Ramah|הָרָמָ֑תָה\rb*, \rb but Saul|וְשָׁא֛וּל\rb* \rb went up|עָלָ֥ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his home|בֵּית֖וֹ\rb* \rb in Gibeah|גִּבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁאֽוּל׃\rb*. \v 35 \rb And to|עַד־\rb* \rb the day|י֣וֹם\rb* \rb of his death|מוֹת֔וֹ\rb*,\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֜ל\rb* \rb never|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb again|יָסַ֨ף\rb* \rb visited|לִרְא֤וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb*. \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb mourned|הִתְאַבֵּ֥ל\rb* \rb for|אֶל־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֑וּל\rb*, \rb and the LORD|וַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb regretted|נִחָ֔ם\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb He had made Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb king|הִמְלִ֥יךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb*.
\c 16
\s1 Samuel Anoints David
\p \v 1 \rb Now the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֗ל\rb*, “\rb How long|עַד־\rb*\rb |מָתַי֙\rb* \rb are you|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb going to mourn|מִתְאַבֵּ֣ל\rb* \rb for|אֶל־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb*, \rb since I|וַאֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb have rejected him|מְאַסְתִּ֔יו\rb* \rb as king|מִמְּלֹ֖ךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*? \rb Fill your horn|קַרְנְךָ֜\rb* \rb with|מַלֵּ֨א\rb* \rb oil|שֶׁ֗מֶן\rb* \rb and go|וְלֵ֤ךְ\rb*. \rb I am sending|אֶֽשְׁלָחֲךָ֙\rb* \rb you to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jesse|יִשַׁ֣י\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of Bethlehem|הַלַּחְמִ֔י\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I have selected|רָאִ֧יתִי\rb* \rb from his sons|בְּבָנָ֛יו\rb* \rb a king|מֶֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb for Myself|לִ֖י\rb*.”
\p \v 2 “\rb How|אֵ֣יךְ\rb* \rb can I go|אֵלֵ֔ךְ\rb*?” \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵל֙\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*. “\rb Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb will hear of it|וְשָׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb and kill me|וַהֲרָגָ֑נִיס\rb*!”
\p \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Take|תִּקַּ֣ח\rb*\rb |עֶגְלַ֤ת\rb* \rb a heifer|בָּקָר֙\rb* \rb with you|בְּיָדֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb and say|וְאָ֣מַרְתָּ֔\rb*, ‘\rb I have come|בָּֽאתִי׃\rb* \rb to sacrifice|לִזְבֹּ֥חַ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֖ה\rb*.’ \v 3 \rb Then invite|וְקָרָ֥אתָ\rb* \rb Jesse|לְיִשַׁ֖י\rb* \rb to the sacrifice|בַּזָּ֑בַח\rb*, \rb and I|וְאָֽנֹכִ֗י\rb* \rb will show you|אוֹדִֽיעֲךָ֙\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb you are to do|תַּעֲשֶׂ֔ה\rb*. \rb You are to anoint|וּמָשַׁחְתָּ֣\rb* \rb for Me|לִ֔י\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb the one|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I indicate|אֹמַ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֵלֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb So Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֗ל\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb had said|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb and went|וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb to Bethlehem|לָ֑חֶם\rb*. \rb When the elders|זִקְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the town|הָעִיר֙\rb* \rb met him|לִקְרָאת֔וֹ\rb*, \rb they trembled|וַיֶּחֶרְד֞וּ\rb* \rb and asked|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Do you come|בּוֹאֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb in peace|שָׁלֹ֥ם\rb*?”
\p \v 5 “\rb In peace|שָׁל֗וֹם\rb*,” \rb he replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר׀\rb*. “\rb I have come|בָּ֔אתִי\rb* \rb to sacrifice|לִזְבֹּ֤חַ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb*. \rb Consecrate yourselves|הִֽתְקַדְּשׁ֔וּ\rb* \rb and come|וּבָאתֶ֥ם\rb* \rb with me|אִתִּ֖י\rb* \rb to the sacrifice|בַּזָּ֑בַח\rb*.”
\p \rb Then he consecrated|וַיְקַדֵּ֤שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jesse|יִשַׁי֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his sons|בָּנָ֔יו\rb* \rb and invited|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to the sacrifice|לַזָּֽבַח׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb When they arrived|בְּבוֹאָ֔ם\rb*, \rb Samuel saw|וַיַּ֖רְא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Eliab|אֱלִיאָ֑ב\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Surely|אַ֛ךְ\rb* \rb here before|נֶ֥גֶד\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb is His anointed|מְשִׁיחֽוֹ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb But the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֗ל\rb*, “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb consider|תַּבֵּ֧ט\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb his appearance|מַרְאֵ֛הוּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb or height|גְּבֹ֥הַּ\rb*\rb |קוֹמָת֖וֹ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I have rejected him|מְאַסְתִּ֑יהוּ\rb*;\rb |כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb the LORD does not see|לֹ֗א\rb* \rb as|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb man|הָאָדָ֔ם\rb* \rb does|יִרְאֶה֙\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb man|הָֽאָדָם֙\rb* \rb sees|יִרְאֶ֣ה\rb* \rb the outward appearance|לַעֵינַ֔יִם\rb*, \rb but the LORD|וַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb sees|יִרְאֶ֥ה\rb* \rb the heart|לַלֵּבָֽב׃\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb Then Jesse|יִשַׁי֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb called|וַיִּקְרָ֤א\rb* \rb Abinadab|אֲבִ֣ינָדָ֔ב\rb* \rb and presented him|וַיַּעֲבִרֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb to|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb who said|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb The LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb has not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb chosen|בָחַ֥ר\rb* \rb this|בָּזֶ֖ה\rb* \rb one either|גַּם־\rb*.”
\p \v 9 \rb Next Jesse|יִשַׁ֖י\rb* \rb presented|וַיַּעֲבֵ֥ר\rb* \rb Shammah|שַׁמָּ֑ה\rb*,\f + \fr 16:9 \fqa Shammah \ft is a variant of \fqa Shimeah\ft , \fqa Shimea\ft , and \fqa Shimei\ft ; see \ref 2 Samuel 13:3|2SA 13:3\ref*, 2 Samuel 21:21, and 1 Chronicles 2:13.\f* \rb but Samuel said|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb The LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb has not|לֹא־\rb* \rb chosen|בָחַ֥ר\rb* \rb this|בָּזֶ֖ה\rb* \rb one either|גַּם־\rb*.”
\p \v 10 \rb Thus Jesse|יִשַׁ֛י\rb* \rb made seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb of his sons|בָּנָ֖יו\rb* \rb pass|וַיַּעֲבֵ֥ר\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb but Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵל֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb him|יִשַׁ֔י\rb*, “\rb The LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has not|לֹא־\rb* \rb chosen|בָחַ֥ר\rb* \rb any of these|בָּאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 11 \rb And Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֣ל\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb him|יִשַׁי֮\rb*, “\rb Are these all|הֲתַ֣מּוּ\rb* \rb the sons you have?|הַנְּעָרִים֒\rb*”
\p “\rb There is still|ע֚וֹד\rb*\rb |שָׁאַ֣ר\rb* \rb the youngest|הַקָּטָ֔ן\rb*,” \rb Jesse replied|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb but he is|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb tending|רֹעֶ֖ה\rb* \rb the sheep|בַּצֹּ֑אן\rb*.”
\p “\rb Send for|שִׁלְחָ֣ה\rb* \rb him|וְקָחֶ֔נּוּ\rb*,” \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֤ל\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |יִשַׁי֙\rb*. “\rb For|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb we will not|לֹא־\rb* \rb sit down to eat|נָסֹ֖ב\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb he arrives|בֹּא֥וֹ\rb*\rb |פֹֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 12 \rb So Jesse sent for his youngest son|וַיִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb and brought him in|וַיְבִיאֵ֙הוּ֙\rb*. \rb He|וְה֣וּא\rb* \rb was ruddy|אַדְמוֹנִ֔י\rb*, \rb with beautiful|יְפֵ֥ה\rb* \rb eyes|עֵינַ֖יִם\rb*\rb |עִם־\rb* \rb and a handsome|וְט֣וֹב\rb* \rb appearance|רֹ֑אִי פ\rb*. \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Rise|ק֥וּם\rb* \rb and anoint him|מְשָׁחֵ֖הוּ\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb is the one|זֶ֥ה\rb*.”
\p \v 13 \rb So Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֜ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb the horn|קֶ֣רֶן\rb* \rb of oil|הַשֶּׁ֗מֶן\rb* \rb and anointed|וַיִּמְשַׁ֣ח\rb* \rb him|אֹתוֹ֮\rb* \rb in the presence|בְּקֶ֣רֶב\rb* \rb of his brothers|אֶחָיו֒\rb*, \rb and the Spirit|רֽוּחַ־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb rushed|וַתִּצְלַ֤ח\rb* \rb upon|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb from that|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb day|מֵהַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb forward|וָמָ֑עְלָה\rb*. \rb Then Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb set out|וַיָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb and went|וַיֵּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb to Ramah|הָרָמָֽתָה׃ס\rb*.
\s1 David Serves Saul
\p \v 14 \rb Now the Spirit|וְר֧וּחַ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb departed|סָ֖רָה\rb* \rb from|מֵעִ֣ם\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֑וּל\rb*, \rb and a spirit|רֽוּחַ־\rb* \rb of distress|רָעָ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 16:14 \ft Or \fqa a harmful spirit\ft ; similarly in verses 15, 16, and 23\f* \rb from|מֵאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb began to torment him|וּבִֽעֲתַ֥תּוּ\rb*. \v 15 \rb Saul’s|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדֵֽי־\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמְר֥וּ\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֑יו\rb*, “\rb Surely|הִנֵּה־\rb*\rb |נָ֧א\rb* \rb a spirit|רֽוּחַ־\rb* \rb of distress|רָעָ֖ה\rb* \rb from God|אֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb is tormenting you|מְבַעִתֶּֽךָ׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb Let our lord|אֲדֹנֵ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb command|יֹאמַר־\rb*\rb |נָ֤א\rb* \rb your servants|עֲבָדֶ֣יךָ\rb* \rb here|לְפָנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb to seek out|יְבַקְשׁ֕וּ\rb* \rb someone|אִ֕ישׁ\rb* \rb who can skillfully|יֹדֵ֖עַ\rb* \rb play|מְנַגֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb the harp|בַּכִּנּ֑וֹר\rb*.\rb |וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb Whenever|בִּֽהְי֨וֹת\rb* \rb the spirit|רֽוּחַ־\rb* \rb of distress|רָעָ֔ה\rb* \rb from God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb is upon you|עָלֶ֤יךָ\rb*, \rb he is to play it|וְנִגֵּ֥ן\rb*,\rb |בְּיָד֖וֹ\rb* \rb and you|לָֽךְ׃פ\rb* \rb will be well|וְט֥וֹב\rb*.”
\p \v 17 \rb And Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb commanded|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb his|אֶל־\rb* \rb servants|עֲבָדָ֑יו\rb*, “\rb Find|רְאוּ־\rb*\rb |נָ֣א\rb* \rb me|לִ֗י\rb* \rb someone|אִ֚ישׁ\rb* \rb who plays|לְנַגֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb well|מֵיטִ֣יב\rb*, \rb and bring him|וַהֲבִיאוֹתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to me|אֵלָֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 18 \rb One|אֶחָ֨ד\rb* \rb of the servants|מֵהַנְּעָרִ֜ים\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*\rb |הִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּעַן֩\rb*, “\rb I have seen|רָאִ֜יתִי\rb* \rb a son|בֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb of Jesse|לְיִשַׁי֮\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Bethlehem|הַלַּחְמִי֒\rb* \rb who knows|יֹדֵ֣עַ\rb* \rb how to play the harp|נַ֠גֵּן\rb*. \rb He is a mighty man|וְגִבּ֨וֹר\rb* \rb of valor|חַ֜יִל\rb*, \rb a warrior|וְאִ֧ישׁ\rb*\rb |מִלְחָמָ֛ה\rb*, \rb eloquent|וּנְב֥וֹן\rb*\rb |דָּבָ֖ר\rb*\rb |וְאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb and handsome|תֹּ֑אַר\rb*, \rb and the LORD|וַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb is with him|עִמּֽוֹ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 19 \rb So Saul|שָׁא֛וּל\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִ֖ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jesse|יִשָׁ֑י\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Send|שִׁלְחָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֛י\rb* \rb me|אֶת־\rb* \rb your son|בִּנְךָ֖\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֥ד\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb is with the sheep|בַּצֹּֽאן׃\rb*.”
\p \v 20 \rb And Jesse|יִשַׁ֜י\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb a donkey loaded with|חֲמ֥וֹר\rb* \rb bread|לֶ֙חֶם֙\rb*, \rb a skin|וְנֹ֣אד\rb* \rb of wine|יַ֔יִן\rb*, \rb and one|אֶחָ֑ד\rb* \rb young goat|וּגְדִ֥י\rb*\rb |עִזִּ֖ים\rb* \rb and sent them|וַיִּשְׁלַ֛ח\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁאֽוּל׃\rb* \rb with|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb his son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֥ד\rb*. \v 21 \rb When David|דָוִד֙\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֤א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb and entered his service|וַֽיַּעֲמֹ֖ד\rb*\rb |לְפָנָ֑יו\rb*, \rb Saul loved him|וַיֶּאֱהָבֵ֣הֽוּ\rb* \rb very much|מְאֹ֔ד\rb*, \rb and David became|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb his|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb armor-bearer|נֹשֵׂ֥א\rb*\rb |כֵלִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb Then Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb word to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jesse|יִשַׁ֖י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Let David|דָוִד֙\rb* \rb remain in my service|יַעֲמָד־\rb*\rb |נָ֤א\rb*\rb |לְפָנַ֔י\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I am pleased with|מָ֥צָא\rb*\rb |חֵ֖ן\rb* \rb him|בְּעֵינָֽי׃\rb*.” \v 23 \rb And whenever|וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb the spirit|רֽוּחַ־\rb* \rb from God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb came|בִּֽהְי֤וֹת\rb* \rb upon|אֶל־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb*, \rb David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb would pick up|וְלָקַ֥ח\rb* \rb his harp|הַכִּנּ֖וֹר\rb* \rb and play|וְנִגֵּ֣ן\rb*\rb |בְּיָד֑וֹ\rb*. \rb Then Saul|לְשָׁאוּל֙\rb* \rb would find relief|וְרָוַ֤ח\rb* \rb and feel better|וְט֣וֹב\rb*\rb |ל֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and the spirit|ר֥וּחַ\rb* \rb of distress|הָרָעָֽה׃פ\rb* \rb would depart|וְסָ֥רָה\rb* \rb from him|מֵעָלָ֖יו\rb*.
\c 17
\s1 Goliath’s Challenge
\p \v 1 \rb Now the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֤ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gathered|וַיַּאַסְפ֨וּ\rb* \rb their forces|מַֽחֲנֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb for war|לַמִּלְחָמָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וַיֵּאָ֣סְפ֔וּ\rb* \rb at Socoh|שֹׂכֹ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in Judah|לִיהוּדָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and they camped|וַֽיַּחֲנ֛וּ\rb* \rb between|בֵּין־\rb* \rb Socoh|שׂוֹכֹ֥ה\rb*\rb |וּבֵין־\rb* \rb and Azekah|עֲזֵקָ֖ה\rb*\rb |בְּאֶ֥פֶס\rb* \rb in Ephes-dammim|דַּמִּֽים׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb Saul|וְשָׁא֤וּל\rb* \rb and the men|וְאִֽישׁ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb assembled|נֶאֶסְפ֔וּ\rb* \rb and camped|וַֽיַּחֲנ֖וּ\rb* \rb in the Valley|בְּעֵ֣מֶק\rb* \rb of Elah|הָאֵלָ֑ה\rb*, \rb arraying themselves|וַיַּעַרְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb for battle|מִלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb against|לִקְרַ֥את\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb The Philistines|וּפְלִשְׁתִּ֞ים\rb* \rb stood|עֹמְדִ֤ים\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb one|מִזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb hill|הָהָר֙\rb* \rb and the Israelites|וְיִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb stood|עֹמְדִ֥ים\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb another|מִזֶּ֑ה\rb*\rb |הָהָ֖ר\rb*, \rb with the valley|וְהַגַּ֖יְא\rb* \rb between them|בֵּינֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Then a champion|אִֽישׁ־\rb*\rb |הַבֵּנַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb named|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Goliath|גָּלְיָ֥ת\rb*, \rb who was from Gath|מִגַּ֑ת\rb*, \rb came out|וַיֵּצֵ֤א\rb* \rb from the Philistine|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb camp|מִמַּחֲנ֣וֹת\rb*. \rb He was six|שֵׁ֥שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb and a span|וָזָֽרֶת׃\rb* \rb in height|גָּבְה֕וֹ\rb*,\f + \fr 17:4 \ft Goliath was approximately 9 feet 9 inches or 297 centimeters tall; LXX, DSS, and Josephus \fqa four cubits and a span in height \ft (approximately 6 feet 9 inches or 206 centimeters tall).\f* \v 5 \rb and he had a bronze|נְחֹ֙שֶׁת֙\rb* \rb helmet|וְכ֤וֹבַע\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his head|רֹאשׁ֔וֹ\rb*. \rb He|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb wore|לָב֑וּשׁ\rb* \rb a bronze|נְחֹֽשֶֽׁת׃\rb* \rb coat|וְשִׁרְי֥וֹן\rb* \rb of mail|קַשְׂקַשִּׂ֖ים\rb* \rb weighing|וּמִשְׁקַל֙\rb*\rb |הַשִּׁרְי֔וֹן\rb* \rb five|חֲמֵשֶׁת־\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִ֥ים\rb* \rb shekels|שְׁקָלִ֖ים\rb*,\f + \fr 17:5 \fqa 5,000 shekels \ft is approximately 125.6 pounds or 57 kilograms.\f* \v 6 \rb and he had armor|וּמִצְחַ֥ת\rb* \rb of bronze|נְחֹ֖שֶׁת\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his legs|רַגְלָ֑יו\rb* \rb and a javelin|וְכִיד֥וֹן\rb* \rb of bronze|נְחֹ֖שֶׁת\rb* \rb slung between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb his shoulders|כְּתֵפָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb The shaft|וְחָץ\rb* \rb of his spear|חֲנִית֗וֹ\rb* \rb was like a weaver’s|אֹֽרְגִ֔ים\rb* \rb beam|כִּמְנוֹר֙\rb*, \rb and its iron|בַּרְזֶ֑ל\rb* \rb point|וְלַהֶ֣בֶת\rb*\rb |חֲנִית֔וֹ\rb* \rb weighed six|שֵׁשׁ־\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֥וֹת\rb* \rb shekels|שְׁקָלִ֖ים\rb*.\f + \fr 17:7 \fqa 600 shekels \ft is approximately 15.1 pounds or 6.8 kilograms.\f* \rb In addition, his shield bearer|וְנֹשֵׂ֥א\rb*\rb |הַצִּנָּ֖ה\rb* \rb went|הֹלֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb before him|לְפָנָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb And Goliath stood|וַֽיַּעֲמֹ֗ד\rb* \rb and shouted|וַיִּקְרָא֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the ranks|מַעַרְכֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Why|לָ֥מָּה\rb* \rb do you come out|תֵצְא֖וּ\rb* \rb and array yourselves|לַעֲרֹ֣ךְ\rb* \rb for battle|מִלְחָמָ֑ה\rb*? \rb Am I|אָנֹכִ֣י\rb* \rb not|הֲל֧וֹא\rb* \rb a Philistine|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֗י\rb*, \rb and are you|וְאַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb not servants|עֲבָדִ֣ים\rb* \rb of Saul|לְשָׁא֔וּל\rb*? \rb Choose|בְּרוּ־\rb* \rb one of your men|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb and have him come down|וְיֵרֵ֥ד\rb* \rb against me|אֵלָֽי׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb he is able|יוּכַ֞ל\rb* \rb to fight|לְהִלָּחֵ֤ם\rb* \rb me|אִתִּי֙\rb* \rb and kill me|וְהִכָּ֔נִי\rb*, \rb then we will be|וְהָיִ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb your|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb servants|לַעֲבָדִ֑ים\rb*. \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֤י\rb* \rb prevail|אֽוּכַל־\rb* \rb against him|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb and kill him|וְהִכִּיתִ֔יו\rb*, \rb then you shall be|וִהְיִ֤יתֶם\rb* \rb our|לָ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb servants|לַעֲבָדִ֔ים\rb* \rb and work for|וַעֲבַדְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb us|אֹתָֽנוּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 10 \rb Then the Philistine|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֔י\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb I|אֲנִ֗י\rb* \rb defy|חֵרַ֛פְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ranks|מַעַרְכ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*! \rb Give|תְּנוּ־\rb* \rb me|לִ֣י\rb* \rb a man|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb to fight|וְנִֽלָּחֲמָ֖ה\rb*\rb |יָֽחַד׃\rb*!”
\p \v 11 \rb On hearing|וַיִּשְׁמַ֤ע\rb* \rb the|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb words|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Philistine|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֖י\rb*, \rb Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb were dismayed|וַיֵּחַ֥תּוּ\rb* \rb and greatly|מְאֹֽד׃פ\rb* \rb afraid|וַיִּֽרְא֖וּ\rb*.
\s1 David Accepts the Challenge
\p \v 12 \rb Now David|וְדָוִד֩\rb* \rb was the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of a man|אִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb named|וּשְׁמ֣וֹ\rb* \rb Jesse|יִשַׁ֔י\rb*, \rb an Ephrathite|אֶפְרָתִ֜י\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֗ה\rb*\rb |מִבֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb from Bethlehem|לֶ֙חֶם֙\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb who had|וְל֖וֹ\rb* \rb eight|שְׁמֹנָ֣ה\rb* \rb sons|בָנִ֑ים\rb*\rb |וְהָאִישׁ֙\rb*. \rb And in the days|בִּימֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb*, \rb Jesse was old|זָקֵ֖ן\rb* \rb and well along|בָּ֥א\rb* \rb in years|בַאֲנָשִֽׁים׃\rb*.\f + \fr 17:12 \ft LXX and Syriac; Hebrew \fqa he had become advanced among men\f* \v 13 \rb |וַיֵּ֨לְכ֜וּ\rb* \rb The three|שְׁלֹ֤שֶׁת\rb* \rb older|הַגְּדֹלִ֔ים\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Jesse|יִשַׁי֙\rb* \rb had followed|הָלְכ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵי־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb into battle|לַמִּלְחָמָ֑ה\rb*:\rb |שְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb*\rb |בָּנָ֗יו\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb*\rb |הָלְכוּ֙\rb*\rb |בַּמִּלְחָמָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְשֵׁ֣ם׀\rb* \rb The firstborn|הַבְּכ֗וֹר\rb* \rb was Eliab|אֱלִיאָ֣ב\rb*, \rb the second|וּמִשְׁנֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb was Abinadab|אֲבִ֣ינָדָ֔ב\rb*, \rb and the third|וְהַשְּׁלִשִׁ֖י\rb* \rb was Shammah|שַׁמָּֽה׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb And David|וְדָוִ֖ד\rb*\rb |ה֣וּא\rb* \rb was the youngest|הַקָּטָ֑ן\rb*.
\p \rb The three|וּשְׁלֹשָׁה֙\rb* \rb oldest|הַגְּדֹלִ֔ים\rb* \rb had followed|הָלְכ֖וּ\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁאֽוּל׃ס\rb*, \v 15 \rb but David|וְדָוִ֛ד\rb* \rb went back and forth|הֹלֵ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |וָשָׁ֖ב\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֑וּל\rb* \rb to tend|לִרְע֛וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his father’s|אָבִ֖יו\rb* \rb sheep|צֹ֥אן\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb in Bethlehem|לָֽחֶם׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb For forty|אַרְבָּעִ֥ים\rb* \rb days|יֽוֹם׃פ\rb* \rb the Philistine|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֖י\rb* \rb came forward|וַיִּגַּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb every morning|הַשְׁכֵּ֣ם\rb* \rb and evening|וְהַעֲרֵ֑ב\rb* \rb to take his stand|וַיִּתְיַצֵּ֖ב\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb One day Jesse|יִשַׁ֜י\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to his son|בְּנ֗וֹ\rb* \rb David|לְדָוִ֣ד\rb*, “\rb Take|קַח־\rb*\rb |נָ֤א\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb ephah|אֵיפַ֤ת\rb* \rb of roasted grain|הַקָּלִיא֙\rb*\f + \fr 17:17 \fqa An ephah \ft is approximately 20 dry quarts or 22 liters of roasted grain.\f* \rb and these|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb ten loaves|וַעֲשָׂרָ֥ה\rb* \rb of bread|לֶ֖חֶם\rb* \rb for your brothers|לְאַחֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb and hurry|וְהָרֵ֥ץ\rb* \rb to their|לְאַחֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֖ה\rb*. \v 18 \rb |וְ֠אֵת\rb* \rb Take also|תָּבִ֖יא\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb ten|עֲשֶׂ֜רֶת\rb* \rb portions|חֲרִצֵ֤י\rb* \rb of cheese|הֶֽחָלָב֙\rb* \rb to the commander|לְשַׂר־\rb* \rb of their unit|הָאָ֑לֶף\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*. \rb Check|תִּפְקֹ֣ד\rb* \rb on the welfare|לְשָׁל֔וֹם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb of your brothers|אַחֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb and bring back|תִּקָּֽח׃\rb* \rb an assurance from them|עֲרֻבָּתָ֖ם\rb*.\f + \fr 17:18 \ft Or \fqa some token from them \ft or \fqa some pledge from them\f* \v 19 \rb They|וְהֵ֙מָּה֙\rb* \rb are with Saul|וְשָׁא֤וּל\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the men|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb in the Valley|בְּעֵ֖מֶק\rb* \rb of Elah|הָֽאֵלָ֑ה\rb*, \rb fighting|נִלְחָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb against|עִם־\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּֽים׃\rb*.”
\p \v 20 \rb So David|דָּוִ֜ד\rb* \rb got up early|וַיַּשְׁכֵּ֨ם\rb* \rb in the morning|בַּבֹּ֗קֶר\rb*, \rb left|וַיִּטֹּ֤שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the flock|הַצֹּאן֙\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb a keeper|שֹׁמֵ֔ר\rb*, \rb loaded up|וַיִּשָּׂ֣א\rb*, \rb and set out|וַיֵּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Jesse|יִשָׁ֑י\rb* \rb had instructed him|צִוָּ֖הוּ\rb*. \rb He reached|וַיָּבֹא֙\rb* \rb the camp|הַמַּעְגָּ֔לָה\rb* \rb as the army|וְהַחַ֗יִל\rb* \rb was marching out|הַיֹּצֵא֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb its position|הַמַּ֣עֲרָכָ֔ה\rb* \rb and shouting|וְהֵרֵ֖עוּ\rb* \rb the battle cry|בַּמִּלְחָמָֽה׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb And Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb and the Philistines|וּפְלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb arrayed|וַתַּעֲרֹ֤ךְ\rb* \rb in formation|מַעֲרָכָ֖ה\rb* \rb against|לִקְרַ֥את\rb* \rb each other|מַעֲרָכָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb Then David|דָּוִ֨ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb left|וַיִּטֹּשׁ֩\rb* \rb his supplies|הַכֵּלִ֜ים\rb* \rb in|מֵעָלָ֗יו\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the care|יַד֙\rb* \rb of the quartermaster|שׁוֹמֵ֣ר\rb*\rb |הַכֵּלִ֔ים\rb* \rb and ran|וַיָּ֖רָץ\rb* \rb to the battle line|הַמַּעֲרָכָ֑ה\rb*. \rb When he arrived|וַיָּבֹ֕א\rb*, \rb he asked|וַיִּשְׁאַ֥ל\rb* \rb his brothers|לְאֶחָ֖יו\rb* \rb how they were doing|לְשָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb And as he|וְה֣וּא׀\rb* \rb was speaking|מְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb with them|עִמָּ֗ם\rb*, \rb suddenly|וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb the champion|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |הַבֵּנַ֡יִם\rb* \rb named|שְׁמ֤וֹ\rb* \rb Goliath|גָּלְיָת֩\rb*, \rb the Philistine|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֨י\rb* \rb from Gath|מִגַּת֙\rb*, \rb came forward|עוֹלֶ֞ה\rb* \rb from the ranks|מִמַּעֲרוֹת\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb and shouted|וַיְדַבֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb his usual words|כַּדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb*, \rb which|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb David|דָּוִֽד׃\rb* \rb also heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֖ע\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb When all|וְכֹל֙\rb* \rb the men|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb saw Goliath|בִּרְאוֹתָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הָאִ֑ישׁ\rb*, \rb they fled|וַיָּנֻ֙סוּ֙\rb* \rb from him|מִפָּנָ֔יו\rb* \rb in great fear|וַיִּֽירְא֖וּ\rb*\rb |מְאֹֽד׃\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb Now the men|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb had been saying|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר׀\rb*, “\rb Do you see how|הַרְּאִיתֶם֙\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb*\rb |כִּ֛י\rb* \rb man|הָאִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb keeps coming out|הָֽעֹלֶה֙\rb*\rb |עֹלֶ֑ה\rb*\rb |וְֽ֠הָיָה\rb* \rb to defy|לְחָרֵ֥ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*? \rb To the man|הָאִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb kills him|יַכֶּ֜נּוּ\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ׀\rb* \rb will give|יַעְשְׁרֶ֥נּוּ\rb* \rb great|גָּד֗וֹל\rb* \rb riches|עֹ֣שֶׁר\rb*. \rb And|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb he will give|יִתֶּן־\rb* \rb him|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb his daughter in marriage|בִּתּוֹ֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb exempt|יַעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb his father’s|אָבִ֔יו\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb from taxation|חָפְשִׁ֖י\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.”
\p \v 26 \rb David|דָּוִ֗ד\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶֽל־\rb* \rb the men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֞ים\rb* \rb who were standing|הָעֹמְדִ֣ים\rb* \rb with him|עִמּוֹ֮\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹר֒\rb*, “\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb will be done|יֵּעָשֶׂ֗ה\rb* \rb for the man|לָאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb kills|יַכֶּה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַלָּ֔ז\rb* \rb Philistine|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֣י\rb* \rb and removes|וְהֵסִ֥יר\rb* \rb this disgrace|חֶרְפָּ֖ה\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*? \rb Just who|מִ֗י\rb* \rb is this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb uncircumcised|הֶֽעָרֵל֙\rb* \rb Philistine|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֤י\rb*, \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he should defy|חֵרֵ֔ף\rb* \rb the armies|מַעַרְכ֖וֹת\rb* \rb of the living|חַיִּֽים׃\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֥ים\rb*?”
\p \v 27 \rb The people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb him|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb about the|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb offer|כַּדָּבָ֥ר\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb That is what|כֹּ֣ה\rb* \rb will be done|יֵעָשֶׂ֔ה\rb* \rb for the man|לָאִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb kills him|יַכֶּֽנּוּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 28 \rb Now when David’s oldest|הַגָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb brother|אָחִ֣יו\rb* \rb Eliab|אֱלִיאָב֙\rb* \rb heard him|וַיִּשְׁמַ֤ע\rb* \rb speaking|בְּדַבְּר֖וֹ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֑ים\rb*, \rb his anger|אַף֩\rb*\rb |אֱלִיאָ֨ב\rb* \rb burned|וַיִּֽחַר־\rb* \rb against David|בְּדָוִ֜ד\rb*. “\rb Why|לָמָּה־\rb* \rb have you come down|יָרַ֗דְתָּ\rb* \rb here|זֶּ֣ה\rb*?” \rb he asked|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר׀\rb*. “\rb And with|וְעַל־\rb* \rb whom|מִ֨י\rb* \rb did you leave|נָטַ֜שְׁתָּ\rb* \rb those|הָהֵ֙נָּה֙\rb* \rb few|מְעַ֨ט\rb* \rb sheep|הַצֹּ֤אן\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֔ר\rb*? \rb I|אֲנִ֧י\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֣עְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your pride|זְדֹנְךָ֗\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb and wickedness|רֹ֣עַ\rb* \rb of heart|לְבָבֶ֔ךָ\rb* —\rb |כִּ֗י\rb* \rb you have come down|יָרָֽדְתָּ׃\rb* \rb to|לְמַ֛עַן\rb* \rb see|רְא֥וֹת\rb* \rb the battle|הַמִּלְחָמָ֖ה\rb*!”
\p \v 29 “\rb What|מֶ֥ה\rb* \rb have I done|עָשִׂ֖יתִי\rb* \rb now|עָ֑תָּה\rb*?”\rb |הֲל֖וֹא\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*. “\rb Was it not|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb just a question|דָּבָ֥ר\rb*?” \v 30 \rb Then he turned|וַיִּסֹּ֤ב\rb* \rb from him|מֵֽאֶצְלוֹ֙\rb* \rb toward|אֶל־\rb*\rb |מ֣וּל\rb* \rb another|אַחֵ֔ר\rb* \rb and asked|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb about the|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb offer|כַּדָּבָ֣ר\rb*, \rb and those people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb answered him|וַיְשִׁבֻ֤הוּ\rb* \rb just as|דָּבָ֔ר\rb*\rb |כַּדָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb the first ones had answered|הָרִאשֽׁוֹן׃\rb*.
\p \v 31 \rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb Now David’s|דָּוִ֑ד\rb* \rb words|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb were overheard|וַיְּשָּֽׁמְעוּ֙\rb*\rb |הַדְּבָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb and reported|וַיַּגִּ֥דוּ\rb* \rb to|לִפְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb*, \rb who sent for him|וַיִּקָּחֵֽהוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 32 \rb And David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb*, “\rb Let no|אַל־\rb* \rb man’s|אָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb heart|לֵב־\rb* \rb fail|יִפֹּ֥ל\rb* \rb on account of|עָלָ֑יו\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb Philistine|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֥י\rb*. \rb Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֣\rb* \rb will go|יֵלֵ֔ךְ\rb* \rb and fight him|וְנִלְחַ֖ם\rb*\rb |עִם־\rb*!”
\p \v 33 \rb But Saul|שָׁא֜וּל\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |דָּוִ֗ד\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*, “\rb You cannot|לֹ֤א\rb*\rb |תוּכַל֙\rb* \rb go out|לָלֶ֙כֶת֙\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb Philistine|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֣י\rb* \rb to fight|לְהִלָּחֵ֖ם\rb* \rb him|עִמּ֑וֹ\rb*.\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb You are|אַ֔תָּה\rb* \rb just a boy|נַ֣עַר\rb*, \rb and he|וְה֛וּא\rb* \rb has been a warrior|אִ֥ישׁ\rb*\rb |מִלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb from his youth|מִנְּעֻרָֽיו׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 34 \rb David|דָּוִד֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |שָׁא֔וּל\rb*, “\rb Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֛\rb* \rb has been tending|רֹעֶ֨ה\rb*\rb |הָיָ֧ה\rb* \rb his father’s|לְאָבִ֖יו\rb* \rb sheep|בַּצֹּ֑אן\rb*, \rb and whenever a lion|הָֽאֲרִי֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb or a bear|הַדּ֔וֹב\rb* \rb came|וּבָ֤א\rb* \rb and carried off|וְנָשָׂ֥א\rb* \rb a lamb|שֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb from the flock|מֵהָעֵֽדֶר׃\rb*, \v 35 \rb I went|וְיָצָ֧אתִי\rb* \rb after it|אַחֲרָ֛יו\rb*, \rb struck it down|וְהִכִּתִ֖יו\rb*, \rb and delivered the lamb|וְהִצַּ֣לְתִּי\rb* \rb from its mouth|מִפִּ֑יו\rb*. \rb If it reared up|וַיָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb against me|עָלַ֔י\rb*, \rb I would grab|וְהֶחֱזַ֙קְתִּי֙\rb* \rb it by its fur|בִּזְקָנ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb strike it down|וְהִכִּתִ֖יו\rb*, \rb and kill it|וַהֲמִיתִּֽיו׃\rb*. \v 36 \rb Your servant|עַבְדֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb has killed|הִכָּ֣ה\rb* \rb lions|הָאֲרִ֛י\rb*\rb |גַּם־\rb* \rb and|גַּ֧ם\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb bears|הַדּ֖וֹב\rb*; \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb uncircumcised|הֶעָרֵ֤ל\rb* \rb Philistine|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֨י\rb* \rb will be|וְֽ֠הָיָה\rb* \rb like one|כְּאַחַ֣ד\rb* \rb of them|מֵהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he has defied|חֵרֵ֔ף\rb* \rb the armies|מַעַרְכֹ֖ת\rb* \rb of the living|חַיִּֽים׃ס\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֥ים\rb*.”
\p \v 37 \rb David|דָּוִד֒\rb* \rb added|וַיֹּאמֶר֮\rb*, “\rb The LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb delivered me|הִצִּלַ֜נִי\rb* \rb from the claws|מִיַּ֤ד\rb* \rb of the lion|הָֽאֲרִי֙\rb* \rb and|וּמִיַּ֣ד\rb* \rb the bear|הַדֹּ֔ב\rb*\rb |ה֣וּא\rb*, \rb will deliver me|יַצִּילֵ֔נִי\rb* \rb from the hand|מִיַּ֥ד\rb* \rb of this|הַזֶּ֑הס\rb* \rb Philistine|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֖י\rb*.”
\p “\rb Go|לֵ֔ךְ\rb*,” \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֤וּל\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |דָּוִד֙\rb*, “\rb and may the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb be|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּֽךְ׃\rb*.”
\s1 David Slays Goliath
\p \v 38 \rb Then Saul|שָׁא֤וּל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb clothed|וַיַּלְבֵּ֨שׁ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb in his own tunic|מַדָּ֔יו\rb*, \rb put|וְנָתַ֛ן\rb* \rb a bronze|נְחֹ֖שֶׁת\rb* \rb helmet|ק֥וֹבַע\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his head|רֹאשׁ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and dressed|וַיַּלְבֵּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb in armor|שִׁרְיֽוֹן׃\rb*. \v 39 \rb David|דָּוִ֣ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb strapped|וַיַּחְגֹּ֣ר\rb* \rb his sword|חַ֠רְבּוֹ\rb* \rb over|מֵעַ֨ל\rb* \rb the tunic|לְמַדָּ֜יו\rb* \rb and tried|וַיֹּ֣אֶל\rb* \rb to walk|לָלֶכֶת֮\rb*, \rb but|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he was not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb accustomed to them|נִסָּה֒\rb*.
\p “\rb I cannot|לֹ֥א\rb*\rb |אוּכַ֛ל\rb* \rb walk|לָלֶ֥כֶת\rb* \rb in these|בָּאֵ֖לֶּה\rb*,”\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֜ד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֗וּל\rb*. “\rb I am not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb accustomed to them|נִסִּ֑יתִי\rb*.” \rb So David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb took them|וַיְסִרֵ֥ם\rb* \rb off|מֵעָלָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 40 \rb And David took|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb his staff|מַקְל֜וֹ\rb* \rb in his hand|בְּיָד֗וֹ\rb*, \rb selected|וַיִּבְחַר־\rb* \rb five|חֲמִשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb smooth|חַלֻּקֵֽי־\rb* \rb stones|אֲבָנִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the brook|הַנַּ֡חַל\rb*, \rb and put|וַיָּ֣שֶׂם\rb* \rb them|אֹ֠תָם\rb* \rb in the pouch|וּבַיַּלְק֖וּט\rb* \rb of his shepherd’s|הָרֹעִ֧ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb bag|בִּכְלִ֨י\rb*. \rb And with his sling|וְקַלְּע֣וֹ\rb* \rb in hand|בְיָד֑וֹ\rb*, \rb he approached|וַיִּגַּ֖שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the Philistine|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּֽי׃\rb*.
\p \v 41 \rb Now the Philistine|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֔י\rb*\rb |הֹלֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb came|וַיֵּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb closer|וְקָרֵ֖ב\rb* \rb and closer to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*, \rb with his shield-bearer|וְהָאִ֛ישׁ\rb*\rb |נֹשֵׂ֥א\rb*\rb |הַצִּנָּ֖ה\rb* \rb before him|לְפָנָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 42 \rb When the Philistine|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֛י\rb* \rb looked|וַיַּבֵּ֧ט\rb* \rb and saw|וַיִּרְאֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb*, \rb he despised him|וַיִּבְזֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he was|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb just a boy|נַ֔עַר\rb*, \rb ruddy|וְאַדְמֹנִ֖י\rb* \rb and|עִם־\rb* \rb handsome|יְפֵ֥ה\rb*\rb |מַרְאֶֽה׃\rb*. \v 43 “\rb Am I|אָנֹ֔כִי\rb* \rb a dog|הֲכֶ֣לֶב\rb*,” \rb he|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּי֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*, “\rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb come|בָֽא־\rb* \rb at me|אֵלַ֖י\rb* \rb with sticks|בַּמַּקְל֑וֹת\rb*?” \rb And the Philistine|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֛י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb cursed|וַיְקַלֵּ֧ל\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb by his gods|בֵּאלֹהָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 44 “\rb Come|לְכָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb here|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֖י\rb*,” \rb he called|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*, “\rb and I will give|וְאֶתְּנָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your flesh|בְּשָׂ֣רְךָ֔\rb* \rb to the birds|לְע֥וֹף\rb* \rb of the air|הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and the beasts|וּלְבֶהֱמַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the field|הַשָּׂדֶֽה׃ס\rb*!”
\p \v 45 \rb But David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Philistine|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֔י\rb*, “\rb You|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb come|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb against me|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb with sword|בְּחֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb and spear|וּבַחֲנִ֣ית\rb* \rb and javelin|וּבְכִיד֑וֹן\rb*, \rb but I|וְאָנֹכִ֣י\rb* \rb come|בָֽא־\rb* \rb against|אֵלֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb you in the name|בְּשֵׁם֙\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֛י\rb* \rb of the armies|מַעַרְכ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you have defied|חֵרַֽפְתָּ׃\rb*. \v 46 \rb This|הַזֶּ֡ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb will deliver you|יְסַגֶּרְךָ֩\rb* \rb into my hand|בְּיָדִ֜י\rb*. \rb This|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb I will strike you down|וְהִכִּיתִ֗ךָ\rb*, \rb cut off your head|רֹֽאשְׁךָ֙\rb*\rb |מֵעָלֶ֔יךָ\rb*,\rb |וַהֲסִרֹתִ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and give|וְנָ֨תַתִּ֜י\rb* \rb the carcasses|פֶּ֣גֶר\rb* \rb of the Philistine|פְלִשְׁתִּים֙\rb* \rb army|מַחֲנֵ֤ה\rb* \rb to the birds|לְע֥וֹף\rb* \rb of the air|הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and the creatures|וּלְחַיַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*. \rb Then the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb world|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb will know|וְיֵֽדְעוּ֙\rb* \rb that|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb there is|יֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb a God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb in Israel|לְיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 47 \rb And all|כָּל־\rb* \rb those|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb assembled here|הַקָּהָ֣ל\rb* \rb will know|וְיֵֽדְעוּ֙\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb it is not|לֹ֛א\rb* \rb by sword|בְּחֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb or spear|וּבַחֲנִ֖ית\rb* \rb that the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb saves|יְהוֹשִׁ֣יעַ\rb*; \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the battle is|הַמִּלְחָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb the LORD’s|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb*, \rb and He will give|וְנָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb all of you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb into our hands|בְּיָדֵֽנוּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 48 \rb |וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb As|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |קָ֣ם\rb* \rb the Philistine|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֔י\rb* \rb started|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb forward|וַיִּקְרַ֖ב\rb* \rb to attack|לִקְרַ֣את\rb* \rb him|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*, \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb ran|וַיָּ֥רָץ\rb* \rb quickly|וַיְמַהֵ֣ר\rb* \rb toward the battle line|הַמַּעֲרָכָ֖ה\rb* \rb to meet|לִקְרַ֥את\rb* \rb him|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּֽי׃\rb*. \v 49 \rb Then David|דָּוִ֨ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb reached|וַיִּשְׁלַח֩\rb*\rb |יָד֜וֹ\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb his bag|הַכֶּ֗לִי\rb*, \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb out|מִשָּׁ֥ם\rb* \rb a stone|אֶ֙בֶן֙\rb*, \rb and slung it|וַיְקַלַּ֔ע\rb*, \rb striking|וַיַּ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Philistine|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֖י\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the forehead|מִצְח֑וֹ\rb*. \rb The stone|הָאֶ֙בֶן֙\rb* \rb sank|וַתִּטְבַּ֤ע\rb* \rb into his forehead|בְּמִצְח֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and he fell|וַיִּפֹּ֥ל\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb facedown|פָּנָ֖יו\rb* \rb on the ground|אָֽרְצָה׃\rb*.
\p \v 50 \rb Thus David|דָּוִ֤ד\rb* \rb prevailed|וַיֶּחֱזַ֨ק\rb* \rb over|מִן־\rb* \rb the Philistine|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּי֙\rb* \rb with a sling|בַּקֶּ֣לַע\rb* \rb and a stone|וּבָאֶ֔בֶן\rb*; \rb without|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb a sword|וְחֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb in his hand|בְּיַד־\rb*\rb |דָּוִֽד׃\rb* \rb he struck down|וַיַּ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Philistine|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֖י\rb* \rb and killed him|וַיְמִיתֵ֑הוּ\rb*. \v 51 \rb David|דָּ֠וִד\rb* \rb ran|וַיָּ֣רָץ\rb* \rb and stood|וַיַּעֲמֹ֨ד\rb* \rb over him|אֶל־\rb*. \rb He grabbed|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Philistine’s|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֜י\rb* \rb sword|חַ֠רְבּוֹ\rb* \rb and pulled it|וַֽיִּשְׁלְפָ֤הּ\rb* \rb from its sheath|מִתַּעְרָהּ֙\rb* \rb and killed him|וַיְמֹ֣תְתֵ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb and he cut off|וַיִּכְרָת־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his head|רֹאשׁ֑וֹ\rb* \rb with the sword|בָּ֖הּ\rb*.
\p \rb When the Philistines|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֛ים\rb* \rb saw|וַיִּרְא֧וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb their hero|גִּבּוֹרָ֖ם\rb* \rb was dead|מֵ֥ת\rb*, \rb they turned and ran|וַיָּנֻֽסוּ׃\rb*. \v 52 \rb Then the men|אַנְשֵׁי֩\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֨ל\rb* \rb and Judah|וִיהוּדָ֜ה\rb* \rb charged forward|וַיָּקֻ֣מוּ\rb* \rb with a shout|וַיָּרִ֗עוּ\rb* \rb and pursued|וַֽיִּרְדְּפוּ֙\rb* \rb the Philistines|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the entrance|בּוֹאֲךָ֣\rb* \rb of Gath|גַ֔יְא\rb*\f + \fr 17:52 \ft LXX; Hebrew \fqa of Gai\ft ; that is, \fqa of the valley\f* \rb and to|וְעַ֖ד\rb* \rb the gates|שַׁעֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Ekron|עֶקְר֑וֹן\rb*. \rb And the bodies|חַֽלְלֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּים֙\rb* \rb were strewn|וַֽיִּפְּל֞וּ\rb* \rb along the Shaaraim|שַׁעֲרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb road|בְּדֶ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb Gath|גַּ֖ת\rb*\rb |וְעַד־\rb* \rb and Ekron|עֶקְרֽוֹן׃\rb*.
\p \v 53 \rb When the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּשֻׁ֙בוּ֙\rb* \rb from their pursuit|מִדְּלֹ֖ק\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb*, \rb they plundered|וַיָּשֹׁ֖סּוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their camps|מַחֲנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 54 \rb David|דָּוִד֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֤ח\rb* \rb the head|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of the Philistine|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֔י\rb* \rb and brought|וַיְבִאֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb it to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*, \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb he put|שָׂ֥ם\rb* \rb Goliath’s weapons|כֵּלָ֖יו\rb* \rb in his own tent|בְּאָהֳלֽוֹ׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 55 \rb As Saul|שָׁא֜וּל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had watched|וְכִרְא֨וֹת\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֗ד\rb* \rb going out|יֹצֵא֙\rb* \rb to confront|לִקְרַ֣את\rb* \rb the Philistine|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֔י\rb*, \rb he said|אָמַ֗ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Abner|אַבְנֵר֙\rb* \rb the commander|שַׂ֣ר\rb* \rb of the army|הַצָּבָ֔א\rb*, “\rb Abner|אַבְנֵ֑ר\rb*, \rb whose|מִי־\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb is this|זֶ֥ה\rb* \rb young man|הַנַּ֖עַר\rb*?”
\p “\rb As surely as you|נַפְשְׁךָ֥\rb* \rb live|חֵֽי־\rb*, \rb O king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*,” \rb Abner|אַבְנֵ֔ר\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I do not|אִם־\rb* \rb know|יָדָֽעְתִּי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 56 “\rb Find out|שְׁאַ֣ל\rb*\rb |אַתָּ֔ה\rb* \rb whose|מִי־\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb this|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb young man is!|הָעָֽלֶם׃ס\rb*” \rb said|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*.
\p \v 57 \rb So when David|דָּוִ֗ד\rb* \rb returned|וּכְשׁ֣וּב\rb* \rb from killing|מֵֽהַכּוֹת֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Philistine|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֔י\rb*, \rb still holding his|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֖י\rb* \rb head|וְרֹ֥אשׁ\rb* \rb in his hand|בְּיָדֽוֹ׃\rb*, \rb Abner|אַבְנֵ֔ר\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֤ח\rb* \rb him|אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb and brought him|וַיְבִאֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֑וּל\rb*.
\p \v 58 “\rb Whose|מִ֥י\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb are you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb*, \rb young man|הַנָּ֑עַר\rb*?” \rb asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb*\rb |אֵלָיו֙\rb*.
\p “\rb I am the son|בֶּֽן־\rb* \rb of your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֥\rb* \rb Jesse|יִשַׁ֖י\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Bethlehem|הַלַּחְמִֽי׃\rb*,” \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*.
\c 18
\s1 Jonathan Befriends David
\p \v 1 \rb After|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb David had finished|כְּכַלֹּתוֹ֙\rb* \rb speaking|לְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb with|אֶל־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb*, \rb the souls|וְנֶ֙פֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb of Jonathan|יְה֣וֹנָתָ֔ן\rb* \rb and David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb* \rb were knit together|נִקְשְׁרָ֖ה\rb*\rb |בְּנֶ֣פֶשׁ\rb*, \rb and Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֖ן\rb* \rb loved him|וַיֶּאֱהָבוֹ\rb* \rb as himself|כְּנַפְשֽׁוֹ׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb And from that|הַה֑וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb kept David with him|וַיִּקָּחֵ֥הוּ\rb* \rb and did not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb let him|נְתָנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb return|לָשׁ֖וּב\rb* \rb to his father’s|אָבִֽיו׃\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֥ית\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Then Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֛ן\rb* \rb made|וַיִּכְרֹ֧ת\rb* \rb a covenant|בְּרִ֑ית\rb* \rb with David|וְדָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb because he loved|בְּאַהֲבָת֥וֹ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb as himself|כְּנַפְשֽׁוֹ׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb And Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֗ן\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb removed|וַיִּתְפַּשֵּׁ֣ט\rb* \rb the robe|הַמְּעִיל֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he was wearing|עָלָ֔יו\rb* \rb and gave|וַֽיִּתְּנֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb it to David|לְדָוִ֑ד\rb*, \rb along with his tunic|וּמַדָּ֕יו\rb*,\rb |וְעַד־\rb* \rb his sword|חַרְבּ֥וֹ\rb*,\rb |וְעַד־\rb* \rb his bow|קַשְׁתּ֖וֹ\rb*,\rb |וְעַד־\rb* \rb and his belt|חֲגֹרֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\s1 Saul Envies David
\p \v 5 \rb So David|דָוִ֜ד\rb* \rb marched out|וַיֵּצֵ֨א\rb* \rb and prospered|יַשְׂכִּ֔יל\rb* \rb in everything|בְּכֹל֩\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb* \rb sent him to do|יִשְׁלָחֶ֤נּוּ\rb*, \rb and Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb set him|וַיְשִׂמֵ֣הוּ\rb* \rb over|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the men|אַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of war|הַמִּלְחָמָ֑ה\rb*. \rb And this was pleasing|וַיִּיטַב֙\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb*, \rb and of Saul’s|שָׁאֽוּל׃פ\rb* \rb officers|עַבְדֵ֥י\rb* \rb as well|וְגַ֕ם\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֵ֖י\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb As the troops|וַיְהִ֣י\rb*\rb |בְּבוֹאָ֗ם\rb* \rb were returning home|בְּשׁ֤וּב\rb* \rb after David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb had killed|מֵהַכּ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Philistine|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֔י\rb*, \rb the women|הַנָּשִׁ֜ים\rb* \rb came out|וַתֵּצֶ֨אנָה\rb* \rb of all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the cities|עָרֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb to meet|לִקְרַ֖את\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֣וּל\rb* \rb with singing|לָשׁוּר\rb* \rb and dancing|וְהַמְּחֹל֔וֹת\rb*, \rb with joyful songs|בְּשִׂמְחָ֖ה\rb*, \rb and with tambourines|בְּתֻפִּ֥ים\rb* \rb and other instruments|וּבְשָׁלִשִֽׁים׃\rb*.\f + \fr 18:6 \ft Possibly \fqa three-stringed instruments \ft or \fqa cymbals \ft or \fqa lutes \ft or \fqa lyres \f* \v 7 \rb And as the women danced|הַֽמְשַׂחֲק֖וֹת\rb*\rb |הַנָּשִׁ֥ים\rb*,\rb |וַתֹּאמַ֑רְןָ\rb* \rb they sang out|וַֽתַּעֲנֶ֛ינָה\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb* \rb has slain|הִכָּ֤ה\rb* \rb his thousands|בְּאַלְפּוֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and David|וְדָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb his tens of thousands|בְּרִבְבֹתָֽיו׃\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb And Saul|לְשָׁא֜וּל\rb* \rb was furious|וַיִּ֨חַר\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֗ד\rb* \rb and resented|וַיֵּ֤רַע\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינָיו֙\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb song|הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb*. “\rb They have ascribed|נָתְנ֤וּ\rb* \rb tens of thousands|רְבָב֔וֹת\rb* \rb to David|לְדָוִד֙\rb*,” \rb he said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb but only|נָתְנ֖וּ\rb* \rb thousands|הָאֲלָפִ֑ים\rb* \rb to me|וְלִ֥י\rb*. \rb What more|וְע֥וֹד\rb* \rb can he have|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb but|אַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb the kingdom|הַמְּלוּכָֽה׃\rb*?” \v 9 \rb And|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb from that|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb day|מֵהַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb forward|וָהָֽלְאָה׃ס\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb kept a jealous eye|עָוֹן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb on David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb The next day|מִֽמָּחֳרָ֗ת\rb* \rb a spirit|רוּחַ֩\rb* \rb of distress|רָעָ֤ה׀\rb*\f + \fr 18:10 \ft Or \fqa a harmful spirit\f* \rb sent from God|אֱלֹהִ֨ים׀\rb* \rb came|וַתִּצְלַ֣ח\rb* \rb upon|אֶל־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb*, \rb and he prophesied|וַיִּתְנַבֵּ֣א\rb* \rb inside the|בְתוֹךְ־\rb* \rb house|הַבַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb while David|וְדָוִ֛ד\rb* \rb played the harp|מְנַגֵּ֥ן\rb*\rb |כְּי֣וֹם׀\rb* \rb as usual|בְּי֑וֹם\rb*. \rb Now Saul|שָׁאֽוּל׃\rb* \rb was holding|בְּיָד֖וֹ\rb* \rb a spear|וְהַחֲנִ֖ית\rb*,\rb |בְּיַד־\rb* \v 11 \rb and he|שָׁאוּל֙\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb hurled it|וַיָּ֤טֶל\rb*\rb |הַחֲנִ֔ית\rb*, \rb thinking|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I will pin|אַכֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb David|בְדָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb to the wall|וּבַקִּ֑יר\rb*.” \rb But David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb* \rb eluded|וַיִּסֹּ֥ב\rb* \rb him|מִפָּנָ֖יו\rb* \rb twice|פַּעֲמָֽיִם׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb So Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb was afraid|וַיִּרָ֥א\rb* \rb of|מִלִּפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֑ד\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb with David|עִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb but|וּמֵעִ֥ם\rb* \rb had departed|סָֽר׃\rb* \rb from Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb*. \v 13 \rb Therefore Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb*\rb |מֵֽעִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb sent David away|וַיְסִרֵ֤הוּ\rb* \rb and gave|וַיְשִׂמֵ֥הוּ\rb* \rb him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb command|שַׂר־\rb* \rb of a thousand men|אָ֑לֶף\rb*. \rb David led|וַיֵּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb the troops out to battle|הָעָֽם׃פ\rb* \rb and back|וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb*\rb |לִפְנֵ֥י\rb*, \v 14 \rb and he continued|וַיְהִ֥י\rb*\rb |דָוִ֛ד\rb* \rb to prosper|מַשְׂכִּ֑יל\rb* \rb in all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb his ways|דְּרָכָ֖ו\rb*, \rb because the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb was with him|עִמּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb When Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֣רְא\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb David|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb was very|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb successful|מַשְׂכִּ֣יל\rb*, \rb he was afraid|וַיָּ֖גָר\rb* \rb of him|מִפָּנָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb But all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb and Judah|וִיהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb loved|אֹהֵ֖ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he|ה֛וּא\rb* \rb was leading them out to battle|יוֹצֵ֥א\rb* \rb and back|וָבָ֖א\rb*\rb |לִפְנֵיהֶֽם׃פ\rb*.
\s1 David Marries Michal
\p \v 17 \rb Then Saul|שָׁא֜וּל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֗ד\rb*, “\rb Here|הִנֵּה֩\rb* \rb is my older|הַגְּדוֹלָ֤ה\rb* \rb daughter|בִתִּ֨י\rb* \rb Merab|מֵרַב֙\rb*.\rb |אֹתָהּ֙\rb* \rb I will give her|אֶתֶּן־\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֣\rb* \rb in marriage|לְאִשָּׁ֔ה\rb*. \rb Only|אַ֚ךְ\rb* \rb be|הֱיֵה־\rb* \rb valiant|חַ֔יִל\rb* \rb for me|לִּ֣י\rb* \rb and fight|וְהִלָּחֵ֖ם\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb battles|מִלְחֲמ֣וֹת\rb*.” \rb But Saul|וְשָׁא֣וּל\rb* \rb was thinking|אָמַ֗ר\rb*, “\rb |אַל־\rb* \rb I need not raise|תְּהִ֤י\rb* \rb my hand|יָדִי֙\rb* \rb against him|בּ֔וֹ\rb*; \rb let the hand|יַד־\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּֽים׃ס\rb* \rb be|וּתְהִי־\rb* \rb against him|ב֖וֹ\rb*.”
\p \v 18 \rb And David|דָּוִ֜ד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֗וּל\rb*, “\rb Who|מִ֤י\rb* \rb am I|אָֽנֹכִי֙\rb*, \rb and what|וּמִ֣י\rb* \rb is my family|חַיַּ֔י\rb* \rb or my father’s|אָבִ֖י\rb* \rb clan|מִשְׁפַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I should become|אֶהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb the son-in-law|חָתָ֖ן\rb* \rb of the king|לַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*?” \v 19 \rb So when it was|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb time|בְּעֵ֥ת\rb*\f + \fr 18:19 \ft Or \fqa But when it was time\f* \rb to give|תֵּ֛ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Saul’s|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb Merab|מֵרַ֥ב\rb* \rb to David|לְדָוִ֑ד\rb*, \rb she|וְהִ֧יא\rb* \rb was given|נִתְּנָ֛ה\rb* \rb in marriage|לְאִשָּֽׁה׃\rb* \rb to Adriel|לְעַדְרִיאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb of Meholah|הַמְּחֹלָתִ֖י\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb Now Saul’s|שָׁא֖וּל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb Michal|מִיכַ֥ל\rb* \rb loved|וַתֶּאֱהַ֛ב\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*, \rb and when this was reported|וַיַּגִּ֣דוּ\rb* \rb to Saul|לְשָׁא֔וּל\rb*, \rb it|הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb pleased|וַיִּשַׁ֥ר\rb* \rb him|בְּעֵינָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 21 “\rb I will give her|אֶתְּנֶ֤נָּה\rb* \rb to David|לּוֹ֙\rb*,” \rb Saul|שָׁא֜וּל\rb* \rb thought|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*, “\rb so that she may be|וּתְהִי־\rb* \rb a snare|לְמוֹקֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb to him|ל֣וֹ\rb*, \rb and the hand|יַד־\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb* \rb may be|וּתְהִי־\rb* \rb against him|ב֖וֹ\rb*.” \rb So Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*, “\rb For a second time|בִּשְׁתַּ֛יִם\rb* \rb now|הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb* \rb you can be my son-in-law|תִּתְחַתֵּ֥ן\rb*.”
\p \v 22 \rb Then Saul|שָׁא֜וּל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb ordered|וַיְצַ֨ו\rb* \rb his servants|עֲבָדָ֗ו\rb*, “\rb Speak|דַּבְּר֨וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֤ד\rb* \rb privately|בַּלָּט֙\rb* \rb and tell him|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, ‘\rb Behold|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb*, \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb is pleased|חָפֵ֤ץ\rb* \rb with you|בְּךָ֙\rb*, \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his servants|עֲבָדָ֖יו\rb* \rb love you|אֲהֵב֑וּךָ\rb*. \rb Now therefore|וְעַתָּ֖ה\rb*, \rb become his|בַּמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb son-in-law|הִתְחַתֵּ֥ן\rb*.’”
\p \v 23 \rb But when Saul’s|שָׁאוּל֙\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדֵ֤י\rb* \rb relayed|וַֽיְדַבְּר֞וּ\rb*\rb |בְּאָזְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb to David|דָוִ֔ד\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb he|דָּוִ֗ד\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Does it seem trivial|הַֽנְקַלָּ֤ה\rb* \rb in your sight|בְעֵֽינֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb to be the son-in-law|הִתְחַתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb of the king|בַּמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*? \rb I|וְאָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb am a poor|רָ֥שׁ\rb* \rb man|אִֽישׁ־\rb* \rb and lightly esteemed|וְנִקְלֶֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 24 \rb And the servants|עַבְדֵ֥י\rb* \rb told|וַיַּגִּ֜דוּ\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֛וּל\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb what|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb*\rb |כַּדְּבָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb David|דָּוִֽד׃פ\rb* \rb had said|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb Saul|שָׁא֜וּל\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Say|תֹאמְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb to David|לְדָוִ֗ד\rb*, ‘\rb The king|לַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb desires|חֵ֤פֶץ\rb* \rb no|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb other dowry|בְּמֹ֔הַר\rb* \rb but|כִּ֗י\rb* \rb a hundred|בְּמֵאָה֙\rb* \rb Philistine|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb foreskins|עָרְל֣וֹת\rb* \rb as revenge|לְהִנָּקֵ֖ם\rb* \rb on his|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb enemies|בְּאֹיְבֵ֣י\rb*.’” \rb But Saul|וְשָׁא֣וּל\rb* \rb intended|חָשַׁ֔ב\rb* \rb to cause David’s|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb death|לְהַפִּ֥יל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb at the hands|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb When the servants|עֲבָדָ֤יו\rb* \rb reported|וַיַּגִּ֨דוּ\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb terms|הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb to David|לְדָוִד֙\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb he|דָוִ֔ד\rb* \rb was pleased|וַיִּשַׁ֤ר\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָר֙\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb to become the king’s|בַּמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb son-in-law|לְהִתְחַתֵּ֖ן\rb*.\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb*\rb |מָלְא֖וּ\rb* \rb Before the wedding day arrived|הַיָּמִֽים׃\rb*, \v 27 \rb |וַיָּ֨קָם\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֜ד\rb* \rb and his men|וַאֲנָשָׁ֗יו\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ׀\rb*\rb |ה֣וּא\rb* \rb and killed|וַיַּ֣ךְ\rb* \rb two hundred|מָאתַ֣יִם\rb*\rb |אִישׁ֒\rb* \rb Philistines|בַּפְּלִשְׁתִּים֮\rb*. \rb He|דָוִד֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb brought|וַיָּבֵ֤א\rb* \rb their foreskins|עָרְלֹ֣תֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and presented them as payment in full|וַיְמַלְא֣וּם\rb* \rb to become|בַּמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb the king’s|לַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb son-in-law|לְהִתְחַתֵּ֖ן\rb*. \rb Then Saul|שָׁא֛וּל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb his daughter|בִּתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Michal|מִיכַ֥ל\rb* \rb to David|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb in marriage|לְאִשָּֽׁה׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 28 \rb When Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb*\rb |וַיֵּ֔דַע\rb* \rb realized|וַיַּ֤רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb was with|עִם־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb* \rb and that his|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb Michal|וּמִיכַ֥ל\rb* \rb loved David|אֲהֵבַֽתְהוּ׃\rb*, \v 29 \rb he|שָׁא֗וּל\rb* \rb grew even more|וַיֹּ֣אסֶף\rb*\rb |ע֑וֹד\rb* \rb afraid|לֵרֹ֛א\rb* \rb of|מִפְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֖ד\rb*. \rb So from then on|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִֽים׃ס\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֛וּל\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb David’s|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb enemy|אֹיֵ֥ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*.
\p \v 30 \rb Every time|מִדֵּ֣י\rb*\rb |צֵאתָ֗ם\rb* \rb the Philistine|פְלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb*\rb |וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb commanders|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb came out for battle|וַיֵּצְא֖וּ\rb*, \rb David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb was more successful|שָׂכַ֤ל\rb* \rb than all|מִכֹּל֙\rb* \rb of Saul’s|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb officers|עַבְדֵ֣י\rb*, \rb so that his name|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb was highly|מְאֹֽד׃ס\rb* \rb esteemed|וַיִּיקַ֥ר\rb*.
\c 19
\s1 Saul Tries to Kill David
\r (\ref Psalm 59:1–17|PSA 59:1-17\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Then Saul|שָׁא֗וּל\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb ordered|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb his son|בְּנוֹ֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb Jonathan|יוֹנָתָ֤ן\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his servants|עֲבָדָ֔יו\rb* \rb to kill|לְהָמִ֖ית\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*.
\p \rb But Jonathan|וִיהֽוֹנָתָן֙\rb*\rb |שָׁא֔וּל\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb delighted|חָפֵ֥ץ\rb* \rb greatly|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb in David|בְּדָוִ֖ד\rb*, \v 2 \rb so he|יְהוֹנָתָן֙\rb* \rb warned|וַיַּגֵּ֤ד\rb* \rb David|לְדָוִ֣ד\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb My father|אָבִ֖י\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֥וּל\rb* \rb intends|מְבַקֵּ֛שׁ\rb* \rb to kill you|לַהֲמִיתֶ֑ךָ\rb*.\rb |וְעַתָּה֙\rb* \rb Be on your guard|הִשָּֽׁמֶר־\rb*\rb |נָ֣א\rb* \rb in the morning|בַבֹּ֔קֶר\rb*; \rb find|וְיָשַׁבְתָּ֥\rb* \rb a secret place|בַסֵּ֖תֶר\rb* \rb and hide there|וְנַחְבֵּֽאתָ׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb I will|וַאֲנִ֨י\rb* \rb go out|אֵצֵ֜א\rb* \rb and stand|וְעָמַדְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb beside|לְיַד־\rb* \rb my father|אָבִ֗י\rb* \rb in the field|בַּשָּׂדֶה֙\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you are|אַתָּ֣ה\rb*,\rb |שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb so I|וַאֲנִ֕י\rb* \rb can ask|אֲדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb about you|בְּךָ֖\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |אָבִ֑י\rb*. \rb And if I find out|וְרָאִ֥יתִי\rb* \rb anything|מָ֖ה\rb*, \rb I will tell|וְהִגַּ֥דְתִּי\rb* \rb you|לָֽךְ׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb Then Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֤ן\rb* \rb spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֨ר\rb* \rb well|ט֔וֹב\rb* \rb of David|בְּדָוִד֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֑יו\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|אֵ֠לָיו\rb*, “\rb The king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb should not|אַל־\rb* \rb sin|יֶחֱטָ֨א\rb* \rb against his servant|בְּעַבְדּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb David|בְדָוִ֗ד\rb*; \rb he has not|ל֤וֹא\rb* \rb sinned|חָטָא֙\rb* \rb against you|לָ֔ךְ\rb*.\rb |וְכִ֥י\rb* \rb In fact|כִּ֣י\rb*, \rb his actions|מַעֲשָׂ֖יו\rb* \rb have been highly|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb beneficial|טוֹב־\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֥\rb*. \v 5 \rb He took|וַיָּשֶׂם֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his life|נַפְשׁ֨וֹ\rb* \rb in his hands|בְכַפּ֜וֹ\rb* \rb when he struck down|וַיַּ֣ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Philistine|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֗י\rb*, \rb and the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb worked|וַיַּ֨עַשׂ\rb* \rb a great|גְדוֹלָה֙\rb* \rb salvation|תְּשׁוּעָ֤ה\rb* \rb for all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*. \rb You saw|רָאִ֖יתָ\rb* \rb it and rejoiced|וַתִּשְׂמָ֑ח\rb*, \rb so why|וְלָ֤מָּה\rb* \rb would you sin|תֶֽחֱטָא֙\rb* \rb against innocent|נָקִ֔י\rb* \rb blood|בְּדָ֣ם\rb* \rb by killing|לְהָמִ֥ית\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb for no reason|חִנָּֽם׃\rb*?”
\p \v 6 \rb Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb listened|וַיִּשְׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb to the voice|בְּק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֑ן\rb* \rb and swore an oath|וַיִּשָּׁבַ֣ע\rb*\rb |שָׁא֔וּל\rb*: “\rb As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb lives|חַי־\rb*, \rb David will not|אִם־\rb* \rb be put to death|יוּמָֽת׃\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb So Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָן֙\rb* \rb summoned|וַיִּקְרָ֤א\rb* \rb David|לְדָוִ֔ד\rb* \rb and told|וַיַּגֶּד־\rb* \rb him|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb things|הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb*. \rb Then Jonathan|יְה֣וֹנָתָ֔ן\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb brought|וַיָּבֵ֨א\rb*\rb |יְהוֹנָתָ֤ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb*, \rb and David|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb was with Saul|לְפָנָ֖יו\rb* \rb as before|כְּאֶתְמ֥וֹל\rb*\rb |שִׁלְשֽׁוֹם׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb When war|הַמִּלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb broke out|לִֽהְי֑וֹת\rb* \rb again|וַתּ֥וֹסֶף\rb*, \rb David|דָוִ֜ד\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּצֵ֨א\rb* \rb and fought|וַיִּלָּ֣חֶם\rb* \rb the Philistines|בַּפְּלִשְׁתִּ֗ים\rb* \rb and struck|וַיַּ֤ךְ\rb* \rb them|בָּהֶם֙\rb* \rb with such a mighty|גְדוֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb blow|מַכָּ֣ה\rb* \rb that they fled|וַיָּנֻ֖סוּ\rb* \rb before him|מִפָּנָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb But as Saul|וְהוּא֙\rb* \rb was sitting|יוֹשֵׁ֔ב\rb* \rb in his house|בְּבֵית֣וֹ\rb* \rb with his spear|וַחֲנִית֖וֹ\rb* \rb in his hand|בְּיָד֑וֹ\rb*, \rb a spirit|ר֨וּחַ\rb* \rb of distress|רָעָה֙\rb*\f + \fr 19:9 \ft Or \fqa a harmful spirit\f* \rb from the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה׀\rb* \rb came|וַתְּהִי֩\rb* \rb upon|אֶל־\rb* \rb him|שָׁא֔וּל\rb*. \rb While David|וְדָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb was playing the harp|מְנַגֵּ֥ן\rb*\rb |בְּיָֽד׃\rb*, \v 10 \rb Saul|שָׁא֜וּל\rb* \rb tried|וַיְבַקֵּ֨שׁ\rb* \rb to pin|לְהַכּ֤וֹת\rb* \rb him|בְּדָוִ֣ד\rb* \rb to the wall|וּבַקִּ֔יר\rb* \rb with his spear|בַּֽחֲנִית֙\rb*. \rb But David|וְדָוִ֛ד\rb* \rb eluded|וַיִּפְטַר֙\rb*\rb |מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb him|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb and the spear|הַחֲנִ֖ית\rb* \rb struck|וַיַּ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb the wall|בַּקִּ֑יר\rb*. \rb And David fled|נָ֥ס\rb* \rb and escaped|וַיִּמָּלֵ֖ט\rb* \rb that|הֽוּא׃פ\rb* \rb night|בַּלַּ֥יְלָה\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb Then Saul|שָׁא֨וּל\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַח֩\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִ֜ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David’s|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֤ית\rb* \rb to watch him|לְשָׁמְר֔וֹ\rb* \rb and kill him|וְלַהֲמִית֖וֹ\rb* \rb in the morning|בַּבֹּ֑קֶר\rb*. \rb But David’s wife|אִשְׁתּוֹ֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb Michal|מִיכַ֤ל\rb* \rb warned|וַתַּגֵּ֣ד\rb* \rb him|לְדָוִ֗ד\rb*, “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you do not|אֵ֨ינְךָ֜\rb* \rb run|מְמַלֵּ֤ט\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb for your life|נַפְשְׁךָ֙\rb* \rb tonight|הַלַּ֔יְלָה\rb*, \rb tomorrow|מָחָ֖ר\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb will be dead|מוּמָֽת׃\rb*!” \v 12 \rb So Michal|מִיכַ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb lowered|וַתֹּ֧רֶד\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb from|בְּעַ֣ד\rb* \rb the window|הַחַלּ֑וֹן\rb*,\rb |וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb and he ran away|וַיִּבְרַ֖ח\rb* \rb and escaped|וַיִּמָּלֵֽט׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb Then Michal|מִיכַ֜ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַתִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb a household idol|הַתְּרָפִ֗ים\rb*\f + \fr 19:13 \ft Or \fqa a household god\ft ; Hebrew \fqa teraphim\ft ; also in verse 16\f* \rb and laid it|וַתָּ֙שֶׂם֙\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the bed|הַמִּטָּ֔ה\rb*,\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb placed|שָׂ֖מָה\rb* \rb some goat hair|כְּבִ֣יר\rb*\rb |הָֽעִזִּ֔ים\rb* \rb on its head|מְרַֽאֲשֹׁתָ֑יו\rb*, \rb and covered|וַתְּכַ֖ס\rb* \rb it with a garment|בַּבָּֽגֶד׃ס\rb*. \v 14 \rb When Saul|שָׁא֛וּל\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb the messengers|מַלְאָכִ֖ים\rb* \rb to seize|לָקַ֣חַת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*, \rb Michal said|וַתֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb He|הֽוּא׃פ\rb* \rb is ill|חֹלֶ֥ה\rb*.”
\p \v 15 \rb But Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb the messengers back|הַמַּלְאָכִ֔ים\rb* \rb to see|לִרְא֥וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb and told them|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Bring|הַעֲל֨וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֧וֹ\rb* \rb up to me|אֵלַ֖י\rb* \rb in his bed|בַמִּטָּ֛ה\rb* \rb so I can kill him|לַהֲמִתֽוֹ׃\rb*.” \v 16 \rb And when the messengers|הַמַּלְאָכִ֔ים\rb* \rb entered|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb*, \rb there was|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb the idol|הַתְּרָפִ֖ים\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the bed|הַמִּטָּ֑ה\rb*\rb |וּכְבִ֥יר\rb* \rb with the goat hair|הָעִזִּ֖ים\rb* \rb on its head|מְרַאֲשֹׁתָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb And Saul|שָׁא֜וּל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb to Michal|מִיכַ֗ל\rb*, “\rb Why|לָ֤מָּה\rb* \rb did you deceive me|רִמִּיתִ֔נִי\rb* \rb like this|כָּ֙כָה֙\rb*? \rb You sent my enemy|אֹיְבִ֖י\rb* \rb away|וַתְּשַׁלְּחִ֥י\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and he has escaped|וַיִּמָּלֵ֑ט\rb*!”
\p \rb Michal|מִיכַל֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb replied|וַתֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |שָׁא֔וּל\rb*, “\rb He|הוּא־\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֛י\rb*, ‘\rb Help me get away|שַׁלְּחִ֖נִי\rb*, \rb or|לָמָ֥ה\rb* \rb I will kill you|אֲמִיתֵֽךְ׃\rb*!’”
\p \v 18 \rb So David|וְדָוִ֨ד\rb* \rb ran away|בָּרַ֜ח\rb* \rb and escaped|וַיִּמָּלֵ֗ט\rb*. \rb And he went|וַיָּבֹ֤א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵל֙\rb* \rb at Ramah|הָרָמָ֔תָה\rb* \rb and told|וַיַּ֨גֶּד־\rb* \rb him|ל֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֑וּל\rb* \rb had done|עָֽשָׂה־\rb* \rb to him|ל֖וֹ\rb*. \rb Then he|הוּא֙\rb* \rb and Samuel|וּשְׁמוּאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb went to Naioth|וַיֵּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb and stayed|וַיֵּשְׁב֖וּ\rb* \rb there|בְּנֹוִית׃\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb When Saul|לְשָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb was told|וַיֻּגַּ֥ד\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*\rb |הִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb that David|דָוִ֔ד\rb* \rb was at Naioth|בְּנֹוִית\rb* \rb in Ramah|בָּרָמָֽה׃\rb*, \v 20 \rb he|שָׁא֣וּל\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֨ח\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִים֮\rb* \rb to seize|לָקַ֣חַת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|דָּוִד֒\rb*. \rb But when they saw|וַיַּ֗רְא\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb the group|לַהֲקַ֤ת\rb* \rb of prophets|הַנְּבִיאִים֙\rb* \rb prophesying|נִבְּאִ֔ים\rb*, \rb with Samuel|וּשְׁמוּאֵ֕ל\rb*\rb |עֹמֵ֥ד\rb* \rb leading them|נִצָּ֖ב\rb*, \rb the Spirit|ר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb came|וַתְּהִ֞י\rb* \rb upon|עַֽל־\rb* \rb them|עֲלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb and Saul’s|שָׁאוּל֙\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאֲכֵ֤י\rb* \rb also|גַּם־\rb* \rb began to prophesy|וַיִּֽתְנַבְּא֖וּ\rb*.\rb |הֵֽמָּה׃\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb When this was reported|וַיַּגִּ֣דוּ\rb* \rb to Saul|לְשָׁא֗וּל\rb*, \rb he sent|וַיִּשְׁלַח֙\rb* \rb more|אֲחֵרִ֔ים\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִ֣ים\rb*, \rb but they|הֵ֑מָּה\rb* \rb began to prophesy|וַיִּֽתְנַבְּא֖וּ\rb* \rb as well|גַּם־\rb*.
\p \rb So Saul|שָׁא֗וּל\rb* \rb tried again|וַיֹּ֣סֶף\rb* \rb and sent|וַיִּשְׁלַח֙\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִ֣ים\rb* \rb a third time|שְׁלִשִׁ֔ים\rb*, \rb and even|גַּם־\rb* \rb they|הֵֽמָּה׃\rb* \rb began to prophesy|וַיִּֽתְנַבְּא֖וּ\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb Finally, Saul himself|ה֜וּא\rb* \rb left for|וַיֵּ֨לֶךְ\rb*\rb |גַּם־\rb* \rb Ramah|הָרָמָ֗תָה\rb* \rb and came|וַיָּבֹא֙\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the large|הַגָּדוֹל֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb cistern|בּ֤וֹר\rb* \rb at Secu|בַּשֶּׂ֔כוּ\rb*, \rb where he asked|וַיִּשְׁאַ֣ל\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֔אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Where|אֵיפֹ֥ה\rb* \rb are Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and David|וְדָוִ֑ד\rb*?”
\p “\rb At Naioth|בְּנֹוִית\rb* \rb in Ramah|בָּרָמָֽה׃\rb*,” \rb he was told|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*\rb |הִנֵּ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb So Saul went|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb*\rb |שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Naioth|נֹוִית\rb* \rb in Ramah|בָּרָמָ֑ה\rb*. \rb But the Spirit|ר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb came|וַתְּהִי֩\rb* \rb upon|עָלָ֨יו\rb* \rb even|גַּם־\rb* \rb Saul|ה֜וּא\rb*, \rb and he walked along|וַיֵּ֤לֶךְ\rb*\rb |הָלוֹךְ֙\rb* \rb prophesying|וַיִּתְנַבֵּ֔א\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb he came to|בֹּא֖וֹ\rb* \rb Naioth|בְּנֹוִית\rb* \rb in Ramah|בָּרָמָֽה׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb Then Saul|ה֜וּא\rb* \rb stripped off|וַיִּפְשַׁ֨ט\rb* \rb his robes|בְּגָדָ֗יו\rb* \rb and also|גַּם־\rb* \rb prophesied|וַיִּתְנַבֵּ֤א\rb*\rb |גַם־\rb*\rb |הוּא֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֔ל\rb*. \rb And he collapsed|וַיִּפֹּ֣ל\rb* \rb and lay naked|עָרֹ֔ם\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb and|וְכָל־\rb* \rb night|הַלָּ֑יְלָה\rb*. \rb That is why|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּן֙\rb* \rb it is said|יֹֽאמְר֔וּ\rb*, “\rb Is Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb also|הֲגַ֥ם\rb* \rb among the prophets|בַּנְּבִיאִֽם׃פ\rb*?”
\c 20
\s1 Jonathan Helps David
\p \v 1 \rb Then David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb fled|וַיִּבְרַ֣ח\rb* \rb from Naioth|מִנֹּוִות\rb* \rb in Ramah|בָּרָמָ֑ה\rb*. \rb He came|וַיָּבֹ֞א\rb* \rb to|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֗ן\rb* \rb and asked|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר׀\rb*, “\rb What|מֶ֤ה\rb* \rb have I done|עָשִׂ֙יתִי֙\rb*? \rb What is|מֶֽה־\rb* \rb my iniquity|עֲוֺנִ֤י\rb*? \rb How|וּמֶֽה־\rb* \rb have I sinned|חַטָּאתִי֙\rb* \rb against|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb your father|אָבִ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb he wants to take|מְבַקֵּ֖שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my life|נַפְשִֽׁי׃\rb*?”
\p \v 2 “\rb Far from it|חָלִילָה֮\rb*!” \rb Jonathan replied|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*. “\rb You will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb die|תָמוּת֒\rb*. \rb Indeed|הִנֵּ֡ה\rb*\rb |לוֹ־\rb*, \rb my father|אָבִ֜י\rb* \rb does nothing|עָשָׂה\rb*,\rb |דָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb great|גָּד֗וֹל\rb* \rb or|א֚וֹ\rb*\rb |דָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb small|קָטֹ֔ן\rb*, \rb without|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb telling|יִגְלֶ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb me|אָזְנִ֑י\rb*. \rb So why|וּמַדּוּעַ֩\rb* \rb would he|אָבִ֥י\rb* \rb hide|יַסְתִּ֨יר\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb matter|הַדָּבָ֥ר\rb* \rb from me|מִמֶּ֛נִּי\rb*? \rb This cannot be true|אֵ֥ין\rb*\rb |זֹֽאת׃\rb*!”
\p \v 3 \rb But David|דָּוִ֗ד\rb* \rb again|ע֜וֹד\rb* \rb vowed|וַיִּשָּׁבַ֨ע\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb Your father|אָבִ֗יךָ\rb* \rb knows very well|יָדֹ֨עַ\rb*\rb |יָדַ֜ע\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I have found|מָצָ֤אתִי\rb* \rb favor|חֵן֙\rb* \rb in your eyes|בְּעֵינֶ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb and he has said|וַיֹּ֛אמֶר\rb*, ‘\rb Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֖ן\rb* \rb must not|אַל־\rb* \rb know|יֵֽדַע־\rb* \rb of this|זֹ֥את\rb*, \rb or|פֶּן־\rb* \rb he will be grieved|יֵֽעָצֵ֑ב\rb*.’ \rb As surely as|וְאוּלָ֗ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb lives|חַי־\rb* \rb and as you|נַפְשֶׁ֔ךָ\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb yourself live|וְחֵ֣י\rb*, \rb there is but a step|כְפֶ֔שַׂע\rb* \rb between me|בֵּינִ֖י\rb* \rb and|וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb death|הַמָּֽוֶת׃\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb Then Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֖ן\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*, “\rb Whatever|מַה־\rb* \rb you|נַפְשְׁךָ֖\rb* \rb desire|תֹּאמַ֥ר\rb*, \rb I will do|וְאֶֽעֱשֶׂה־\rb* \rb for you|לָּֽךְ׃פ\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb So David|דָּוִ֜ד\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb him|יְהוֹנָתָ֗ן\rb*, “\rb Look|הִֽנֵּה־\rb*, \rb tomorrow|מָחָ֔ר\rb* \rb is the New Moon|חֹ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb*,\f + \fr 20:5 \ft That is, the New Moon feast; also in verses 18, 24, and 27\f* \rb and I am|וְאָנֹכִ֛י\rb* \rb supposed to dine|יָשֹׁב־\rb*\rb |אֵשֵׁ֥ב\rb*\rb |לֶאֱכ֑וֹל\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*. \rb Instead, let me go|וְשִׁלַּחְתַּ֙נִי֙\rb* \rb and hide|וְנִסְתַּרְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb in the field|בַשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb* \rb until|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb the third|הַשְּׁלִשִֽׁית׃\rb* \rb evening from now|הָעֶ֥רֶב\rb*. \v 6 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb your father|אָבִ֑יךָ\rb* \rb misses me at all|פָּקֹ֥ד\rb*\rb |יִפְקְדֵ֖נִי\rb*, \rb tell him|וְאָמַרְתָּ֗\rb*, ‘\rb David|דָוִד֙\rb* \rb urgently requested|נִשְׁאֹל֩\rb*\rb |נִשְׁאַ֨ל\rb* \rb my permission|מִמֶּ֤נִּי\rb* \rb to hurry|לָרוּץ֙\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb to Bethlehem|לֶ֣חֶם\rb*, \rb his hometown|עִיר֔וֹ\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb there is|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb an annual|הַיָּמִ֛ים\rb* \rb sacrifice|זֶ֧בַח\rb* \rb for his whole|לְכָל־\rb* \rb clan|הַמִּשְׁפָּחָֽה׃\rb*.’ \v 7 \rb If|אִם־\rb*\rb |כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb he says|יֹאמַ֛ר\rb*, ‘\rb Good|ט֖וֹב\rb*,’ \rb then your servant|לְעַבְדֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb is safe|שָׁל֣וֹם\rb*, \rb but if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb he is enraged|חָרֹ֤ה\rb*\rb |יֶֽחֱרֶה֙\rb*\rb |ל֔וֹ\rb*, \rb you will know|דַּ֕ע\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he has evil|הָרָעָ֖ה\rb*\rb |מֵעִמּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb intentions|כָלְתָ֥ה\rb*. \v 8 \rb Therefore show|וְעָשִׂ֤יתָ\rb* \rb kindness|חֶ֙סֶד֙\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb your servant|עַבְדֶּ֔ךָ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb you have brought|הֵבֵ֥אתָ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb me|עַבְדְּךָ֖\rb* \rb into a covenant|בִּבְרִ֣ית\rb* \rb with|עִמָּ֑ךְ\rb* \rb you before the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*. \rb If|וְאִם־\rb* \rb there is|יֶשׁ־\rb* \rb iniquity|עָוֺן֙\rb* \rb in me|בִּ֤י\rb*, \rb then kill me|הֲמִיתֵ֣נִי\rb* \rb yourself|אַ֔תָּה\rb*; \rb why|לָמָּה־\rb*\rb |זֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb should you bring me|תְבִיאֵֽנִי׃פ\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb your father|אָבִ֖יךָ\rb*?”
\p \v 9 “\rb Never|חָלִ֣ילָה\rb*!”\rb |לָּ֑ךְ\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֖ן\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*. “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb I ever found out|יָדֹ֣עַ\rb*\rb |אֵדַ֗ע\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb my father|אָבִי֙\rb*\rb |לָב֣וֹא\rb* \rb had evil|הָרָעָ֜ה\rb*\rb |מֵעִ֤ם\rb* \rb intentions|כָלְתָ֨ה\rb* \rb against you|עָלֶ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb would I not|וְלֹ֥א\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb tell|אַגִּ֥יד\rb* \rb you|לָֽךְ׃ס\rb*?”
\s1 Jonathan and David Renew Their Covenant
\p \v 10 \rb Then David|דָּוִד֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb Jonathan|יְה֣וֹנָתָ֔ן\rb*, “\rb Who|מִ֖י\rb* \rb will tell|יַגִּ֣יד\rb* \rb me|לִ֑י\rb* \rb if|א֛וֹ\rb*\rb |מַה־\rb* \rb your father|אָבִ֖יךָ\rb* \rb answers|יַּעַנְךָ֥\rb* \rb you harshly|קָשָֽׁה׃ס\rb*?”
\p \v 11 “\rb Come|לְכָ֖ה\rb*,” \rb he|יְהֽוֹנָתָן֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |דָּוִ֔ד\rb*, “\rb let us go out|וְנֵצֵ֣א\rb* \rb to the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֑ה\rb*.”
\p \rb So the two|שְׁנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb of them went out|וַיֵּצְא֥וּ\rb* \rb into the field|הַשָּׂדֶֽה׃ס\rb*, \v 12 \rb and Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֜ן\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |דָּוִ֗ד\rb*, “\rb By the LORD|יְהוָ֞ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*,\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I will sound out|אֶחְקֹ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my father|אָבִ֗י\rb* \rb by this time|כָּעֵ֤ת׀\rb* \rb tomorrow|מָחָר֙\rb* \rb or the next day|הַשְּׁלִשִׁ֔ית\rb*. \rb If|וְהִנֵּה־\rb* \rb he is favorable|ט֖וֹב\rb* \rb toward|אֶל־\rb* \rb you|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*, \rb will I not|וְלֹֽא־\rb*\rb |אָז֙\rb* \rb send|אֶשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb for you|אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and tell|וְגָלִ֖יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb you|אָזְנֶֽךָ׃\rb*? \v 13 \rb But if|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb my father|אָבִ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb intends|יֵיטִ֨ב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb bring evil|הָֽרָעָה֙\rb* \rb on you|עָלֶ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb then may the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb punish|כֹּֽה־\rb*\rb |יַעֲשֶׂה֩\rb* \rb me|לִֽיהוֹנָתָ֜ן\rb*, \rb and ever so|וְכֹ֣ה\rb* \rb severely|יֹסִ֗יף\rb*, \rb if I do not tell|וְגָלִ֙יתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb you|אָזְנֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb and send you on your way|וְשִׁלַּחְתִּ֖יךָ\rb*\rb |וְהָלַכְתָּ֣\rb* \rb in safety|לְשָׁל֑וֹם\rb*. \rb May the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb be|וִיהִ֤י\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּ֔ךְ\rb*, \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He has been|הָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb my father|אָבִֽי׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb And|וְלֹ֖א\rb* \rb as long as|אִם־\rb*\rb |עוֹדֶ֣נִּי\rb* \rb I live|חָ֑י\rb*,\rb |וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb treat|תַעֲשֶׂ֧ה\rb* \rb me|עִמָּדִ֛י\rb* \rb with the LORD’s|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb loving devotion|חֶ֥סֶד\rb*,\f + \fr 20:14 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa chesed \ft are translated here and in most cases throughout the Scriptures as \fqa loving devotion\ft ; the range of meaning includes \fqa love\ft , \fqa goodness\ft , \fqa kindness\ft , \fqa faithfulness\ft , and \fqa mercy\ft , as well as \fqa loyalty to a covenant\ft .\f* \rb that I may not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb die|אָמֽוּת׃\rb*, \v 15 \rb and do not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb ever|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָ֑ם\rb* \rb cut off|תַכְרִ֧ת\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb your loving devotion|חַסְדְּךָ֛\rb* \rb from|מֵעִ֥ם\rb* \rb my household|בֵּיתִ֖י\rb*— \rb not|וְלֹ֗א\rb* \rb even when the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb cuts off|בְּהַכְרִ֤ת\rb* \rb every one|אִ֕ישׁ\rb* \rb of David’s|דָוִ֔ד\rb* \rb enemies|אֹיְבֵ֣י\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֖ל\rb* \rb the face|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאֲדָמָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 16 \rb So Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֖ן\rb* \rb made a covenant|וַיִּכְרֹ֥ת\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of David, saying|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*, “\rb May the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb hold|מִיַּ֖ד\rb* \rb David’s|דָוִֽד׃\rb* \rb enemies|אֹיְבֵ֥י\rb* \rb accountable|וּבִקֵּ֣שׁ\rb*.” \v 17 \rb And Jonathan|יְהֽוֹנָתָן֙\rb* \rb had David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb reaffirm|וַיּ֤וֹסֶף\rb* \rb his vow|לְהַשְׁבִּ֣יעַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb out of love|בְּאַהֲבָת֖וֹ\rb* \rb for him|אֹת֑וֹ\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Jonathan loved David|אֲהֵבֽוֹ׃ס\rb* \rb as he loved|אַהֲבַ֥ת\rb* \rb himself|נַפְשׁ֖וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb Then Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֖ן\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּֽאמֶר־\rb* \rb to David|ל֥וֹ\rb*, “\rb Tomorrow|מָחָ֣ר\rb* \rb is the New Moon|חֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb and you will be missed|וְנִפְקַ֕דְתָּ\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb your seat|מוֹשָׁבֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb will be empty|יִפָּקֵ֖ד\rb*. \v 19 \rb When you have stayed three days|וְשִׁלַּשְׁתָּ֙\rb*, \rb hurry|מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb down|תֵּרֵ֣ד\rb*\rb |וּבָאתָ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּק֔וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you hid|נִסְתַּ֥רְתָּ\rb*\rb |שָּׁ֖ם\rb* \rb on the day|בְּי֣וֹם\rb* \rb this trouble began|הַֽמַּעֲשֶׂ֑ה\rb*, \rb and remain|וְיָ֣שַׁבְתָּ֔\rb* \rb beside|אֵ֖צֶל\rb* \rb the stone|הָאֶ֥בֶן\rb* \rb Ezel|הָאָֽזֶל׃\rb*.\f + \fr 20:19 \fqa Ezel \ft means \fqa departure\ft .\f* \v 20 \rb I|וַאֲנִ֕י\rb* \rb will shoot|אוֹרֶ֑ה\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb arrows|הַחִצִּ֖ים\rb* \rb to the side of it|צִדָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb as if I were aiming|לְשַֽׁלַּֽח־\rb* \rb at a target|לְמַטָּרָֽה׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb Then|וְהִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb I will send|אֶשְׁלַ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a boy and say|הַנַּ֔עַר\rb*, ‘\rb Go|לֵ֖ךְ\rb*, \rb find|מְצָ֣א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the arrows|הַחִצִּ֑ים\rb*!’ \rb Now, if|אִם־\rb* \rb I expressly say|אָמֹר֩\rb*\rb |אֹמַ֨ר\rb* \rb to him|לַנַּ֜עַר\rb*, ‘\rb Look|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb*, \rb the arrows|הַחִצִּ֣ים׀\rb* \rb are on this side|וָהֵ֗נָּה\rb* \rb of you|מִמְּךָ֣\rb*; \rb bring them|קָחֶ֧נּוּ׀\rb*,’ \rb then come|וָבֹ֛אָה\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb as surely as the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb lives|חַי־\rb*, \rb it is safe|שָׁל֥וֹם\rb* \rb for you|לְךָ֛\rb*, \rb and there is no|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb danger|דָּבָ֖ר\rb*. \v 22 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb I say|אֹמַר֙\rb*\rb |כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb to the young man|לָעֶ֔לֶם\rb*, ‘\rb Look|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb*, \rb the arrows are|הַחִצִּ֖ים\rb* \rb beyond you|מִמְּךָ֣\rb*,’ \rb then|וָהָ֑לְאָה\rb* \rb you must go|לֵ֕ךְ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb has sent you away|שִֽׁלַּחֲךָ֖\rb*. \v 23 \rb And as for the matter|וְהַ֨דָּבָ֔ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you|וָאָ֑תָּה\rb*\rb |הִנֵּ֧ה\rb* \rb and I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb have discussed|דִּבַּ֖רְנוּ\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb is a witness between|בֵּינִ֥י\rb* \rb you and me|וּבֵינְךָ֖\rb* \rb forever|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָֽם׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 24 \rb So David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb hid|וַיִּסָּתֵ֥ר\rb* \rb in the field|בַּשָּׂדֶ֑ה\rb*, \rb and when the New Moon|הַחֹ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb had come|וַיְהִ֣י\rb*, \rb the king|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb*\rb |עַל\rb*\rb |הַלֶּ֖חֶם\rb* \rb sat down|וַיֵּ֧שֶׁב\rb* \rb to eat|לֶאֱכֽוֹל׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb He|הַ֠מֶּלֶךְ\rb* \rb sat|וַיֵּ֣שֶׁב\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb his usual|כְּפַ֣עַם׀\rb*\rb |בְּפַ֗עַם\rb* \rb place|מ֨וֹשָׁב֜וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |מוֹשַׁב֙\rb* \rb by the wall|הַקִּ֔יר\rb*, \rb opposite|וַיָּ֙קָם֙\rb* \rb Jonathan|יְה֣וֹנָתָ֔ן\rb* \rb and|וַיֵּ֥שֶׁב\rb* \rb beside|מִצַּ֣ד\rb* \rb Abner|אַבְנֵ֖ר\rb*\rb |שָׁא֑וּל\rb*,\f + \fr 20:25 \ft LXX; Hebrew \fqa by the wall. Jonathan arose and Abner sat down by Saul’s side,\f* \rb but David’s|דָּוִֽד׃\rb* \rb place|מְק֥וֹם\rb* \rb was empty|וַיִּפָּקֵ֖ד\rb*. \v 26 \rb Saul|שָׁא֛וּל\rb* \rb said|דִבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb nothing|וְלֹֽא־\rb*\rb |מְא֖וּמָה\rb* \rb that|הַה֑וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb he thought|אָמַר֙\rb*, “\rb Something has happened to|מִקְרֶ֣ה\rb* \rb David|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb to make him ceremonially unclean|בִּלְתִּ֥י\rb*\rb |טָה֛וֹר\rb*— \rb surely|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he is|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb unclean|לֹ֥א\rb*\rb |טָהֽוֹר׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 27 \rb But|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb on the day after|מִֽמָּחֳרַ֤ת\rb* \rb the New Moon|הַחֹ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb*, \rb the second day|הַשֵּׁנִ֔י\rb*, \rb David’s|דָּוִ֑דס\rb* \rb place|מְק֣וֹם\rb* \rb was still empty|וַיִּפָּקֵ֖ד\rb*, \rb and Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb his son|בְּנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֣ן\rb*, “\rb Why|מַדּ֜וּעַ\rb* \rb hasn’t|לֹא־\rb* \rb the son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Jesse|יִשַׁ֛י\rb* \rb come|בָ֧א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the meal|הַלָּֽחֶם׃\rb* \rb either|גַּם־\rb* \rb yesterday|תְּמ֥וֹל\rb* \rb or today|גַּם־\rb*\rb |הַיּ֖וֹם\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*?”
\p \v 28 \rb Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֖ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |שָׁא֑וּל\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּ֥עַן\rb*, “\rb David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb*\rb |מֵעִמָּדִ֖י\rb* \rb urgently requested|נִשְׁאֹ֨ל\rb*\rb |נִשְׁאַ֥ל\rb* \rb my permission to|עַד־\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb go to Bethlehem|לָֽחֶם׃\rb*, \v 29 \rb saying|וַיֹּ֡אמֶר\rb*, ‘\rb Please|נָ֡א\rb* \rb let me go|שַׁלְּחֵ֣נִי\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb our clan|מִשְׁפָּחָ֨ה\rb*\rb |לָ֜נוּ\rb* \rb is holding a sacrifice|זֶבַח֩\rb* \rb in the city|בָּעִ֗יר\rb*,\rb |וְה֤וּא\rb* \rb and my brother|אָחִ֔י\rb* \rb has told me|צִוָּֽה־\rb* \rb to be there|לִי֙\rb*. \rb So now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb*, \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb I have found|מָצָ֤אתִי\rb* \rb favor|חֵן֙\rb* \rb in your eyes|בְּעֵינֶ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb please|נָּ֖א\rb* \rb let me go|אִמָּ֥לְטָה\rb* \rb and see|וְאֶרְאֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my brothers|אֶחָ֑י\rb*.’ \rb That is why|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb he has not|לֹא־\rb* \rb come|בָ֔א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃ס\rb* \rb table|שֻׁלְחַ֖ן\rb*.”
\s1 Saul Seeks to Kill Jonathan
\p \v 30 \rb Then Saul’s|שָׁאוּל֙\rb* \rb anger|אַ֤ף\rb* \rb burned|וַיִּֽחַר־\rb* \rb against Jonathan|בִּיה֣וֹנָתָ֔ן\rb*, \rb and he said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|ל֔וֹ\rb*, “\rb You son|בֶּֽן־\rb* \rb of a perverse|נַעֲוַ֖ת\rb* \rb and rebellious woman|הַמַּרְדּ֑וּת\rb*! \rb Do I not|הֲל֣וֹא\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֗עְתִּי\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb have chosen|בֹחֵ֤ר\rb* \rb the son|לְבֶן־\rb* \rb of Jesse|יִשַׁ֔י\rb* \rb to your own shame|לְבָ֨שְׁתְּךָ֔\rb* \rb and to the shame|וּלְבֹ֖שֶׁת\rb* \rb of the mother|אִמֶּֽךָ׃\rb* \rb who bore you|עֶרְוַ֥ת\rb*? \v 31 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |כָל־\rb* \rb as long as|הַיָּמִ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jesse|יִשַׁי֙\rb* \rb lives|חַ֣י\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb this earth|הָאֲדָמָ֔ה\rb*, \rb neither|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb nor your kingdom|וּמַלְכוּתֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb shall be established|תִכּ֖וֹן\rb*. \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb send for him|שְׁלַ֨ח\rb* \rb and bring|וְקַ֤ח\rb* \rb him|אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֔י\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb he|הֽוּא׃ס\rb* \rb must surely die|מָ֖וֶת\rb*!”
\p \v 32 “\rb Why|לָ֥מָּה\rb* \rb must he be put to death|יוּמַ֖ת\rb*?” \rb Jonathan|יְה֣וֹנָתָ֔ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb replied|וַיַּ֙עַן֙\rb*.\rb |אָבִ֑יו\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֛יו\rb* “\rb What|מֶ֥ה\rb* \rb has he done|עָשָֽׂה׃\rb*?”
\p \v 33 \rb Then Saul|שָׁא֧וּל\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb hurled|וַיָּ֨טֶל\rb* \rb his spear|הַחֲנִ֛ית\rb* \rb at Jonathan|עָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb to kill him|לְהַכֹּת֑וֹ\rb*. \rb So Jonathan|יְה֣וֹנָתָ֔ן\rb* \rb knew|וַיֵּ֙דַע֙\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |הִ֛יא\rb*\rb |מֵעִ֥ם\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֖יו\rb* \rb was determined|כָ֥לָה\rb* \rb to kill|לְהָמִ֥ית\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִֽד׃ס\rb*. \v 34 \rb Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֛ן\rb* \rb got up|וַיָּ֧קָם\rb* \rb from|מֵעִ֥ם\rb* \rb the table|הַשֻּׁלְחָ֖ן\rb* \rb in fierce|בָּחֳרִי־\rb* \rb anger|אָ֑ף\rb* \rb and did not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb eat|אָכַ֞ל\rb* \rb any food|לֶ֔חֶם\rb* \rb that second|הַשֵּׁנִי֙\rb* \rb day|בְּיוֹם־\rb* \rb of the month|הַחֹ֤דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb he was grieved|נֶעְצַב֙\rb* \rb by|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb his father’s|אָבִֽיו׃ס\rb* \rb shameful treatment|הִכְלִמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb of|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*.
\p \v 35 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb In the morning|בַבֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֛ן\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּצֵ֧א\rb* \rb to the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb* \rb for the appointment|לְמוֹעֵ֣ד\rb* \rb with David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*, \rb and a small|קָטֹ֖ן\rb* \rb boy|וְנַ֥עַר\rb* \rb was with him|עִמּֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 36 \rb He said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to the boy|לְנַעֲר֔וֹ\rb*, “\rb Run|רֻ֗ץ\rb* \rb and find|מְצָ֥א\rb*\rb |נָא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the arrows|הַ֣חִצִּ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb shoot|מוֹרֶ֑ה\rb*.” \rb And as the boy|הַנַּ֣עַר\rb* \rb ran|רָ֔ץ\rb*, \rb Jonathan|וְהֽוּא־\rb* \rb shot|יָרָ֥ה\rb* \rb an arrow|הַחֵ֖צִי\rb* \rb beyond him|לְהַעֲבִרֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 37 \rb When the boy|הַנַּ֙עַר֙\rb* \rb reached|וַיָּבֹ֤א\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb the place where|מְק֣וֹם\rb* \rb Jonathan’s|יְהוֹנָתָ֑ן\rb* \rb arrow|הַחֵ֔צִי\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb had fallen|יָרָ֖ה\rb*, \rb Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֜ן\rb* \rb called|וַיִּקְרָ֨א\rb* \rb to|אַחֲרֵ֤י\rb* \rb him|הַנַּ֙עַר֙\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֔אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Isn’t|הֲל֥וֹא\rb* \rb the arrow|הַחֵ֖צִי\rb* \rb beyond you|מִמְּךָ֥\rb*\rb |וָהָֽלְאָה׃\rb*?” \v 38 \rb Then Jonathan|יְהֽוֹנָתָן֙\rb* \rb cried out|וַיִּקְרָ֤א\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb*\rb |הַנַּ֔עַר\rb*, “\rb Hurry|מְהֵרָ֥ה\rb*! \rb Make haste|ח֖וּשָׁה\rb*! \rb Do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb delay|תַּעֲמֹ֑ד\rb*!”\rb |יְהֽוֹנָתָן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַחֵצִי\rb* \rb So the boy|נַ֤עַר\rb* \rb picked up the arrow|וַיְלַקֵּ֞ט\rb* \rb and returned|וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his master|אֲדֹנָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 39 \rb But the boy|וְהַנַּ֖עַר\rb* \rb did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֣ע\rb* \rb anything|מְא֑וּמָה\rb*; \rb only|אַ֤ךְ\rb* \rb Jonathan|יְהֽוֹנָתָן֙\rb* \rb and David|וְדָוִ֔ד\rb* \rb knew|יָדְע֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the arrangement|הַדָּבָֽר׃\rb*. \v 40 \rb Then Jonathan|יְהֽוֹנָתָן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּתֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb his equipment|כֵּלָ֔יו\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the boy|הַנַּ֖עַר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Go|לֵ֖ךְ\rb*, \rb take it back|הָבֵ֥יא\rb* \rb to the city|הָעִֽיר׃\rb*.”
\p \v 41 \rb When the young man|הַנַּעַר֮\rb* \rb had gone|בָּא֒\rb*, \rb David|וְדָוִ֗ד\rb* \rb got up|קָ֚ם\rb* \rb from the south|הַנֶּ֔גֶב\rb* \rb side of the stone|מֵאֵ֣צֶל\rb*,\f + \fr 20:41 \ft Hebrew \fqa from the south side\ft ; LXX \fqa from beside the stone\f* \rb fell|וַיִּפֹּ֨ל\rb* \rb facedown|לְאַפָּ֥יו\rb*\rb |אַ֛רְצָה\rb*, \rb and bowed|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֖חוּ\rb* \rb three|שָׁלֹ֣שׁ\rb* \rb times|פְּעָמִ֑ים\rb*. \rb Then he and Jonathan kissed|וַֽיִּשְּׁק֣וּ׀\rb* \rb each|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb other|רֵעֵ֗הוּ\rb* \rb and wept|וַיִּבְכּוּ֙\rb* \rb together|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |רֵעֵ֔הוּ\rb* — \rb though|עַד־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb wept more|הִגְדִּֽיל׃\rb*.
\p \v 42 \rb And Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֛ן\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb to David|לְדָוִ֖ד\rb*, “\rb Go|לֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb in peace|לְשָׁל֑וֹם\rb*, \rb for|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb the two|שְׁנֵ֜ינוּ\rb* \rb of us|אֲנַ֗חְנוּ\rb* \rb have sworn|נִשְׁבַּ֨עְנוּ\rb* \rb in the name|בְּשֵׁ֤ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, ‘\rb May the LORD|יְהוָ֞ה\rb* \rb be|יִֽהְיֶ֣ה׀\rb* \rb a witness between|בֵּינִ֣י\rb* \rb you and me|וּבֵינֶ֗ךָ\rb*, \rb and between|וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb your descendants|זַרְעֲךָ֖\rb* \rb and|וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb mine|זַרְעִ֛י\rb* \rb forever|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָֽם׃פ\rb*.’” \rb Then David got up|וַיָּ֖קָם\rb* \rb and departed|וַיֵּלַ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb and Jonathan|וִיהוֹנָתָ֖ן\rb* \rb went back|בָּ֥א\rb* \rb into the city|הָעִֽיר׃\rb*.
\c 21
\s1 David Takes the Consecrated Bread
\r (\ref Matthew 12:1–8|MAT 12:1-8\ref*; \ref Mark 2:23–28|MRK 2:23-28\ref*; \ref Luke 6:1–5|LUK 6:1-5\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Then David|דָוִד֙\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֤א\rb* \rb to Nob|נֹ֔בֶה\rb*, \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ahimelech|אֲחִימֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֑ן\rb*. \rb And when Ahimelech|אֲחִימֶ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb met|לִקְרַ֣את\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֗ד\rb*, \rb he trembled|וַיֶּחֱרַ֨ד\rb* \rb and asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb him|לוֹ֙\rb*, “\rb Why are|מַדּ֤וּעַ\rb* \rb you|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb alone|לְבַדֶּ֔ךָ\rb*? \rb Why is|וְאִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb no one|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb with you|אִתָּֽךְ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 2 “\rb The king|הַמֶּלֶךְ֮\rb* \rb has given me|צִוַּ֣נִי\rb* \rb a mission|דָבָר֒\rb*,” \rb David|דָּוִ֜ד\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |לַאֲחִימֶ֣לֶךְ\rb*\rb |הַכֹּהֵ֗ן\rb*. “\rb He told|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb me|אֵלַ֗י\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb no one|אַל־\rb* \rb is to know|יֵ֧דַע\rb*\rb |מְא֛וּמָה\rb* \rb about|אֶת־\rb* \rb the mission|הַדָּבָ֛ר\rb* \rb on which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֥י\rb* \rb am sending you|שֹׁלֵֽחֲךָ֖\rb*\rb |וַאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |צִוִּיתִ֑ךָ\rb*. \rb And|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb I have directed|יוֹדַ֔עְתִּי\rb* \rb my young men|הַנְּעָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb to meet me|אֶל־\rb* \rb at a certain place|מְק֥וֹם\rb*\rb |פְּלֹנִ֖י\rb*\rb |אַלְמוֹנִֽי׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb Now then|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb*, \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb do you have|יֵּ֧שׁ\rb* \rb on|תַּֽחַת־\rb* \rb hand|יָדְךָ֛\rb*? \rb Give me|תְּנָ֣ה\rb*\rb |בְיָדִ֑י\rb* \rb five loaves of|חֲמִשָּׁה־\rb* \rb bread|לֶ֖חֶם\rb*, \rb or|א֖וֹ\rb* \rb whatever can be found|הַנִּמְצָֽא׃\rb*.”
\p \v 4 “\rb There is no|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb common|חֹ֖ל\rb* \rb bread|לֶ֥חֶם\rb* \rb on|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb hand|יָדִ֑י\rb*,” \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֤ן\rb* \rb replied|וַיַּ֨עַן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |דָּוִד֙\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֔אמֶר\rb*, “\rb but|אִם־\rb* \rb there is some|יֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb consecrated|קֹ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb bread|לֶ֤חֶם\rb* — \rb provided that|אִם־\rb* \rb the young men|הַנְּעָרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb have kept themselves|נִשְׁמְר֥וּ\rb* \rb from women|מֵאִשָּֽׁה׃פ\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb David|דָּוִ֨ד\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּעַן֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |ל֗וֹ\rb*, “\rb Women have|אִשָּׁ֤ה\rb* \rb indeed|אִם־\rb* \rb been kept|עֲצֻֽרָה־\rb* \rb from us|לָ֙נוּ֙\rb*, \rb as is usual|שִׁלְשֹׁ֔ם\rb* \rb when I set out|בְּצֵאתִ֕י\rb*. \rb And the bodies|כְלֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the young men|הַנְּעָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb are|וַיִּהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb holy|קֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb even|וְהוּא֙\rb* \rb on common|חֹ֔ל\rb* \rb missions|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb*. \rb How much|וְאַ֕ף\rb* \rb more so|כִּ֥י\rb*\rb |יִקְדַּ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |בַּכֶּֽלִי׃\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֖וֹם\rb*!”
\p \v 6 \rb So the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb him|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb the consecrated bread|קֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb since|כִּי֩\rb* \rb there was|הָ֨יָה\rb* \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb bread|לֶ֗חֶם\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֜ם\rb* \rb but|אִם־\rb* \rb the Bread|לֶ֤חֶם\rb* \rb of the Presence|הַפָּנִים֙\rb*, \rb which had been removed|הַמּֽוּסָרִים֙\rb* \rb from before|מִלִּפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and replaced with|לָשׂוּם֙\rb* \rb hot|חֹ֔ם\rb* \rb bread|לֶ֣חֶם\rb* \rb on the day|בְּי֖וֹם\rb* \rb it was taken away|הִלָּקְחֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb Now one|אִישׁ֩\rb* \rb of Saul’s|שָׁא֜וּל\rb* \rb servants|מֵעַבְדֵ֨י\rb* \rb was there|וְשָׁ֡ם\rb* \rb that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*, \rb detained|נֶעְצָר֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*. \rb And his name was|וּשְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Doeg|דֹּאֵ֣ג\rb* \rb the Edomite|הָאֲדֹמִ֑י\rb*, \rb the chief|אַבִּ֥יר\rb* \rb shepherd|הָרֹעִ֖ים\rb* \rb for|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Saul|לְשָׁאֽוּל׃\rb*.
\s1 David Flees to Gath
\r (\ref Psalm 34:1–22|PSA 34:1-22\ref*; \ref Psalm 56:1–13|PSA 56:1-13\ref*)
\p \v 8 \rb Then David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb Ahimelech|לַאֲחִימֶ֔לֶךְ\rb*, “\rb Is there|יֶשׁ־\rb* \rb not|וְאִ֛ין\rb* \rb a spear|חֲנִ֣ית\rb* \rb or|אוֹ־\rb* \rb sword|חָ֑רֶב\rb* \rb on|תַֽחַת־\rb* \rb hand|יָדְךָ֖\rb* \rb here|פֹּ֥ה\rb*? \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |גַם־\rb* \rb I have brought|לָקַ֣חְתִּי\rb* \rb neither|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb my sword|חַרְבִּ֤י\rb* \rb nor|וְגַם־\rb* \rb my weapons|כֵּלַי֙\rb* \rb with me|בְיָדִ֔י\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb mission|דְבַר־\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb urgent|נָחֽוּץ׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 9 \rb The priest|הַכֹּהֵ֗ן\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb The sword|חֶרֶב֩\rb* \rb of Goliath|גָּלְיָ֨ת\rb* \rb the Philistine|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֜י\rb*, \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you killed|הִכִּ֣יתָ׀\rb* \rb in the Valley|בְּעֵ֣מֶק\rb* \rb of Elah|הָאֵלָ֗ה\rb*, \rb is here|הִנֵּה־\rb*; \rb it is|הִ֞יא\rb* \rb wrapped|לוּטָ֣ה\rb* \rb in a cloth|בַשִּׂמְלָה֮\rb* \rb behind|אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb the ephod|הָאֵפוֹד֒\rb*. \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you want|אֹתָ֤הּ\rb*, \rb you may take it|תִּֽקַּח־\rb*\rb |לְךָ֙\rb*\rb |קָ֔ח\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb there is no|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb other|אַחֶ֛רֶת\rb* \rb but this one|זוּלָתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb here|בָּזֶ֑ה\rb*.”
\p \rb And David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb*, “\rb There is none|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb like it|כָּמ֖וֹהָ\rb*; \rb give it|תְּנֶ֥נָּה\rb* \rb to me|לִּֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 10 \rb That|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּוֹם־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*\rb |וַיָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb fled|וַיִּבְרַ֥ח\rb* \rb from|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֑וּל\rb* \rb and went|וַיָּבֹ֕א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Achish|אָכִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb king of|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb Gath|גַּֽת׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb But the servants|עַבְדֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Achish|אָכִישׁ֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמְר֜וּ\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֔יו\rb*, “\rb Is this|זֶ֥ה\rb* \rb not|הֲלוֹא־\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֖ד\rb*, \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*? \rb Did they not|הֲל֣וֹא\rb* \rb sing|יַעֲנ֤וּ\rb* \rb about him|לָזֶ֗ה\rb* \rb in their dances|בַמְּחֹלוֹת֙\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 ‘\rb Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb* \rb has slain|הִכָּ֤ה\rb* \rb his thousands|בְּאַלְפּוֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and David|וְדָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb his tens of thousands|בְּרִבְבֹתוֹ׃\rb*’?”
\p \v 12 \rb Now David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb* \rb took|וַיָּ֧שֶׂם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb to heart|בִּלְבָב֑וֹ\rb* \rb and was very much|מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb afraid|וַיִּרָ֣א\rb* \rb of|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb Achish|אָכִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Gath|גַּֽת׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb So he changed|וַיְשַׁנּ֤וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his behavior|טַעְמוֹ֙\rb* \rb before them|בְּעֵ֣ינֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and feigned madness|וַיִּתְהֹלֵ֖ל\rb* \rb in their hands|בְּיָדָ֑ם\rb*; \rb he scratched|וַיְתַו\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the doors|דַּלְת֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the gate|הַשַּׁ֔עַר\rb* \rb and let his saliva|רִיר֖וֹ\rb* \rb run|וַיּ֥וֹרֶד\rb* \rb down|אֶל־\rb* \rb his beard|זְקָנֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb Then Achish|אָכִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his servants|עֲבָדָ֑יו\rb*, “\rb Look|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb*, \rb you can see that|תִרְאוּ֙\rb* \rb the man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb is insane|מִשְׁתַּגֵּ֔עַ\rb*! \rb Why|לָ֛מָּה\rb* \rb have you brought|תָּבִ֥יאוּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb to me|אֵלָֽי׃\rb*? \v 15 \rb Am I|אָ֔נִי\rb* \rb in need of|חֲסַ֤ר\rb* \rb madmen|מְשֻׁגָּעִים֙\rb*, \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb you have brought|הֲבֵאתֶ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this man|זֶ֔ה\rb* \rb to rave|לְהִשְׁתַּגֵּ֖עַ\rb* \rb in my presence|עָלָ֑י\rb*? \rb Must this man|הֲזֶ֖ה\rb* \rb come|יָב֥וֹא\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb my house|בֵּיתִֽי׃ס\rb*?”
\c 22
\s1 David Flees to Adullam and Mizpeh
\r (\ref Psalm 57:1–11|PSA 57:1-11\ref*; \ref Psalm 142:1–7|PSA 142:1-7\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb So David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb left|וַיֵּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb Gath|מִשָּׁ֔ם\rb* \rb and took refuge|וַיִּמָּלֵ֖ט\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the cave|מְעָרַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Adullam|עֲדֻלָּ֑ם\rb*. \rb When his brothers|אֶחָיו֙\rb* \rb and the rest of|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his father’s|אָבִ֔יו\rb* \rb household|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb heard about it|וַיִּשְׁמְע֤וּ\rb*, \rb they went down|וַיֵּרְד֥וּ\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb there|שָֽׁמָּה׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb And all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who were distressed|מָצ֜וֹק\rb* \rb or|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |אִ֨ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb indebted|נֹשֶׁא֙\rb*\rb |וְכָל־\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb or discontented|מַר־\rb*\rb |נֶ֔פֶשׁ\rb* \rb rallied|וַיִּֽתְקַבְּצ֣וּ\rb* \rb around him|אֵ֠לָיו\rb*, \rb and he became|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb their|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb leader|לְשָׂ֑ר\rb*. \rb About four|כְּאַרְבַּ֥ע\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֖וֹת\rb* \rb men|אִֽישׁ׃\rb* \rb were|וַיִּהְי֣וּ\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֔וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb From there|מִשָּׁ֖ם\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֧לֶךְ\rb* \rb to Mizpeh|מִצְפֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb of Moab|מוֹאָ֑ב\rb*, \rb where he said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר׀\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Moab|מוֹאָ֗ב\rb*, “\rb Please|נָ֞א\rb* \rb let my father|אָבִ֤י\rb* \rb and mother|וְאִמִּי֙\rb* \rb stay|יֵֽצֵא־\rb*\f + \fr 22:3 \ft Syriac and Vulgate; Hebrew \fqa go forth\f* \rb with you|אִתְּכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb until|עַ֚ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I learn|אֵדַ֔ע\rb* \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb* \rb will do|יַּֽעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb for me|לִּ֖י\rb*.” \v 4 \rb So he left them|וַיַּנְחֵ֕ם\rb* \rb in|אֶת־\rb* \rb the care|פְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Moab|מוֹאָ֑ב\rb*, \rb and they stayed|וַיֵּשְׁב֣וּ\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb time|יְמֵ֥י\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb was|הֱיוֹת־\rb* \rb in the stronghold|בַּמְּצוּדָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Then the prophet|הַנָּבִ֜יא\rb* \rb Gad|גָּ֨ד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֗ד\rb*, “\rb Do not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb stay|תֵשֵׁב֙\rb* \rb in the stronghold|בַּמְּצוּדָ֔ה\rb*. \rb Depart|לֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb and go|וּבָֽאתָ־\rb* \rb into|לְּךָ֖\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*.” \rb So David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb left|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb and went|וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb* \rb to the forest|יַ֥עַר\rb* \rb of Hereth|חָֽרֶת׃ס\rb*.
\s1 Saul Slays the Priests of Nob
\r (\ref Psalm 52:1–9|PSA 52:1-9\ref*)
\p \v 6 \rb Soon Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb learned|וַיִּשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*\rb |וַאֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb and his men|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |אִתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb had been discovered|נוֹדַ֣ע\rb*. \rb At that time Saul|וְשָׁאוּל֩\rb* \rb was sitting|יוֹשֵׁ֨ב\rb* \rb under|תַּֽחַת־\rb* \rb the tamarisk tree|הָאֶ֤שֶׁל\rb* \rb on the hill|בָּֽרָמָה֙\rb* \rb at Gibeah|בַּגִּבְעָ֜ה\rb*, \rb with his spear|וַחֲנִית֣וֹ\rb* \rb in hand|בְיָד֔וֹ\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his servants|עֲבָדָ֖יו\rb* \rb standing|נִצָּבִ֥ים\rb* \rb around him|עָלָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb Then Saul|שָׁא֗וּל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to his servants|לַֽעֲבָדָיו֙\rb*,\rb |הַנִּצָּבִ֣ים\rb*\rb |עָלָ֔יו\rb* “\rb Listen|שִׁמְעוּ־\rb*,\rb |נָ֖א\rb* \rb men|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Benjamin|יְמִינִ֑י\rb*!\rb |גַּם־\rb* \rb Is the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jesse|יִשַׁי֙\rb* \rb giving|יִתֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb all|לְכֻלְּכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb of you fields|שָׂד֣וֹת\rb* \rb and vineyards|וּכְרָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb and making|יָשִׂ֔ים\rb* \rb you|לְכֻלְּכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb commanders|שָׂרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of thousands|אֲלָפִ֖ים\rb* \rb or|וְשָׂרֵ֥י\rb* \rb hundreds|מֵאֽוֹת׃\rb*? \v 8 \rb Is that|כִּי֩\rb* \rb why all|כֻּלְּכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb of you have conspired|קְשַׁרְתֶּ֨ם\rb* \rb against me|עָלַ֗י\rb*? \rb Not one of you|וְאֵין־\rb* \rb told|גֹּלֶ֤ה\rb* \rb me|אֶת־\rb* \rb that|אָזְנִי֙\rb* \rb my own son|בְּנִ֣י\rb* \rb had made a covenant|בִּכְרָת־\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jesse|יִשַׁ֔י\rb*. \rb Not one|וְאֵין־\rb* \rb of you|מִכֶּ֛ם\rb* \rb has shown concern|חֹלֶ֥ה\rb* \rb for me|עָלַ֖י\rb* \rb or revealed|וְגֹלֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to me|אָזְנִ֑י\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb my son|בְּנִ֨י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has stirred up|הֵקִים֩\rb* \rb my own servant|עַבְדִּ֥י\rb* \rb to lie in wait|לְאֹרֵ֖ב\rb* \rb against me|עָלַ֛י\rb*, \rb as is the case today|כַּיּ֥וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּֽה׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 9 \rb But Doeg|דֹּאֵ֣ג\rb* \rb the Edomite|הָאֲדֹמִ֗י\rb*, \rb who|וְה֛וּא\rb* \rb had stationed himself|נִצָּ֥ב\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb Saul’s|שָׁא֖וּל\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדֵֽי־\rb*, \rb answered|וַיַּ֜עַן\rb*: “\rb I saw|רָאִ֙יתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jesse|יִשַׁ֔י\rb* \rb come|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ahimelech|אֲחִימֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahitub|אֲחִטֽוּב׃\rb* \rb at Nob|נֹ֔בֶה\rb*. \v 10 \rb Ahimelech inquired|וַיִּשְׁאַל־\rb* \rb of the LORD|בַּֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb for him|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb and gave|נָ֣תַן\rb* \rb him|ל֑וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֗ת\rb* \rb provisions|וְצֵידָ֖ה\rb*. \rb He also gave|נָ֥תַן\rb* \rb him|לֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb the sword|חֶ֛רֶב\rb* \rb of Goliath|גָּלְיָ֥ת\rb* \rb the Philistine|הַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֖י\rb*.”
\p \v 11 \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֡לֶךְ\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb messengers to summon|לִקְרֹא֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Ahimelech|אֲחִימֶ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֗ן\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahitub|אֲחִיט֜וּב\rb*, \rb and his father’s|אָבִ֛יו\rb* \rb whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb family|בֵּ֥ית\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb were priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb* \rb at Nob|בְּנֹ֑ב\rb*. \rb And all|כֻלָּ֖ם\rb* \rb of them came|וַיָּבֹ֥אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃ס\rb*. \v 12 “\rb Listen|שְֽׁמַֽע־\rb* \rb now|נָ֖א\rb*, \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahitub|אֲחִיט֑וּב\rb*,” \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb*.
\p “\rb Here I am|הִנְנִ֥י\rb*, \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִֽי׃\rb*,” \rb he replied|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb And Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb him|אֵלוֹ\rb*, “\rb Why|לָ֚מָּה\rb* \rb have you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb and the son|וּבֶן־\rb* \rb of Jesse|יִשָׁ֑י\rb* \rb conspired|קְשַׁרְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb against me|עָלַ֔י\rb*? \rb You gave|בְּתִתְּךָ֨\rb* \rb him|ל֜וֹ\rb* \rb bread|לֶ֣חֶם\rb* \rb and a sword|וְחֶ֗רֶב\rb* \rb and inquired|וְשָׁא֥וֹל\rb* \rb of God|בֵּֽאלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb for him|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb so that he could rise up|לָק֥וּם\rb* \rb against me|אֵלַ֛י\rb* \rb to lie in wait|לְאֹרֵ֖ב\rb*, \rb as he is doing today|כַּיּ֥וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּֽה׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb Ahimelech|אֲחִימֶ֛לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּ֧עַן\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Who|וּמִ֤י\rb* \rb among all|בְכָל־\rb* \rb your servants|עֲבָדֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb is as faithful|נֶאֱמָ֔ן\rb* \rb as David|כְּדָוִ֣ד\rb*, \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb son-in-law|וַחֲתַ֥ן\rb*, \rb the captain|וְסָ֥ר\rb* \rb of|אֶל־\rb* \rb your bodyguard|מִשְׁמַעְתֶּ֖ךָ\rb* \rb and honored|וְנִכְבָּ֥ד\rb* \rb in your house|בְּבֵיתֶֽךָ׃\rb*? \v 15 \rb Was that day|הַיּ֧וֹם\rb* \rb the first time|הַחִלֹּ֛תִי\rb* \rb I inquired|לְשָׁאוֹל\rb* \rb of God|בֵאלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb for him|ל֥וֹ\rb*? \rb Far be it|חָלִ֣ילָה\rb* \rb from me|לִּ֑י\rb*! \rb Let not|אַל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb accuse|יָשֵׂם֩\rb*\rb |דָבָר֙\rb* \rb your servant|בְּעַבְדּ֤וֹ\rb* \rb or any|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb of my father’s|אָבִ֔י\rb* \rb household|בֵּ֣ית\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֙\rb* \rb knew|יָדַ֤ע\rb* \rb nothing|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb of this|זֹ֔את\rb* \rb whole|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb affair|דָּבָ֥ר\rb* — \rb not in part|קָטֹ֖ן\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb in whole|גָדֽוֹל׃\rb*.”
\p \v 16 \rb But the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb You will surely die|מ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |תָּמ֖וּת\rb*, \rb Ahimelech|אֲחִימֶ֑לֶךְ\rb*, \rb you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb your father’s|אָבִֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֥ית\rb*!”
\p \v 17 \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֡לֶךְ\rb* \rb ordered|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb the guards|לָרָצִים֩\rb* \rb at his side|הַנִּצָּבִ֨ים\rb*\rb |עָלָ֜יו\rb*, “\rb Turn|סֹ֥בּוּ\rb* \rb and kill|וְהָמִ֣יתוּ׀\rb* \rb the priests|כֹּהֲנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb they too|גַם־\rb*\rb |יָדָם֙\rb* \rb sided with|עִם־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*. \rb For|וְכִ֤י\rb* \rb they knew|יָֽדְעוּ֙\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb was fleeing|בֹרֵ֣חַ\rb*, \rb but they did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb tell|גָל֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb me|אָזְנוֹ\rb*.”
\p \rb But the king’s|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדֵ֤י\rb* \rb would|אָב֞וּ\rb* \rb not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb lift|לִשְׁלֹ֣חַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a hand|יָדָ֔ם\rb* \rb to strike|לִפְגֹ֖עַ\rb* \rb the priests|בְּכֹהֲנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb So the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb ordered|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb Doeg|לְדוֹיֵג\rb*, “\rb You|אַתָּ֔ה\rb* \rb turn|סֹ֣ב\rb* \rb and strike down|וּפְגַ֖ע\rb* \rb the priests|בַּכֹּהֲנִ֑ים\rb*!”
\p \rb And Doeg|דּוֹיֵג\rb* \rb the Edomite|הָאֲדֹמִ֗י\rb* \rb turned|וַיִּסֹּ֞ב\rb* \rb and struck down|וַיִּפְגַּע־\rb* \rb the priests|בַּכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb himself|הוּא֙\rb*. \rb On that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb he killed|וַיָּ֣מֶת׀\rb* \rb eighty-five|שְׁמֹנִ֤ים\rb*\rb |וַחֲמִשָּׁה֙\rb* \rb men|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb who wore|נֹשֵׂ֖א\rb* \rb the linen|בָּֽד׃\rb* \rb ephod|אֵפ֥וֹד\rb*. \v 19 \rb |וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb He also put|הִכָּ֣ה\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb* \rb to the sword|חֶ֔רֶב\rb* \rb Nob|נֹ֤ב\rb*, \rb the city|עִיר־\rb* \rb of the priests|הַכֹּֽהֲנִים֙\rb*, \rb with its men|מֵאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb and|וְעַד־\rb* \rb women|אִשָּׁ֔ה\rb*, \rb children|מֵעוֹלֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and|וְעַד־\rb* \rb infants|יוֹנֵ֑ק\rb*, \rb oxen|וְשׁ֧וֹר\rb*, \rb donkeys|וַחֲמ֛וֹר\rb*, \rb and sheep|וָשֶׂ֖ה\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb*\rb |חָֽרֶב׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb But one|אֶחָ֗ד\rb* \rb of the sons|בֵּן־\rb* \rb of Ahimelech|לַאֲחִימֶ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahitub|אֲחִט֔וּב\rb* \rb escaped|וַיִּמָּלֵ֣ט\rb*. \rb His name|וּשְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb was Abiathar|אֶבְיָתָ֑ר\rb*, \rb and he fled|וַיִּבְרַ֖ח\rb* \rb to|אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb David|דָוִֽד׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb And Abiathar|אֶבְיָתָ֖ר\rb* \rb told|וַיַּגֵּ֥ד\rb* \rb David|לְדָוִ֑ד\rb* \rb that|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb had killed|הָרַ֣ג\rb* \rb the priests|כֹּהֲנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb Then David|דָּוִ֜ד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to Abiathar|לְאֶבְיָתָ֗ר\rb*, “\rb I knew|יָדַ֜עְתִּי\rb* \rb that Doeg|דּוֹיֵג\rb* \rb the Edomite|הָאֲדֹמִ֔י\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb was there|שָׁם֙\rb* \rb that|הַהוּא֙\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֤וֹם\rb*, \rb and that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he was sure to tell|הַגֵּ֥ד\rb*\rb |יַגִּ֖יד\rb* \rb Saul|לְשָׁא֑וּל\rb*. \rb I myself|אָנֹכִ֣י\rb* \rb am responsible|סַבֹּ֔תִי\rb* \rb for the lives|נֶ֖פֶשׁ\rb* \rb of everyone|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb in your father’s|אָבִֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֥ית\rb*. \v 23 \rb Stay|שְׁבָ֤ה\rb* \rb with me|אִתִּי֙\rb*; \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּירָ֔א\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb he who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb seeks|יְבַקֵּ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your life|נַפְשֶׁ֑ךָ\rb* \rb is seeking|יְבַקֵּ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb mine as well|נַפְשִׁ֖י\rb*.\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb You|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb will be safe|מִשְׁמֶ֥רֶת\rb* \rb with me|עִמָּדִֽי׃\rb*.”
\c 23
\s1 David Delivers Keilah
\p \v 1 \rb Now it was reported|וַיַּגִּ֥דוּ\rb* \rb to David|לְדָוִ֖ד\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Look|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb*, \rb the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּים֙\rb* \rb are fighting|נִלְחָמִ֣ים\rb* \rb against Keilah|בִּקְעִילָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְהֵ֖מָּה\rb* \rb and looting|שֹׁסִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the threshing floors|הַגֳּרָנֽוֹת׃\rb*.”
\p \v 2 \rb So David|דָּוִ֤ד\rb* \rb inquired|וַיִּשְׁאַ֨ל\rb* \rb of the LORD|בַּֽיהוָה֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb Should I go|הַאֵלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb and attack|וְהִכֵּ֔יתִי\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֑לֶּהס\rb* \rb Philistines|בַּפְּלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb*?”
\p \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֗ד\rb*, “\rb Go|לֵ֚ךְ\rb* \rb and attack|וְהִכִּ֣יתָ\rb* \rb the Philistines|בַפְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb and save|וְהוֹשַׁעְתָּ֖\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Keilah|קְעִילָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 3 \rb But David’s|דָוִד֙\rb* \rb men|אַנְשֵׁ֤י\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמְר֜וּ\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֔יו\rb*, “\rb Look|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb*, \rb we|אֲנַ֥חְנוּ\rb* \rb are afraid|יְרֵאִ֑ים\rb* \rb here|פֹ֛ה\rb* \rb in Judah|בִּֽיהוּדָ֖ה\rb*; \rb how much more|וְאַף֙\rb* \rb if|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb we go|נֵלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb to Keilah|קְעִלָ֔ה\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb the armies of|מַֽעַרְכ֖וֹת\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּֽים׃ס\rb*?”
\p \v 4 \rb Once again|וַיּ֨וֹסֶף\rb*\rb |ע֤וֹד\rb*, \rb David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb inquired|לִשְׁאֹ֣ל\rb* \rb of the LORD|בַּֽיהוָ֔הס\rb*, \rb and the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb answered him|וַֽיַּעֲנֵ֖הוּ\rb*: “\rb Go|רֵ֣ד\rb* \rb at once|ק֚וּם\rb* \rb to Keilah|קְעִילָ֔ה\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb will deliver|נֹתֵ֛ן\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb into your hand|בְּיָדֶֽךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb Then David|דָּוִד֩\rb* \rb and his men|וְאֲנָשׁוֹ\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb to Keilah|קְעִילָ֜ה\rb*, \rb fought|וַיִּלָּ֣חֶם\rb* \rb against the Philistines|בַּפְּלִשְׁתִּ֗ים\rb*, \rb and carried off|וַיִּנְהַג֙\rb* \rb their livestock|מִקְנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb striking|וַיַּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb them|בָּהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb with a mighty|גְדוֹלָ֑ה\rb* \rb blow|מַכָּ֣ה\rb*. \rb So David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb saved|וַיֹּ֣שַׁע\rb* \rb the people|יֹשְׁבֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Keilah|קְעִילָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 6 (\rb Now|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb Abiathar|אֶבְיָתָ֧ר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahimelech|אֲחִימֶ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb had brought|יָרַ֥ד\rb* \rb the ephod|אֵפ֖וֹד\rb* \rb with him|בְּיָדֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb when he fled|בִּ֠בְרֹחַ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb at Keilah|קְעִילָ֑ה\rb*.)
\s1 Saul Pursues David
\r (\ref Psalm 54:1–7|PSA 54:1-7\ref*)
\p \v 7 \rb When Saul|לְשָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb was told|וַיֻּגַּ֣ד\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb had gone|בָ֥א\rb* \rb to Keilah|קְעִילָ֑ה\rb*, \rb he|שָׁא֗וּל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb has delivered|נִכַּ֨ר\rb* \rb him|אֹת֤וֹ\rb* \rb into my hand|בְּיָדִ֔י\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb he has trapped himself|נִסְגַּ֣ר\rb* \rb by entering|לָב֔וֹא\rb* \rb a town|בְּעִ֖יר\rb* \rb with gates|דְּלָתַ֥יִם\rb* \rb and bars|וּבְרִֽיחַ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb Then Saul|שָׁא֛וּל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb summoned|וַיְשַׁמַּ֥ע\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his troops|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb to go|לָרֶ֣דֶת\rb* \rb to war|לַמִּלְחָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb at Keilah|קְעִילָ֔ה\rb* \rb and besiege|לָצ֥וּר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and his men|אֲנָשָֽׁיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb When David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb learned|וַיֵּ֣דַע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb was plotting|מַחֲרִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb evil|הָרָעָ֑ה\rb* \rb against him|עָלָ֔יו\rb*, \rb he said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Abiathar|אֶבְיָתָ֣ר\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb*, “\rb Bring|הַגִּ֖ישָׁה\rb* \rb the ephod|הָאֵפֽוֹד׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 10 \rb And David|דָּוִד֒\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמֶר֮\rb*, “\rb O LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֔\rb* \rb has heard|שָׁמֹ֤עַ\rb*\rb |שָׁמַע֙\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb intends|מְבַקֵּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb to come|לָב֣וֹא\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Keilah|קְעִילָ֑ה\rb* \rb and destroy|לְשַׁחֵ֥ת\rb* \rb the city|לָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb on my account|בַּעֲבוּרִֽי׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb Will the citizens|בַעֲלֵי֩\rb* \rb of Keilah|קְעִילָ֨ה\rb* \rb surrender me|הֲיַסְגִּרֻ֣נִי\rb* \rb into his hand|בְיָד֜וֹ\rb*?\f + \fr 23:11 \ft Some manuscripts omit this question.\f* \rb Will Saul|שָׁא֗וּל\rb* \rb come down|הֲיֵרֵ֣ד\rb*, \rb as|כַּֽאֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb Your servant|עַבְדֶּ֔ךָ\rb* \rb has heard|שָׁמַ֣ע\rb*? \rb O LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb please|נָ֖א\rb* \rb tell|הַגֶּד־\rb* \rb Your servant|לְעַבְדֶּ֑ךָס\rb*.”
\p “\rb He will|יֵרֵֽד׃\rb*,” \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb So David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Will the citizens|בַּעֲלֵ֧י\rb* \rb of Keilah|קְעִילָ֛ה\rb* \rb surrender|הֲיַסְגִּ֜רוּ\rb* \rb me|אֹתִ֥י\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb my men|אֲנָשַׁ֖י\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֑וּל\rb*?”
\p “\rb They will|יַסְגִּֽירוּ׃ס\rb*,” \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb Then David|דָּוִ֨ד\rb* \rb and his men|וַאֲנָשָׁ֜יו\rb*, \rb about six|כְּשֵׁשׁ־\rb* \rb hundred strong|מֵא֣וֹת\rb*, \rb set out|וַיָּקָם֩\rb*\rb |אִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb and departed|וַיֵּצְאוּ֙\rb* \rb from Keilah|מִקְּעִלָ֔ה\rb*, \rb moving from place to place|וַיִּֽתְהַלְּכ֖וּ\rb*\rb |בַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |יִתְהַלָּ֑כוּ\rb*. \rb When Saul|וּלְשָׁא֣וּל\rb* \rb was told|הֻגַּ֗ד\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb had escaped|נִמְלַ֤ט\rb* \rb from Keilah|מִקְּעִילָ֔ה\rb*, \rb he declined|וַיֶּחְדַּ֖ל\rb* \rb to go forth|לָצֵֽאת׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb And David|דָּוִ֤ד\rb* \rb stayed|וַיֵּ֨שֶׁב\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּר֙\rb* \rb strongholds|בַּמְּצָד֔וֹת\rb*\rb |וַיֵּ֥שֶׁב\rb* \rb and in the hill country|בָּהָ֖ר\rb* \rb of the Wilderness|בְּמִדְבַּר־\rb* \rb of Ziph|זִ֑יף\rb*. \rb Day|כָּל־\rb* \rb after day|הַיָּמִ֔ים\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb* \rb searched for him|וַיְבַקְשֵׁ֤הוּ\rb*, \rb but God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb would not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb deliver David|נְתָנ֥וֹ\rb* \rb into his hand|בְּיָדֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb While David|דָוִ֔ד\rb* \rb was in Horesh|בַּחֹֽרְשָׁה׃ס\rb* \rb in the Wilderness|בְּמִדְבַּר־\rb* \rb of Ziph|זִ֖יף\rb*, \rb he|וְדָוִ֥ד\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֣רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb had come out|יָצָ֥א\rb* \rb to take|לְבַקֵּ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his life|נַפְשׁ֑וֹ\rb*. \v 16 \rb And|וַיָּ֙קָם֙\rb* \rb Saul’s|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֣ן\rb* \rb came|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb in Horesh|חֹ֑רְשָׁה\rb* \rb and strengthened|וַיְחַזֵּ֥ק\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his hand|יָד֖וֹ\rb* \rb in God|בֵּאלֹהִֽים׃\rb*, \v 17 \rb saying|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*,\rb |אֵלָ֜יו\rb* “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּירָ֗א\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb my father|אָבִ֔י\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֣וּל\rb* \rb will never|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb lay a hand on|תִֽמְצָאֲךָ֙\rb* \rb you|יַ֚ד\rb*. \rb And you|וְאַתָּה֙\rb* \rb will be king|תִּמְלֹ֣ךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb and I will|וְאָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb be|אֶֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb your|לְּךָ֣\rb* \rb second-in-command|לְמִשְׁנֶ֑ה\rb*. \rb Even|וְגַם־\rb* \rb my father|אָבִ֖י\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֥וּל\rb* \rb knows|יֹדֵ֥עַ\rb* \rb this is true|כֵּֽן׃\rb*.”
\p \v 18 \rb So the two|שְׁנֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb of them made|וַיִּכְרְת֧וּ\rb* \rb a covenant|בְּרִ֖ית\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb And David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb remained|וַיֵּ֤שֶׁב\rb* \rb in Horesh|בַּחֹ֔רְשָׁה\rb*, \rb while Jonathan|וִיהוֹנָתָ֖ן\rb* \rb went|הָלַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb home|לְבֵיתֽוֹ׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb Then the Ziphites|זִפִים֙\rb* \rb came up|וַיַּעֲל֤וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb at Gibeah|הַגִּבְעָ֖תָה\rb* \rb and said|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Is not|הֲל֣וֹא\rb* \rb David|דָ֠וִד\rb* \rb hiding|מִסְתַּתֵּ֨ר\rb* \rb among us|עִמָּ֤נוּ\rb* \rb in the strongholds|בַמְּצָדוֹת֙\rb* \rb at Horesh|בַּחֹ֔רְשָׁה\rb*, \rb on the hill|בְּגִבְעַת֙\rb* \rb of Hachilah|הַֽחֲכִילָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb south|מִימִ֥ין\rb* \rb of Jeshimon|הַיְשִׁימֽוֹן׃\rb*? \v 20 \rb Now|וְ֠עַתָּה\rb*, \rb O king|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb*, \rb come down|רֵ֑ד\rb* \rb whenever|לְכָל־\rb* \rb your soul|נַפְשְׁךָ֥\rb* \rb desires|אַוַּ֨ת\rb*\rb |לָרֶ֖דֶת\rb*, \rb and we will be responsible|וְלָ֥נוּ\rb* \rb for delivering him|הַסְגִּיר֖וֹ\rb* \rb into your hand|בְּיַ֥ד\rb*\rb |הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 21 “\rb May you|אַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb be blessed|בְּרוּכִ֥ים\rb* \rb by the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb*,” \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb*, “\rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you have had compassion|חֲמַלְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb on me|עָלָֽי׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb Please|נָ֞א\rb* \rb go|לְכוּ־\rb* \rb and prepare|הָכִ֣ינוּ\rb* \rb further|ע֗וֹד\rb*. \rb Investigate|וּדְע֤וּ\rb* \rb and watch|וּרְאוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |מְקוֹמוֹ֙\rb* \rb carefully where|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he goes|תִּֽהְיֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |רַגְל֔וֹ\rb* \rb and who|מִ֥י\rb* \rb has seen him|רָאָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֑ם\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb I am told that|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb he|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb is extremely cunning|עָר֥וֹם\rb*\rb |יַעְרִ֖ם\rb*. \v 23 \rb Observe|וּרְא֣וּ\rb* \rb and find out|וּדְע֗וּ\rb* \rb all|מִכֹּ֤ל\rb* \rb the places|הַמַּֽחֲבֹאִים֙\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he hides|יִתְחַבֵּ֣א\rb*.\rb |שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb Then come back|וְשַׁבְתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַי֙\rb* \rb with|אֶל־\rb* \rb certainty|נָכ֔וֹן\rb*, \rb and I will go|וְהָלַכְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb with you|אִתְּכֶ֑ם\rb*.\rb |וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb he is|יֶשְׁנ֣וֹ\rb* \rb in the land|בָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*, \rb I will search him out|וְחִפַּשְׂתִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb among all|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the clans|אַלְפֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 24 \rb So they set out|וַיָּק֛וּמוּ\rb* \rb and went|וַיֵּלְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb to Ziph|זִ֖יפָה\rb* \rb ahead of|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֑וּל\rb*. \rb Now David|וְדָוִ֨ד\rb* \rb and his men|וַאֲנָשָׁ֜יו\rb* \rb were in the Wilderness|בְּמִדְבַּ֤ר\rb* \rb of Maon|מָעוֹן֙\rb* \rb in the Arabah|בָּעֲרָבָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶ֖ל\rb* \rb south|יְמִ֥ין\rb* \rb of Jeshimon|הַיְשִׁימֽוֹן׃\rb*, \v 25 \rb and Saul|שָׁא֣וּל\rb* \rb and his men|וַאֲנָשָׁיו֮\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb to seek him|לְבַקֵּשׁ֒\rb*. \rb When David|לְדָוִ֔ד\rb* \rb was told about it|וַיַּגִּ֣דוּ\rb*, \rb he went down|וַיֵּ֣רֶד\rb* \rb to the rock|הַסֶּ֔לַע\rb* \rb and stayed|וַיֵּ֖שֶׁב\rb* \rb in the Wilderness|בְּמִדְבַּ֣ר\rb* \rb of Maon|מָע֑וֹן\rb*. \rb And when Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb heard of this|וַיִּשְׁמַ֣ע\rb*, \rb he pursued|וַיִּרְדֹּ֥ף\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵֽי־\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb there|מִדְבַּ֥ר\rb*\rb |מָעֽוֹן׃\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb Saul|שָׁא֜וּל\rb* \rb was proceeding along|וַיֵּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb one|מִזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb side|מִצַּ֤ד\rb* \rb of the mountain|הָהָר֙\rb*, \rb and David|וְדָוִ֧ד\rb* \rb and his men|וַאֲנָשָׁ֛יו\rb* \rb along the other|מִזֶּ֑ה\rb*\rb |וַיְהִ֨י\rb* \rb side|מִצַּ֥ד\rb*.\rb |הָהָ֖ר\rb* \rb Even though David|דָוִ֜ד\rb* \rb was hurrying|נֶחְפָּ֤ז\rb* \rb to get away|לָלֶ֙כֶת֙\rb*\rb |מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |שָׁא֔וּל\rb*, \rb Saul|וְשָׁא֣וּל\rb* \rb and his men|וַאֲנָשָׁ֗יו\rb* \rb were closing|עֹֽטְרִ֛ים\rb* \rb in on|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֥ד\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and his men|אֲנָשָׁ֖יו\rb* \rb to capture them|לְתָפְשָֽׂם׃\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb Then a messenger|וּמַלְאָ֣ךְ\rb* \rb came|בָּ֔א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Come|וְלֵ֔כָה\rb* \rb quickly|מַהֲרָ֣ה\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb have raided|פָשְׁט֥וּ\rb* \rb the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*!” \v 28 \rb So Saul|שָׁא֗וּל\rb* \rb broke off|וַיָּ֣שָׁב\rb* \rb his pursuit|מִרְדֹף֙\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of David|דָוִ֔ד\rb* \rb and went|וַיֵּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb to meet|לִקְרַ֣את\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb*. \rb That is why|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֗ן\rb* \rb that|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb place|לַמָּק֣וֹם\rb* \rb is called|קָֽרְאוּ֙\rb*\rb |סֶ֖לַע\rb* \rb Sela-hammahlekoth|הַֽמַּחְלְקֽוֹת׃\rb*.\f + \fr 23:28 \fqa Sela-hammahlekoth \ft means \fqa Rock of Escape\ft .\f* \v 29 \rb And David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb went up|וַיַּ֥עַל\rb* \rb from there|מִשָּׁ֑ם\rb* \rb and lived|וַיֵּ֖שֶׁב\rb* \rb in the strongholds|בִּמְצָד֥וֹת\rb*\rb |עֵֽין־\rb* \rb of En-gedi|גֶּֽדִי׃\rb*.
\c 24
\s1 David Spares Saul
\p \v 1 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb After|כַּֽאֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb had returned|שָׁ֣ב\rb* \rb from pursuing|מֵאַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb*, \rb he was told|וַיַּגִּ֤דוּ\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*\rb |הִנֵּ֣ה\rb* “\rb David|דָוִ֔ד\rb* \rb is in the wilderness|בְּמִדְבַּ֖ר\rb*\rb |עֵ֥ין\rb* \rb of En-gedi|גֶּֽדִי׃ס\rb*.” \v 2 \rb So Saul|שָׁא֗וּל\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֧שֶׁת\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִ֛ים\rb* \rb chosen|בָּח֖וּר\rb* \rb men|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and went|וַיֵּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb to look for|לְבַקֵּ֤שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb and his men|וַֽאֲנָשָׁ֔יו\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the region|פְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the Rocks|צוּרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Wild Goats|הַיְּעֵלִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Soon Saul came|וַ֠יָּבֹא\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the sheepfolds|הַצֹּ֤אן\rb*\rb |גִּדְר֨וֹת\rb* \rb along|עַל־\rb* \rb the road|הַדֶּ֙רֶךְ֙\rb*, \rb where there was|וְשָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb a cave|מְעָרָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and he|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb went in|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb to relieve|לְהָסֵ֣ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb himself|רַגְלָ֑יו\rb*.\f + \fr 24:3 \ft Literally \fqa cover his feet\ft , a euphemism for relieving oneself\f* \rb And David|וְדָוִד֙\rb* \rb and his men|וַאֲנָשָׁ֔יו\rb* \rb were hiding|יֹשְׁבִֽים׃\rb* \rb in the recesses|בְּיַרְכְּתֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the cave|הַמְּעָרָ֖ה\rb*. \v 4 \rb So David’s|דָוִ֜ד\rb* \rb men|אַנְשֵׁ֨י\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמְרוּ֩\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֗יו\rb*, “\rb This is|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb the day|הַיּ֜וֹם\rb* \rb about which|אֲ‍ֽשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֧ר\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֗יךָ\rb*, ‘\rb Behold|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb*, \rb I|אָנֹכִ֜י\rb* \rb will deliver|נֹתֵ֤ן\rb* \rb your enemy|אֹיְבֶיךָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb into your hand|בְּיָדֶ֔ךָ\rb*, \rb that you may do|וְעָשִׂ֣יתָ\rb* \rb with him|לּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb you wish|יִטַ֣ב\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֶ֑יךָ\rb*.’”
\p \rb Then David|דָּוִ֗ד\rb* \rb crept up|וַיָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb and stealthily|בַּלָּֽט׃\rb* \rb cut off|וַיִּכְרֹ֛ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a corner|כְּנַֽף־\rb* \rb of Saul’s|לְשָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb robe|הַמְּעִ֥יל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb |וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb Afterward|אַֽחֲרֵי־\rb*\rb |כֵ֔ן\rb*, \rb David’s|דָּוִ֖ד\rb*\rb |אֹת֑וֹ\rb* \rb conscience|לֵב־\rb* \rb was stricken|וַיַּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb because|עַ֚ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he had cut off|כָּרַ֔ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the corner|כָּנָ֖ף\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb of Saul’s robe|לְשָׁאֽוּל׃ס\rb*. \v 6 \rb So he said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to his men|לַאֲנָשָׁ֜יו\rb*, “\rb The LORD|מֵֽיהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb forbid|חָלִ֧ילָה\rb* \rb that|אִם־\rb* \rb I|לִּ֣י\rb* \rb should do|אֶעֱשֶׂה֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb such|הַזֶּ֤ה\rb* \rb a thing|הַדָּבָ֨ר\rb* \rb to my master|לַֽאדֹנִי֙\rb*, \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb anointed|לִמְשִׁ֣יחַ\rb*. \rb May I never lift|לִשְׁלֹ֥חַ\rb* \rb my hand|יָדִ֖י\rb* \rb against him|בּ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb since|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb is the LORD’s|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb anointed|מְשִׁ֥יחַ\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb With these words|בַּדְּבָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֤ד\rb* \rb restrained|וַיְשַׁסַּ֨ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his men|אֲנָשָׁיו֙\rb*, \rb and he did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb let them|נְתָנָ֖ם\rb* \rb rise up|לָק֣וּם\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֑וּל\rb*. \rb Then Saul|וְשָׁא֛וּל\rb* \rb left|קָ֥ם\rb* \rb the cave|מֵהַמְּעָרָ֖ה\rb* \rb and went|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb on his way|בַּדָּֽרֶךְ׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb After|אַחֲרֵי־\rb* \rb that|כֵ֗ן\rb*, \rb David|דָּוִ֜ד\rb* \rb got up|וַיָּ֨קָם\rb*, \rb went out|וַיֵּצֵא֙\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the cave|הַמְּעָרָה\rb*, \rb and called out|וַיִּקְרָ֧א\rb* \rb to|אַֽחֲרֵי־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֛וּל\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֖ר\rb* “\rb My lord|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*!”
\p \rb When Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb* \rb looked|וַיַּבֵּ֤ט\rb* \rb behind him|אַֽחֲרָ֔יו\rb*, \rb David|דָּוִ֥ד\rb* \rb bowed|וַיִּקֹּ֨ד\rb* \rb facedown|אַפַּ֛יִם\rb*\rb |אַ֖רְצָה\rb* \rb in reverence|וַיִּשְׁתָּֽחוּ׃ס\rb* \v 9 \rb and|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to Saul|לְשָׁא֔וּל\rb*, “\rb Why|לָ֧מָּה\rb* \rb do you listen|תִשְׁמַ֛ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to the words|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of men|אָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb who say|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, ‘\rb Look|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb*, \rb David|דָוִ֔ד\rb* \rb intends|מְבַקֵּ֖שׁ\rb* \rb to harm you|רָעָתֶֽךָ׃\rb*’ ? \v 10 \rb Behold|הִנֵּה֩\rb*, \rb this|הַזֶּ֜ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֨וֹם\rb* \rb you have seen|רָא֣וּ\rb* \rb with your own eyes|עֵינֶ֗יךָ\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה׀\rb*\rb |הַיּ֤וֹם׀\rb* \rb delivered you|נְתָנְךָ֩\rb* \rb into my hand|בְּיָדִי֙\rb* \rb in the cave|בַּמְּעָרָ֔ה\rb*. \rb I was told|וְאָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb to kill you|לַהֲרָגֲךָ֖\rb*, \rb but I spared|וַתָּ֣חָס\rb* \rb you|עָלֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb and said|וָאֹמַ֗ר\rb*, ‘\rb I will not|לֹא־\rb* \rb lift|אֶשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb my hand|יָדִי֙\rb* \rb against my lord|בַּֽאדֹנִ֔י\rb*, \rb since|כִּי־\rb* \rb he|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb is the LORD’s|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb anointed|מְשִׁ֥יחַ\rb*.’
\p \v 11 \rb See|רְאֵ֔ה\rb*,\rb |גַּ֗ם\rb* \rb my father|וְאָבִ֣י\rb*, \rb look|רְאֵ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb at the corner|כְּנַ֥ף\rb* \rb of your robe|מְעִילְךָ֖\rb* \rb in my hand|בְּיָדִ֑י\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֡י\rb* \rb I cut it|כְּנַ֨ף\rb*\rb |מְעִֽילְךָ֜\rb* \rb off|בְּכָרְתִי֩\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb but I did not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb kill you|הֲרַגְתִּ֗יךָ\rb*. \rb Know|דַּ֤ע\rb* \rb and see|וּרְאֵה֙\rb* \rb that|כִּי֩\rb* \rb there is no|אֵ֨ין\rb* \rb evil|רָעָ֤ה\rb* \rb or rebellion|וָפֶ֙שַׁע֙\rb* \rb in my hands|בְּיָדִ֜י\rb*. \rb I have not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb sinned|חָטָ֣אתִי\rb* \rb against you|לָ֔ךְ\rb*, \rb even though you|וְאַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb are hunting me down|צֹדֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to take|לְקַחְתָּֽהּ׃\rb* \rb my life|נַפְשִׁ֖י\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb May the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb judge|יִשְׁפֹּ֤ט\rb* \rb between you and me|בֵּינִ֣י\rb*\rb |וּבֵינֶ֔ךָ\rb*, \rb and may the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb take vengeance|וּנְקָמַ֥נִי\rb* \rb on you|מִמֶּ֑ךָּ\rb*, \rb but my hand|וְיָדִ֖י\rb* \rb will never|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be|תִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb against you|בָּֽךְ׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb As|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the old|הַקַּדְמֹנִ֔י\rb* \rb proverb|מְשַׁל֙\rb* \rb says|יֹאמַ֗ר\rb*, ‘\rb Wickedness|רֶ֑שַׁע\rb* \rb proceeds|יֵ֣צֵא\rb* \rb from the wicked|מֵרְשָׁעִ֖ים\rb*.’ \rb But my hand|וְיָדִ֖י\rb* \rb will never|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be|תִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb against you|בָּֽךְ׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb Against|אַחֲרֵ֨י\rb* \rb whom|מִ֤י\rb* \rb has the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb come out|יָצָא֙\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb*? \rb Whom|מִ֖י\rb* \rb are you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb pursuing|רֹדֵ֑ף\rb*\rb |אַֽחֲרֵי֙\rb*? \rb A dead|מֵ֔ת\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb dog|כֶּ֣לֶב\rb*? \rb A|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb flea|פַּרְעֹ֥שׁ\rb*? \v 15 \rb May the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb be|וְהָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb our judge|לְדַיָּ֔ן\rb* \rb and decide|וְשָׁפַ֖ט\rb* \rb between you and me|בֵּינִ֣י\rb*\rb |וּבֵינֶ֑ךָ\rb*. \rb May He take notice|וְיֵ֙רֶא֙\rb* \rb and plead|וְיָרֵ֣ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my case|רִיבִ֔י\rb* \rb and deliver me|וְיִשְׁפְּטֵ֖נִי\rb* \rb from your hand|מִיָּדֶֽךָ׃פ\rb*.”
\s1 David’s Oath to Saul
\p \v 16 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb When David|דָּוִ֗ד\rb* \rb had finished|כְּכַלּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb saying|לְדַבֵּ֞ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb things|הַדְּבָרִ֤ים\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |שָׁא֔וּל\rb*, \rb Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb called back|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Is that|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb your voice|הֲקֹלְךָ֥\rb*, \rb David|דָוִ֑ד\rb* \rb my son|בְּנִ֣י\rb*?”
\p \rb Then Saul|שָׁא֛וּל\rb* \rb wept|וַיֵּֽבְךְּ׃\rb* \rb aloud|וַיִּשָּׂ֥א\rb*\rb |קֹל֖וֹ\rb* \v 17 \rb and said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*, “\rb You|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb are more righteous|צַדִּ֥יק\rb* \rb than I|מִמֶּ֑נִּי\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb you|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb have rewarded me|גְּמַלְתַּ֣נִי\rb* \rb with good|הַטּוֹבָ֔ה\rb*, \rb though I|וַאֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb have rewarded you|גְּמַלְתִּ֥יךָ\rb* \rb with evil|הָרָעָֽה׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb And you|וְאַתְּ\rb* \rb have declared|הִגַּ֣דְתָּ\rb* \rb this day|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb how|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you have treated|עָשִׂ֥יתָה\rb* \rb me|אִתִּ֖י\rb* \rb well|טוֹבָ֑ה\rb*,\rb |אֵת֩\rb* \rb for when|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb delivered me|סִגְּרַ֧נִי\rb* \rb into your hand|בְּיָדְךָ֖\rb*, \rb you did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb kill me|הֲרַגְתָּֽנִי׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb When|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb a man|אִישׁ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb finds|יִמְצָ֥א\rb* \rb his enemy|אֹ֣יְב֔וֹ\rb*, \rb does he let him go|וְשִׁלְּח֖וֹ\rb* \rb away|בְּדֶ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb unharmed|טוֹבָ֑ה\rb*? \rb May the LORD|וַֽיהוָה֙\rb* \rb reward you|יְשַׁלֶּמְךָ֣\rb* \rb with good|טוֹבָ֔ה\rb* \rb for|תַּ֚חַת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you have done|עָשִׂ֖יתָה\rb* \rb for me|לִֽי׃\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb Now|וְעַתָּה֙\rb* \rb I know|יָדַ֔עְתִּי\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb for sure that|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb you will be king|מָלֹ֖ךְ\rb*\rb |תִּמְל֑וֹךְ\rb* \rb and that the kingdom|מַמְלֶ֖כֶת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb will be established|וְקָ֙מָה֙\rb* \rb in your hands|בְּיָ֣דְךָ֔\rb*. \v 21 \rb So now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb*, \rb swear|הִשָּׁ֤בְעָה\rb* \rb to me|לִּי֙\rb* \rb by the LORD|בַּֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb that you will not|אִם־\rb* \rb cut off|תַּכְרִ֥ית\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my descendants|זַרְעִ֖י\rb*\rb |אַֽחֲרָ֑י\rb*\rb |וְאִם־\rb* \rb or wipe out|תַּשְׁמִ֥יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my name|שְׁמִ֖י\rb* \rb from my father’s|אָבִֽי׃\rb* \rb house|מִבֵּ֥ית\rb*.”
\p \v 22 \rb So David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb gave his oath|וַיִּשָּׁבַ֥ע\rb* \rb to Saul|לְשָׁא֑וּל\rb*. \rb Then Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb returned|וַיֵּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb home|בֵּית֔וֹ\rb*, \rb but David|וְדָוִד֙\rb* \rb and his men|וַֽאֲנָשָׁ֔יו\rb* \rb went up|עָל֖וּ\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the stronghold|הַמְּצוּדָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\c 25
\s1 The Death of Samuel
\p \v 1 \rb When Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb died|וַיָּ֣מָת\rb*, \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb gathered|וַיִּקָּבְצ֤וּ\rb* \rb to mourn|וַיִּסְפְּדוּ־\rb* \rb for him|ל֔וֹ\rb*; \rb and they buried him|וַיִּקְבְּרֻ֥הוּ\rb* \rb at his home|בְּבֵית֖וֹ\rb* \rb in Ramah|בָּרָמָ֑ה\rb*.
\p \rb Then David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb set out|וַיָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb and went down|וַיֵּ֖רֶד\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Wilderness|מִדְבַּ֥ר\rb* \rb of Paran|פָּארָֽן׃ס\rb*.\f + \fr 25:1 \ft Hebrew and some LXX manuscripts; other LXX manuscripts \fqa Maon\f*
\s1 David, Nabal, and Abigail
\p \v 2 \rb Now there was a man|וְאִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb in Maon|בְּמָע֜וֹן\rb* \rb whose business|וּמַעֲשֵׂ֣הוּ\rb* \rb was in Carmel|בַכַּרְמֶ֗ל\rb*. \rb He was a very|מְאֹ֔ד\rb*\rb |וְל֛וֹ\rb* \rb wealthy|גָּד֣וֹל\rb* \rb man|וְהָאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb with a thousand|וְאֶ֣לֶף\rb* \rb goats|עִזִּ֑ים\rb* \rb and three|שְׁלֹֽשֶׁת־\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִ֖ים\rb* \rb sheep|צֹ֥אן\rb*, \rb which he was|וַיְהִ֛י\rb* \rb shearing|בִּגְזֹ֥ז\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |צֹאנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb in Carmel|בַּכַּרְמֶֽל׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb His|הָאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֤ם\rb* \rb was Nabal|נָבָ֔ל\rb*, \rb and his wife’s|אִשְׁתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb name was|וְשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb Abigail|אֲבִגָ֑יִל\rb*. \rb She was an intelligent|טֽוֹבַת־\rb*\rb |שֶׂ֙כֶל֙\rb* \rb and beautiful|וִ֣יפַת\rb*\rb |תֹּ֔אַר\rb* \rb woman|וְהָאִשָּׁ֤ה\rb*, \rb but her husband|וְהָאִ֥ישׁ\rb*, \rb a Calebite|כְלִבּוֹ׃\rb*, \rb was harsh|קָשֶׁ֛ה\rb* \rb and evil|וְרַ֥ע\rb* \rb in his dealings|מַעֲלָלִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וְה֥וּא\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb While David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb was in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֑ר\rb*, \rb he heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Nabal|נָבָ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb was shearing|גֹזֵ֥ז\rb* \rb sheep|צֹאנֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb So David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb ten|עֲשָׂרָ֣ה\rb* \rb young men|נְעָרִ֑ים\rb* \rb and instructed them|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |דָּוִ֜ד\rb*\rb |לַנְּעָרִ֗ים\rb*, “\rb Go up|עֲל֤וּ\rb*\rb |וּבָאתֶ֣ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Nabal|נָבָ֔ל\rb* \rb at Carmel|כַרְמֶ֙לָה֙\rb*. \rb Greet him|וּשְׁאֶלְתֶּם־\rb*\rb |ל֥וֹ\rb*\rb |לְשָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb* \rb in my name|בִשְׁמִ֖י\rb* \v 6 \rb and say to him|וַאֲמַרְתֶּ֥ם\rb*\rb |כֹּ֖ה\rb*, ‘\rb Long life to you|לֶחָ֑י\rb*, \rb and peace|שָׁלוֹם֙\rb* \rb to you|וְאַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb and to your house|וּבֵיתְךָ֣\rb*\rb |שָׁל֔וֹם\rb* \rb and to all|וְכֹ֥ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb belongs to you|לְךָ֖\rb*\rb |שָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb I hear|שָׁמַ֔עְתִּי\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb it is time for shearing|גֹזְזִ֖ים\rb*.\rb |עַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb When your shepherds|הָרֹעִ֤ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb were|הָי֣וּ\rb* \rb with us|עִמָּ֔נוּ\rb*, \rb we did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb harass them|הֶכְלַמְנ֗וּם\rb*, \rb and nothing|וְלֹֽא־\rb*\rb |מְא֔וּמָה\rb* \rb of theirs|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb was missing|נִפְקַ֤ד\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb time|יְמֵ֖י\rb* \rb they were|הֱיוֹתָ֥ם\rb* \rb in Carmel|בַּכַּרְמֶֽל׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb Ask|שְׁאַ֨ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your young men|נְעָרֶ֜יךָ\rb*, \rb and they will tell|וְיַגִּ֣ידוּ\rb* \rb you|לָ֗ךְ\rb*. \rb So let my young men|הַנְּעָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb find|וְיִמְצְא֨וּ\rb* \rb favor with you|חֵן֙\rb*,\rb |בְּעֵינֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb we have come|בָּ֑נוּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the day|י֥וֹם\rb* \rb of a feast|ט֖וֹב\rb*. \rb Please|נָּ֗א\rb*\rb |אֵת֩\rb* \rb give|תְּנָה־\rb* \rb whatever|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you can spare|תִּמְצָ֤א\rb*\rb |יָֽדְךָ֙\rb* \rb to your servants|לַעֲבָדֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and to your son|וּלְבִנְךָ֖\rb* \rb David|לְדָוִֽד׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 9 \rb When David’s|דָוִ֔ד\rb* \rb young men|נַעֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb arrived|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb*, \rb they relayed|וַיְדַבְּר֧וּ\rb* \rb all|כְּכָל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb*\rb |בְּשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Nabal|נָבָ֛ל\rb* \rb on behalf of David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*. \rb Then they waited|וַיָּנֽוּחוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb |וַיַּ֨עַן\rb* \rb But Nabal|נָבָ֜ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֔אמֶר\rb* \rb them|עַבְדֵ֤י\rb*\rb |דָוִד֙\rb*, “\rb Who|מִ֥י\rb* \rb is David|דָוִ֖ד\rb*? \rb Who is|וּמִ֣י\rb* \rb this son of|בֶן־\rb* \rb Jesse|יִשָׁ֑י\rb*? \rb Many|רַבּ֣וּ\rb* \rb servants|עֲבָדִ֔ים\rb* \rb these days|הַיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb are breaking away|הַמִּתְפָּ֣רְצִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb from|מִפְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb their masters|אֲדֹנָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb Why should I take|וְלָקַחְתִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my bread|לַחְמִי֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb water|מֵימַ֔י\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb and the meat|טִבְחָתִ֔י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have slaughtered|טָבַ֖חְתִּי\rb* \rb for my shearers|לְגֹֽזְזָ֑י\rb*, \rb and give them|וְנָֽתַתִּי֙\rb* \rb to these men|לַֽאֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb whose origin|אֵ֥י\rb*\rb |מִזֶּ֖ה\rb*\rb |הֵֽמָּה׃\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb I do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֔עְתִּי\rb*?”
\p \v 12 \rb So David’s|דָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb men|נַעֲרֵֽי־\rb* \rb turned around|וַיַּהַפְכ֥וּ\rb*\rb |לְדַרְכָּ֑ם\rb* \rb and went back|וַיָּשֻׁ֙בוּ֙\rb*,\rb |וַיָּבֹ֔אוּ\rb* \rb and they relayed|וַיַּגִּ֣דוּ\rb* \rb to him|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb all|כְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb these|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֥ים\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb And David|דָּוִ֨ד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb to his men|לַאֲנָשָׁ֜יו\rb*, “\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Strap on|חִגְר֣וּ׀\rb* \rb your swords|חַרְבּ֗וֹ\rb*!” \rb So David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |חַרְבּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and|גַּם־\rb* \rb all his men|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb strapped on|וַֽיַּחְגְּרוּ֙\rb* \rb their swords|חַרְבּ֔וֹ\rb*\rb |וַיַּחְגֹּ֥ר\rb*, \rb and about four|כְּאַרְבַּ֤ע\rb* \rb hundred|מֵאוֹת֙\rb* \rb men|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb followed|וַֽיַּעֲל֣וּ׀\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֗ד\rb*, \rb while two hundred|וּמָאתַ֖יִם\rb* \rb stayed|יָשְׁב֥וּ\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb the supplies|הַכֵּלִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb Meanwhile, one|אֶחָ֛ד\rb* \rb of Nabal’s|נַֽעַר־\rb* \rb young men|מֵהַנְּעָרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb informed|הִגִּ֧יד\rb* \rb Nabal’s|נָבָ֔ל\rb* \rb wife|אֵ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb Abigail|וְלַאֲבִיגַ֙יִל֙\rb*, “\rb Look|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb*, \rb David|דָּוִ֨ד\rb* \rb sent|שָׁלַח֩\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִ֧ים׀\rb* \rb from the wilderness|מֵֽהַמִּדְבָּ֛ר\rb* \rb to greet|לְבָרֵ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb our master|אֲדֹנֵ֖ינוּ\rb*, \rb but he screamed|וַיָּ֥עַט\rb* \rb at them|בָּהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb Yet these men|וְהָ֣אֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb were very|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb good|טֹבִ֥ים\rb* \rb to us|לָ֖נוּ\rb*. \rb When we were|בִּֽהְיוֹתֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb in the field|בַּשָּׂדֶֽה׃\rb*, \rb we were not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb harassed|הָכְלַ֙מְנוּ֙\rb*, \rb and nothing|וְלֹֽא־\rb*\rb |מְא֔וּמָה\rb* \rb of ours went missing|פָקַ֣דְנוּ\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb time|יְמֵי֙\rb* \rb we lived|הִתְהַלַּ֣כְנוּ\rb* \rb among them|אִתָּ֔ם\rb*. \v 16 \rb They were|הָי֣וּ\rb* \rb a wall|חוֹמָה֙\rb* \rb around us|עָלֵ֔ינוּ\rb*, \rb both|גַּם־\rb* \rb day|יוֹמָ֑ם\rb* \rb and|גַּם־\rb* \rb night|לַ֖יְלָה\rb*, \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb time|יְמֵ֛י\rb* \rb we were|הֱיוֹתֵ֥נוּ\rb* \rb herding|רֹעִ֥ים\rb* \rb our sheep|הַצֹּֽאן׃\rb* \rb near them|עִמָּ֖ם\rb*. \v 17 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb consider carefully|דְּעִ֤י\rb*\rb |וּרְאִי֙\rb* \rb what|מַֽה־\rb* \rb you must do|תַּעֲשִׂ֔י\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb disaster|הָרָעָ֛ה\rb* \rb looms|כָלְתָ֧ה\rb* \rb over|אֶל־\rb* \rb our master|אֲדֹנֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb and|וְעַ֣ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his household|בֵּית֑וֹ\rb*. \rb For he is such|וְהוּא֙\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb a scoundrel|בְּלִיַּ֔עַל\rb* \rb that nobody can speak|מִדַּבֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָֽיו׃\rb*!”
\s1 Abigail Intercedes for Nabal
\p \v 18 \rb Then Abigail|אֲבוֹגַיִל\rb* \rb hurried|וַתְּמַהֵ֣ר\rb* \rb and took|וַתִּקַּח֩\rb* \rb two hundred|מָאתַ֨יִם\rb* \rb loaves of bread|לֶ֜חֶם\rb*, \rb two|וּשְׁנַ֣יִם\rb* \rb skins|נִבְלֵי־\rb* \rb of wine|יַ֗יִן\rb*, \rb five|וְחָמֵ֨שׁ\rb* \rb butchered|עֲשָׂווֹת\rb* \rb sheep|צֹ֤אן\rb*, \rb five|וְחָמֵ֤שׁ\rb* \rb seahs|סְאִים֙\rb* \rb of roasted grain|קָלִ֔י\rb*,\f + \fr 25:18 \fqa 5 seahs \ft is approximately 33 dry quarts or 36.5 liters of roasted grain.\f* \rb a hundred|וּמֵאָ֥ה\rb* \rb clusters of raisins|צִמֻּקִ֖ים\rb*, \rb and two hundred|וּמָאתַ֣יִם\rb* \rb cakes of figs|דְּבֵלִ֑ים\rb*. \rb She loaded them|וַתָּ֖שֶׂם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb donkeys|הַחֲמֹרִֽים׃\rb* \v 19 \rb and said|וַתֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to her young men|לִנְעָרֶ֙יהָ֙\rb*, “\rb Go|עִבְר֣וּ\rb* \rb ahead of me|לְפָנַ֔י\rb*. \rb I will be|הִנְנִ֖י\rb* \rb right behind you|אַחֲרֵיכֶ֣ם\rb*.”\rb |בָּאָ֑ה\rb* \rb But she did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb tell|הִגִּֽידָה׃\rb* \rb her husband|וּלְאִישָׁ֥הּ\rb* \rb Nabal|נָבָ֖ל\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb |וְהָיָ֞ה\rb* \rb As Abigail|הִ֣יא׀\rb* \rb came riding|רֹכֶ֣בֶת\rb*\rb |עַֽל־\rb* \rb her donkey|הַחֲמ֗וֹר\rb*\rb |וְיֹרֶ֙דֶת֙\rb* \rb into a mountain|הָהָ֔ר\rb* \rb ravine|בְּסֵ֣תֶר\rb*, \rb she saw|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb David|דָוִד֙\rb* \rb and his men|וַאֲנָשָׁ֔יו\rb* \rb coming down|יֹרְדִ֖ים\rb* \rb toward her|לִקְרָאתָ֑הּ\rb*, \rb and she met|וַתִּפְגֹּ֖שׁ\rb* \rb them|אֹתָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb Now David|וְדָוִ֣ד\rb* \rb had just|אַךְ֩\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֗ר\rb*, “\rb In vain|לַשֶּׁ֨קֶר\rb* \rb I have protected|שָׁמַ֜רְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb belonged to this man|לָזֶה֙\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֔ר\rb*. \rb Nothing|וְלֹא־\rb*\rb |מִכָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb belongs to him|ל֖וֹ\rb*\rb |מְא֑וּמָה\rb* \rb has gone missing|נִפְקַ֥ד\rb*, \rb yet he has paid me back|וַיָּֽשֶׁב־\rb*\rb |לִ֥י\rb* \rb evil|רָעָ֖ה\rb* \rb for|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb good|טוֹבָֽה׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb May God|אֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb punish|כֹּה־\rb*\rb |יַעֲשֶׂ֧ה\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֖ד\rb*\rb |לְאֹיְבֵ֥י\rb*,\f + \fr 25:22 \ft Some LXX manuscripts; MT \fqa David’s enemies\f* \rb and ever so|וְכֹ֣ה\rb* \rb severely|יֹסִ֑יף\rb*, \rb if I let|אִם־\rb* \rb one|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb male|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb belonging to Nabal|ל֛וֹ\rb* \rb survive|אַשְׁאִ֧יר\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb morning|הַבֹּ֖קֶר\rb*\rb |מַשְׁתִּ֥ין\rb*\rb |בְּקִֽיר׃\rb*.”
\p \v 23 \rb When Abigail|אֲבִיגַ֙יִל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb saw|וַתֵּ֤רֶא\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*, \rb she quickly|וַתְּמַהֵ֕ר\rb* \rb got off|וַתֵּ֖רֶד\rb*\rb |מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb the donkey|הַחֲמ֑וֹר\rb*, \rb fell|וַתִּפֹּ֞ל\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb facedown|פָּנֶ֔יהָ\rb*, \rb and bowed|וַתִּשְׁתַּ֖חוּ\rb*\rb |אָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb before|לְאַפֵּ֤י\rb* \rb him|דָוִד֙\rb*. \v 24 \rb She fell|וַתִּפֹּל֙\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb his feet|רַגְלָ֔יו\rb* \rb and said|וַתֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb My lord|אֲדֹנִ֖י\rb*, \rb may the blame be|הֶֽעָוֺ֑ן\rb* \rb on me alone|בִּי־\rb*\rb |אֲנִ֥י\rb*, \rb but please|נָ֤א\rb* \rb let your servant|אֲמָֽתְךָ֙\rb* \rb speak|וּֽתְדַבֶּר־\rb* \rb to you|בְּאָזְנֶ֔יךָ\rb*; \rb hear|וּשְׁמַ֕ע\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of your servant|אֲמָתֶֽךָ׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb My lord|אֲדֹנִ֣י׀\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb should pay no|אַל־\rb*\rb |נָ֣א\rb* \rb attention|יָשִׂ֣ים\rb*\rb |לִבּ֡וֹ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֜ה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb scoundrel|הַבְּלִיַּ֨עַל\rb*\rb |אִישׁ֩\rb* \rb Nabal|נָבָ֗ל\rb*,\f + \fr 25:25 \fqa Nabal \ft means \fqa fool\ft .\f* \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb he|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb lives up to his name|כִשְׁמוֹ֙\rb*:\rb |כֶּן־\rb* \rb His name|שְׁמ֔וֹ\rb* \rb means Fool|נָבָ֣ל\rb*, \rb and folly|וּנְבָלָ֖ה\rb* \rb accompanies him|עִמּ֑וֹ\rb*. \rb I|וַֽאֲנִי֙\rb*, \rb your servant|אֲמָ֣תְךָ֔\rb*, \rb did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb see|רָאִ֛יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my lord’s|אֲדֹנִ֖י\rb* \rb young men|נַעֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you sent|שָׁלָֽחְתָּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֗י\rb*, \rb as surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb lives|חַי־\rb* \rb and you|נַפְשְׁךָ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb yourself live|וְחֵֽי־\rb*, \rb since the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb has held you back|מְנָעֲךָ֤\rb* \rb from|מִבּ֣וֹא\rb* \rb bloodshed|בְדָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb and from avenging|וְהוֹשֵׁ֥עַ\rb* \rb yourself|לָ֑ךְ\rb* \rb with your own hand|יָדְךָ֖\rb*,\rb |וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb may your enemies|אֹיְבֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and those who seek|וְהַֽמְבַקְשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb harm|רָעָֽה׃\rb* \rb for|אֶל־\rb* \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֖י\rb* \rb be|יִֽהְי֤וּ\rb* \rb like Nabal|כְנָבָל֙\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb Now|וְעַתָּה֙\rb* \rb let this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb gift|הַבְּרָכָ֣ה\rb* \rb your servant|שִׁפְחָתְךָ֖\rb* \rb has brought|הֵבִ֥יא\rb* \rb to my lord|לַֽאדֹנִ֑י\rb* \rb be given|וְנִתְּנָה֙\rb* \rb to the young men|לַנְּעָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb who follow|הַמִּֽתְהַלְּכִ֖ים\rb*\rb |בְּרַגְלֵ֥י\rb* \rb you|אֲדֹנִֽי׃\rb*. \v 28 \rb Please|נָ֖א\rb* \rb forgive|שָׂ֥א\rb* \rb your servant’s|אֲמָתֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb offense|לְפֶ֣שַׁע\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb will surely make|עָשֹֽׂה־\rb*\rb |יַעֲשֶׂה֩\rb* \rb a lasting|נֶאֱמָ֗ן\rb* \rb dynasty|בַּ֣יִת\rb* \rb for my lord|לַֽאדֹנִ֜י\rb*, \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb he|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb fights|נִלְחָ֔ם\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb battles|מִלְחֲמ֤וֹת\rb*. \rb May no evil|וְרָעָ֛ה\rb*\rb |לֹא־\rb* \rb be found|תִמָּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb in you|בְךָ֖\rb* \rb as long as you live|מִיָּמֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb And should someone|וַיָּ֤קָם\rb*\rb |אָדָם֙\rb* \rb pursue you|לִרְדָפְךָ֔\rb* \rb and seek|וּלְבַקֵּ֖שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your life|נַפְשֶׁ֑ךָ\rb*, \rb then the life|נֶ֨פֶשׁ\rb* \rb of my lord|אֲדֹנִ֜י\rb* \rb will be|וְֽהָיְתָה֩\rb* \rb bound securely|צְרוּרָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb by|אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb in the bundle|בִּצְר֣וֹר\rb* \rb of the living|הַחַיִּ֗ים\rb*. \rb But|וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb He shall fling away|יְקַלְּעֶ֔נָּה\rb*\rb |בְּת֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb the lives|נֶ֤פֶשׁ\rb* \rb of your enemies|אֹיְבֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb like stones|כַּ֥ף\rb* \rb from a sling|הַקָּֽלַע׃\rb*.\f + \fr 25:29 \ft Literally \fqa fling away the souls of your enemies as from the pocket of a sling\f*
\p \v 30 \rb |וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb has done|יַעֲשֶׂ֤ה\rb* \rb for my lord|לַֽאדֹנִ֔י\rb* \rb all|כְּכֹ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the good|הַטּוֹבָ֖ה\rb* \rb He promised|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*, \rb and when He has appointed you|וְצִוְּךָ֥\rb* \rb ruler|לְנָגִ֖יד\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb over|עָלֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*, \v 31 \rb then my lord|לַאדֹנִ֗י\rb* \rb will have|תִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb no|וְלֹ֣א\rb*\rb |זֹ֣את׀\rb* \rb remorse|לְפוּקָה֩\rb* \rb or guilt|וּלְמִכְשׁ֨וֹל\rb* \rb of conscience|לֵ֜ב\rb* \rb over needless|חִנָּ֔ם\rb* \rb bloodshed|וְלִשְׁפָּךְ־\rb*\rb |דָּם֙\rb* \rb and|אֲדֹנִ֖י\rb*\rb |ל֑וֹ\rb* \rb revenge|וּלְהוֹשִׁ֥יעַ\rb*. \rb And when the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb has dealt well|וְהֵיטִ֤ב\rb* \rb with my lord|לַֽאדֹנִ֔י\rb*, \rb may you remember|וְזָכַרְתָּ֖\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your servant|אֲמָתֶֽךָ׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 32 \rb Then David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to Abigail|לַאֲבִיגַ֑ל\rb*, “\rb Blessed be|בָּר֤וּךְ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb sent you|שְׁלָחֵ֛ךְ\rb* \rb to meet me|לִקְרָאתִֽי׃\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*! \v 33 \rb Blessed is|וּבָר֥וּךְ\rb* \rb your discernment|טַעְמֵ֖ךְ\rb*, \rb and blessed are|וּבְרוּכָ֣ה\rb* \rb you|אָ֑תְּ\rb*, \rb because|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֤וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּה֙\rb*\rb |מִבּ֣וֹא\rb* \rb you kept me|כְּלִתִ֜נִי\rb* \rb from bloodshed|בְדָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb and from avenging myself|וְהֹשֵׁ֥עַ\rb* \rb by my own hand|יָדִ֖י\rb*\rb |לִֽי׃\rb*. \v 34 \rb Otherwise|וְאוּלָ֗ם\rb*, \rb as surely as the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb lives|חַי־\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb has restrained me|מְנָעַ֔נִי\rb* \rb from harming|מֵהָרַ֖ע\rb* \rb you|אֹתָ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb if you had not|כִּ֣י׀\rb*\rb |לוּלֵ֣י\rb* \rb come|וַתָּבֹאתִי\rb* \rb quickly|מִהַ֗רְתְּ\rb* \rb to meet me|לִקְרָאתִ֔י\rb*, \rb then surely|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb no|אִם־\rb* \rb male|מַשְׁתִּ֥ין\rb* \rb belonging to Nabal|לְנָבָ֛ל\rb* \rb would have been left alive|נוֹתַ֧ר\rb* \rb by|עַד־\rb* \rb morning|הַבֹּ֖קֶר\rb* \rb light|א֥וֹר\rb*\rb |בְּקִֽיר׃\rb*.”
\p \v 35 \rb Then David|דָּוִד֙\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb accepted|וַיִּקַּ֤ח\rb* \rb from her hand|מִיָּדָ֔הּ\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb she had brought|הֵבִ֖יאָה\rb* \rb him|ל֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and he said|אָמַ֗ר\rb* \rb to her|וְלָ֣הּ\rb*, “\rb Go|עֲלִ֤י\rb* \rb home|לְבֵיתֵ֔ךְ\rb* \rb in peace|לְשָׁלוֹם֙\rb*. \rb See|רְאִי֙\rb*, \rb I have heeded|שָׁמַ֣עְתִּי\rb* \rb your voice|בְקוֹלֵ֔ךְ\rb* \rb and granted your request|וָאֶשָּׂ֖א\rb*\rb |פָּנָֽיִךְ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 36 \rb When Abigail|אֲבִיגַ֣יִל׀\rb* \rb returned|וַתָּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Nabal|נָבָ֡ל\rb*, \rb there|וְהִנֵּה־\rb* \rb he was|לוֹ֩\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵית֜וֹ\rb*,\rb |כְּמִשְׁתֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb holding a feast|מִשְׁתֶּ֨ה\rb* \rb fit for a king|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb*,\rb |נָבָל֙\rb* \rb in high|ט֣וֹב\rb*\rb |עָלָ֔יו\rb*\rb |וְה֥וּא\rb* \rb spirits|וְלֵ֤ב\rb* \rb and very|עַד־\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb drunk|שִׁכֹּ֖ר\rb*. \rb So she|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb told|הִגִּ֣ידָה\rb* \rb him|לּ֗וֹ\rb*\rb |דָּבָ֥ר\rb* \rb nothing|קָטֹ֛ן\rb*\rb |וְגָד֖וֹל\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb morning|הַבֹּֽקֶר׃\rb* \rb light|א֥וֹר\rb*.
\p \v 37 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb In the morning|בַבֹּ֗קֶר\rb* \rb when Nabal|מִנָּבָ֔ל\rb* \rb was sober|בְּצֵ֤את\rb*\rb |הַיַּ֙יִן֙\rb*, \rb his wife|אִשְׁתּ֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb told|וַתַּגֶּד־\rb* \rb him|ל֣וֹ\rb* \rb about these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb events|הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb*, \rb and his heart|לִבּוֹ֙\rb* \rb failed|וַיָּ֤מָת\rb* \rb within him|בְּקִרְבּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and he|וְה֖וּא\rb* \rb became|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb like a stone|לְאָֽבֶן׃\rb*. \v 38 \rb |וַיְהִ֖י\rb* \rb About ten|כַּעֲשֶׂ֣רֶת\rb* \rb days later|הַיָּמִ֑ים\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb struck|וַיִּגֹּ֧ף\rb* \rb Nabal|נָבָ֖ל\rb* \rb dead|וַיָּמֹֽת׃\rb*.
\s1 David Marries Abigail
\p \v 39 \rb On hearing|וַיִּשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb Nabal|נָבָל֒\rb* \rb was dead|מֵ֣ת\rb*, \rb David|דָּוִד֮\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֡אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Blessed be|בָּר֣וּךְ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֡ה\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb has upheld|רָב֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my cause|רִ֨יב\rb* \rb against|מִיַּ֣ד\rb* \rb the reproach|חֶרְפָּתִ֜י\rb* \rb of Nabal|נָבָ֗ל\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb has restrained|חָשַׂ֣ךְ\rb* \rb His servant|עַבְדּוֹ֙\rb* \rb from evil|מֵֽרָעָ֔ה\rb*. \rb For|וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has brought|הֵשִׁ֥יב\rb* \rb the wickedness|רָעַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Nabal|נָבָ֔ל\rb* \rb down upon his own head|בְּרֹאשׁ֑וֹ\rb*.”
\p \rb Then David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb word|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to Abigail|בַּאֲבִיגַ֔יִל\rb*, \rb asking|לְקַחְתָּ֥הּ\rb* \rb her to become|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb his wife|לְאִשָּֽׁה׃\rb*. \v 40 \rb When his|דָוִ֛ד\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדֵ֥י\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֜אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Abigail|אֲבִיגַ֖יִל\rb* \rb at Carmel|הַכַּרְמֶ֑לָה\rb*, \rb they said|וַיְדַבְּר֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֙יהָ֙\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* “\rb David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb has sent us|שְׁלָחָ֣נוּ\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֔יִךְ\rb* \rb to take you|לְקַחְתֵּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb as his|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb wife|לְאִשָּֽׁה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 41 \rb She arose|וַתָּ֕קָם\rb*, \rb bowed|וַתִּשְׁתַּ֥חוּ\rb* \rb facedown|אַפַּ֖יִם\rb*,\rb |אָ֑רְצָה\rb* \rb and said|וַתֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Here is|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb your servant|אֲמָֽתְךָ֙\rb*, \rb ready to serve|לְשִׁפְחָ֔ה\rb* \rb and to wash|לִרְחֹ֕ץ\rb* \rb the feet|רַגְלֵ֖י\rb* \rb of my lord’s|אֲדֹנִֽי׃\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדֵ֥י\rb*.”
\p \v 42 \rb So Abigail|אֲבִיגַ֗יִל\rb*\rb |וַתָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb hurried|וַתְּמַהֵ֞ר\rb* \rb and got on|וַתִּרְכַּב֙\rb*\rb |עַֽל־\rb* \rb a donkey|הַחֲמ֔וֹר\rb*, \rb and attended|הַהֹלְכ֖וֹת\rb* \rb by five|וְחָמֵשׁ֙\rb* \rb of her maidens|נַעֲרֹתֶ֔יהָ\rb*\rb |לְרַגְלָ֑הּ\rb*, \rb she followed|וַתֵּ֗לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אַֽחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb David’s|דָוִ֔ד\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאֲכֵ֣י\rb* \rb and became|וַתְּהִי־\rb* \rb his|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb wife|לְאִשָּֽׁה׃\rb*.
\p \v 43 \rb David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb had also|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb married|לָקַ֥ח\rb* \rb Ahinoam|אֲחִינֹ֛עַם\rb* \rb of Jezreel|מִֽיִּזְרְעֶ֑אל\rb*. \rb So she and Abigail were both|שְׁתֵּיהֶ֥ן\rb*\rb |וַתִּהְיֶ֛יןָ\rb* \rb his|ל֖וֹ\rb*\rb |גַּֽם־\rb* \rb wives|לְנָשִֽׁים׃ס\rb*. \v 44 \rb But Saul|וְשָׁא֗וּל\rb* \rb had given|נָתַ֛ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his daughter|בִּתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Michal|מִיכַ֥ל\rb*, \rb David’s|דָּוִ֑ד\rb* \rb wife|אֵ֣שֶׁת\rb*, \rb to Palti|לְפַלְטִ֥י\rb*\f + \fr 25:44 \fqa Palti \ft is a variant of \fqa Paltiel\ft ; see \ref 2 Samuel 3:15|2SA 3:15\ref*.\f* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Laish|לַ֖יִשׁ\rb*, \rb who was|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb from Gallim|מִגַּלִּֽים׃\rb*.
\c 26
\s1 David Again Spares Saul
\p \v 1 \rb Then the Ziphites|הַזִּפִים֙\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֤אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb at Gibeah|הַגִּבְעָ֖תָה\rb* \rb and said|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Is not|הֲל֨וֹא\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֤ד\rb* \rb hiding|מִסְתַּתֵּר֙\rb* \rb on the hill|בְּגִבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Hachilah|הַחֲכִילָ֔ה\rb*, \rb opposite|עַ֖ל\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Jeshimon|הַיְשִׁימֹֽן׃\rb*?” \v 2 \rb |וַיָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb So Saul|שָׁא֗וּל\rb*, \rb accompanied by|וְאִתּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹֽשֶׁת־\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִ֥ים\rb* \rb chosen|בְּחוּרֵ֣י\rb* \rb men|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb went down|וַיֵּ֙רֶד֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Wilderness|מִדְבַּר־\rb* \rb of Ziph|זִ֔יף\rb* \rb to search for|לְבַקֵּ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb there|בְּמִדְבַּר־\rb*\rb |זִֽיף׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Saul|שָׁא֜וּל\rb* \rb camped|וַיִּ֨חַן\rb* \rb beside|עַל־\rb* \rb the road|הַדָּ֑רֶךְ\rb* \rb at the hill|בְּגִבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Hachilah|הַחֲכִילָ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb opposite|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Jeshimon|הַיְשִׁימֹ֖ן\rb*, \rb but David|וְדָוִד֙\rb* \rb was living|יֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֔ר\rb*. \rb When he realized|וַיַּ֕רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֛וּל\rb* \rb had followed|בָ֥א\rb* \rb him|אַחֲרָ֖יו\rb* \rb there|הַמִּדְבָּֽרָה׃\rb*, \v 4 \rb David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb sent out|וַיִּשְׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb spies|מְרַגְּלִ֑ים\rb* \rb to verify|וַיֵּ֕דַע\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |נָכֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb had arrived|בָ֥א\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Then David|דָּוִ֗ד\rb* \rb set out|וַיָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb and went|וַיָּבֹא֮\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּקוֹם֮\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁאוּל֒\rb* \rb had camped|חָנָה־\rb*.\rb |שָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb He|דָּוִ֗ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֣רְא\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּקוֹם֙\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb and Abner|וְאַבְנֵ֥ר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ner|נֵ֖ר\rb*, \rb the general|שַׂר־\rb* \rb of his army|צְבָא֑וֹ\rb*, \rb had lain down|שָֽׁכַב־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֣ם\rb*. \rb Saul|וְשָׁאוּל֙\rb* \rb was lying|שֹׁכֵ֣ב\rb* \rb inside the inner circle of the camp|בַּמַּעְגָּ֔ל\rb*, \rb with the troops|וְהָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb camped|חֹנִ֥ים\rb* \rb around him|סְבִיבֹתוֹ׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb And David|דָּוִ֜ד\rb* \rb asked|וַיַּ֨עַן\rb* \rb Ahimelech|אֲחִימֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb the Hittite|הַחִתִּ֗י\rb* \rb and|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb Abishai|אֲבִישַׁ֨י\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zeruiah|צְרוּיָ֜ה\rb*, \rb Joab’s|יוֹאָב֙\rb* \rb brother|אֲחִ֤י\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* “\rb Who|מִֽי־\rb* \rb will go down|יֵרֵ֥ד\rb* \rb with me|אִתִּ֛י\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֑ה\rb*?”
\p “\rb I will|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb go|אֵרֵ֥ד\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּֽךְ׃\rb*,” \rb answered|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb Abishai|אֲבִישַׁ֔י\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb That night|לַיְלָה֒\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֨ד\rb* \rb and Abishai|וַאֲבִישַׁ֥י׀\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹא֩\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the troops|הָעָם֮\rb*, \rb and Saul|שָׁא֗וּל\rb* \rb was lying|שֹׁכֵ֤ב\rb* \rb there|וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb asleep|יָשֵׁן֙\rb* \rb in the inner circle of the camp|בַּמַּעְגָּ֔ל\rb*, \rb with his spear|וַחֲנִית֥וֹ\rb* \rb stuck|מְעוּכָֽה־\rb* \rb in the ground|בָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb by his head|מְרַאֲשֹׁתוֹ\rb*. \rb And Abner|וְאַבְנֵ֣ר\rb* \rb and the troops|וְהָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb were lying|שֹׁכְבִ֖ים\rb* \rb around him|סְבִיבֹתוֹ׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb Abishai|אֲבִישַׁי֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*, “\rb Today|הַיּ֛וֹם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֥ים\rb* \rb has delivered|סִגַּ֨ר\rb* \rb your enemy|אוֹיִבְךָ֖\rb* \rb into your hand|בְּיָדֶ֑ךָ\rb*. \rb Now, therefore,|וְעַתָּה֩\rb* \rb please|נָ֜א\rb* \rb let me thrust the spear|בַּחֲנִ֤ית\rb* \rb through him|אַכֶּ֨נּוּ\rb* \rb into the ground|וּבָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb with one|אַחַ֔ת\rb* \rb stroke|פַּ֣עַם\rb*. \rb I will not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb need to strike him twice|אֶשְׁנֶ֖ה\rb*\rb |לֽוֹ׃\rb*!”
\p \v 9 \rb But David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Abishai|אֲבִישַׁ֖י\rb*, “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb destroy him|תַּשְׁחִיתֵ֑הוּ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb who|מִ֣י\rb* \rb can extend|שָׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb a hand|יָד֛וֹ\rb* \rb against the LORD’s|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb anointed|בִּמְשִׁ֥יחַ\rb* \rb and be guiltless|וְנִקָּֽה׃פ\rb*?” \v 10 \rb David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb added|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*, “\rb As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb lives|חַי־\rb*, \rb the LORD Himself|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb will strike him down|יִגָּפֶ֑נּוּ\rb*; \rb either|אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb his day|יוֹמ֤וֹ\rb* \rb will come|יָבוֹא֙\rb* \rb and he will die|וָמֵ֔ת\rb*, \rb or|א֧וֹ\rb* \rb he will go|יֵרֵ֖ד\rb* \rb into battle|בַמִּלְחָמָ֛ה\rb* \rb and perish|וְנִסְפָּֽה׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb But the LORD|מֵֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb forbid|חָלִ֤ילָה\rb* \rb that I|לִּי֙\rb* \rb should extend|מִשְּׁלֹ֥חַ\rb* \rb my hand|יָדִ֖י\rb* \rb against the LORD’s|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb anointed|בִּמְשִׁ֣יחַ\rb*. \rb Instead|וְ֠עַתָּה\rb*, \rb take|קַח־\rb*\rb |נָ֨א\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb the spear|הַחֲנִ֜ית\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb and water|הַמַּ֖יִם\rb* \rb jug|צַפַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb by his head|מְרַאֲשֹׁתוֹ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and let us go|וְנֵ֥לֲכָה\rb*\rb |לָּֽנוּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 12 \rb So David|דָּוִ֨ד\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּח֩\rb* \rb the spear|הַחֲנִ֜ית\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and water|הַמַּ֙יִם֙\rb*\rb |מֵרַאֲשֹׁתֵ֣י\rb* \rb jug|צַפַּ֤חַת\rb* \rb by Saul’s head|שָׁא֔וּל\rb*, \rb and they departed|וַיֵּלְכ֖וּ\rb*. \rb No|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb one saw them|רֹאֶה֩\rb* \rb or|וְאֵ֨ין\rb* \rb knew about it|יוֹדֵ֜עַ\rb*, \rb nor did anyone|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb wake up|מֵקִ֗יץ\rb*; \rb they all|כֻלָּם֙\rb* \rb remained asleep|יְשֵׁנִ֔ים\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb a deep sleep|תַּרְדֵּמַ֣ת\rb* \rb from the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb had fallen|נָפְלָ֖ה\rb* \rb on them|עֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\s1 David Reproves Abner
\p \v 13 \rb Then David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb crossed|וַיַּעֲבֹ֤ר\rb* \rb to the other side|הָעֵ֔בֶר\rb* \rb and stood|וַיַּעֲמֹ֥ד\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb atop|רֹאשׁ־\rb* \rb the mountain|הָהָ֖ר\rb* \rb at a distance|מֵֽרָחֹ֑ק\rb*; \rb there was a wide|רַ֥ב\rb* \rb gulf|הַמָּק֖וֹם\rb* \rb between them|בֵּינֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb And David|דָוִ֜ד\rb* \rb shouted|וַיִּקְרָ֨א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the troops|הָעָ֗ם\rb* \rb and to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb Abner|אַבְנֵ֤ר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ner|נֵר֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb Will you not|הֲל֥וֹא\rb* \rb answer me|תַעֲנֶ֖ה\rb*, \rb Abner|אַבְנֵ֑ר\rb*?”
\p “\rb Who|מִ֥י\rb* \rb are you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb who calls|קָרָ֥אתָ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃פ\rb*?” \rb Abner|אַבְנֵר֙\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֔אמֶר\rb* \rb replied|וַיַּ֤עַן\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb So David|דָּוִ֨ד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Abner|אַבְנֵ֜ר\rb*, “\rb You are|אַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb a man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*, \rb aren’t you|הֲלוֹא־\rb*? \rb And who|וּמִ֤י\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb is your equal|כָמ֙וֹךָ֙\rb*? \rb Why then|וְלָ֙מָּה֙\rb* \rb did you not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb protect|שָׁמַ֔רְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb your lord|אֲדֹנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb when|כִּי־\rb* \rb one|אַחַ֣ד\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb came|בָא֙\rb* \rb to destroy him|לְהַשְׁחִ֖ית\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֲדֹנֶֽיךָ׃\rb*? \v 16 \rb This|הַזֶּה֮\rb* \rb thing|הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you have done|עָשִׂיתָ֒\rb* \rb is not|לֹא־\rb* \rb good|ט֞וֹב\rb*. \rb As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*\rb |כִּ֤י\rb* \rb lives|חַי־\rb*, \rb all of you|בְנֵי־\rb* \rb deserve to die|מָ֙וֶת֙\rb*, \rb since you|אַתֶּ֔ם\rb* \rb did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb protect|שְׁמַרְתֶּ֛ם\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb your lord|אֲדֹנֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*,\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb anointed|מְשִׁ֣יחַ\rb*. \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb look around|רְאֵ֗ה\rb*. \rb Where|אֵֽי־\rb* \rb are the king’s|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb spear|חֲנִ֥ית\rb* \rb and water|הַמַּ֖יִם\rb* \rb jug|צַפַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb were by his head|מְרַאֲשֹׁתוֹ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 17 \rb Then Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb recognized|וַיַּכֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb David’s|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb voice|ק֣וֹל\rb* \rb and asked|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Is that|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb your voice|הֲקוֹלְךָ֥\rb*, \rb David|דָוִ֑ד\rb* \rb my son|בְּנִ֣י\rb*?”
\p “\rb It is my voice|קוֹלִ֖י\rb*, \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֥י\rb* \rb and king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*,” \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb And he continued|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Why|לָ֥מָּה\rb*\rb |זֶּ֛ה\rb* \rb is my lord|אֲדֹנִ֥י\rb* \rb pursuing|רֹדֵ֖ף\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb his servant|עַבְדּ֑וֹ\rb*?\rb |כִּ֚י\rb* \rb What|מֶ֣ה\rb* \rb have I done|עָשִׂ֔יתִי\rb*? \rb What|וּמַה־\rb* \rb evil|רָעָֽה׃\rb* \rb is in my hand|בְּיָדִ֖י\rb*? \v 19 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb please|נָא֙\rb*, \rb may my lord|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb hear|יִֽשְׁמַֽע־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of his servant|עַבְדּ֑וֹ\rb*: \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֞ה\rb* \rb has stirred you up|הֱסִֽיתְךָ֥\rb* \rb against me|בִי֙\rb*, \rb then may He accept|יָרַ֣ח\rb* \rb an offering|מִנְחָ֔ה\rb*. \rb But if|וְאִ֣ם׀\rb* \rb men have done it|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |הָאָדָ֗ם\rb*, \rb may they|הֵם֙\rb* \rb be cursed|אֲרוּרִ֥ים\rb* \rb in the presence|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*! \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֗וֹם\rb* \rb they have driven me away|גֵרְשׁ֣וּנִי\rb* \rb from sharing|מֵהִסְתַּפֵּ֜חַ\rb* \rb in the inheritance|בְּנַחֲלַ֤ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, ‘\rb Go|לֵ֥ךְ\rb*, \rb serve|עֲבֹ֖ד\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִֽים׃\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֥ים\rb*.’ \v 20 \rb So|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb let my blood|דָּֽמִי֙\rb* \rb fall|יִפֹּ֤ל\rb* \rb to the ground|אַ֔רְצָה\rb* \rb far from|מִנֶּ֖גֶד\rb* \rb the presence|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb has come out|יָצָ֞א\rb* \rb to look for|לְבַקֵּשׁ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a|אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb flea|פַּרְעֹ֣שׁ\rb*, \rb like|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb one who hunts|יִרְדֹּ֥ף\rb* \rb a partridge|הַקֹּרֵ֖א\rb* \rb in the mountains|בֶּהָרִֽים׃\rb*.”
\s1 Saul Acknowledges His Sin
\p \v 21 \rb Then Saul|שָׁא֨וּל\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb*, “\rb I have sinned|חָטָ֜אתִי\rb*. \rb Come back|שׁ֣וּב\rb*, \rb David|דָוִ֗ד\rb* \rb my son|בְּנִֽי־\rb*.\rb |כִּ֠י\rb* \rb I will never|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb harm|אָרַ֤ע\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֙\rb* \rb again|ע֔וֹד\rb*, \rb because|תַּ֠חַת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֑ה\rb*\rb |הִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb you considered|בְּעֵינֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb my life|נַפְשִׁ֛י\rb* \rb precious|יָקְרָ֥ה\rb*. \rb I have played the fool|הִסְכַּ֛לְתִּי\rb* \rb and have committed a grave|הַרְבֵּ֥ה\rb*\rb |מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb error|וָאֶשְׁגֶּ֖ה\rb*!”
\p \v 22 “\rb Here|הִנֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb is the king’s|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb spear|הַחֲנִית\rb*,” \rb David|דָּוִד֙\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֔אמֶר\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּ֤עַן\rb*. “\rb Let one of|אֶחָ֥ד\rb* \rb the young men|מֵֽהַנְּעָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb come over|וְיַעֲבֹ֛ר\rb* \rb and get it|וְיִקָּחֶֽהָ׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb May the LORD|וַֽיהוָה֙\rb* \rb repay|יָשִׁ֣יב\rb* \rb every man|לָאִ֔ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb for his righteousness|צִדְקָת֖וֹ\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb faithfulness|אֱמֻנָת֑וֹ\rb*. \rb For|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה׀\rb* \rb delivered you|נְתָנְךָ֨\rb* \rb into my hand|בְּיָ֔ד\rb* \rb today|הַיּוֹם֙\rb*, \rb but|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb I would not|אָבִ֔יתִי\rb* \rb extend|לִשְׁלֹ֥חַ\rb* \rb my hand|יָדִ֖י\rb* \rb against the LORD’s|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb anointed|בִּמְשִׁ֥יחַ\rb*. \v 24 \rb As surely as|וְהִנֵּ֗ה\rb*\rb |כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I valued|בְּעֵינָ֑י\rb*\rb |גָּדְלָ֧ה\rb* \rb your life|נַפְשְׁךָ֛\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֖ה\rb*, \rb so|כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb may the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb value|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb*\rb |תִּגְדַּ֤ל\rb* \rb my life|נַפְשִׁי֙\rb* \rb and rescue me|וְיַצִּלֵ֖נִי\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb trouble|צָרָֽה׃פ\rb*.”
\p \v 25 \rb Saul|שָׁא֜וּל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb him|דָּוִ֗ד\rb*, “\rb May you|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb be blessed|בָּר֤וּךְ\rb*, \rb David|דָוִ֔ד\rb* \rb my son|בְּנִ֣י\rb*.\rb |גַּ֚ם\rb*\rb |תַעֲשֶׂ֔ה\rb* \rb You will accomplish great things|עָשֹׂ֣ה\rb* \rb and|וְגַ֖ם\rb* \rb will surely prevail|יָכֹ֣ל\rb*\rb |תּוּכָ֑ל\rb*.”
\p \rb So David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb on his way|לְדַרְכּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and Saul|וְשָׁא֖וּל\rb* \rb returned|שָׁ֥ב\rb* \rb home|לִמְקוֹמֽוֹ׃פ\rb*.
\c 27
\s1 David and the Philistines
\p \v 1 \rb David, however|דָּוִד֙\rb*, \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb himself|לִבּ֔וֹ\rb*, “\rb One|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb of these days|יוֹם־\rb* \rb now|עַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb I will be swept away|אֶסָּפֶ֥ה\rb* \rb by the hand|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֑וּל\rb*. \rb There is nothing|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb better|ט֜וֹב\rb* \rb for me|לִ֨י\rb* \rb than|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb to escape|הִמָּלֵ֥ט\rb*\rb |אִמָּלֵ֣ט׀\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֗ים\rb*. \rb Then Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb* \rb will stop|וְנוֹאַ֨שׁ\rb* \rb searching|לְבַקְשֵׁ֤נִי\rb* \rb for me|מִמֶּ֤נִּי\rb*\rb |עוֹד֙\rb* \rb all over|בְּכָל־\rb*\rb |גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb and I will slip|וְנִמְלַטְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb out of his hand|מִיָּדֽוֹ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 2 \rb So David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb set out|וַיָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb with|עִמּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb his six|וְשֵׁשׁ־\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֥וֹת\rb* \rb men|אִ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb and went|וַיַּעֲבֹ֣ר\rb*\rb |ה֔וּא\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Achish|אָכִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Maoch|מָע֖וֹךְ\rb*,\f + \fr 27:2 \fqa Maoch \ft is a variant of \fqa Maacah\ft ; see \ref 1 Kings 2:39|1KI 2:39\ref*.\f* \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Gath|גַּֽת׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb David|דָּוִ֨ד\rb* \rb and his men|וַאֲנָשָׁ֖יו\rb* \rb settled|וַיֵּשֶׁב֩\rb* \rb in Gath|בְּגַ֛ת\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb Achish|אָכִ֥ישׁ\rb*\rb |ה֥וּא\rb*. \rb Each man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb had his family with him|וּבֵית֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb had his two|וּשְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb wives|נָשָׁ֔יו\rb*: \rb Ahinoam|אֲחִינֹ֙עַם֙\rb* \rb of Jezreel|הַיִּזְרְעֵאלִ֔ית\rb* \rb and Abigail|וַאֲבִיגַ֥יִל\rb* \rb of Carmel|הַֽכַּרְמְלִֽית׃\rb*, \rb the widow|אֵֽשֶׁת־\rb* \rb of Nabal|נָבָ֖ל\rb*. \v 4 \rb And when Saul|לְשָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb learned|וַיֻּגַּ֣ד\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb had fled|בָרַ֥ח\rb* \rb to Gath|גַּ֑ת\rb*, \rb he no|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb longer|יוֹסַף\rb*\rb |ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb searched for him|לְבַקְשֽׁוֹ׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Then David|דָּוִ֜ד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Achish|אָכִ֗ישׁ\rb*, “\rb If|אִם־\rb*\rb |נָא֩\rb* \rb I have found|מָצָ֨אתִי\rb* \rb favor|חֵ֤ן\rb* \rb in your eyes|בְּעֵינֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*, \rb let me be assigned|יִתְּנוּ־\rb*\rb |לִ֣י\rb* \rb a place|מָק֗וֹם\rb* \rb in one|בְּאַחַ֛ת\rb* \rb of the outlying|הַשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb* \rb towns|עָרֵ֥י\rb*, \rb so I can live|וְאֵ֣שְׁבָה\rb* \rb there|שָּׁ֑ם\rb*. \rb For why|וְלָ֨מָּה\rb* \rb should your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֛\rb* \rb live|יֵשֵׁ֧ב\rb* \rb in the royal|הַמַּמְלָכָ֖ה\rb* \rb city|בְּעִ֥יר\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּֽךְ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 6 \rb That|הַה֖וּא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb Achish|אָכִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb him|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb Ziklag|צִֽקְלָ֑ג\rb*, \rb and|לָכֵ֞ן\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃פ\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb it|צִֽקְלַג֙\rb* \rb still belongs to|הָיְתָ֤ה\rb* \rb the kings|לְמַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*. \v 7 \rb And the time|הַיָּמִ֔ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb lived|יָשַׁ֥ב\rb* \rb in Philistine|פְלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb* \rb territory|בִּשְׂדֵ֣ה\rb* \rb amounted to|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb*\rb |מִסְפַּ֣ר\rb* \rb a year|יָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb and four|וְאַרְבָּעָ֥ה\rb* \rb months|חֳדָשִֽׁים׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb Now David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb and his men|וַֽאֲנָשָׁ֔יו\rb* \rb went up|וַיַּ֤עַל\rb* \rb and raided|וַֽיִּפְשְׁט֛וּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the Geshurites|הַגְּשׁוּרִ֥י\rb*, \rb the Girzites|וְהַגִּרְזִי\rb*, \rb and the Amalekites|וְהָעֲמָלֵקִ֑י\rb*. (\rb From|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb ancient times|מֵֽעוֹלָ֔ם\rb*\rb |בּוֹאֲךָ֥\rb* \rb these people|הֵ֜נָּה\rb* \rb had inhabited|יֹשְׁב֤וֹת\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb extending to Shur|שׁ֖וּרָה\rb* \rb and|וְעַד־\rb*\rb |אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*.) \v 9 \rb Whenever David|דָוִד֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb attacked|וְהִכָּ֤ה\rb* \rb a territory|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*, \rb he did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb leave|יְחַיֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb a man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb or woman alive|וְאִשָּׁ֑ה\rb*, \rb but he took|וְלָקַח֩\rb* \rb the flocks|צֹ֨אן\rb* \rb and herds|וּבָקָ֜ר\rb*, \rb the donkeys|וַחֲמֹרִ֤ים\rb*, \rb camels|וּגְמַלִּים֙\rb*, \rb and clothing|וּבְגָדִ֔ים\rb*.
\p \rb Then he would return|וַיָּ֖שָׁב\rb*\rb |וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Achish|אָכִֽישׁ׃\rb*, \v 10 \rb who|אָכִ֔ישׁ\rb*\rb |אַל־\rb* \rb would ask him|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb What have you raided today|פְּשַׁטְתֶּ֖ם\rb*\rb |הַיּ֑וֹם\rb*?”
\p \rb And David|דָּוִ֗ד\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb would reply|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb The Negev|נֶ֤גֶב\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb*,” \rb or|וְעַל־\rb* “\rb The Negev|נֶ֣גֶב\rb* \rb of Jerahmeel|הַיַּרְחְמְאֵלִ֔י\rb*,” \rb or|וְאֶל־\rb* “\rb The Negev|נֶ֖גֶב\rb* \rb of the Kenites|הַקֵּינִֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 11 \rb David|דָוִ֗ד\rb* \rb did not leave|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb a man|וְאִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb or woman|וְאִשָּׁ֜ה\rb* \rb alive|יְחַיֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb to be brought|לְהָבִ֥יא\rb* \rb to Gath|גַת֙\rb*, \rb for he said|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb Otherwise|פֶּן־\rb* \rb they will report|יַגִּ֥דוּ\rb* \rb us|עָלֵ֖ינוּ\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, ‘\rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb David|דָוִד֙\rb* \rb did|עָשָׂ֤ה\rb*.’” \rb And this|וְכֹ֣ה\rb* \rb was David’s custom|מִשְׁפָּט֔וֹ\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb time|הַ֨יָּמִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he lived|יָשַׁ֖ב\rb* \rb in Philistine|פְלִשְׁתִּֽים׃\rb* \rb territory|בִּשְׂדֵ֥ה\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb So Achish|אָכִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb trusted|וַיַּאֲמֵ֥ן\rb* \rb David|בְּדָוִ֣ד\rb*, \rb thinking|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Since he has made himself an utter stench|הַבְאֵ֤שׁ\rb*\rb |הִבְאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb to his people|בְּעַמּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb Israel|בְיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb he will be|וְהָ֥יָה\rb* \rb my|לִ֖י\rb* \rb servant|לְעֶ֥בֶד\rb* \rb forever|עוֹלָֽם׃פ\rb*.”
\c 28
\s1 The Philistines Gather against Israel
\p \v 1 \rb Now|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb in those|הָהֵ֔ם\rb* \rb days|בַּיָּמִ֣ים\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֤ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gathered|וַיִּקְבְּצ֨וּ\rb* \rb their forces|מַֽחֲנֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb for warfare|לַצָּבָ֔א\rb*\rb |לְהִלָּחֵ֖ם\rb* \rb against Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb So Achish|אָכִישׁ֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*, “\rb You must understand|יָדֹ֣עַ\rb*\rb |תֵּדַ֗ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb and your men|וַאֲנָשֶֽׁיךָ׃\rb* \rb are to go out|תֵּצֵ֣א\rb* \rb to battle|בַֽמַּחֲנֶ֔ה\rb* \rb with me|אִתִּי֙\rb*.”
\p \v 2 \rb David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |אָכִ֔ישׁ\rb*, “\rb Then|לָכֵן֙\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb will come to know|תֵדַ֔ע\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb your servant|עַבְדֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb can do|יַעֲשֶׂ֖ה\rb*.”
\p “\rb Very well|לָכֵ֗ן\rb*,” \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb Achish|אָכִישׁ֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |דָּוִ֔ד\rb*. “\rb I will make you|אֲשִֽׂימְךָ֖\rb* \rb my bodyguard|שֹׁמֵ֧ר\rb*\rb |לְרֹאשִׁ֛י\rb* \rb for life|הַיָּמִֽים׃פ\rb*.”
\p \v 3 \rb Now by this time Samuel|וּשְׁמוּאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb had died|מֵ֔ת\rb*, \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb had mourned|וַיִּסְפְּדוּ־\rb* \rb for him|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb and buried him|וַיִּקְבְּרֻ֥הוּ\rb* \rb in Ramah|בָרָמָ֖ה\rb*, \rb his own city|וּבְעִיר֑וֹ\rb*. \rb And Saul|וְשָׁא֗וּל\rb* \rb had removed|הֵסִ֛יר\rb* \rb the mediums|הָאֹב֥וֹת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and spiritists|הַיִּדְּעֹנִ֖ים\rb* \rb from the land|מֵהָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb The Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb*\rb |וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb gathered together|וַיִּקָּבְצ֣וּ\rb* \rb and camped|וַיַּחֲנ֣וּ\rb* \rb at Shunem|בְשׁוּנֵ֑ם\rb*, \rb while Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gathered|וַיִּקְבֹּ֤ץ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and camped|וַֽיַּחֲנ֖וּ\rb* \rb at Gilboa|בַּגִּלְבֹּֽעַ׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb When Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֥רְא\rb* \rb the Philistine|פְלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb* \rb army|מַחֲנֵ֣ה\rb*, \rb he|לִבּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb was afraid|וַיִּרָ֕א\rb* \rb and trembled|וַיֶּחֱרַ֥ד\rb* \rb violently|מְאֹֽד׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb He inquired|וַיִּשְׁאַ֤ל\rb*\rb |שָׁאוּל֙\rb* \rb of the LORD|בַּֽיהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb but the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb answer him|עָנָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb by dreams|בַּחֲלֹמ֛וֹת\rb* \rb or|גַּ֧ם\rb* \rb Urim|בָּאוּרִ֖ים\rb*\f + \fr 28:6 \ft Literally \fqa Lights\f*\rb |גַּ֥ם\rb* \rb or|גַּ֥ם\rb* \rb prophets|בַּנְּבִיאִֽם׃\rb*.
\s1 Saul and the Medium of Endor
\p \v 7 \rb Then Saul|שָׁא֜וּל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to his servants|לַעֲבָדָ֗יו\rb*, “\rb Find|בַּקְּשׁוּ־\rb* \rb me|לִי֙\rb* \rb a woman|אֵ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb who is|בַּעֲלַת־\rb* \rb a medium|א֔וֹב\rb*, \rb so I can go|וְאֵלְכָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb and consult|וְאֶדְרְשָׁה־\rb* \rb her|בָּ֑הּ\rb*.”
\p “\rb There is|הִנֵּ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֥שֶׁת\rb*\rb |בַּֽעֲלַת־\rb* \rb a medium|א֖וֹב\rb*\rb |בְּעֵ֥ין\rb* \rb at Endor|דּֽוֹר׃\rb*,” \rb his servants|עֲבָדָיו֙\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּאמְר֤וּ\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb So Saul|שָׁא֗וּל\rb* \rb disguised himself|וַיִּתְחַפֵּ֣שׂ\rb* \rb by putting on|וַיִּלְבַּשׁ֙\rb* \rb different|אֲחֵרִ֔ים\rb* \rb clothes|בְּגָדִ֣ים\rb*, \rb and he set out|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb*\rb |ה֗וּא\rb* \rb with|עִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb two|וּשְׁנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of his men|אֲנָשִׁים֙\rb*. \rb They came|וַיָּבֹ֥אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the woman|הָאִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb at night|לָ֑יְלָה\rb*, \rb and Saul said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Consult|קָסוֹמִי\rb*\rb |נָ֥א\rb* \rb a spirit|בָּא֔וֹב\rb* \rb for me|לִי֙\rb*. \rb Bring up|וְהַ֣עֲלִי\rb* \rb for me|לִ֔י\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb the one|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I name|אֹמַ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֵלָֽיִךְ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 9 \rb But the woman|הָֽאִשָּׁ֜ה\rb* \rb replied|וַתֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֗יו\rb*, “\rb Surely|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֙עְתָּ֙\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb has done|עָשָׂ֣ה\rb*, \rb how|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he has killed|הִכְרִ֛ית\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the mediums|הָאֹב֥וֹת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and spiritists|הַיִּדְּעֹנִ֖י\rb* \rb in|מִן־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*. \rb Why|וְלָמָ֥ה\rb* \rb have you|אַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb set a trap|מִתְנַקֵּ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |בְּנַפְשִׁ֖י\rb* \rb to get me killed|לַהֲמִיתֵֽנִי׃\rb*?”
\p \v 10 \rb Then Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb swore|וַיִּשָּׁ֤בַֽע\rb* \rb to her|לָהּ֙\rb* \rb by the LORD|בַּֽיהוָ֖ה\rb*:\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* “\rb As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֕ה\rb* \rb lives|חַי־\rb*, \rb no|אִֽם־\rb* \rb punishment|עָוֺ֖ן\rb* \rb shall come upon you|יִקְּרֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb for|בַּדָּבָ֥ר\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 11 “\rb Whom|מִ֖י\rb* \rb shall I bring up|אַֽעֲלֶה־\rb* \rb for you|לָּ֑ךְ\rb*?” \rb the woman|הָֽאִשָּׁ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb asked|וַתֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*.
\p “\rb Bring up|הַֽעֲלִי־\rb*\rb |לִֽי׃\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֖ל\rb*,” \rb he replied|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb But when the woman|הָֽאִשָּׁה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb saw|וַתֵּ֤רֶא\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb she cried out|וַתִּזְעַ֖ק\rb* \rb in a loud|גָּד֑וֹל\rb* \rb voice|בְּק֣וֹל\rb* \rb and|הָאִשָּׁ֨ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb to Saul|שָׁא֧וּל\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֛ר\rb*, “\rb Why|לָ֥מָּה\rb* \rb have you deceived me|רִמִּיתָ֖נִי\rb*? \rb You|וְאַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb are Saul|שָׁאֽוּל׃\rb*!”
\p \v 13 “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּֽירְאִ֖י\rb*,” \rb the king|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |לָ֥הּ\rb*. “\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb What|מָ֣ה\rb* \rb do you see|רָאִ֑ית\rb*?”
\p “\rb I see|רָאִ֖יתִי\rb* \rb a god|אֱלֹהִ֥ים\rb*\f + \fr 28:13 \ft Or \fqa I see a spirit \ft or \fqa I see a divine being\f* \rb coming up|עֹלִ֥ים\rb* \rb out of|מִן־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*,” \rb the woman|הָֽאִשָּׁה֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb answered|וַתֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*.
\p \v 14 “\rb What|מַֽה־\rb* \rb does he look like?|תָּאֳר֔וֹ\rb*” \rb asked Saul|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*.
\p “\rb An old|זָקֵן֙\rb* \rb man|אִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb is coming up|עֹלֶ֔ה\rb*,” \rb she replied|וַתֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*. “\rb And he is|וְה֥וּא\rb* \rb wearing|עֹטֶ֖ה\rb* \rb a robe|מְעִ֑יל\rb*.”
\p \rb So Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb* \rb knew|וַיֵּ֤דַע\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb it|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb was Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֣ל\rb*, \rb and he bowed|וַיִּקֹּ֥ד\rb* \rb facedown|אַפַּ֛יִם\rb*\rb |אַ֖רְצָה\rb* \rb in reverence|וַיִּשְׁתָּֽחוּ׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Then Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵל֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb*, “\rb Why|לָ֥מָּה\rb* \rb have you disturbed me|הִרְגַּזְתַּ֖נִי\rb* \rb by bringing me up|לְהַעֲל֣וֹת\rb*\rb |אֹתִ֑י\rb*?”
\p “\rb I am|לִ֨י\rb* \rb deeply|מְאֹ֜ד\rb* \rb distressed|צַר־\rb*,” \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁ֠אוּל\rb*. “\rb The Philistines|וּפְלִשְׁתִּ֣ים׀\rb* \rb are fighting|נִלְחָמִ֣ים\rb* \rb against me|בִּ֗י\rb*, \rb and God|וֵֽאלֹהִ֞ים\rb* \rb has turned away|סָ֤ר\rb* \rb from me|מֵֽעָלַי֙\rb*. \rb He no|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֗וֹד\rb* \rb answers me|עָנָ֣נִי\rb*, \rb either|גַּ֤ם\rb* \rb by|בְּיַֽד־\rb* \rb prophets|הַנְּבִיאִם֙\rb* \rb or|גַּם־\rb* \rb by dreams|בַּ֣חֲלֹמ֔וֹת\rb*. \rb So I have called|וָאֶקְרָאֶ֣ה\rb* \rb on you|לְךָ֔\rb* \rb to tell me|לְהוֹדִיעֵ֖נִי\rb* \rb what|מָ֥ה\rb* \rb to do|אֶעֱשֶֽׂה׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 16 “\rb Why|וְלָ֖מָּה\rb* \rb do you consult me|תִּשְׁאָלֵ֑נִי\rb*,” \rb asked|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֔ל\rb*, “\rb since the LORD|וַיהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb has turned away|סָ֥ר\rb* \rb from you|מֵעָלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb and become|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb your enemy|עָרֶֽךָ׃\rb*? \v 17 \rb He|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb has done|וַיַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb exactly what|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb He spoke|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb through me|בְּיָדִ֑י\rb*: \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has torn|וַיִּקְרַ֨ע\rb* \rb the kingdom|הַמַּמְלָכָה֙\rb* \rb out of your hand|מִיָּדֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb and given it|וַֽיִּתְּנָ֖הּ\rb* \rb to your neighbor|לְרֵעֲךָ֥\rb* \rb David|לְדָוִֽד׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb Because|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb you did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb obey|שָׁמַ֙עְתָּ֙\rb*\rb |בְּק֣וֹל\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb or|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb carry out|עָשִׂ֥יתָ\rb* \rb His burning|חֲרוֹן־\rb* \rb anger|אַפּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb against Amalek|בַּעֲמָלֵ֑ק\rb*,\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּן֙\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has done|עָשָֽׂה־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֥\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּֽה׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb Moreover|גַּ֣ם\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְ֠הוָה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will deliver|וְיִתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֤ל\rb* \rb with you|עִמְּךָ֙\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb and tomorrow|וּמָחָ֕ר\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb and your sons|וּבָנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb will be with me|עִמִּ֑י\rb*. \rb And|גַּ֚ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb will deliver|יִתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb the army|מַחֲנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּֽים׃\rb*.”
\p \v 20 \rb Immediately|וַיְמַהֵ֣ר\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֗וּל\rb* \rb fell|וַיִּפֹּ֤ל\rb* \rb flat|מְלֹא־\rb*\rb |קֽוֹמָתוֹ֙\rb* \rb on the ground|אַ֔רְצָה\rb*, \rb terrified|וַיִּרָ֥א\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֖ד\rb* \rb by the words|מִדִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Samuel|שְׁמוּאֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb And|גַּם־\rb* \rb his strength|כֹּ֙חַ֙\rb*\rb |ב֔וֹ\rb* \rb was|הָ֣יָה\rb* \rb gone|לֹא־\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he had not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb eaten|אָכַל֙\rb* \rb anything|לֶ֔חֶם\rb* \rb all that|כָּל־\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֖וֹם\rb* \rb and|וְכָל־\rb* \rb night|הַלָּֽיְלָה׃\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb When the woman|הָֽאִשָּׁה֙\rb* \rb came|וַתָּב֤וֹא\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb* \rb and saw|וַתֵּ֖רֶא\rb* \rb how|כִּי־\rb* \rb distraught he was|נִבְהַ֣ל\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֑ד\rb*, \rb she said|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֗יו\rb*, “\rb Look|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb*, \rb your maidservant|שִׁפְחָֽתְךָ֙\rb* \rb has obeyed|שָׁמְעָ֤ה\rb* \rb your voice|בְּקוֹלֶ֔ךָ\rb*. \rb I took|וָאָשִׂ֤ים\rb* \rb my life|נַפְשִׁי֙\rb* \rb in my hands|בְּכַפִּ֔י\rb* \rb and did|וָֽאֶשְׁמַע֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |דְּבָרֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb as|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you told|דִּבַּ֖רְתָּ\rb* \rb me|אֵלָֽי׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb please|נָ֤א\rb*\rb |גַם־\rb*\rb |אַתָּה֙\rb*\rb |בְּק֣וֹל\rb* \rb listen|שְׁמַֽע־\rb* \rb to your servant|שִׁפְחָתֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb and let me set|וְאָשִׂ֧מָה\rb* \rb a morsel|פַּת־\rb* \rb of bread|לֶ֖חֶם\rb* \rb before you|לְפָנֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb so you may eat|וֶאֱכ֑וֹל\rb* \rb and have|וִיהִ֤י\rb*\rb |בְךָ֙\rb* \rb the strength|כֹּ֔חַ\rb* \rb to|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb go|תֵלֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb on your way|בַּדָּֽרֶךְ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 23 \rb Saul refused|וַיְמָאֵ֗ן\rb*, \rb saying|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb I will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb eat|אֹכַ֔ל\rb*.” \rb But his servants|עֲבָדָיו֙\rb* \rb joined|וְגַם־\rb* \rb the woman|הָ֣אִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb in urging|וַיִּפְרְצוּ־\rb* \rb him|ב֤וֹ\rb*, \rb and he heeded|וַיִּשְׁמַ֖ע\rb* \rb their voice|לְקֹלָ֑ם\rb*. \rb He got up|וַיָּ֙קָם֙\rb* \rb from the ground|מֵֽהָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb and sat|וַיֵּ֖שֶׁב\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the bed|הַמִּטָּֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb The woman|וְלָאִשָּׁ֤ה\rb* \rb had a fattened|מַרְבֵּק֙\rb* \rb calf|עֵֽגֶל־\rb* \rb at her house|בַּבַּ֔יִת\rb*, \rb and she quickly|וַתְּמַהֵ֖ר\rb* \rb slaughtered it|וַתִּזְבָּחֵ֑הוּ\rb*. \rb She also took|וַתִּקַּח־\rb* \rb flour|קֶ֣מַח\rb*, \rb kneaded it|וַתָּ֔לָשׁ\rb*, \rb and baked|וַתֹּפֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb unleavened bread|מַצּֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb She served|וַתַּגֵּ֧שׁ\rb* \rb it to|לִפְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֛וּל\rb*\rb |וְלִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb and his servants|עֲבָדָ֖יו\rb*, \rb and they ate|וַיֹּאכֵ֑לוּ\rb*. \rb And that|הַהֽוּא׃פ\rb* \rb night|בַּלַּ֥יְלָה\rb* \rb they got up|וַיָּקֻ֥מוּ\rb* \rb and left|וַיֵּלְכ֖וּ\rb*.
\c 29
\s1 The Philistines Reject David
\p \v 1 \rb Now the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֛ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb brought all|כָּל־\rb* \rb their forces|מַחֲנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb together|וַיִּקְבְּצ֧וּ\rb* \rb at Aphek|אֲפֵ֑קָה\rb*, \rb while Israel|וְיִשְׂרָאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb camped|חֹנִ֔ים\rb* \rb by the spring|בַּעַ֖יִן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb in Jezreel|בְּיִזְרְעֶֽאל׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb As the Philistine|פְלִשְׁתִּים֙\rb* \rb leaders|וְסַרְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb marched out with|עֹֽבְרִ֔ים\rb* \rb their units of hundreds|לְמֵא֖וֹת\rb* \rb and thousands|וְלַאֲלָפִ֑ים\rb*, \rb David|וְדָוִ֣ד\rb* \rb and his men|וַאֲנָשָׁ֗יו\rb* \rb marched|עֹֽבְרִ֛ים\rb* \rb behind them|בָּאַחֲרֹנָ֖ה\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb Achish|אָכִֽישׁ׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Then the commanders|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּֽאמְרוּ֙\rb*, “\rb What about|מָ֖ה\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb Hebrews|הָעִבְרִ֣ים\rb*?”
\p \rb Achish|אָכִ֜ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |פְלִשְׁתִּ֗ים\rb*\rb |שָׂרֵ֣י\rb*, “\rb Is this|זֶ֨ה\rb* \rb not|הֲלֽוֹא־\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֜ד\rb*, \rb the servant|עֶ֣בֶד׀\rb* \rb of King|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֣וּל\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*? \rb He|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb has been|הָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb with me|אִתִּי֙\rb* \rb all these|זֶ֤ה\rb* \rb days|יָמִים֙\rb*, \rb even|אוֹ־\rb*\rb |זֶ֣ה\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֔ים\rb*, \rb and from|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb the day|מִיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb he defected|נָפְל֖וֹ\rb* \rb until today|עַד־\rb*\rb |הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּֽה׃פ\rb* \rb I have found|מָצָ֤אתִי\rb* \rb no fault|מְא֔וּמָה\rb* \rb in him|בוֹ֙\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb But the commanders|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֗ים\rb* \rb were angry|וַיִּקְצְפ֨וּ\rb* \rb with Achish|עָלָ֜יו\rb* \rb and told|וַיֹּ֣אמְרוּ\rb* \rb him|לוֹ֩\rb*\rb |שָׂרֵ֨י\rb*\rb |פְלִשְׁתִּ֜ים\rb*, “\rb Send that man|הָאִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb back|הָשֵׁ֣ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and let him return|וְיָשֹׁב֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the place|מְקוֹמוֹ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you assigned|הִפְקַדְתּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb him|שָׁ֔ם\rb*. \rb He must not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb go down|יֵרֵ֤ד\rb* \rb with us|עִמָּ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb into battle|בַּמִּלְחָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb only|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb to become|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb our|לָּ֥נוּ\rb* \rb adversary|לְשָׂטָ֖ן\rb* \rb during the war|בַּמִּלְחָמָ֑ה\rb*. \rb What better way|וּבַמֶּ֗ה\rb* \rb for him to regain the favor|יִתְרַצֶּ֥ה\rb*\rb |זֶה֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb of his master|אֲדֹנָ֔יו\rb* \rb than|הֲל֕וֹא\rb* \rb with the heads|בְּרָאשֵׁ֖י\rb* \rb of our men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |הָהֵֽם׃\rb*? \v 5 \rb Is this|זֶ֣ה\rb* \rb not|הֲלוֹא־\rb* \rb the David|דָוִ֔ד\rb* \rb about whom|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb they sing|יַעֲנוּ־\rb*\rb |ל֛וֹ\rb* \rb in their dances|בַּמְּחֹל֖וֹת\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 ‘\rb Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb* \rb has slain|הִכָּ֤ה\rb* \rb his thousands|בַּֽאֲלָפָ֔יו\rb*,
\q2 \rb and David|וְדָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb his tens of thousands|בְּרִבְבֹתוֹ׃ס\rb*’?”
\p \v 6 \rb So Achish|אָכִ֜ישׁ\rb* \rb summoned|וַיִּקְרָ֨א\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֗ד\rb* \rb and told him|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*,\rb |אֵ֠לָיו\rb* “\rb As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֞ה\rb*\rb |כִּי־\rb* \rb lives|חַי־\rb*, \rb you|אַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb have been upright|יָשָׁ֣ר\rb*, \rb and it seems right|וְט֣וֹב\rb* \rb in my sight|בְּ֠עֵינַי\rb* \rb that you should march in and out|צֵאתְךָ֨\rb*\rb |וּבֹאֲךָ֤\rb* \rb with me|אִתִּי֙\rb* \rb in the army|בַּֽמַּחֲנֶ֔ה\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb I have found|מָצָ֤אתִֽי\rb* \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb fault|רָעָ֔ה\rb* \rb in you|בְךָ֙\rb* \rb from the day|מִיּ֛וֹם\rb* \rb you came|בֹּאֲךָ֥\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֖י\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*. \rb But you|אָֽתָּה׃\rb* \rb are not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb good|ט֥וֹב\rb* \rb in the sight|וּבְעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the leaders|הַסְּרָנִ֖ים\rb*. \v 7 \rb Therefore turn back|שׁ֖וּב\rb* \rb now|וְעַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb and go|וְלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb in peace|בְּשָׁל֑וֹם\rb*, \rb so that you will not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb do anything|תַעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb to displease|בְּעֵינֵ֖י\rb*\rb |רָ֔ע\rb* \rb the leaders|סַרְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּֽים׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 8 “\rb But|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb what|מֶ֤ה\rb* \rb have I done|עָשִׂ֙יתִי֙\rb*?” \rb David|דָּוִ֜ד\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |אָכִ֗ישׁ\rb*. “\rb What|וּמַה־\rb* \rb have you found|מָּצָ֣אתָ\rb* \rb against your servant|בְעַבְדְּךָ֔\rb*, \rb from the day|מִיּוֹם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I came|הָיִ֣יתִי\rb* \rb to you|לְפָנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb until today|עַ֖ד\rb*,\rb |הַיּ֣וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb to|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb keep me from|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb going along|אָבוֹא֙\rb* \rb to fight|וְנִלְחַ֔מְתִּי\rb* \rb against the enemies|בְּאֹיְבֵ֖י\rb* \rb of my lord|אֲדֹנִ֥י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 9 \rb Achish|אָכִישׁ֮\rb* \rb replied|וַיַּ֣עַן\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |דָּוִד֒\rb*, “\rb I know|יָדַ֕עְתִּי\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you are|אַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb as pleasing|ט֥וֹב\rb* \rb in my sight|בְּעֵינַ֖י\rb* \rb as an angel|כְּמַלְאַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*. \rb But|אַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb the commanders|שָׂרֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּים֙\rb* \rb have said|אָֽמְר֔וּ\rb*, ‘\rb He must not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb go|יַעֲלֶ֥ה\rb* \rb into battle|בַּמִּלְחָמָֽה׃\rb* \rb with us|עִמָּ֖נוּ\rb*.’ \v 10 \rb Now then|וְעַתָּה֙\rb*, \rb get up early|הַשְׁכֵּ֣ם\rb* \rb in the morning|בַּבֹּ֔קֶר\rb*, \rb along with your master’s|אֲדֹנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb servants|וְעַבְדֵ֥י\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb came|בָּ֣אוּ\rb* \rb with you|אִתָּ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb and go|וָלֵֽכוּ׃\rb* \rb as soon as|וְהִשְׁכַּמְתֶּ֣ם\rb*\rb |בַּבֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb it is light|וְא֥וֹר\rb*.”
\p \v 11 \rb So David|דָּוִ֜ד\rb*\rb |ה֤וּא\rb* \rb and his men|וַֽאֲנָשָׁיו֙\rb*\rb |לָלֶ֣כֶת\rb* \rb got up early|וַיַּשְׁכֵּ֨ם\rb* \rb in the morning|בַּבֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb to return|לָשׁ֖וּב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb*. \rb And the Philistines|וּפְלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb went up|עָל֥וּ\rb* \rb to Jezreel|יִזְרְעֶֽאל׃ס\rb*.
\c 30
\s1 The Amalekites Raid Ziklag
\p \v 1 \rb On the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֑י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*\rb |וַיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֧ד\rb* \rb and his men|וַאֲנָשָׁ֛יו\rb* \rb arrived|בְּבֹ֨א\rb* \rb in Ziklag|צִֽקְלַ֖ג\rb*, \rb and the Amalekites|וַעֲמָלֵקִ֣י\rb* \rb had raided|פָֽשְׁט֗וּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the Negev|נֶ֙גֶב֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb*\rb |צִ֣קְלַ֔ג\rb*, \rb attacked|וַיַּכּוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Ziklag|צִ֣קְלַ֔ג\rb*, \rb and burned it down|וַיִּשְׂרְפ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖הּ\rb*\rb |בָּאֵֽשׁ׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb They had taken captive|וַיִּשְׁבּ֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the women and all|הַנָּשִׁ֤ים\rb*\f + \fr 30:2 \ft LXX; Hebrew does not include \fqa and all\ft .\f* \rb who were|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb there|בָּהּ֙\rb*, \rb both young|מִקָּטֹ֣ן\rb* \rb and|וְעַד־\rb* \rb old|גָּד֔וֹל\rb*. \rb They had not killed|הֵמִ֖יתוּ\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb anyone|אִ֑ישׁ\rb*, \rb but had carried them off|וַיִּֽנְהֲג֔וּ\rb* \rb as they went|וַיֵּלְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb on their way|לְדַרְכָּֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb When David|דָוִ֤ד\rb* \rb and his men|וַֽאֲנָשָׁיו֙\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֨א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb*, \rb they found|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb it burned down|שְׂרוּפָ֖ה\rb*\rb |בָּאֵ֑שׁ\rb* \rb and their wives|וּנְשֵׁיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb and sons|וּבְנֵיהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבְנֹתֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb taken captive|נִשְׁבּֽוּ׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb So David|דָוִ֜ד\rb* \rb and the troops|וְהָעָ֧ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֛וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb lifted up|וַיִּשָּׂ֨א\rb* \rb their voices|קוֹלָ֖ם\rb* \rb and wept|וַיִּבְכּ֑וּ\rb* \rb until|עַ֣ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb they had no|אֵין־\rb*\rb |בָּהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb strength|כֹּ֖חַ\rb* \rb left to weep|לִבְכּֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb David’s|דָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb two|וּשְׁתֵּ֥י\rb* \rb wives|נְשֵֽׁי־\rb*, \rb Ahinoam|אֲחִינֹ֙עַם֙\rb* \rb of Jezreel|הַיִּזְרְעֵלִ֔ית\rb* \rb and Abigail|וַאֲבִיגַ֕יִל\rb* \rb the widow|אֵ֖שֶׁת\rb* \rb of Nabal|נָבָ֥ל\rb* \rb of Carmel|הַֽכַּרְמְלִֽי׃\rb*, \rb had been taken captive|נִשְׁבּ֑וּ\rb*. \v 6 \rb And David|לְדָוִ֜ד\rb* \rb was greatly|מְאֹ֗ד\rb* \rb distressed|וַתֵּ֨צֶר\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb spoke|אָמְר֤וּ\rb* \rb of stoning him|לְסָקְל֔וֹ\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the soul|נֶ֣פֶשׁ\rb* \rb of every man|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb grieved|מָ֙רָה֙\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb*\rb |הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb his sons|בְּנוֹ\rb* \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb daughters|בְּנֹתָ֑יו\rb*. \rb But David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb found strength|וַיִּתְחַזֵּ֣ק\rb* \rb in the LORD|בַּיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb his God|אֱלֹהָֽיו׃ס\rb*.
\s1 David Destroys the Amalekites
\p \v 7 \rb Then David|דָּוִ֗ד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Abiathar|אֶבְיָתָ֤ר\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵן֙\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahimelech|אֲחִימֶ֔לֶךְ\rb*, “\rb Bring|הַגִּֽישָׁה־\rb*\rb |נָּ֥א\rb* \rb me|לִ֖י\rb* \rb the ephod|הָאֵפֹ֑ד\rb*.”
\p \rb So Abiathar|אֶבְיָתָ֛ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb brought|וַיַּגֵּ֧שׁ\rb* \rb it|הָאֵפֹ֖ד\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb him|דָּוִֽד׃\rb*, \v 8 \rb and David|דָּוִ֤ד\rb* \rb inquired|וַיִּשְׁאַ֨ל\rb* \rb of the LORD|בַּֽיהוָה֙\rb*: “\rb Should I pursue|אֶרְדֹּ֛ף\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb these|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb raiders|הַגְּדוּד־\rb*? \rb Will I overtake them|הַֽאַשִּׂגֶ֑נּוּ\rb*?”
\p “\rb Pursue them|רְדֹ֔ף\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb*,” \rb the LORD replied|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*, “\rb for you will surely overtake them|הַשֵּׂ֥ג\rb*\rb |תַּשִּׂ֖יג\rb* \rb and rescue the captives|וְהַצֵּ֥ל\rb*\rb |תַּצִּֽיל׃\rb*.”
\p \v 9 \rb So|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֗ד\rb*\rb |ה֚וּא\rb* \rb and his six|וְשֵׁשׁ־\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֥וֹת\rb* \rb men|אִישׁ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |אִתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the Brook|נַ֣חַל\rb* \rb of Besor|הַבְּשׂ֑וֹר\rb*, \rb where some stayed behind|וְהַנּֽוֹתָרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |עָמָֽדוּ׃\rb* \v 10 \rb because|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |וַיַּֽעַמְדוּ֙\rb* \rb two hundred|מָאתַ֣יִם\rb* \rb men|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb were too exhausted|פִּגְּר֔וּ\rb* \rb to cross|מֵעֲבֹ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the brook|נַ֥חַל\rb*\rb |הַבְּשֽׂוֹר׃\rb*. \rb But David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*\rb |ה֖וּא\rb* \rb and four|וְאַרְבַּע־\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֣וֹת\rb* \rb men|אִ֑ישׁ\rb* \rb continued in pursuit|וַיִּרְדֹּ֣ף\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb Now his men found|וַֽיִּמְצְא֤וּ\rb*\rb |אִישׁ־\rb* \rb an Egyptian|מִצְרִי֙\rb* \rb in the field|בַּשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb* \rb and brought|וַיִּקְח֥וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*. \rb They gave|וַיִּתְּנוּ־\rb* \rb the man|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb water|מָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb to drink|וַיַּשְׁקֻ֖הוּ\rb* \rb and food|לֶ֙חֶם֙\rb* \rb to eat|וַיֹּ֔אכַל\rb* — \v 12 \rb |וַיִּתְּנוּ־\rb*\rb |לוֹ֩\rb* \rb a piece|פֶ֨לַח\rb* \rb of a fig cake|דְּבֵלָ֜ה\rb* \rb and two|וּשְׁנֵ֤י\rb* \rb clusters of raisins|צִמֻּקִים֙\rb*. \rb So he ate|וַיֹּ֔אכַל\rb* \rb and was revived|וַתָּ֥שָׁב\rb*\rb |רוּח֖וֹ\rb*,\rb |אֵלָ֑יו\rb* \rb for|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb he had not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb had any|אָ֤כַל\rb* \rb food|לֶ֙חֶם֙\rb*\rb |וְלֹא־\rb* \rb or|שָׁ֣תָה\rb* \rb water|מַ֔יִם\rb* \rb for three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֥ה\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb and three|וּשְׁלֹשָׁ֥ה\rb* \rb nights|לֵילֽוֹת׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb Then David|דָוִד֙\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb him|ל֤וֹ\rb*, “\rb To whom|לְֽמִי־\rb* \rb do you belong|אַ֔תָּה\rb*, \rb and where|וְאֵ֥י\rb*\rb |מִזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb are you from|אָ֑תָּה\rb*?”
\p “\rb I am|אָנֹ֗כִי\rb* \rb an Egyptian|מִצְרִ֣י\rb*,” \rb he replied|וַיֹּ֜אמֶר\rb*\rb |נַ֧עַר\rb*, “\rb the slave|עֶ֚בֶד\rb* \rb of an Amalekite|עֲמָֽלֵקִ֔י\rb*\rb |לְאִ֣ישׁ\rb*. \rb My master|אֲדֹנִ֛י\rb* \rb abandoned me|וַיַּעַזְבֵ֧נִי\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹשָֽׁה׃\rb* \rb days ago|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb when|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I fell ill|חָלִ֖יתִי\rb*. \v 14 \rb We|אֲנַ֡חְנוּ\rb* \rb raided|פָּשַׁ֜טְנוּ\rb* \rb the Negev|נֶ֧גֶב\rb* \rb of the Cherethites|הַכְּרֵתִ֛י\rb*,\rb |וְעַל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the territory of Judah|לִֽיהוּדָ֖ה\rb*,\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and the Negev|נֶ֣גֶב\rb* \rb of Caleb|כָּלֵ֑ב\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and we burned down|שָׂרַ֥פְנוּ\rb*\rb |בָאֵֽשׁ׃\rb* \rb Ziklag|צִקְלַ֖ג\rb*.”
\p \v 15 “\rb Will you lead me|הֲתוֹרִדֵ֖נִי\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb these|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb raiders|הַגְּד֣וּד\rb*?” \rb David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*.
\p \rb And the man replied|וַיֹּ֡אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Swear|הִשָּׁבְעָה֩\rb* \rb to me|לִּ֨י\rb* \rb by God|בֵֽאלֹהִ֜ים\rb* \rb that you will not|אִם־\rb* \rb kill me|תְּמִיתֵ֗נִי\rb* \rb or|וְאִם־\rb* \rb deliver me|תַּסְגִּרֵ֙נִי֙\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of my master|אֲדֹנִ֔י\rb*, \rb and I will lead you|וְאוֹרִֽדְךָ֖\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb them|הַגְּד֥וּד\rb*\rb |הַזֶּֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 16 \rb So he led David down|וַיֹּ֣רִדֵ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb and there were the Amalekites|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb spread out|נְטֻשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb eating|אֹכְלִ֤ים\rb*, \rb drinking|וְשֹׁתִים֙\rb*, \rb and celebrating|וְחֹ֣גְגִ֔ים\rb*\rb |בְּכֹל֙\rb* \rb the great|הַגָּד֔וֹל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb amount of plunder|הַשָּׁלָ֣ל\rb* \rb they had taken|לָקְח֛וּ\rb* \rb from the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb and the land|וּמֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb And David|דָּוִ֛ד\rb* \rb struck them down|וַיַּכֵּ֥ם\rb* \rb from twilight|מֵהַנֶּ֥שֶׁף\rb* \rb until|וְעַד־\rb* \rb the evening|הָעֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb of the next day|לְמָֽחֳרָתָ֑ם\rb*. \rb Not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb escaped|נִמְלַ֤ט\rb*,\rb |מֵהֶם֙\rb* \rb except|כִּי֩\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb four|אַרְבַּ֨ע\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֧וֹת\rb* \rb young|נַ֛עַר\rb* \rb men|אִֽישׁ־\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb fled|וַיָּנֻֽסוּ׃\rb*, \rb riding off|רָכְב֥וּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb camels|הַגְּמַלִּ֖ים\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb So David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb recovered|וַיַּצֵּ֣ל\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the Amalekites|עֲמָלֵ֑ק\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb had taken|לָקְח֖וּ\rb*, \rb including|דָּוִֽד׃\rb*\rb |הִצִּ֥יל\rb* \rb his two|שְׁתֵּ֥י\rb* \rb wives|נָשָׁ֖יו\rb*. \v 19 \rb Nothing|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb was missing|נֶעְדַּר־\rb*\rb |לָ֠הֶם\rb*,\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb young|הַקָּטֹ֨ן\rb* \rb or|וְעַד־\rb* \rb old|הַגָּד֜וֹל\rb*,\rb |וְעַד־\rb* \rb son|בָּנִ֤ים\rb* \rb or daughter|וּבָנוֹת֙\rb*, \rb or any|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb of the plunder|וּמִשָּׁלָ֔ל\rb*\rb |וְעַ֛ד\rb* \rb the Amalekites had taken|לָקְח֖וּ\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb David|דָּוִֽד׃\rb* \rb brought everything|הַכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb back|הֵשִׁ֥יב\rb*. \v 20 \rb And he|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the flocks|הַצֹּ֖אן\rb* \rb and herds|וְהַבָּקָ֑ר\rb*, \rb which his men drove|נָהֲג֗וּ\rb* \rb ahead of|לִפְנֵי֙\rb* \rb the other livestock|הַמִּקְנֶ֣ה\rb*,\rb |הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb calling out|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb*, “\rb This|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb is David’s|דָּוִֽד׃\rb* \rb plunder|שְׁלַ֥ל\rb*!”
\s1 The Spoils Are Divided
\p \v 21 \rb When David|דָוִ֗ד\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the two hundred|מָאתַ֨יִם\rb* \rb men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֜ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb had been too exhausted|פִּגְּר֣וּ׀\rb* \rb to follow|מִלֶּ֣כֶת׀\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb him|דָוִ֗ד\rb* \rb and who were left behind|וַיֹּֽשִׁיבֻם֙\rb* \rb at the Brook|בְּנַ֣חַל\rb* \rb of Besor|הַבְּשׂ֔וֹר\rb*, \rb they came out|וַיֵּֽצְאוּ֙\rb* \rb to meet|לִקְרַ֣את\rb* \rb him|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb and|וְלִקְרַ֖את\rb* \rb the troops|הָעָ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֑וֹ\rb*. \rb As David|דָּוִד֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb approached|וַיִּגַּ֤שׁ\rb* \rb the men|הָעָ֔ם\rb*, \rb he greeted them|וַיִּשְׁאַ֥ל\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |לְשָׁלֽוֹם׃ס\rb*, \v 22 \rb but|וַיַּ֜עַן\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the wicked|רָ֣ע\rb* \rb and worthless|וּבְלִיַּ֗עַל\rb* \rb men|אִֽישׁ־\rb* \rb among those|מֵֽהָאֲנָשִׁים֮\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb had gone|הָלְכ֣וּ\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִד֒\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמְר֗וּ\rb*, “\rb Because|יַ֚עַן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb go|הָלְכ֣וּ\rb* \rb with us|עִמִּ֔י\rb*, \rb we will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb share with them|נִתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb the plunder|מֵהַשָּׁלָ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb we recovered|הִצַּ֑לְנוּ\rb*, \rb except|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb for each|אִ֤ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb man’s wife|אִשְׁתּוֹ֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and children|בָּנָ֔יו\rb*. \rb They may take them|וְיִנְהֲג֖וּ\rb* \rb and go|וְיֵלֵֽכוּ׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 23 \rb But David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb My brothers|אֶחָ֑י\rb*,\rb |אֵ֠ת\rb* \rb you must not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb do|תַעֲשׂ֥וּ\rb* \rb this|כֵ֖ן\rb* \rb with what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb has given|נָתַ֨ן\rb* \rb us|לָ֙נוּ֙\rb*. \rb He has protected|וַיִּשְׁמֹ֣ר\rb* \rb us|אֹתָ֔נוּ\rb* \rb and delivered|וַיִּתֵּ֗ן\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb into our hands|בְּיָדֵֽנוּ׃\rb* \rb the raiders|הַגְּד֛וּד\rb* \rb who came|הַבָּ֥א\rb* \rb against us|עָלֵ֖ינוּ\rb*. \v 24 \rb Who|וּמִי֙\rb* \rb will listen|יִשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb to your|לָכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb proposal|לַדָּבָ֖ר\rb*?\rb |הַזֶּ֑ה\rb*\rb |כִּ֞י\rb* \rb The share|כְּחֵ֣לֶק׀\rb* \rb of the one who went|הַיֹּרֵ֣ד\rb* \rb to battle|בַּמִּלְחָמָ֗ה\rb* \rb will match the share|וּֽכְחֵ֛לֶק\rb* \rb of the one who stayed|הַיֹּשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb the supplies|הַכֵּלִ֖ים\rb*. \rb They will share|יַחֲלֹֽקוּ׃ס\rb* \rb alike|יַחְדָּ֥ו\rb*.”
\p \v 25 \rb And so it has been|וַיְהִ֕י\rb* \rb from that|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb day|מֵֽהַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb forward|וָמָ֑עְלָה\rb*. \rb David established this|וַיְשִׂמֶ֜הָ\rb* \rb statute|לְחֹ֤ק\rb* \rb and ordinance|וּלְמִשְׁפָּט֙\rb* \rb for Israel|לְיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this very|הַזֶּֽה׃פ\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb When David|דָוִד֙\rb* \rb arrived|וַיָּבֹ֤א\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ziklag|צִ֣קְלַ֔ג\rb*, \rb he sent|וַיְשַׁלַּ֧ח\rb* \rb some of the plunder|מֵֽהַשָּׁלָ֛ל\rb* \rb to his friends|לְרֵעֵ֣הוּ\rb*, \rb the elders|לְזִקְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Here|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb is a gift|בְּרָכָ֔ה\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶם֙\rb* \rb from the plunder|מִשְּׁלַ֖ל\rb* \rb of the LORD’s|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb enemies|אֹיְבֵ֥י\rb*.” \v 27 \rb He sent gifts to those|לַאֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb*\rb |בְּבֵֽית־\rb* \rb in Bethel|אֵ֛ל\rb*,\rb |וְלַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Ramoth|בְּרָמֽוֹת־\rb* \rb Negev|נֶ֖גֶב\rb*,\rb |וְלַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb and Jattir|בְּיַתִּֽר׃\rb*; \v 28 \rb to those|וְלַאֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb in Aroer|בַּעֲרֹעֵ֛ר\rb*,\rb |וְלַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Siphmoth|בְּשִֽׂפְמ֖וֹת\rb*,\rb |וְלַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb and Eshtemoa|בְּאֶשְׁתְּמֹֽעַ׃ס\rb*; \v 29 \rb to those|וְלַאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in Racal|בְּרָכָ֗ל\rb* \rb and|וְלַֽאֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb in the cities|בְּעָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Jerahmeelites|הַיְּרַחְמְאֵלִ֔י\rb*\rb |וְלַאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb and|בְּעָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb Kenites|הַקֵּינִֽי׃\rb*; \v 30 \rb to those|וְלַאֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb in Hormah|בְּחָרְמָ֛ה\rb*,\rb |וְלַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |בְּבוֹר־\rb* \rb Bor-ashan|עָשָׁ֖ן\rb*,\rb |וְלַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb and Athach|בַּעֲתָֽךְ׃\rb*; \v 31 \rb and to those|וְלַאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in Hebron|בְּחֶבְר֑וֹן\rb* \rb and in all|וּֽלְכָל־\rb* \rb the places|הַמְּקֹמ֛וֹת\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb*\rb |ה֥וּא\rb* \rb and his men|וַאֲנָשָֽׁיו׃פ\rb* \rb had roamed|הִתְהַלֶּךְ־\rb*.\rb |שָׁ֥ם\rb*
\c 31
\s1 Saul’s Overthrow and Death
\r (\ref 2 Samuel 1:1–16|2SA 1:1-16\ref*; \ref 1 Chronicles 10:1–6|1CH 10:1-6\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Now the Philistines|וּפְלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb fought|נִלְחָמִ֣ים\rb* \rb against Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb and the men|אַנְשֵׁ֤י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb fled|וַיָּנֻ֜סוּ\rb* \rb before|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb them|פְלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb and many fell|וַיִּפְּל֥וּ\rb* \rb slain|חֲלָלִ֖ים\rb* \rb on Mount|בְּהַ֥ר\rb* \rb Gilboa|הַגִּלְבֹּֽעַ׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb The Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb hotly pursued|וַיַּדְבְּק֣וּ\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֖וּל\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his sons|בָּנָ֑יו\rb*, \rb and they killed|וַיַּכּ֣וּ\rb*\rb |פְלִשְׁתִּ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Saul’s|שָׁאֽוּל׃\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Jonathan|יְהוֹנָתָ֧ן\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Abinadab|אֲבִינָדָ֛ב\rb*, \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |מַלְכִּי־\rb* \rb Malchishua|שׁ֖וּעַ\rb*. \v 3 \rb When the battle|הַמִּלְחָמָה֙\rb* \rb intensified|וַתִּכְבַּ֤ד\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֔וּל\rb*, \rb the archers|הַמּוֹרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֲנָשִׁ֣ים\rb*\rb |בַּקָּ֑שֶׁת\rb* \rb overtook him|וַיִּמְצָאֻ֥הוּ\rb*\rb |מֵהַמּוֹרִֽים׃\rb* \rb and wounded him|וַיָּ֥חֶל\rb* \rb critically|מְאֹ֖ד\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Then Saul|שָׁאוּל֩\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to his armor-bearer|לְנֹשֵׂ֨א\rb*\rb |כֵלָ֜יו\rb*, “\rb Draw|שְׁלֹ֥ף\rb* \rb your sword|חַרְבְּךָ֣׀\rb* \rb and run me through|וְדָקְרֵ֣נִי\rb* \rb with it|בָ֗הּ\rb*, \rb or|פֶּן־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֤לֶּה\rb* \rb uncircumcised men|הָעֲרֵלִ֨ים\rb* \rb will come|יָ֠בוֹאוּ\rb* \rb and run me through|וּדְקָרֻ֙נִי֙\rb* \rb and torture|וְהִתְעַלְּלוּ־\rb* \rb me|בִ֔י\rb*!”
\p \rb But his armor-bearer|נֹשֵׂ֣א\rb*\rb |כֵלָ֔יו\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb was terrified|יָרֵ֖א\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb and refused|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb to do it|אָבָה֙\rb*. \rb So Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֤ח\rb* \rb his own sword|הַחֶ֔רֶב\rb* \rb and fell|וַיִּפֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb on it|עָלֶֽיהָ׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb When his armor-bearer|נֹשֵֽׂא־\rb*\rb |כֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֥רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֑וּל\rb* \rb was dead|מֵ֣ת\rb*, \rb he|ה֛וּא\rb* \rb too|גַּם־\rb* \rb fell|וַיִּפֹּ֥ל\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his own sword|חַרְבּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb and died|וַיָּ֥מָת\rb* \rb with him|עִמּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb So Saul|שָׁא֡וּל\rb*, \rb his three|וּשְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb sons|בָּנָיו֩\rb*, \rb his armor-bearer|וְנֹשֵׂ֨א\rb*\rb |כֵלָ֜יו\rb*, \rb and|גַּ֧ם\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his men|אֲנָשָׁ֛יו\rb* \rb died|וַיָּ֣מָת\rb* \rb together|יַחְדָּֽו׃\rb* \rb that same|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb*.
\s1 The Philistines Possess the Towns
\r (\ref 1 Chronicles 10:7–10|1CH 10:7-10\ref*)
\p \v 7 \rb When the Israelites|אַנְשֵֽׁי־\rb*\rb |יִ֠שְׂרָאֵל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb along|בְּעֵ֨בֶר\rb* \rb the valley|הָעֵ֜מֶק\rb*\rb |וַאֲשֶׁ֣ר׀\rb* \rb and those on the other side|בְּעֵ֣בֶר\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֗ן\rb* \rb saw|וַיִּרְא֣וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the army|אַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb had fled|נָ֙סוּ֙\rb* \rb and that|וְכִי־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁא֣וּל\rb* \rb and his sons|וּבָנָ֑יו\rb* \rb had died|מֵ֖תוּ\rb*, \rb they abandoned|וַיַּעַזְב֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their cities|הֶֽעָרִים֙\rb* \rb and ran away|וַיָּנֻ֔סוּ\rb*. \rb So the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb and occupied|וַיֵּֽשְׁב֖וּ\rb* \rb their cities|בָּהֶֽן׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb |וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb The next day|מִֽמָּחֳרָ֔ת\rb*, \rb when the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb to strip|לְפַשֵּׁ֖ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the dead|הַחֲלָלִ֑ים\rb*, \rb they found|וַֽיִּמְצְא֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Saul|שָׁאוּל֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his three|שְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb sons|בָּנָ֔יו\rb* \rb fallen|נֹפְלִ֖ים\rb* \rb on Mount|בְּהַ֥ר\rb* \rb Gilboa|הַגִּלְבֹּֽעַ׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb They cut off|וַֽיִּכְרְתוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Saul’s head|רֹאשׁ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb stripped off|וַיַּפְשִׁ֖יטוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his armor|כֵּלָ֑יו\rb*, \rb and sent|וַיְשַׁלְּח֨וּ\rb* \rb messengers throughout the land|בְאֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֜ים\rb*\rb |סָבִ֗יב\rb* \rb to proclaim the news|לְבַשֵּׂ֛ר\rb* \rb in the temples|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of their idols|עֲצַבֵּיהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and among their people|הָעָֽם׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb They put|וַיָּשִׂ֙מוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his armor|כֵּלָ֔יו\rb* \rb in the temple|בֵּ֖ית\rb* \rb of the Ashtoreths|עַשְׁתָּר֑וֹת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and hung|תָּקְע֔וּ\rb* \rb his body|גְּוִיָּתוֹ֙\rb* \rb on the wall|בְּחוֹמַ֖ת\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Beth-shan|שָֽׁן׃\rb*.
\s1 Jabesh-gilead’s Tribute to Saul
\r (\ref 1 Chronicles 10:11–14|1CH 10:11-14\ref*)
\p \v 11 \rb When the people|יֹשְׁבֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Jabesh-gilead|יָבֵ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |גִּלְעָ֑ד\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמְע֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb had done|עָשׂ֥וּ\rb* \rb to Saul|לְשָׁאֽוּל׃\rb*, \v 12 \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb their men|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of valor|חַיִל֮\rb* \rb set out|וַיָּק֜וּמוּ\rb*, \rb journeyed|וַיֵּלְכ֣וּ\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb night|הַלַּיְלָה֒\rb*, \rb and retrieved|וַיִּקְח֞וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the bodies|גְּוִיַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of Saul|שָׁא֗וּל\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb and|גְּוִיֹּ֣ת\rb* \rb his sons|בָּנָ֔יו\rb* \rb from the wall|מֵחוֹמַ֖ת\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Beth-shan|שָׁ֑ן\rb*.
\p \rb When they arrived|וַיָּבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb at Jabesh|יָבֵ֔שָׁה\rb*, \rb they burned|וַיִּשְׂרְפ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb the bodies there|שָֽׁם׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb Then they took|וַיִּקְחוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their bones|עַצְמֹ֣תֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and buried them|וַיִּקְבְּר֥וּ\rb* \rb under|תַֽחַת־\rb* \rb the tamarisk tree|הָאֶ֖שֶׁל\rb* \rb in Jabesh|בְּיָבֵ֑שָׁה\rb*, \rb and they fasted|וַיָּצֻ֖מוּ\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִֽים׃פ\rb*.
